bric/cyberware-rust/pulls/278/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/80f11a458f72b44d826ed2cffa6ec8312956f3ba"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3770607587","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/278#issuecomment-3770607587","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/278","id":3770607587,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7gvufj","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-20T01:11:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T01:33:31Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nReplaces per-service cached plugin resolution with a shared GtsPluginSelector, adds lock-free ThrottledLog for warning throttling, enables scoped client lookups via ClientHub::try_get_scoped, and changes error variants to carry unavailability reasons (PluginUnavailable / ServiceUnavailable) across example and system tenant resolver modules.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Plugin Selector Infrastructure** <br> `libs/modkit/src/plugins/mod.rs` | New public `GtsPluginSelector` providing resettable single‑flight async resolution with cached `Arc<str>` and `get_or_init()` / `reset()` APIs; includes concurrency tests. |\n| **Throttled Logging Infrastructure** <br> `libs/modkit/src/telemetry/throttled_log.rs`, `libs/modkit/src/telemetry/mod.rs` | New public `ThrottledLog` with lock‑free interval gating (`should_log()`); module re-export added. |\n| **Crate Exports** <br> `libs/modkit/src/lib.rs` | Exposed `plugins` module and re-exported `GtsPluginSelector` at crate root. |\n| **ClientHub Enhancement** <br> `libs/modkit/src/client_hub.rs` | Added `pub fn try_get_scoped<T>(&self, scope: &ClientScope) -> Option<Arc<T>>` for scoped client lookup; tests for hit/miss added. |\n| **Example & System Error Types** <br> `examples/.../domain/error.rs`, `modules/system/.../domain/error.rs`, `examples/.../tenant_resolver-sdk/src/error.rs`, `modules/system/.../tenant_resolver-sdk/src/error.rs` | Replaced `PluginClientNotFound { gts_id }` with `PluginUnavailable { gts_id, reason }`; added `TenantResolverError::ServiceUnavailable(String)`; updated bidirectional `From` mappings. |\n| **Service Refactoring (Example & System)** <br> `examples/.../domain/service.rs`, `modules/system/.../domain/service.rs` | Removed per-service resolved cache and `ResolvedPlugin`; added `selector: GtsPluginSelector` and `unavailable_log_throttle: ThrottledLog`; `resolve_plugin()` now returns `String` (instance id); `get_plugin()` uses selector + `try_get_scoped()` and emits throttled warnings; added `pub fn new(...)`. |\n| **REST Error Mapping** <br> `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-gw/src/api/rest/error.rs` | Mapping updated to convert `PluginUnavailable` into `StatusCode::SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE` with reason-aware message. |\n| **Minor API Surface** <br> `libs/modkit/src/lib.rs`, tests | New public exports and accompanying tests added across the crate. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant Service\n    participant GtsPluginSelector\n    participant ClientHub\n    participant PluginClient\n\n    Client->>Service: get_plugin()\n    activate Service\n    Service->>GtsPluginSelector: get_or_init(resolve_fn)\n    activate GtsPluginSelector\n    alt cached\n        GtsPluginSelector-->>Service: Arc<str> (gts_id)\n    else resolve needed\n        GtsPluginSelector->>GtsPluginSelector: acquire single-flight lock\n        GtsPluginSelector->>resolve_fn: call async resolver\n        resolve_fn-->>GtsPluginSelector: String (gts_id)\n        GtsPluginSelector->>GtsPluginSelector: cache Arc<str>\n        GtsPluginSelector-->>Service: Arc<str> (gts_id)\n    end\n    deactivate GtsPluginSelector\n\n    Service->>Service: build ClientScope from gts_id\n    Service->>ClientHub: try_get_scoped<PluginClient>(scope)\n    activate ClientHub\n    alt client present\n        ClientHub-->>Service: Some(Arc<PluginClient>)\n    else missing\n        ClientHub-->>Service: None\n    end\n    deactivate ClientHub\n\n    alt client present\n        Service-->>Client: PluginClient\n    else missing\n        Service->>Service: if unavailable_log_throttle.should_log() then log\n        Service-->>Client: PluginUnavailable { gts_id, reason }\n    end\n    deactivate Service\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Bechma  \n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped and cached an id so neat,  \n> I whispered once when plugins beat,  \n> Scoped beans I fetch from hub and tree,  \n> Throttled warnings let silence be,  \n> Hooray — unavailable reasons set free!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                       |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                       |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The PR title accurately summarizes the main changes: adding GtsPluginSelector and ThrottledLog to modkit for lazy plugin resolution, which is the primary focus of the changeset. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                              |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_ass