to avoid filesystem mutations; exposes read-only modkit config introspection APIs and re-exports; adds serde_yaml and a comprehensive CLI test suite.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Server CLI & Entry** <br> `apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs`, `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml` | New CLI flags `--list-modules`, `--dump-modules-config-yaml`, `--dump-modules-config-json`; `--mock` applied before dumps; added `serde_yaml` as a dev-dependency. |\n| **Config Dump Implementation** <br> `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs` | New module exposing `list_module_names`, `render_effective_modules_config`, `redact_dsn_password`, `dump_effective_modules_config_yaml`, `dump_effective_modules_config_json` (redacts DSNs, serializes YAML/JSON). |\n| **Core Config (dry-run) & API** <br> `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs` | Threaded `dry_run: bool` through SQLite DSN builders and `build_final_db_for_module`; skip filesystem mutations when dry-run; added render/list/dump public APIs and tests. |\n| **Bootstrap Re-exports** <br> `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/mod.rs` | Re-exported `dump_effective_modules_config_json`, `dump_effective_modules_config_yaml`, `list_module_names`, `render_effective_modules_config`. |\n| **Manifests / Features** <br> `libs/modkit/Cargo.toml` | Added optional `serde_yaml` dependency and included in bootstrap feature. |\n| **CLI Tests** <br> `apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs` | Large suite of CLI tests for listing, YAML/JSON dumps, redaction, `--mock`, and multi-module scenarios. |\n| **Docs: API Rename** <br> `docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`, `modules/system/types-registry/.../lib.rs` | Documentation and examples: `DirectoryApi` → `DirectoryClient`; `TypesRegistryApi` → `TypesRegistryClient` in examples. |\n| **CI Workflow** <br> `.github/workflows/scorecard.yml` | Simplified analysis job condition; pinned upload-sarif action to a specific commit hash. |\n| **Minor Refactors** <br> `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/{scanner.rs,validator.rs}` | Internal conditional refactors and import reorderings (behavior preserved). |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    actor User\n    participant CLI as \"hyperspot-server CLI\"\n    participant Main as \"main.rs\"\n    participant Modkit as \"modkit::bootstrap::config\"\n    participant Dump as \"config::dump\"\n    participant Ser as \"serde (JSON/YAML)\"\n\n    User->>CLI: run with --list-modules / --dump-*\n    CLI->>Main: parsed args\n    Main->>Modkit: load AppConfig\n    Modkit-->>Main: AppConfig\n    alt --mock present\n        Main->>Modkit: override_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config)\n        Modkit-->>Main: mocked AppConfig\n    end\n    Main->>Dump: list_module_names / dump_effective_modules_config_*(AppConfig)\n    Dump->>Modkit: parse per-module configs & resolve DB info (dry_run guarded)\n    Modkit-->>Dump: module entries (DSNs redacted)\n    Dump->>Ser: serialize to JSON or YAML\n    Ser-->>Dump: rendered string\n    Dump-->>Main: output string\n    Main-->>CLI: print and exit\n    CLI-->>User: display\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~50 minutes\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer  \n- Bechma  \n- alizid10\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hop through configs, soft and quick,  \n> > I list your modules and make YAML slick,  \n> > I hide the passwords, dry-runs skip the dirt,  \n> > Mocked DBs hum, no filesystem hurt,  \n> > A happy rabbit cheers the dump — a tiny skitter!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 4 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning)</summary>\n\n|         Check name         | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                    | Resolution                                                                                                                                                      |\n| :------------------------: | :--------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ⚠️ Warning | Minor out-of-scope changes detected: scorecard.yml workflow update and documentation edits to DirectoryApi/DirectoryClient in MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md are unrelated to the primary objective of adding config dump CLI flags. | Consider moving scorecard.yml and DirectoryApi/DirectoryClient documentation changes to separate PRs to keep this PR focused on the config dump feature [`#206`]. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (4 passed)</summary>\n\n|      Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| :-----------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check  | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n|     Title check     | ✅ Passed | The title clearly describes the main change: adding CLI flags to dump effective per-module configuration, which aligns with the primary objective of the changeset.                                                                                                                |\n| Linked Issues check | ✅ Passed | All primary objectives from issue `#206` are met: CLI options implemented for dumping config (--list-modules, --dump-modules-config-yaml, --dump-modules-config-json), DSN password redaction applied, dry-run mode for read-only inspection, and comprehensive test coverage added. |\n|  Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3767496978/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3767507681","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#issuecomment-3767507681","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/277","id":3767507681,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7gj5rh","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-19T10:10:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T12:20:05Z","body":"<!--MERGIFY-CI-INSIGHTS-REPORT-->\n# 🧪 CI Insights\n\nHere's what we observed from your CI run for c302c16e.\n\n## 🟢 All jobs passed!\n\nBut CI Insights is watching 👀","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3767507681/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":10562,"client_id":"Iv1.d035f68f69425dc1","slug":"mergify","node_id":"MDM6QXBwMTA1NjI=","owner":{"login":"Mergifyio","id":37838584,"node_id":"MDEyOk9yZ2FuaXphdGlvbjM3ODM4NTg0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37838584?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio","html_url":"https://github.com/Mergifyio","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mergifyio/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"Mergify","description":"Pull requests automation service.","external_url":"https://mergify.com","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","created_at":"2018-03-30T10:19:51Z","updated_at":"2026-03-02T11:02:56Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","deployments":"write","emails":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","merge_queues":"read","metadata":"read","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"read","workflows":"write"},"events":["branch_protection_configuration","branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","deployment_status","issue_comment","member","membership","merge_group","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","push","repository","repository_ruleset","status","team","team_add","workflow_job","workflow_run"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704136811","pull_request_review_id":3677350122,"id":2704136811,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hLdpr","diff_hunk":"@@ -1153,6 +1153,173 @@ pub fn module_home(app: &AppConfig, module_name: &str) -> PathBuf {\n     PathBuf::from(&app.server.home_dir).join(module_name)\n }\n \n+// ---- Effective Module Configuration Dump Support ----\n+\n+/// List all module names present in the configuration.\n+///\n+/// Returns a sorted vector of module names that are configured in the `AppConfig`.\n+/// This is useful for discovering available modules before dumping their configuration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+/// ```no_run\n+/// use modkit::bootstrap::AppConfig;\n+/// # fn example(config: &AppConfig) {\n+/// let modules = modkit::bootstrap::config::list_module_names(config);\n+/// for module in modules {\n+///     println!(\"Module: {}\", module);\n+/// }\n+/// # }\n+/// ```\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn list_module_names(app: &AppConfig) -> Vec<String> {\n+    let mut names: Vec<String> = app.modules.keys().cloned().collect();\n+    names.sort();\n+    names\n+}\n+\n+/// Render effective configuration for all loaded modules.\n+///\n+/// This function builds a complete view of the effective runtime configuration\n+/// for each module that is successfully loaded in the `ModuleRegistry`.\n+///\n+/// For each module, it includes:\n+/// - `runtime`: Module runtime type (local/oop) if configured\n+/// - `config`: Module-specific configuration section (as-is from config file)\n+/// - `database`: Final resolved database configuration with redacted DSN (if applicable)\n+///\n+/// # Errors\n+/// Returns an error if configuration parsing or database resolution fails.\n+pub fn render_effective_modules_config(app: &AppConfig) -> Result<serde_json::Value> {\n+    use serde_json::json;\n+\n+    let home_dir = PathBuf::from(&app.server.home_dir);\n+    let mut modules_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+    // Iterate over all modules in the configuration\n+    for module_name in app.modules.keys() {\n+        let mut module_entry = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+        // Get runtime configuration if present\n+        if let Ok(Some(runtime_config)) = get_module_runtime_config(app, module_name) {\n+            module_entry.insert(\n+                \"runtime\".to_owned(),\n+                json!({\n+                    \"type\": match runtime_config.mod_type {\n+                        RuntimeKind::Local => \"local\",\n+                        RuntimeKind::Oop => \"oop\",\n+                    }\n+                }),\n+            );\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get module config section (the \"config\" field)\n+        if let Ok(module_config) = parse_module_config(app, module_name) {\n+            if !module_config.config.is_null() {\n+                module_entry.insert(\"config\".to_owned(), module_config.config);\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get database configuration (resolved DSN + pool)\n+        if let Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) = build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir) {\n+            // Redact password in DSN\n+            let redacted_dsn = redact_dsn_password(&dsn)?;\n+\n+            let mut db_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+            db_config.insert(\"dsn\".to_owned(), json!(redacted_dsn));\n+\n+            // Add pool configuration if present\n+            let mut pool_map = serde_json::Map::new();\n+            if let Some(max_conns) = pool.max_conns {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"max_conns\".to_owned(), json!(max_conns));\n+            }\n+            if let Some(min_conns) = pool.min_conns {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"min_conns\".to_owned(), json!(min_conns));\n+            }\n+            if let Some(acquire_timeout) = pool.acquire_timeout {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"acquire_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", acquire_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(idle_timeout) = pool.idle_timeout {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"idle_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", idle_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(max_lifetime) = pool.max_lifetime {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"max_lifetime\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", max_lifetime.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(test_before_acquire) = pool.test_before_acquire {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"test_before_acquire\".to_owned(), json!(test_before_acquire));\n+            }\n+\n+            if !pool_map.is_empty() {\n+                db_config.insert(\"pool\".to_owned(), json!(pool_map));\n+            }\n+\n+            module_entry.insert(\"database\".to_owned(), json!(db_config));\n+        }\n+\n+        // Only add module to output if it has any configuration\n+        if !module_entry.is_empty() {\n+            modules_config.insert(module_name.clone(), json!(module_entry));\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    Ok(json!(modules_config))\n+}","path":"libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs","commit_id":"48074954f35cfc129a652af967b3c2cf0bfe25e5","original_commit_id":"a34c3be6ee2f1185521514f0c71cf5c892ada9c4","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, let's find the build_final_db_for_module function definition\nrg -n \"fn build_final_db_for_module\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -A 30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1298\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Get more of the function\nrg -n \"fn build_final_db_for_module\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -A 80 | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3265\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for create_dir_all in the entire file\nrg -n \"create_dir_all\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -B 3 -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2104\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Now let's find where render_effective_modules_config is called\nrg -n \"render_effective_modules_config\" libs/modkit/src -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4891\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's also check which functions call finalize_sqlite_dsn to understand the call chain\nrg -n \"finalize_sqlite_dsn\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 432\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check where dump_effective_modules_config_json and dump_effective_modules_config_yaml are used\nrg -n \"dump_effective_modules_config\" libs/modkit/src -B 2 -A 2 | grep -v \"^--$\" | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2998\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check the main CLI entry point to see how these functions are used\nfd -t f \"main.rs\" libs/modkit/src | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's search across the entire codebase for where dump_effective_modules_config functions are called\nrg -n \"dump_effective_modules_config_json|dump_effective_modules_config_yaml\" --type rust | grep -v \"^libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 512\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's look for CLI argument handling that might call these functions\nfd -t f \"*.rs\" | xargs grep -l \"dump.*config\\|dump-.*config\" | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 347\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's look at the CLI usage in main.rs\nrg -n \"dump_effective_modules_config\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs -B 10 -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1193\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's also examine what CLI arguments trigger this\nrg -n \"dump-modules-config\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs -B 5 -A 5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's find the CLI struct definition\nrg -n \"struct CliArgs\\|dump_modules_config\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs -B 2 -A 15 | head -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check the full context around the dump config calls to understand the CLI behavior\ncat apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | head -200 | tail -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3675\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's see the finalize_sqlite_dsn function in detail to understand all the places where create_dir_all is called\nrg -n \"fn finalize_sqlite_dsn\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -A 100 | head -120\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4061\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check if there are any tests that show the side effect behavior\nrg -n \"test.*render_effective_modules_config\" libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs -A 30 | head -80\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3221\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Side effect in inspection commands: `render_effective_modules_config` creates module directories for SQLite paths.**\n\nThe function calls `build_final_db_for_module`, which eventually invokes `build_sqlite_dsn`. This function calls `std::fs::create_dir_all` to create `home_dir/module_name` directories across five code paths. When users run `--dump-modules-config-yaml` or `--dump-modules-config-json` CLI flags to inspect configuration, these directories are created as an unintended side effect.\n\nFor read-only inspection commands, consider:\n1. Adding a `dry_run` parameter to `build_final_db_for_module` to skip directory creation\n2. Documenting this behavior in CLI help text\n3. Using a separate resolution path that doesn't create directories\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs` around lines 1192 - 1274,\nrender_effective_modules_config is causing unintended side effects because\nbuild_final_db_for_module -> build_sqlite_dsn currently calls\nstd::fs::create_dir_all for SQLite paths; add a dry_run (bool) parameter to\nbuild_final_db_for_module and propagate it through to build_sqlite_dsn so that\nwhen dry_run is true the function returns the resolved DSN without creating\ndirectories, then call build_final_db_for_module(..., dry_run: true) from\nrender_effective_modules_config (and update other call sites as needed); also\nupdate build_sqlite_dsn to skip create_dir_all if dry_run is true and consider\ndocumenting the CLI flags to note the read-only inspection behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @bit8shift\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T10:21:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T10:55:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704136811","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704136811"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704136811"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704136811/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1192,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":1274,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":122,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175462","pull_request_review_id":3677393735,"id":2704175462,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hLnFm","diff_hunk":"@@ -134,6 +149,30 @@ async fn main() -> Result<()> {\n         return Ok(());\n     }\n \n+    // List all configured modules and exit if requested\n+    if cli.list_modules {\n+        let modules = list_module_names(&config);\n+        println!(\"Configured modules ({}):\", modules.len());\n+        for module in modules {\n+            println!(\"  - {module}\");\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // Dump modules config in YAML format and exit if requested\n+    if cli.dump_modules_config_yaml {\n+        let yaml = dump_effective_modules_config_yaml(&config)?;\n+        println!(\"{yaml}\");\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // Dump modules config in JSON format and exit if requested\n+    if cli.dump_modules_config_json {\n+        let json = dump_effective_modules_config_json(&config)?;\n+        println!(\"{json}\");\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }","path":"apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs","commit_id":"c302c16e714d2f6d5a16407e919469a1780d1718","original_commit_id":"9c16f61d4db6494b01082cf02efec880f54f3323","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | head -200 | tail -100\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4336\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"override_modules_with_mock_db\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 251\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"cli\\.mock\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"struct.*Cli\\|pub.*mock\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ -A 3\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | sed -n '200,220p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1036\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"mock\\|Mock\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"struct Cli\\|pub struct\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"pub struct Cli\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ -A 20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"#\\[command\\]|#\\[derive\\|pub struct Cli|pub bool mock\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ -B 2 -A 10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfd \"*.rs\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ | xargs rg -l \"Cli\" | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 642\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind apps/hyperspot-server/src -name \"*.rs\" -type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 145\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"struct Cli\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ -A 30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2056\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -n \"mock\" apps/hyperspot-server/src/ -i --no-heading\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1194\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | sed -n '230,250p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1202\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | sed -n '1,100p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3475\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs | sed -n '88,180p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3877\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Apply `--mock` override to module config dumps.**\n\nThe `--mock` flag is not respected in the dump paths (lines 163–173). If `--mock --dump-modules-config-yaml` is used, the output shows real DSNs instead of `sqlite::memory:`. Since these dumps should reflect the effective configuration with all CLI overrides applied, apply the mock override before dumping:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     if cli.dump_modules_config_yaml {\n+        if cli.mock {\n+            override_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config);\n+        }\n         let yaml = dump_effective_modules_config_yaml(&config)?;\n         println!(\"{yaml}\");\n         return Ok(());\n     }\n\n     if cli.dump_modules_config_json {\n+        if cli.mock {\n+            override_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config);\n+        }\n         let json = dump_effective_modules_config_json(&config)?;\n         println!(\"{json}\");\n         return Ok(());\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\nNote: The `--print-config` path (line 147) has the same issue and should also respect `--mock`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs` around lines 152 - 174, The module-dump\nand list/print branches fetch and print from the original config without\napplying the CLI --mock override; before calling list_module_names,\ndump_effective_modules_config_yaml, dump_effective_modules_config_json, or the\n--print-config logic, apply the same mock override mutation to the in-memory\nconfig (the same code path used when processing cli.mock) so the effective\nconfig reflects sqlite::memory: and other mock substitutions; in short, ensure\nyou mutate/override config with the CLI --mock handling before invoking\nlist_module_names(&config), dump_effective_modules_config_yaml(&config),\ndump_effective_modules_config_json(&config) or the print-config output.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 54f2c1c\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T10:33:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:41:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704175462","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175462"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704175462"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175462/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":156,"original_start_line":152,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":178,"original_line":174,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":64,"position":74,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175470","pull_request_review_id":3677393735,"id":2704175470,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hLnFu","diff_hunk":"@@ -1153,6 +1153,173 @@ pub fn module_home(app: &AppConfig, module_name: &str) -> PathBuf {\n     PathBuf::from(&app.server.home_dir).join(module_name)\n }\n \n+// ---- Effective Module Configuration Dump Support ----\n+\n+/// List all module names present in the configuration.\n+///\n+/// Returns a sorted vector of module names that are configured in the `AppConfig`.\n+/// This is useful for discovering available modules before dumping their configuration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+/// ```no_run\n+/// use modkit::bootstrap::AppConfig;\n+/// # fn example(config: &AppConfig) {\n+/// let modules = modkit::bootstrap::config::list_module_names(config);\n+/// for module in modules {\n+///     println!(\"Module: {}\", module);\n+/// }\n+/// # }\n+/// ```\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn list_module_names(app: &AppConfig) -> Vec<String> {\n+    let mut names: Vec<String> = app.modules.keys().cloned().collect();\n+    names.sort();\n+    names\n+}\n+\n+/// Render effective configuration for all loaded modules.\n+///\n+/// This function builds a complete view of the effective runtime configuration\n+/// for each module that is successfully loaded in the `ModuleRegistry`.\n+///\n+/// For each module, it includes:\n+/// - `runtime`: Module runtime type (local/oop) if configured\n+/// - `config`: Module-specific configuration section (as-is from config file)\n+/// - `database`: Final resolved database configuration with redacted DSN (if applicable)\n+///\n+/// # Errors\n+/// Returns an error if configuration parsing or database resolution fails.\n+pub fn render_effective_modules_config(app: &AppConfig) -> Result<serde_json::Value> {\n+    use serde_json::json;\n+\n+    let home_dir = PathBuf::from(&app.server.home_dir);\n+    let mut modules_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+    // Iterate over all modules in the configuration\n+    for module_name in app.modules.keys() {\n+        let mut module_entry = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+        // Get runtime configuration if present\n+        if let Ok(Some(runtime_config)) = get_module_runtime_config(app, module_name) {\n+            module_entry.insert(\n+                \"runtime\".to_owned(),\n+                json!({\n+                    \"type\": match runtime_config.mod_type {\n+                        RuntimeKind::Local => \"local\",\n+                        RuntimeKind::Oop => \"oop\",\n+                    }\n+                }),\n+            );\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get module config section (the \"config\" field)\n+        if let Ok(module_config) = parse_module_config(app, module_name) {\n+            if !module_config.config.is_null() {\n+                module_entry.insert(\"config\".to_owned(), module_config.config);\n+            }\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get database configuration (resolved DSN + pool)\n+        if let Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) = build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir) {\n+            // Redact password in DSN\n+            let redacted_dsn = redact_dsn_password(&dsn)?;\n+\n+            let mut db_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+            db_config.insert(\"dsn\".to_owned(), json!(redacted_dsn));\n+\n+            // Add pool configuration if present\n+            let mut pool_map = serde_json::Map::new();\n+            if let Some(max_conns) = pool.max_conns {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"max_conns\".to_owned(), json!(max_conns));\n+            }\n+            if let Some(min_conns) = pool.min_conns {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"min_conns\".to_owned(), json!(min_conns));\n+            }\n+            if let Some(acquire_timeout) = pool.acquire_timeout {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"acquire_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", acquire_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(idle_timeout) = pool.idle_timeout {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"idle_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", idle_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(max_lifetime) = pool.max_lifetime {\n+                pool_map.insert(\n+                    \"max_lifetime\".to_owned(),\n+                    json!(format!(\"{}s\", max_lifetime.as_secs())),\n+                );\n+            }\n+            if let Some(test_before_acquire) = pool.test_before_acquire {\n+                pool_map.insert(\"test_before_acquire\".to_owned(), json!(test_before_acquire));\n+            }\n+\n+            if !pool_map.is_empty() {\n+                db_config.insert(\"pool\".to_owned(), json!(pool_map));\n+            }\n+\n+            module_entry.insert(\"database\".to_owned(), json!(db_config));\n+        }","path":"libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs","commit_id":"48074954f35cfc129a652af967b3c2cf0bfe25e5","original_commit_id":"9c16f61d4db6494b01082cf02efec880f54f3323","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Propagate module/DB errors instead of silently skipping them.**\n\n`render_effective_modules_config` currently ignores parse/DB errors via `if let Ok(...)`, even though the doc says errors should be returned. This can hide misconfigurations and yield misleading dumps. Consider using `?` to propagate errors and parse once per module.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    // Iterate over all modules in the configuration\n-    for module_name in app.modules.keys() {\n+    // Iterate over all modules in the configuration\n+    for module_name in app.modules.keys() {\n         let mut module_entry = serde_json::Map::new();\n \n-        // Get runtime configuration if present\n-        if let Ok(Some(runtime_config)) = get_module_runtime_config(app, module_name) {\n+        let ModuleConfig { runtime, config, .. } = parse_module_config(app, module_name)\n+            .with_context(|| format!(\"Invalid module config for '{module_name}'\"))?;\n+\n+        // Get runtime configuration if present\n+        if let Some(runtime_config) = runtime {\n             module_entry.insert(\n                 \"runtime\".to_owned(),\n                 json!({\n                     \"type\": match runtime_config.mod_type {\n@@\n-        if let Ok(module_config) = parse_module_config(app, module_name) {\n-            if !module_config.config.is_null() {\n-                module_entry.insert(\"config\".to_owned(), module_config.config);\n-            }\n-        }\n+        if !config.is_null() {\n+            module_entry.insert(\"config\".to_owned(), config);\n+        }\n@@\n-        if let Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) = build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir) {\n+        if let Some((dsn, pool)) = build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir)? {\n             // Redact password in DSN\n             let redacted_dsn = redact_dsn_password(&dsn)?;\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs` around lines 1198 - 1265, The loop\nin render_effective_modules_config silently swallows errors from\nget_module_runtime_config, parse_module_config, and build_final_db_for_module\nvia if let Ok(...) checks; change these to propagate errors (use ? on the\nResult-returning calls) so misconfigurations are returned instead of skipped,\nand call parse_module_config once per module to reuse its result; ensure\nredact_dsn_password still uses ? to propagate its error and keep building the\nmodule_entry (runtime, config, database) only when values are present from the\nsuccessful calls to get_module_runtime_config, parse_module_config, and\nbuild_final_db_for_module.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T10:33:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T10:57:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704175470","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175470"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2704175470"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704175470/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1198,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":1265,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":113,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704202355","pull_request_review_id":3677424175,"id":2704202355,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hLt