` to SHA commit for supply chain security.**\n\nAll other actions in this workflow are pinned to SHA commits, but `github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3` uses a mutable version tag. This inconsistency poses a supply chain risk and will likely lower the Scorecard's own \"Pinned-Dependencies\" check score.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n       - name: \"Upload to code-scanning\"\n-        uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3\n+        uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@3c8d1abf587ffce02620e8b44b3f91275ccbbd7d # v3.31.10\n         with:\n           sarif_file: results.sarif\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n      - name: \"Upload to code-scanning\"\n        uses: github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@3c8d1abf587ffce02620e8b44b3f91275ccbbd7d # v3.31.10\n        with:\n          sarif_file: results.sarif\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/scorecard.yml around lines 75 - 78, The workflow step\nnamed \"Upload to code-scanning\" currently uses the mutable action reference\ngithub/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3; change the uses entry to pin that action\nto its full commit SHA (e.g., github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@<COMMIT_SHA>) so\nthe step uses an immutable, verifiable version — update the uses value and keep\nthe sarif_file: results.sarif line unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits da6770a to 9a75b66","created_at":"2026-01-21T04:26:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:58:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917267","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917267"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917267"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":75,"original_start_line":75,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":78,"original_line":78,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":78,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917270","pull_request_review_id":3685296194,"id":2710917270,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hlVCW","diff_hunk":"@@ -128,12 +143,41 @@ async fn main() -> Result<()> {\n \n     tracing::info!(\"HyperSpot Server starting\");\n \n+    // Apply --mock override to config if requested (before any dumps)\n+    if cli.mock {\n+        override_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config);\n+    }\n+\n     // Print config and exit if requested\n     if cli.print_config {\n         println!(\"Effective configuration:\\n{}\", config.to_yaml()?);\n         return Ok(());\n     }\n \n+    // List all configured modules and exit if requested\n+    if cli.list_modules {\n+        let modules = list_module_names(&config);\n+        println!(\"Configured modules ({}):\", modules.len());\n+        for module in modules {\n+            println!(\"  - {module}\");\n+        }\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // Dump modules config in YAML format and exit if requested\n+    if cli.dump_modules_config_yaml {\n+        let yaml = dump_effective_modules_config_yaml(&config)?;\n+        println!(\"{yaml}\");\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }\n+\n+    // Dump modules config in JSON format and exit if requested\n+    if cli.dump_modules_config_json {\n+        let json = dump_effective_modules_config_json(&config)?;\n+        println!(\"{json}\");\n+        return Ok(());\n+    }","path":"apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs","commit_id":"c302c16e714d2f6d5a16407e919469a1780d1718","original_commit_id":"41852522b60c7d9a3a0c14ba9930a0254dbd528c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Read‑only flags still execute logging/OTEL side effects.**\n\nThese early‑exit branches run after logging/OTEL initialization and the startup probe/span (around Line 123), which can create log files/dirs and trigger network probes—contrary to the read‑only inspection intent and can pollute stdout. Consider short‑circuiting immediately after config load/mock override (before `init_logging_unified` / OTEL probe), and—if you need truly no‑side‑effects—use a config‑load path that doesn’t create `home_dir` or log directories for these flags.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs` around lines 146 - 179, The read-only CLI\nflags (print_config, list_modules, dump_effective_modules_config_yaml,\ndump_effective_modules_config_json and cli.mock) are being handled after\nlogging/OTEL/startup probe initialization, which causes side effects; move the\nearly-exit handling so that after loading and applying\noverride_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config) you check cli.print_config /\ncli.list_modules / cli.dump_* and return before calling init_logging_unified or\nstarting the startup probe/span (i.e., short-circuit immediately after config\nload/mock override), and if necessary add a config-only load path that does not\ncreate home/log directories or initialize OTEL to guarantee no filesystem or\nnetwork side effects.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 54f2c1c","created_at":"2026-01-21T04:26:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:41:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917270","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917270"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917270"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917270/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":145,"original_start_line":146,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":178,"original_line":179,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":75,"position":74,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917271","pull_request_review_id":3685296194,"id":2710917271,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hlVCX","diff_hunk":"@@ -619,7 +550,7 @@ impl MyModuleApi for MyModuleGrpcClient {\n use std::sync::Arc;\n use anyhow::Result;\n use modkit::client_hub::ClientHub;\n-use module_orchestrator_sdk::DirectoryApi;\n+use module_orchestrator_sdk::DirectoryClient;\n use crate::{MyModuleApi, MyModuleGrpcClient, SERVICE_NAME};","path":"docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md","commit_id":"41852522b60c7d9a3a0c14ba9930a0254dbd528c","original_commit_id":"41852522b60c7d9a3a0c14ba9930a0254dbd528c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Doc snippets still reference `DirectoryApi` after the rename.**\n\nAfter changing the import (Line 553), the example functions and usage still mention `DirectoryApi` (e.g., Line 557, Line 566, Line 580) and the table row still says “DirectoryApi + gRPC client.” This makes the docs inconsistent and the snippet non‑compiling. Please replace those references with `DirectoryClient`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested doc fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n@@\n-pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryApi) -> Result<()> {\n+pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n@@\n-pub async fn build_client(resolver: &dyn DirectoryApi) -> Result<Arc<dyn MyModuleApi>> {\n+pub async fn build_client(resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<Arc<dyn MyModuleApi>> {\n@@\n-    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n+    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n@@\n-| Registration | `expose_*_client()`     | DirectoryApi + gRPC client |\n+| Registration | `expose_*_client()`     | DirectoryClient + gRPC client |\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1473-1480\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md` around lines 553 - 554, The docs import was\nupdated to use DirectoryClient but remaining examples and the table still refer\nto DirectoryApi; update all occurrences of DirectoryApi to DirectoryClient in\nthe code snippets and explanatory text (e.g., the example functions that use\nDirectoryApi and the table row mentioning “DirectoryApi + gRPC client”),\nensuring consistency with the imported symbols (DirectoryClient, MyModuleApi,\nMyModuleGrpcClient, SERVICE_NAME); apply the same replacements in the other\naffected snippet mentioned (the later example block that still uses\nDirectoryApi).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits da6770a to 9a75b66","created_at":"2026-01-21T04:26:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:58:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917271","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917271"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917271"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917271/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":553,"original_start_line":553,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":554,"original_line":554,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":82,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917272","pull_request_review_id":3685296194,"id":2710917272,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hlVCY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,217 @@\n+//! Effective module configuration dump support.\n+//!\n+//! This module provides utilities for inspecting and dumping the effective\n+//! runtime configuration of modules, including resolved database DSNs and pool settings.\n+\n+use super::{build_final_db_for_module, parse_module_config, AppConfig, RuntimeKind};\n+use anyhow::{Context, Result};\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+use url::Url;\n+\n+/// List all module names present in the configuration.\n+///\n+/// Returns a sorted vector of module names that are configured in the `AppConfig`.\n+/// This is useful for discovering available modules before dumping their configuration.\n+///\n+/// # Example\n+/// ```no_run\n+/// use modkit::bootstrap::AppConfig;\n+/// # fn example(config: &AppConfig) {\n+/// let modules = modkit::bootstrap::config::list_module_names(config);\n+/// for module in modules {\n+///     println!(\"Module: {}\", module);\n+/// }\n+/// # }\n+/// ```\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn list_module_names(app: &AppConfig) -> Vec<String> {\n+    let mut names: Vec<String> = app.modules.keys().cloned().collect();\n+    names.sort();\n+    names\n+}\n+\n+/// Render effective configuration for all loaded modules.\n+///\n+/// This function builds a complete view of the effective runtime configuration\n+/// for each module that is successfully loaded in the `ModuleRegistry`.\n+///\n+/// For each module, it includes:\n+/// - `runtime`: Module runtime type (local/oop) if configured\n+/// - `config`: Module-specific configuration section (as-is from config file)\n+/// - `database`: Final resolved database configuration with redacted DSN (if applicable)\n+///\n+/// This is a read-only inspection operation that does not create any directories\n+/// or modify the filesystem.\n+///\n+/// Modules with configuration errors are logged as warnings and skipped,\n+/// allowing inspection of valid modules even when some are misconfigured.\n+///\n+/// This function never returns an error - all failures are logged as warnings\n+/// and the problematic modules are skipped.\n+///\n+/// # Errors\n+/// Returns an error if JSON serialization fails.\n+pub fn render_effective_modules_config(app: &AppConfig) -> Result<serde_json::Value> {\n+    use serde_json::json;\n+\n+    let home_dir = PathBuf::from(&app.server.home_dir);\n+    let mut modules_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+    // Iterate over all modules in the configuration\n+    for module_name in app.modules.keys() {\n+        let mut module_entry = serde_json::Map::new();\n+\n+        // Parse module config once for efficiency\n+        let parsed_config = match parse_module_config(app, module_name) {\n+            Ok(config) => config,\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                tracing::warn!(\n+                    module = %module_name,\n+                    error = %e,\n+                    \"Failed to parse module config, skipping\"\n+                );\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+        };\n+\n+        // Get runtime configuration if present\n+        if let Some(runtime_config) = parsed_config.runtime {\n+            module_entry.insert(\n+                \"runtime\".to_owned(),\n+                json!({\n+                    \"type\": match runtime_config.mod_type {\n+                        RuntimeKind::Local => \"local\",\n+                        RuntimeKind::Oop => \"oop\",\n+                    }\n+                }),\n+            );\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get module config section (the \"config\" field)\n+        if !parsed_config.config.is_null() {\n+            module_entry.insert(\"config\".to_owned(), parsed_config.config);\n+        }\n+\n+        // Get database configuration (resolved DSN + pool) - use dry_run=true\n+        match build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir, true) {\n+            Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) => {\n+                // Redact password in DSN (warn and skip if this fails)\n+                let redacted_dsn = match redact_dsn_password(&dsn) {\n+                    Ok(redacted) => redacted,\n+                    Err(e) => {\n+                        tracing::warn!(\n+                            module = %module_name,\n+                            dsn = %dsn,\n+                            error = %e,\n+                            \"Failed to redact DSN password, skipping database config\"\n+                        );\n+                        continue;\n+                    }","path":"libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs","commit_id":"c302c16e714d2f6d5a16407e919469a1780d1718","original_commit_id":"41852522b60c7d9a3a0c14ba9930a0254dbd528c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Redaction failure drops the whole module, but the warning says otherwise.**\n\n`continue` skips adding the module entry entirely, even though the warning says “skipping database config.” Either update the log message to “skipping module” or keep the module entry and omit only the DB section. The latter preserves runtime/config output for otherwise valid modules.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix to skip only the DB section</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                let redacted_dsn = match redact_dsn_password(&dsn) {\n-                    Ok(redacted) => redacted,\n-                    Err(e) => {\n-                        tracing::warn!(\n-                            module = %module_name,\n-                            dsn = %dsn,\n-                            error = %e,\n-                            \"Failed to redact DSN password, skipping database config\"\n-                        );\n-                        continue;\n-                    }\n-                };\n-\n-                let mut db_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n-                db_config.insert(\"dsn\".to_owned(), json!(redacted_dsn));\n-\n-                // Add pool configuration if present\n-                let mut pool_map = serde_json::Map::new();\n-                if let Some(max_conns) = pool.max_conns {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\"max_conns\".to_owned(), json!(max_conns));\n-                }\n-                if let Some(min_conns) = pool.min_conns {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\"min_conns\".to_owned(), json!(min_conns));\n-                }\n-                if let Some(acquire_timeout) = pool.acquire_timeout {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\n-                        \"acquire_timeout\".to_owned(),\n-                        json!(format!(\"{}s\", acquire_timeout.as_secs())),\n-                    );\n-                }\n-                if let Some(idle_timeout) = pool.idle_timeout {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\n-                        \"idle_timeout\".to_owned(),\n-                        json!(format!(\"{}s\", idle_timeout.as_secs())),\n-                    );\n-                }\n-                if let Some(max_lifetime) = pool.max_lifetime {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\n-                        \"max_lifetime\".to_owned(),\n-                        json!(format!(\"{}s\", max_lifetime.as_secs())),\n-                    );\n-                }\n-                if let Some(test_before_acquire) = pool.test_before_acquire {\n-                    pool_map.insert(\"test_before_acquire\".to_owned(), json!(test_before_acquire));\n-                }\n-\n-                if !pool_map.is_empty() {\n-                    db_config.insert(\"pool\".to_owned(), json!(pool_map));\n-                }\n-\n-                module_entry.insert(\"database\".to_owned(), json!(db_config));\n+                let redacted_dsn = match redact_dsn_password(&dsn) {\n+                    Ok(redacted) => Some(redacted),\n+                    Err(e) => {\n+                        tracing::warn!(\n+                            module = %module_name,\n+                            dsn = %dsn,\n+                            error = %e,\n+                            \"Failed to redact DSN password, skipping database config\"\n+                        );\n+                        None\n+                    }\n+                };\n+\n+                if let Some(redacted_dsn) = redacted_dsn {\n+                    let mut db_config = serde_json::Map::new();\n+                    db_config.insert(\"dsn\".to_owned(), json!(redacted_dsn));\n+\n+                    // Add pool configuration if present\n+                    let mut pool_map = serde_json::Map::new();\n+                    if let Some(max_conns) = pool.max_conns {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\"max_conns\".to_owned(), json!(max_conns));\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(min_conns) = pool.min_conns {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\"min_conns\".to_owned(), json!(min_conns));\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(acquire_timeout) = pool.acquire_timeout {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\n+                            \"acquire_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                            json!(format!(\"{}s\", acquire_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                        );\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(idle_timeout) = pool.idle_timeout {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\n+                            \"idle_timeout\".to_owned(),\n+                            json!(format!(\"{}s\", idle_timeout.as_secs())),\n+                        );\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(max_lifetime) = pool.max_lifetime {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\n+                            \"max_lifetime\".to_owned(),\n+                            json!(format!(\"{}s\", max_lifetime.as_secs())),\n+                        );\n+                    }\n+                    if let Some(test_before_acquire) = pool.test_before_acquire {\n+                        pool_map.insert(\"test_before_acquire\".to_owned(), json!(test_before_acquire));\n+                    }\n+\n+                    if !pool_map.is_empty() {\n+                        db_config.insert(\"pool\".to_owned(), json!(pool_map));\n+                    }\n+\n+                    module_entry.insert(\"database\".to_owned(), json!(db_config));\n+                }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs` around lines 95 - 109, The current\nlogic in build_final_db_for_module/dump flow calls redact_dsn_password and on\nErr(e) logs a warning and uses continue, which drops the entire module output\ndespite the message saying only the DB config is skipped; change this so the\nmodule entry is still emitted but without the DB section: when\nredact_dsn_password fails (in the match handling the Ok(Some((dsn, pool)))\nbranch), log the warning with module_name and dsn as now, then do not\ncontinue—instead set a flag or option (e.g., redacted_dsn = None or skip_db =\ntrue) and proceed to build the module entry but omit/skip adding the database\nfields (dsn/pool) to the dumped config; keep existing success path (Ok(redacted)\n=> include DB data) unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits da6770a to 9a75b66","created_at":"2026-01-21T04:26:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T04:58:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917272","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2710917272"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#discussion_r2710917272"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-ru