ptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs`:\n- Around line 1192-1274: render_effective_modules_config is causing unintended\nside effects because build_final_db_for_module -> build_sqlite_dsn currently\ncalls std::fs::create_dir_all for SQLite paths; add a dry_run (bool) parameter\nto build_final_db_for_module and propagate it through to build_sqlite_dsn so\nthat when dry_run is true the function returns the resolved DSN without creating\ndirectories, then call build_final_db_for_module(..., dry_run: true) from\nrender_effective_modules_config (and update other call sites as needed); also\nupdate build_sqlite_dsn to skip create_dir_all if dry_run is true and consider\ndocumenting the CLI flags to note the read-only inspection behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1276-1293`: **Consider consolidating with existing `redact_dsn_for_logging` function.**\n\nThere's a similar function `redact_dsn_for_logging` at line 895 that performs the same operation but uses `\"***\"` as the placeholder instead of `\"***REDACTED***\"`. Consider consolidating these into a single function with a configurable placeholder to reduce duplication.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n-/// Redacts password from DSN for logging\n-fn redact_dsn_for_logging(dsn: &str) -> Result<String> {\n+/// Redacts password from DSN with a configurable placeholder.\n+fn redact_dsn_password_with_placeholder(dsn: &str, placeholder: &str) -> Result<String> {\n     if dsn.contains('@') {\n         let parsed = Url::parse(dsn)?;\n         let mut log_url = parsed;\n         if log_url.password().is_some() {\n-            log_url.set_password(Some(\"***\")).ok();\n+            log_url.set_password(Some(placeholder)).ok();\n         }\n         Ok(log_url.to_string())\n     } else {\n         Ok(dsn.to_owned())\n     }\n }\n+\n+/// Redacts password from DSN for logging (uses \"***\")\n+fn redact_dsn_for_logging(dsn: &str) -> Result<String> {\n+    redact_dsn_password_with_placeholder(dsn, \"***\")\n+}\n+\n+/// Redacts password from DSN for security (uses \"***REDACTED***\")\n+fn redact_dsn_password(dsn: &str) -> Result<String> {\n+    redact_dsn_password_with_placeholder(dsn, \"***REDACTED***\")\n+}\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`2607-2803`: **Good test coverage for the new functionality.**\n\nThe tests cover important scenarios including:\n- Sorted module listing\n- Empty module list edge case\n- DSN password redaction with various formats\n- Multi-module rendering\n- Both YAML and JSON output formats\n\nOne optional enhancement: consider adding a test case for when `build_final_db_for_module` fails for one module to verify partial rendering behavior (currently the function appears to silently skip failed modules via the `if let Ok(...)` pattern on line 1223).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-3677350122","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-36773501