fig with the CLI\n--mock handling before invoking list_module_names(&config),\ndump_effective_modules_config_yaml(&config),\ndump_effective_modules_config_json(&config) or the print-config output.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs`:\n- Around line 1198-1265: The loop in render_effective_modules_config silently\nswallows errors from get_module_runtime_config, parse_module_config, and\nbuild_final_db_for_module via if let Ok(...) checks; change these to propagate\nerrors (use ? on the Result-returning calls) so misconfigurations are returned\ninstead of skipped, and call parse_module_config once per module to reuse its\nresult; ensure redact_dsn_password still uses ? to propagate its error and keep\nbuilding the module_entry (runtime, config, database) only when values are\npresent from the successful calls to get_module_runtime_config,\nparse_module_config, and build_final_db_for_module.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1222-1224`: **Inspection path still creates module directories for SQLite DSNs.**\n\n`render_effective_modules_config` calls `build_final_db_for_module`, which can invoke `create_dir_all` when resolving SQLite paths. For read-only CLI dumps, consider a dry-run resolution path or documenting the side effect.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`52-67`: **Consider making inspection flags mutually exclusive to avoid ambiguous precedence.**\n\nMultiple flags can be set simultaneously and the first match wins later in `main` (Line 146+). Using `clap::ArgGroup` or `conflicts_with` would make the CLI behavior explicit and user-friendly.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1198-1200`: **Stabilize dump output order for reproducibility.**\n\nIteration over `HashMap` keys is nondeterministic, so YAML/JSON outputs can shuffle across runs. Iterating over `list_module_names(app)` (sorted) would make dumps stable and easier to diff/test.  \n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 1267-1271\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-3677393735","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-3677393735"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T10:33:02Z","commit_id":"9c16f61d4db6494b01082cf02efec880f54f3323"},{"id":3685296194,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bqShC","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 6**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `232-232`: **Update import to use the new SDK structure.**\n> \n> The import path still references the old API structure. This should be updated to match the new SDK architecture documented elsewhere in this README (lines 264, 267).\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📦 Proposed fix to use the new SDK import</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -use nodes_registry::contract::client::NodesRegistryApi;\n> +use nodes_registry_sdk::NodesRegistryClient;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-17`: **Documentation references outdated trait name.**\n> \n> The module-level doc comment (line 1) and the example in the trait doc (line 15) still reference `TypesRegistryApi`, but the trait has been renamed to `TypesRegistryClient`. Update these for consistency.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested documentation fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -//! `TypesRegistryApi` trait definition.\n> +//! `TypesRegistryClient` trait definition.\n> ```\n> \n> And in the example on line 15:\n> ```diff\n> -/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n> +/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-27`: **Documentation references outdated `TypesRegistryApi` name.**\n> \n> The module-level docs and code examples still reference `TypesRegistryApi` (lines 4, 13, 16), but the actual re-export on line 37 is now `TypesRegistryClient`. This inconsistency could confuse SDK consumers.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested doc update</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  //! This crate provides the public API for the `types-registry` module:\n> -//! - `TypesRegistryApi` trait for inter-module communication\n> +//! - `TypesRegistryClient` trait for inter-module communication\n>  //! - `GtsEntity` model representing registered GTS entities\n>  //! - `ListQuery` for filtering entity listings\n>  //! - `TypesRegistryError` for error handling\n>  //!\n>  //! ## Usage\n>  //!\n>  //! Consumers obtain the client from `ClientHub`:\n>  //! ```ignore\n> -//! use types_registry_sdk::TypesRegistryApi;\n> +//! use types_registry_sdk::TypesRegistryClient;\n>  //!\n>  //! // Get the client from ClientHub\n> -//! let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n> +//! let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/domain/local_client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-16`: **Update doc comments to match `TypesRegistryClient` rename.**\n> \n> Docstrings at Line 1 and Line 14 still reference `TypesRegistryApi`, which no longer matches the trait name after the rename. Please update to avoid confusion.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -//! Local client implementing the `TypesRegistryApi` trait.\n> +//! Local client implementing the `TypesRegistryClient` trait.\n> @@\n> -/// This client implements the `TypesRegistryApi` trait and delegates\n> +/// This client implements the `TypesRegistryClient` trait and delegates\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `208-229`: **Comment/code inconsistency: only one context type is inserted.**\n> \n> The comment on line 224 says \"Insert both context types for compatibility during migration\" but only `SecurityContext` is inserted. If backward compatibility with the old `SecurityCtx` type is needed, consider adding it. Otherwise, update the comment to reflect the current behavior.\n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested comment fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>                      async move {\n> -                        // Insert both context types for compatibility during migration\n> +                        // Insert SecurityContext for the auth-disabled path\n>                          req.extensions_mut().insert(sec_context);\n>                          next.run(req).await\n>                      }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.github/workflows/scorecard.yml:\n- Around line 24-25: The conditional in the workflow line \"if:\ngithub.event.repository.default_branch == github.ref_name || github.event_name\n== 'pull_request'\" contains a dead branch because 'pull_request' is not included\nin the workflow triggers; either remove the dead clause \"|| github.event_name ==\n'pull_request'\" from that if expression or add \"pull_request\" to the workflow's\non: triggers so the check can ever be true—update the condition or the workflow\ntriggers accordingly (refer to the exact conditional string and the workflow's\non: section).\n- Around line 75-78: The workflow step named \"Upload to code-scanning\" currently\nuses the mutable action reference github/codeql-action/upload-sarif@v3; change\nthe uses entry to pin that action to its full commit SHA (e.g.,\ngithub/codeql-action/upload-sarif@<COMMIT_SHA>) so the step uses an immutable,\nverifiable version — update the uses value and keep the sarif_file:\nresults.sarif line unchanged.\n\nIn `@apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs`:\n- Around line 146-179: The read-only CLI flags (print_config, list_modules,\ndump_effective_modules_config_yaml, dump_effective_modules_config_json and\ncli.mock) are being handled after logging/OTEL/startup probe initialization,\nwhich causes side effects; move the early-exit handling so that after loading\nand applying override_modules_with_mock_db(&mut config) you check\ncli.print_config / cli.list_modules / cli.dump_* and return before calling\ninit_logging_unified or starting the startup probe/span (i.e., short-circuit\nimmediately after config load/mock override), and if necessary add a config-only\nload path that does not create home/log directories or initialize OTEL to\nguarantee no filesystem or network side effects.\n\nIn `@docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`:\n- Around line 553-554: The docs import was updated to use DirectoryClient but\nremaining examples and the table still refer to DirectoryApi; update all\noccurrences of DirectoryApi to DirectoryClient in the code snippets and\nexplanatory text (e.g., the example functions that use DirectoryApi and the\ntable row mentioning “DirectoryApi + gRPC client”), ensuring consistency with\nthe imported symbols (DirectoryClient, MyModuleApi, MyModuleGrpcClient,\nSERVICE_NAME); apply the same replacements in the other affected snippet\nmentioned (the later example block that still uses DirectoryApi).\n\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs`:\n- Around line 95-109: The current logic in build_final_db_for_module/dump flow\ncalls redact_dsn_password and on Err(e) logs a warning and uses continue, which\ndrops the entire module output despite the message saying only the DB config is\nskipped; change this so the module entry is still emitted but without the DB\nsection: when redact_dsn_password fails (in the match handling the Ok(Some((dsn,\npool))) branch), log the warning with module_name and dsn as now, then do not\ncontinue—instead set a flag or option (e.g., redacted_dsn = None or skip_db =\ntrue) and proceed to build the module entry but omit/skip adding the database\nfields (dsn/pool) to the dumped config; keep existing success path (Ok(redacted)\n=> include DB data) unchanged.\n\nIn `@modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/lib.rs`:\n- Around line 16-20: The module doc comment still mentions the old name\nTypesRegistryApi; update that doc comment to reference the new exported type\nname TypesRegistryClient (the public re-exports include TypesRegistryClient) so\nthe docs match the current API; locate the top-level doc comment above the pub\nuse block and replace any occurrence of \"TypesRegistryApi\" with\n\"TypesRegistryClient\".\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`111-112`: **Optional: reuse `ensure_tool` for consistency.**\n\nThis keeps the install logic centralized and consistent with other targets like `cargo-clippy` and `cargo-deny`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested change</summary>\n\n```diff\n dylint:\n-\t`@command` -v cargo-dylint >/dev/null || (echo \"Installing cargo-dylint...\" && cargo install cargo-dylint)\n-\t`@command` -v dylint-link >/dev/null || (echo \"Installing dylint-link...\" && cargo install dylint-link)\n+\t$(call ensure_tool,cargo-dylint)\n+\t$(call ensure_tool,dylint-link)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-3685296194","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/277#pullrequestreview-3685296194"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/277"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-21T04:26:27Z","commit_id":"41852522b60c7d9a3a0c14ba9930a0254dbd528c"},{"id":3685375268,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bql0k","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs`:\n- Around line 49-54: The doc comment for render_effective_modules_config is\ncontradictory: it claims the function \"never returns an error\" but also has a \"#\nErrors\" section about serialization and there is no serialization in the body;\nupdate the documentation to be accurate by removing the erroneous \"# Errors\"\nblock and adjusting the summary to state that the function always returns a\nValue (or that errors are logged and modules skipped) so the comment matches the\nactual signature and behavior of render_effective_modules_config.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`54-57`: **Same MSRV concern as above (let-chains).**\n\n---\n\n`151-154`: **Same MSRV concern as above (let-chains).**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`642-718`: **Prefer asserting on parsed YAML/JSON instead of raw substrings.**  \nYou already parse the output; asserting on structured values makes these tests less brittle if serializers change quoting/formatting. The JSON test can be fully structure-based; the YAML test can do the same once parsed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Example refactor (JSON test)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    // Should be valid JSON format\n-    assert!(\n-        stdout.contains(\"\\\"test_module\\\"\"),\n-        \"Should contain module name in JSON\"\n-    );\n-    assert!(\n-        stdout.contains(\"\\\"config\\\"\"),\n-        \"Should contain config section\"\n-    );\n-    assert!(stdout.contains(\"\\\"setting\\\"\"), \"Should contain config keys\");\n-    assert!(stdout.contains(\"\\\"value\\\"\"), \"Should contain config values\");\n-\n-    // Should contain database section\n-    assert!(\n-        stdout.contains(\"\\\"database\\\"\"),\n-        \"Should contain database section\"\n-    );\n-    assert!(stdout.contains(\"\\\"dsn\\\"\"), \"Should contain DSN field\");\n-\n-    // Password should be redacted\n-    assert!(\n-        stdout.contains(\"***REDACTED***\"),\n-        \"Password should be redacted in JSON\"\n-    );\n-    assert!(\n-        !stdout.contains(\"secret123\"),\n-        \"Password should not appear in JSON output\"\n-    );\n-\n-    // Verify it's parseable JSON\n-    let parsed: Result<serde_json::Value, _> = serde_json::from_str(&stdout);\n-    assert!(parsed.is_ok(), \"Output should be valid JSON\");\n-\n-    // Verify structure\n-    if let Ok(json) = parsed {\n-        assert!(json.is_object(), \"Root should be an object\");\n-        let obj = json.as_object().unwrap();\n-        assert!(\n-            obj.contains_key(\"test_module\"),\n-            \"Should have test_module key\"\n-        );\n-    }\n+    let json: serde_json::Value =\n+        serde_json::from_str(&stdout).expect(\"Output should be valid JSON\");\n+    let module = json.get(\"test_module\").expect(\"Should have test_module key\");\n+    let config = module\n+        .get(\"config\")\n+        .and_then(|v| v.as_object())\n+        .expect(\"Should have config section\");\n+    assert_eq!(config.get(\"setting\").and_then(|v| v.as_str()), Some(\"value\"));\n+    assert_eq!(config.get(\"number\").and_then(|v| v.as_i64()), Some(123));\n+    let database = module\n+        .get(\"database\")\n+        .and_then(|v| v.as_object())\n+        .expect(\"Should have database section\");\n+    let dsn = database\n+        .get(\"dsn\")\n+        .and_then(|v| v.as_str())\n+        .expect(\"Should have dsn field\");\n+    assert!(dsn.contains(\"***REDACTED***\"));\n+    assert!(!dsn.contains(\"secret123\"));\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 720-799\n\n---\n\n`844-867`: **Consider making the expected behavior explicit once CLI semantics are finalized.**  \nRight now the test accepts either success or failure, which can mask regressions if the intended behavior is fixed later.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/dump.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`90-165`: **Skip DB resolution when the module has no database config to reduce warning noise.**  \n`build_final_db_for_module` logs warnings for modules without DB config; you already have `parsed_config.database` to short-circuit and avoid duplicate parsing.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        match build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir, true) {\n-            Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) => {\n+        if parsed_config.database.is_some() {\n+            match build_final_db_for_module(app, module_name, &home_dir, true) {\n+                Ok(Some((dsn, pool))) => {\n                     // Redact password in DSN (warn and skip DB section if this fails, but keep module)\n                     let redacted_dsn = match redact_dsn_password(&dsn) {\n                         Ok(redacted) => redacted,\n                         Err(e) => {\n                             tracing::warn!(\n                                 module = %module_name,\n                                 error = %e,\n                                 \"Failed to redact DSN password, skipping database config for this module\"\n                             );\n                             // Continue processing this module, just skip the DB section\n                             // Add module entry even without DB config\n                             if !module_entry.is_empty() {\n                                 modules_config.insert(module_name.clone(), json!(module_entry));\n                             }\n                             continue;\n                         }\n                     };\n@@\n-            Ok(None) => {\n-                // Module has no database config, skip\n-            }\n-            Err(e) => {\n-                tracing::warn!(\n-                    module = %module_name,\n-                    error = %e,\n-                    \"Failed to build database config, skipping\"\n-                );\n-            }\n-        }\n+                }\n+                Ok(None) => {\n+                    // Module has no database config, skip\n+                }\n+                Err(e) => {\n+                    tracing::warn!(\n+                        module = %module_name,\n+                        error = %e,\n+                        \"Failed to build database config, skipping\"\n+                    );\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is