a Windows OoP path adjusted, and wait_for_health enhanced with attempt logging.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Port Migration (8087 → 8086)** <br> `testing/docker/docker-compose.yml`, `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile`, `testing/e2e/conftest.py`, `testing/e2e/modules/file_parser/generate_file_parser_golden.py` | Host/container port mappings and exposed port changed to 8086; default E2E/test base URLs updated from 8087→8086. |\n| **Build/Feature Flags & CLI** <br> `Makefile`, `scripts/ci.py` | Adds public `E2E_ARGS` Makefile variable (default `--features users-info-example`) and wires it into `e2e-docker`; `scripts/ci.py` exposes `--features` on e2e CLI, forwards it as `CARGO_FEATURES` build-arg, and adds `--force-recreate` to docker-compose up. |\n| **CI Health & Process Handling** <br> `scripts/ci.py` | `wait_for_health` now tracks attempt counts, logs warnings every 10 attempts, handles additional exceptions, and reports attempts on success/failure; server process handling adjusted in `cmd_e2e`. |\n| **Docker Build & Runtime Image** <br> `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` | Builder base updated to `rust:1.92-bookworm`; added `libprotobuf-dev` and `proto/` copy; build step now conditionally uses `ARG CARGO_FEATURES` to run cargo with provided features; exposed port and runtime CMD updated to run quickstart config. |\n| **Configuration Updates** <br> `config/quickstart-windows.yaml`, `config/quickstart.yaml` | Windows OoP module config path switched to relative `./config/oop-example.yaml`; tenant YAML restructured (root parent_id null, division/department IDs and parents changed, Frontend marked SOFT_DELETED and Backend added). |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Dev as Developer / Makefile\n  participant CI as CI Script (`scripts/ci.py`)\n  participant Builder as Docker Build (hyperspot.Dockerfile)\n  participant Compose as docker-compose\n  participant Server as Hyperspot Server\n  participant Tests as E2E Tests\n\n  Dev->>CI: invoke e2e-docker with $(E2E_ARGS)\n  CI->>Builder: docker build --build-arg CARGO_FEATURES=... (if provided)\n  Builder-->>CI: built image (with/without features)\n  CI->>Compose: docker-compose up --force-recreate (image)\n  Compose->>Server: start container (bind 0.0.0.0:8086)\n  Tests->>Server: run E2E tests against http://localhost:8086\n  CI->>CI: wait_for_health polls server (logs attempts)\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~25 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through ports and build-time cheer,  \n> Flags tucked neatly, features near,  \n> Proto crumbs and paths made right,  \n> Eight‑oh‑six hums through day and night,  \n> Tests run swiftly—carrots in sight! 🥕\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status     | Explanation                                                                           | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :--------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ⚠️ Warning | Docstring coverage is 42.86% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (2 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name    | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                  |\n| :---------------: | :------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------