-148,21 +148,26 @@ def cmd_quickstart(_args):\n     )\n \n \n-def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=30):\n+def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=120):\n     url = f\"{base_url.rstrip('/')}/healthz\"\n     step(f\"Waiting for API to be ready at {url}\")\n     start = time.time()\n+    attempt = 0\n     while True:\n         try:\n+            attempt += 1\n             with urlopen(url, timeout=1) as resp:\n                 if 200 <= resp.status < 300:\n-                    print(\"API is ready\")\n+                    print(f\"API is ready (after {attempt} attempts)\")\n                     return\n-        except (URLError, HTTPError):\n-            pass\n+        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError) as e:\n+            # Server may be starting up or restarting\n+            if attempt % 10 == 0:  # Log every 10 attempts\n+                print(f\"Still waiting... (attempt {attempt}, error: {type(e).__name__})\")\n ","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"30cfd54ba729b0a446665d24fea6e1d2c6faf224","original_commit_id":"7cd2f9e5a7aff83693fba545da9c78693587140a","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Restrict health-check URL schemes to http/https.**\n\n`base_url` is user-controlled (env/CLI), and `urlopen` will accept `file:` or custom schemes. It’s safer to enforce http/https before opening the URL.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒 Proposed fix (scheme validation)</summary>\n\n```diff\n+from urllib.parse import urlparse\n+\n def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=120):\n-    url = f\"{base_url.rstrip('/')}/healthz\"\n+    parsed = urlparse(base_url)\n+    if parsed.scheme not in (\"http\", \"https\"):\n+        print(f\"ERROR: Unsupported URL scheme for health check: {parsed.scheme}\")\n+        sys.exit(1)\n+    url = f\"{base_url.rstrip('/')}/healthz\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.14.13)</summary>\n\n159-159: Audit URL open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of `file:` or custom schemes is often unexpected.\n\n(S310)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 151 - 167, The wait_for_health function currently\ncalls urlopen on a user-controlled base_url which may use unsafe schemes; before\nbuilding the health URL and calling urlopen, parse base_url (use\nurllib.parse.urlparse) and validate that parsed.scheme is \"http\" or \"https\",\nraising a ValueError or printing an error and exiting if not allowed; update\nreferences in wait_for_health to use the validated scheme and ensure the error\nhandling/logging mentions invalid scheme and the offending base_url.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T09:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T09:34:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2703964864","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2703964864"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2703964864"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2703964864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":151,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":167,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":24,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2703964881","pull_request_review_id":3677149816,"id":2703964881,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hKzrR","diff_hunk":"@@ -148,21 +148,26 @@ def cmd_quickstart(_args):\n     )\n \n \n-def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=30):\n+def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=120):\n     url = f\"{base_url.rstrip('/')}/healthz\"\n     step(f\"Waiting for API to be ready at {url}\")\n     start = time.time()\n+    attempt = 0\n     while True:\n         try:\n+            attempt += 1\n             with urlopen(url, timeout=1) as resp:\n                 if 200 <= resp.status < 300:\n-                    print(\"API is ready\")\n+                    print(f\"API is ready (after {attempt} attempts)\")\n                     return\n-        except (URLError, HTTPError):\n-            pass\n+        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError) as e:\n+            # Server may be starting up or restarting\n+            if attempt % 10 == 0:  # Log every 10 attempts\n+                print(f\"Still waiting... (attempt {attempt}, error: {type(e).__name__})\")\n \n         if time.time() - start > timeout_secs:\n-            print(\"ERROR: The API readiness check timed out\")\n+            print(f\"ERROR: The API readiness check timed out after {attempt} attempts\")\n+            print(\"Hint: Check server logs with: docker compose -f testing/docker/docker-compose.yml logs file_parser_api\")\n             sys.exit(1)","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"7a6e54e30b18eada871727b91e062e70fcaf1edb","original_commit_id":"7cd2f9e5a7aff83693fba545da9c78693587140a","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Make the timeout hint conditional to avoid noisy local-mode output.**\n\n`wait_for_health` is used as a local probe; on timeout it prints a docker-specific hint even when not in docker mode. Consider making the hint optional.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Suggested tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=120):\n+def wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=120, timeout_hint=None):\n@@\n-        if time.time() - start > timeout_secs:\n-            print(f\"ERROR: The API readiness check timed out after {attempt} attempts\")\n-            print(\"Hint: Check server logs with: docker compose -f testing/docker/docker-compose.yml logs file_parser_api\")\n+        if time.time() - start > timeout_secs:\n+            print(f\"ERROR: The API readiness check timed out after {attempt} attempts\")\n+            if timeout_hint:\n+                print(timeout_hint)\n             sys.exit(1)\n```\n\nThen pass the hint only in docker mode.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py` around lines 168 - 171, The timeout branch in wait_for_health\nprints a Docker-specific hint unconditionally; change wait_for_health (in\nscripts/ci.py) to accept an optional parameter (e.g., show_docker_hint or\nhint_msg) and only print the docker compose hint when that flag is true (or\nhint_msg is provided), then update callers that run in Docker mode to pass true\n(or the hint string) while local-mode callers leave it false/omit it so the hint\nis not printed in non-Docker runs.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T09:34:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T09:34:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2703964881","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2703964881"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2703964881"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2703964881/reactions","tot