Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Port exposure likely mismatches runtime bind address.**  \nThe Dockerfile now exposes 8086, but `config/quickstart.yaml` still binds the API gateway to `127.0.0.1:8087` (used by the CMD). That mismatch can make E2E tests hit the wrong port. Align the quickstart `bind_addr` (or runtime flags) with 8086.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Minimal alignment fix (if 8086 is the new default)</summary>\n\n```diff\n# config/quickstart.yaml\n-      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8087\"\n+      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8086\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` around lines 46 - 47, The Dockerfile\nexposes port 8086 but the runtime config still binds the API gateway to\n127.0.0.1:8087, causing a mismatch; update the bind address in\nconfig/quickstart.yaml (the bind_addr setting) or the Dockerfile/CMD flags so\nthe runtime listens on the exposed port (e.g., change bind_addr to 0.0.0.0:8086\nor to 127.0.0.1:8086 if you only need localhost), and ensure the CMD that\ncurrently references 127.0.0.1:8087 is updated to the chosen host:port so E2E\ntests hit the correct port.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @ziqwerty\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T11:36:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T08:33:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2704396585","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704396585"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2704396585"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704396585/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":46,"original_start_line":46,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":47,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707298604","pull_request_review_id":3680964645,"id":2707298604,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hXhks","diff_hunk":"@@ -34,8 +43,8 @@ COPY --from=builder /build/target/debug/hyperspot-server /app/hyperspot-server\n # Copy config used in CMD\n COPY --from=builder /build/config /app/config\n \n-# Expose the HTTP port (default 8080 for E2E)\n-EXPOSE 8087\n+# Expose the HTTP port for E2E tests\n+EXPOSE 8086","path":"testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile","commit_id":"7a6e54e30b18eada871727b91e062e70fcaf1edb","original_commit_id":"7a6e54e30b18eada871727b91e062e70fcaf1edb","user":{"login":"ziqwerty","id":35517593,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1NTE3NTkz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35517593?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty","html_url":"https://github.com/ziqwerty","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ziqwerty/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It is intentional to run e2e tests on port 8086, to avoid conflict with main service port 8087 in the event that developers might want to run both concurrently.\r\nref: https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/254#discussion_r2697439012","created_at":"2026-01-20T08:32:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T08:32:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2707298604","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707298604"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2707298604"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707298604/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":46,"original_start_line":46,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":47,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704396585,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707302557","pull_request_review_id":3680969188,"id":2707302557,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hXiid","diff_hunk":"@@ -34,8 +43,8 @@ COPY --from=builder /build/target/debug/hyperspot-server /app/hyperspot-server\n # Copy config used in CMD\n COPY --from=builder /build/config /app/config\n \n-# Expose the HTTP port (default 8080 for E2E)\n-EXPOSE 8087\n+# Expose the HTTP port for E2E tests\n+EXPOSE 8086","path":"testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile","commit_id":"7a6e54e30b18eada871727b91e062e70fcaf1edb","original_commit_id":"7a6e54e30b18eada871727b91e062e70fcaf1edb","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check the bind_addr in config/quickstart.yaml\necho \"=== Checking bind_addr in config/quickstart.yaml ===\"\ngrep -n \"bind_addr\" config/quickstart.yaml || echo \"No bind_addr found in quickstart.yaml\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking docker-compose environment variable override ===\"\ngrep -A2 -B2 \"APP__MODULES__api_gateway__CONFIG__BIND_ADDR\" testing/docker/docker-compose.yml\n```\n\nLength of output: 425\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@ziqwerty` Thank you for the clarification! I can confirm that docker-compose correctly handles this through the environment variable override:\n\n```yaml\nAPP__MODULES__api_gateway__CONFIG__BIND_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8086\n```\n\nThis overrides the `bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8087\"` from `config/quickstart.yaml` when running E2E tests via docker-compose, so the setup correctly uses port 8086 for E2E while leaving 8087 available for the main development service.\n\nThe intentional port separation makes sense for concurrent development workflows. My apologies for the noise!\n\n\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: ziqwerty\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 276\nFile: testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile:46-47\nTimestamp: 2026-01-20T08:33:08.629Z\nLearning: In the hyperspot project, E2E tests intentionally run on port 8086 to avoid conflicts with the main service running on port 8087, allowing developers to run both concurrently. The docker-compose configuration overrides the quickstart.yaml bind_addr via the APP__MODULES__api_gateway__CONFIG__BIND_ADDR environment variable.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-20T08:33:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T08:33:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2707302557","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707302557"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#discussion_r2707302557"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2707302557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":46,"original_start_line":46,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":47,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704396585,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3677149816,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bLNp4","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 168-171: The timeout branch in wait_for_health prints a\nDocker-specific hint unconditionally; change wait_for_health (in scripts/ci.py)\nto accept an optional parameter (e.g., show_docker_hint or hint_msg) and only\nprint the docker compose hint when that flag is true (or hint_msg is provided),\nthen update callers that run in Docker mode to pass true (or the hint string)\nwhile local-mode callers leave it false/omit it so the hint is not printed in\nnon-Docker runs.\n- Around line 151-167: The wait_for_health function currently calls urlopen on a\nuser-controlled base_url which may use unsafe schemes; before building the\nhealth URL and calling urlopen, parse base_url (use urllib.parse.urlparse) and\nvalidate that parsed.scheme is \"http\" or \"https\", raising a ValueError or\nprinting an error and exiting if not allowed; update references in\nwait_for_health to use the validated scheme and ensure the error\nhandling/logging mentions invalid scheme and the offending base_url.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`545-549`: **Consider aligning docker default `--features` with local mode.**\n\nLocal mode starts with `users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example`, but docker defaults to only `users-info-example`. If the standard E2E suite expects tenant-resolver, docker runs may miss it unless `--features` is provided.  \n \n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Possible default alignment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        default=\"users-info-example\",\n+        default=\"users-info-example,tenant-resolver-example\",\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#pullrequestreview-3677149816","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/276#pullrequestreview-3677149816"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/276"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T09:34:42Z","commit_id":"7cd2f9e5a7aff83693fba545da9c78693587140a"},{"id":3677657425,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bNJlR","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/