mary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n> \n> * `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n> \n> </details>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📒 Files selected for processing (9)</summary>\n> \n> * `Cargo.toml`\n> * `Makefile`\n> * `apps/gts-docs-validator/Cargo.toml`\n> * `apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md`\n> * `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs`\n> * `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs`\n> * `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs`\n> * `dylint_lints/README.md`\n> * `scripts/ci.py`\n> \n> </details>\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: rate limited by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_start -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ## Other AI code review bot(s) detected\n> \n> CodeRabbit has detected other AI code review bot(s) in this pull request and will avoid duplicating their findings in the review comments. This may lead to a less comprehensive review.\n\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_end -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a new Rust CLI crate `gts-docs-validator` (scanner + validator) to the workspace, integrates it into Makefile and CI (`gts-docs*` make targets and a `gts-docs` CI subcommand), updates documentation (dylint_lints README) to document GTS validators, and adjusts two types-registry spec expectations for derived-type IDs.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Build system & CI** <br> `Makefile`, `scripts/ci.py`, `Cargo.toml` | New Make targets: `gts-docs`, `gts-docs-test`, `gts-docs-vendor`, `gts-docs-release`, `gts-docs-vendor-release`; `.PHONY` extended; `check` invokes `gts-docs`; `scripts/ci.py` adds `cmd_gts_docs`, a `gts-docs` subcommand, and calls it from `cmd_check`; workspace adds `apps/gts-docs-validator` and workspace deps (`glob`, `colored`). |\n| **GTS Docs Validator crate (metadata & entry)** <br> `apps/gts-docs-validator/Cargo.toml`, `apps/gts-docs-validator/README.md`, `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` | New binary crate `gts-docs-validator` with Clap CLI (`paths`, `--vendor`, `--exclude`, `--json`, `--verbose`); orchestrates discovery, scanning, validation, JSON/human output; README and usage docs added. |\n| **Scanner implementation & tests** <br> `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs` | File discovery for `.md/.json/.yaml/.yml` with exclude/skip patterns, false-positive heuristics, UTF‑8-safe context extraction; exposes `find_files` and `scan_file`; includes unit tests. |\n| **Validation core & public types** <br> `apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs` | Validation core with public types `GtsError`, `ValidationResult`, functions `validate_gts_segment` and `validate_gts_id`, example/vendor/wildcard heuristics, and unit tests. |\n| **Documentation updates** <br> `dylint_lints/README.md` | Expanded GTS validators section (DE0901–DE0903), added quick-start commands referencing new Make targets and the docs validator. |\n| **Spec adjustments** <br> `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/specs/types-registry/spec.md`, `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/.../spec.md` | Updated expected derived-type suffix in two scenarios from `orders.v1` to `orders.order.v1` in chained GTS IDs; only expectation strings changed. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant CLI as CLI / Make / CI\n    participant FS as File System\n    participant Scanner as Scanner\n    participant Validator as Validator\n    participant Output as Output Handler\n\n    CLI->>Scanner: find_files(paths, exclude)\n    Scanner->>FS: traverse dirs, list & read matching files\n    loop per file\n        Scanner->>FS: read file contents\n        Scanner->>Validator: validate_gts_id(token, vendor, allow_wildcards)\n        Validator-->>Scanner: errors or ok\n        Scanner->>Scanner: collect errors with context\n    end\n    Scanner->>Output: produce ValidationResult\n    alt JSON output\n        Output->>CLI: serialize JSON, return exit code\n    else Human-readable\n        Output->>CLI: colorize, group errors, print, return exit code\n    end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~55 minutes\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I nibble docs from page to page,  \n> I chase each GTS across the page,  \n> I flag the odd, applaud the right,  \n> I hop away at fall of night,  \n> Leaving a carrot-coded light.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                   |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'feat: Add GTS documentation validator and associated tests' directly and clearly describes the main changes: introduction of a new GTS documentation validator tool and its tests. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 95.58% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                           |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3760963468/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3765211665","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#issuecomment-3765211665","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/266","id":3765211665,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7gbJIR","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-18T11:53:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:53:28Z","body":"@yoskini , I'd suggest to add optional parameter to validate gts vendor as well, then we can specify it in our Makefile, like\r\n\r\ngts-rust --vendor x validate-id ./src\r\n\r\nThe problem is that in many places we have code like\r\ngts.hx.a.b.c.v1~...  # where 'hx' is hypernetix\r\n\r\nwhile we actually want it to be:\r\ngts.x.a.b.c.v1~... # where 'x' is a placeholder, meaning any for now. Later it could become just 'cf' - Cyber Fabric\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3765211665/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3768236902","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#issuecomment-3768236902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/266","id":3768236902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7gmrtm","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/me