``\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 157\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`clap 4.5 rust derive short flag V version conflict automatic reserved flags`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: clap v4.5 auto-generates a version flag (-V / --version). If you give a derived Arg the same short ('V') you get a conflict. Disable the auto-version flag and add your own.\n\nHow to fix (derive):\n- Disable the auto version flag on the parser: #[command(disable_version_flag = true)]. [1][2]\n- Then add your field with the short you want (or add a custom version arg using ArgAction::Version). Example pattern shown on StackOverflow. [3]\n\nReferences\n- Command::disable_version_flag documentation. [1]\n- clap derive docs (#[command(...)] and version behavior). [2]\n- Example showing disable_version_flag + custom flag with derive. [3]\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Remove short flag `-V` due to conflict with clap's auto-generated version flag.**\n\nWith `#[command(author, version, ...)]` enabled, clap 4.5 automatically reserves `-V/--version`. Using `-V` as the short flag for vendor creates a conflict. Either remove the short flag or disable clap's auto-generated version flag and customize it.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix (remove short flag)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    #[arg(long)]\n     vendor: Option<String>,\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    /// Expected vendor for all GTS IDs (validates vendor matches)\n    /// Example: --vendor x ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\"\n    ///\n    /// Note: Example vendors are always tolerated: acme, globex, example, demo, test, sample, tutorial\n    #[arg(long)]\n    vendor: Option<String>,\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 54 - 60, The vendor field's\nshort flag conflicts with clap's auto-generated -V/--version; remove the short\nflag on the vendor argument (change #[arg(long, short = 'V')] for the vendor\nfield to just #[arg(long)] or #[arg(long, value_name = \"...\")] so the vendor\nOption<String> (symbol vendor) no longer uses -V and avoids the clash with\nclap's version flag; update any related docs/tests that referenced -V\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @yoskini\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:09:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:41:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717555","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717555"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717555"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717555/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":54,"original_start_line":54,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":60,"original_line":60,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":60,"position":60,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717566","pull_request_review_id":3678032430,"id":2704717566,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hNrb-","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@\n+//! GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+//!\n+//! This tool validates GTS (Global Type System) identifiers in documentation files\n+//! (.md, .json, .yaml), complementing the Rust-based DE0901 lint that validates\n+//! GTS identifiers in source code.\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! ```bash\n+//! # Validate docs with vendor filter\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x docs modules libs examples\n+//!\n+//! # With exclusions\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\" .\n+//!\n+//! # JSON output\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --json docs\n+//! ```\n+\n+// CLI tools are expected to print to stdout/stderr\n+#![allow(\n+    clippy::print_stdout,\n+    clippy::print_stderr,\n+    clippy::exit,\n+    clippy::expect_used\n+)]\n+\n+mod scanner;\n+mod validator;\n+\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+use std::process::ExitCode;\n+\n+use clap::Parser;\n+use colored::Colorize;\n+\n+use crate::scanner::{find_files, scan_file};\n+use crate::validator::ValidationResult;\n+\n+/// GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+///\n+/// Validates GTS identifiers in .md, .json, and .yaml files.\n+/// Ensures all GTS IDs follow the correct format and optionally validates\n+/// that they use a specific vendor.\n+#[derive(Parser, Debug)]\n+#[command(name = \"gts-docs-validator\")]\n+#[command(author, version, about, long_about = None)]\n+struct Cli {\n+    /// Paths to scan (files or directories)\n+    /// Defaults to: docs, modules, libs, examples\n+    #[arg(value_name = \"PATH\")]\n+    paths: Vec<PathBuf>,\n+\n+    /// Expected vendor for all GTS IDs (validates vendor matches)\n+    /// Example: --vendor x ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\"\n+    ///\n+    /// Note: Example vendors are always tolerated: acme, globex, example, demo, test, sample, tutorial\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    vendor: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Exclude patterns (can be specified multiple times)\n+    /// Supports glob patterns. Example: --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\"\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'e', action = clap::ArgAction::Append)]\n+    exclude: Vec<String>,\n+\n+    /// Output results as JSON\n+    #[arg(long)]\n+    json: bool,\n+\n+    /// Show verbose output including file scanning progress\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'v')]\n+    verbose: bool,\n+}\n+\n+/// Default directories to scan if none specified\n+const DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"docs\", \"modules\", \"libs\", \"examples\"];\n+\n+fn main() -> ExitCode {\n+    let cli = Cli::parse();\n+\n+    // Determine paths to scan\n+    let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n+        DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(PathBuf::from)\n+            .filter(|p| p.exists())\n+            .collect()\n+    } else {\n+        cli.paths.clone()\n+    };","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fail fast when no paths exist to scan.**  \nCurrently this can exit success after scanning zero files.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n         DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n             .iter()\n             .map(PathBuf::from)\n             .filter(|p| p.exists())\n             .collect()\n     } else {\n         cli.paths.clone()\n     };\n+\n+    if paths.is_empty() {\n+        eprintln!(\"No existing paths to scan. Provide paths explicitly.\");\n+        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n        DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n            .iter()\n            .map(PathBuf::from)\n            .filter(|p| p.exists())\n            .collect()\n    } else {\n        cli.paths.clone()\n    };\n\n    if paths.is_empty() {\n        eprintln!(\"No existing paths to scan. Provide paths explicitly.\");\n        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n    }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs` around lines 82 - 90, After computing\nthe paths vector (the variable paths created from cli.paths or\nDEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS), add a fail-fast check: if paths.is_empty() then log or print\na clear error mentioning no paths were found (reference DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS and\ncli.paths) and terminate with a non-zero exit (so main returns an error or calls\nprocess::exit(1)). Place this check immediately after the paths assignment (in\nmain) so the program does not continue and report success when there is nothing\nto scan.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit db935b7","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:09:54Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717566","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717566"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717566"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717566/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":82,"original_start_line":82,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":97,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":90,"position":97,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717574","pull_request_review_id":3678032430,"id":2704717574,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hNrcG","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! File scanning functionality for GTS documentation validation\n+\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use glob::Pattern;\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use walkdir::WalkDir;\n+\n+use crate::validator::{is_bad_example_context, is_wildcard_context, validate_gts_id, GtsError};\n+\n+/// File patterns to scan\n+const FILE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\"*.md\", \"*.json\", \"*.yaml\", \"*.yml\"];\n+\n+/// Directories to skip\n+const SKIP_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"target\", \"node_modules\", \".git\", \"vendor\", \".gts-spec\"];\n+\n+/// Files to skip (relative paths)\n+const SKIP_FILES: &[&str] = &[\"docs/api/api.json\"];\n+\n+/// Patterns that look like GTS but aren't (false positives)\n+const FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    r\"^gts\\.rs$\",     // Rust file named gts.rs\n+    r\"^gts\\.[a-z]+$\", // Single component like gts.rs, gts.py\n+];\n+\n+/// Pattern to find GTS-looking strings\n+/// Must have at least 2 dots after gts. to catch potential GTS IDs\n+/// Include hyphen so we can catch and report invalid hyphens\n+fn gts_pattern() -> Regex {\n+    Regex::new(r\"gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\").expect(\"Invalid regex pattern\")\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a path matches any of the exclude patterns\n+fn matches_exclude(path: &Path, exclude_patterns: &[Pattern]) -> bool {\n+    let path_str = path.to_string_lossy();\n+    for pattern in exclude_patterns {\n+        if pattern.matches(&path_str) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+        // Also try matching just the file/dir name\n+        if let Some(name) = path.file_name() {\n+            if pattern.matches(&name.to_string_lossy()) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if path contains any skip directories\n+fn in_skip_dir(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    for component in path.components() {\n+        if let std::path::Component::Normal(name) = component {\n+            if SKIP_DIRS\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|skip| name.to_string_lossy() == *skip)\n+            {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if file matches any of the file patterns\n+fn matches_file_pattern(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    if let Some(ext) = path.extension() {\n+        let ext_str = ext.to_string_lossy().to_lowercase();\n+        let with_dot = format!(\"*.{ext_str}\");\n+        FILE_PATTERNS.iter().any(|p| *p == with_dot)\n+    } else {\n+        false\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Find all files to scan in the given paths\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn find_files(paths: &[PathBuf], exclude: &[String], verbose: bool) -> Vec<PathBuf> {\n+    let mut files = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Parse exclude patterns\n+    let exclude_patterns: Vec<Pattern> = exclude\n+        .iter()\n+        .filter_map(|p| match Pattern::new(p) {\n+            Ok(pat) => Some(pat),\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                if verbose {\n+                    eprintln!(\"Warning: Invalid exclude pattern '{p}': {e}\");\n+                }\n+                None\n+            }\n+        })\n+        .collect();\n+\n+    for path in paths {\n+        if path.is_file() {\n+            if matches_file_pattern(path) && !matches_exclude(path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                files.push(path.clone());\n+            }\n+        } else if path.is_dir() {\n+            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n+                .follow_links(true)\n+                .into_iter()\n+                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n+            {\n+                let file_path = entry.path();\n+\n+                // Skip directories in skip list\n+                if in_skip_dir(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Only process files\n+                if !file_path.is_file() {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check file pattern\n+                if !matches_file_pattern(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check exclude patterns\n+                if matches_exclude(file_path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Excluding: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check against skip files\n+                let rel_path = file_path.to_string_lossy();\n+                if SKIP_FILES.iter().any(|skip| rel_path.contains(skip)) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Skipping: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                files.push(file_path.to_path_buf());\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    files.sort();\n+    files.dedup();\n+    files\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a matched string is a false positive\n+fn is_false_positive(gts_id: &str) -> bool {\n+    for pattern in FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS {\n+        if let Ok(re) = Regex::new(pattern) {\n+            if re.is_match(gts_id) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Scan a single file for GTS identifiers and validate them\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn scan_file(path: &Path, expected_vendor: Option<&str>, verbose: bool) -> Vec<GtsError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            if verbose {\n+                eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n+            }\n+            return errors;\n+        }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Surface unreadable files as validation failures.**  \nSilent skipping means CI can pass with zero validation on unreadable files.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n         Ok(c) => c,\n         Err(e) => {\n             if verbose {\n                 eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n             }\n-            return errors;\n+            return vec![GtsError {\n+                file: path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                gts_id: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+                context: String::new(),\n+            }];\n         }\n     };\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n        Ok(c) => c,\n        Err(e) => {\n            if verbose {\n                eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n            }\n            return vec![GtsError {\n                file: path.to_path_buf(),\n                line: 0,\n                column: 0,\n                gts_id: String::new(),\n                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n                context: String::new(),\n            }];\n        }\n    };\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs` around lines 168 - 175, The current\nfs::read_to_string(path) error branch silently returns the existing errors vec,\nskipping unreadable files; change it to record the read failure as a validation\nerror instead of quietly exiting. In the match arm that handles Err(e) for\nfs::read_to_string, push a descriptive validation failure into the errors\ncollection (include path.display() and e) so unreadable files count as failures;\npreserve the verbose eprintln when verbose is true but do not return\nearly—return errors only after recording the failure. Target the match around\nfs::read_to_string, the variables path, e, verbose, and the errors collection to\nimplement this change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @yoskini\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:09:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717574","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717574"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2704717574"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717574/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":165,"original_start_line":168,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":179,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":175,"position":179,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704717581","pull_request_review_id":3678032430,"id":2704717581,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hNrcN","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! File scanning functionality for GTS documentation validation\n+\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use glob::Pattern;\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use walkdir::WalkDir;\n+\n+use crate::validator::{is_bad_example_context, is_wildcard_context, validate_gts_id, GtsError};\n+\n+/// File patterns to scan\n+const FILE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\"*.md\", \"*.json\", \"*.yaml\", \"*.yml\"];\n+\n+/// Directories to skip\n+const SKIP_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"target\", \"node_modules\", \".git\", \"vendor\", \".gts-spec\"];\n+\n+/// Files to skip (relative paths)\n+const SKIP_FILES: &[&str] = &[\"docs/api/api.json\"];\n+\n+/// Patterns that look like GTS but aren't (false positives)\n+const FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    r\"^gts\\.rs$\",     // Rust file named gts.rs\n+    r\"^gts\\.[a-z]+$\", // Single component like gts.rs, gts.py\n+];\n+\n+/// Pattern to find GTS-looking strings\n+/// Must have at least 2 dots after gts. to catch potential GTS IDs\n+/// Include hyphen so we can catch and report invalid hyphens\n+fn gts_pattern() -> Regex {\n+    Regex::new(r\"gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\").expect(\"Invalid regex pattern\")\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a path matches any of the exclude patterns\n+fn matches_exclude(path: &Path, exclude_patterns: &[Pattern]) -> bool {\n+    let path_str = path.to_string_lossy();\n+    for pattern in exclude_patterns {\n+        if pattern.matches(&path_str) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+        // Also try matching just the file/dir name\n+        if let Some(name) = path.file_name() {\n+            if pattern.matches(&name.to_string_lossy()) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if path contains any skip directories\n+fn in_skip_dir(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    for component in path.components() {\n+        if let std::path::Component::Normal(name) = component {\n+            if SKIP_DIRS\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|skip| name.to_string_lossy() == *skip)\n+            {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if file matches any of the file patterns\n+fn matches_file_pattern(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    if let Some(ext) = path.extension() {\n+        let ext_str = ext.to_string_lossy().to_lowercase();\n+        let with_dot = format!(\"*.{ext_str}\");\n+        FILE_PATTERNS.iter().any(|p| *p == with_dot)\n+    } else {\n+        false\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Find all files to scan in the given paths\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn find_files(paths: &[PathBuf], exclude: &[String], verbose: bool) -> Vec<PathBuf> {\n+    let mut files = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Parse exclude patterns\n+    let exclude_patterns: Vec<Pattern> = exclude\n+        .iter()\n+        .filter_map(|p| match Pattern::new(p) {\n+            Ok(pat) => Some(pat),\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                if verbose {\n+                    eprintln!(\"Warning: Invalid exclude pattern '{p}': {e}\");\n+                }\n+                None\n+            }\n+        })\n+        .collect();\n+\n+    for path in paths {\n+        if path.is_file() {\n+            if matches_file_pattern(path) && !matches_exclude(path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                files.push(path.clone());\n+            }\n+        } else if path.is_dir() {\n+            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n+                .follow_links(true)\n+                .into_iter()\n+                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n+            {\n+                let file_path = entry.path();\n+\n+                // Skip directories in skip list\n+                if in_skip_dir(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Only process files\n+                if !file_path.is_file() {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check file pattern\n+                if !matches_file_pattern(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check exclude patterns\n+                if matches_exclude(file_path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Excluding: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check against skip files\n+                let rel_path = file_path.to_string_lossy();\n+                if SKIP_FILES.iter().any(|skip| rel_path.contains(skip)) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Skipping: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                files.push(file_path.to_path_buf());\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    files.sort();\n+    files.dedup();\n+    files\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a matched string is a false positive\n+fn is_false_positive(gts_id: &str) -> bool {\n+    for pattern in FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS {\n+        if let Ok(re) = Regex::new(pattern) {\n+            if re.is_match(gts_id) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Scan a single file for GTS identifiers and validate them\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn scan_file(path: &Path, expected_vendor: Option<&str>, verbose: bool) -> Vec<GtsError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            if verbose {\n+                eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n+            }\n+            return errors;\n+        }\n+    };\n+\n+    let lines: Vec<&str> = content.lines().collect();\n+    let gts_re = gts_pattern();\n+\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+        let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n+\n+        for mat in gts_re.find_iter(line) {\n+            let gts_id = mat.as_str();\n+            let col = mat.start() + 1;\n+\n+            // Skip false positives\n+            if is_false_positive(gts_id) {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            // Skip if in bad example context\n+            let prev_lines: Vec<&str> = lines[..line_idx].iter().copied().collect();\n+            if is_bad_example_context(line, &prev_lines) {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            // Check if wildcards are allowed\n+            let allow_wildcards = is_wildcard_context(line, mat.start());\n+\n+            // Validate the identifier\n+            let validation_errors = validate_gts_id(gts_id, expected_vendor, allow_wildcards);\n+\n+            for err in validation_errors {\n+                // Extract context\n+                let context_start = mat.start().saturating_sub(20);\n+                let context_end = (mat.end() + 20).min(line.len());\n+                let mut context = line[context_start..context_end].to_string();\n+                if context_start > 0 {\n+                    context = format!(\"...{context}\");\n+                }\n+                if context_end < line.len() {\n+                    context = format!(\"{context}...\");\n+                }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs","commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/