tch: expected '{}', found '{}' in '{}'\",\n                                 expected, vendor, original\n                             ));\n                         }\n                     }\n                 }\n             }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n            // Even if gts library failed, still check vendor\n            if let Some(expected) = expected_vendor {\n                if let Some(first_seg) = non_empty_segments.first() {\n                    let parts: Vec<&str> = first_seg.split('.').collect();\n                    if let Some(vendor) = parts.first() {\n                        if *vendor != expected && !is_example_vendor(vendor) {\n                            errors.push(format!(\n                                \"Vendor mismatch: expected '{}', found '{}' in '{}'\",\n                                expected, vendor, original\n                            ));\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs` around lines 292 - 306, The\nvendor-check in the error path should mirror the success path by skipping\nexample vendors: when inspecting the first segment's vendor (using\nnon_empty_segments, parts, vendor) ensure you call is_example_vendor(vendor) and\ndo not push a \"Vendor mismatch\" error if it returns true; otherwise proceed with\nthe existing mismatch check against expected_vendor. Update the block that\ncurrently compares *vendor != expected to first guard with\nis_example_vendor(vendor) to prevent fa