ndor:\n+\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--vendor x \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Run tests for GTS documentation validator\n+gts-docs-test:\n+\tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"a5ad52553831166705ad17e55ce7c22db7b04ddd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify vendor behavior in the gts-docs comment.**  \nThe comment says “The --vendor option ensures…”, but the `gts-docs` target does not pass `--vendor`. This is a minor doc mismatch that can confuse users; either move that comment to `gts-docs-vendor` or update it to reflect the default behavior.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# The --vendor option ensures all GTS IDs use the expected vendor (e.g., \"x\" placeholder, later \"cf\" for Cyber Fabric)\n+# Vendor enforcement is available via the gts-docs-vendor target (--vendor x)\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n## Validate GTS identifiers in .md and .json files (DE0903)\n# Uses gts-docs-validator from apps/gts-docs-validator\n# Vendor enforcement is available via the gts-docs-vendor target (--vendor x)\ngts-docs:\n\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n\n## Validate GTS docs with vendor check (ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\")\ngts-docs-vendor:\n\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n\t\t--vendor x \\\n\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n\n## Run tests for GTS documentation validator\ngts-docs-test:\n\tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile` around lines 92 - 111, The comment above the gts-docs Makefile\ntarget incorrectly claims “The --vendor option ensures…” even though the\ngts-docs target does not pass --vendor; update the comment to accurately reflect\ndefault behavior or move that vendor-specific sentence to the gts-docs-vendor\ntarget. Specifically, change the explanatory text around the gts-docs target\n(and/or relocate the vendor sentence) so that gts-docs remains documented as\nrunning the validator without --vendor while gts-docs-vendor documents the\nvendor x enforcement, referencing the Makefile targets gts-docs and\ngts-docs-vendor and the --vendor option in the description.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Confirmed as addressed by @yoskini\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:46:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705063807","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705063807"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705063807"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705063807/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":92,"original_start_line":92,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":126,"original_line":111,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":32,"position":57,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705071885","pull_request_review_id":3678446764,"id":2705071885,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPB8N","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! File scanning functionality for GTS documentation validation\n+\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use glob::Pattern;\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use walkdir::WalkDir;\n+\n+use crate::validator::{is_bad_example_context, is_wildcard_context, validate_gts_id, GtsError};\n+\n+/// File patterns to scan\n+const FILE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\"*.md\", \"*.json\", \"*.yaml\", \"*.yml\"];\n+\n+/// Directories to skip\n+const SKIP_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"target\", \"node_modules\", \".git\", \"vendor\", \".gts-spec\"];\n+\n+/// Files to skip (relative paths)\n+const SKIP_FILES: &[&str] = &[\"docs/api/api.json\"];\n+\n+/// Patterns that look like GTS but aren't (false positives)\n+const FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    r\"^gts\\.rs$\",     // Rust file named gts.rs\n+    r\"^gts\\.[a-z]+$\", // Single component like gts.rs, gts.py\n+];\n+\n+/// Pattern to find GTS-looking strings\n+/// Must have at least 2 dots after gts. to catch potential GTS IDs\n+/// Include hyphen so we can catch and report invalid hyphens\n+fn gts_pattern() -> Regex {\n+    Regex::new(r\"gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\").expect(\"Invalid regex pattern\")\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a path matches any of the exclude patterns\n+fn matches_exclude(path: &Path, exclude_patterns: &[Pattern]) -> bool {\n+    let path_str = path.to_string_lossy();\n+    for pattern in exclude_patterns {\n+        if pattern.matches(&path_str) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+        // Also try matching just the file/dir name\n+        if let Some(name) = path.file_name() {\n+            if pattern.matches(&name.to_string_lossy()) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if path contains any skip directories\n+fn in_skip_dir(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    for component in path.components() {\n+        if let std::path::Component::Normal(name) = component {\n+            if SKIP_DIRS\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|skip| name.to_string_lossy() == *skip)\n+            {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if file matches any of the file patterns\n+fn matches_file_pattern(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    if let Some(ext) = path.extension() {\n+        let ext_str = ext.to_string_lossy().to_lowercase();\n+        let with_dot = format!(\"*.{ext_str}\");\n+        FILE_PATTERNS.iter().any(|p| *p == with_dot)\n+    } else {\n+        false\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Find all files to scan in the given paths\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn find_files(paths: &[PathBuf], exclude: &[String], verbose: bool) -> Vec<PathBuf> {\n+    let mut files = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Parse exclude patterns\n+    let exclude_patterns: Vec<Pattern> = exclude\n+        .iter()\n+        .filter_map(|p| match Pattern::new(p) {\n+            Ok(pat) => Some(pat),\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                if verbose {\n+                    eprintln!(\"Warning: Invalid exclude pattern '{p}': {e}\");\n+                }\n+                None\n+            }\n+        })\n+        .collect();\n+\n+    for path in paths {\n+        if path.is_file() {\n+            if matches_file_pattern(path) && !matches_exclude(path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                files.push(path.clone());\n+            }\n+        } else if path.is_dir() {\n+            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n+                .follow_links(true)\n+                .into_iter()\n+                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n+            {\n+                let file_path = entry.path();\n+\n+                // Skip directories in skip list\n+                if in_skip_dir(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Only process files\n+                if !file_path.is_file() {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check file pattern\n+                if !matches_file_pattern(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check exclude patterns\n+                if matches_exclude(file_path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Excluding: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check against skip files\n+                let rel_path = file_path.to_string_lossy();\n+                if SKIP_FILES.iter().any(|skip| rel_path.contains(skip)) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Skipping: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                files.push(file_path.to_path_buf());\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    files.sort();\n+    files.dedup();\n+    files\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a matched string is a false positive\n+fn is_false_positive(gts_id: &str) -> bool {\n+    for pattern in FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS {\n+        if let Ok(re) = Regex::new(pattern) {\n+            if re.is_match(gts_id) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Scan a single file for GTS identifiers and validate them\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn scan_file(path: &Path, expected_vendor: Option<&str>, verbose: bool) -> Vec<GtsError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            if verbose {\n+                eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n+            }\n+            return errors;\n+        }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"yoskini","id":20127030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTI3MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20127030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini","html_url":"https://github.com/yoskini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Done","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:47:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:47:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705071885","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705071885"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705071885"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705071885/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":165,"original_start_line":168,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":179,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704717574,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":175,"position":179,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705072597","pull_request_review_id":3678447481,"id":2705072597,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPCHV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@\n+//! GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+//!\n+//! This tool validates GTS (Global Type System) identifiers in documentation files\n+//! (.md, .json, .yaml), complementing the Rust-based DE0901 lint that validates\n+//! GTS identifiers in source code.\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! ```bash\n+//! # Validate docs with vendor filter\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x docs modules libs examples\n+//!\n+//! # With exclusions\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\" .\n+//!\n+//! # JSON output\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --json docs\n+//! ```\n+\n+// CLI tools are expected to print to stdout/stderr\n+#![allow(\n+    clippy::print_stdout,\n+    clippy::print_stderr,\n+    clippy::exit,\n+    clippy::expect_used\n+)]\n+\n+mod scanner;\n+mod validator;\n+\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+use std::process::ExitCode;\n+\n+use clap::Parser;\n+use colored::Colorize;\n+\n+use crate::scanner::{find_files, scan_file};\n+use crate::validator::ValidationResult;\n+\n+/// GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+///\n+/// Validates GTS identifiers in .md, .json, and .yaml files.\n+/// Ensures all GTS IDs follow the correct format and optionally validates\n+/// that they use a specific vendor.\n+#[derive(Parser, Debug)]\n+#[command(name = \"gts-docs-validator\")]\n+#[command(author, version, about, long_about = None)]\n+struct Cli {\n+    /// Paths to scan (files or directories)\n+    /// Defaults to: docs, modules, libs, examples\n+    #[arg(value_name = \"PATH\")]\n+    paths: Vec<PathBuf>,\n+\n+    /// Expected vendor for all GTS IDs (validates vendor matches)\n+    /// Example: --vendor x ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\"\n+    ///\n+    /// Note: Example vendors are always tolerated: acme, globex, example, demo, test, sample, tutorial\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    vendor: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Exclude patterns (can be specified multiple times)\n+    /// Supports glob patterns. Example: --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\"\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'e', action = clap::ArgAction::Append)]\n+    exclude: Vec<String>,\n+\n+    /// Output results as JSON\n+    #[arg(long)]\n+    json: bool,\n+\n+    /// Show verbose output including file scanning progress\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'v')]\n+    verbose: bool,\n+}\n+\n+/// Default directories to scan if none specified\n+const DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"docs\", \"modules\", \"libs\", \"examples\"];\n+\n+fn main() -> ExitCode {\n+    let cli = Cli::parse();\n+\n+    // Determine paths to scan\n+    let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n+        DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(PathBuf::from)\n+            .filter(|p| p.exists())\n+            .collect()\n+    } else {\n+        cli.paths.clone()\n+    };","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"yoskini","id":20127030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTI3MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20127030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini","html_url":"https://github.com/yoskini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Done","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:47:57Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:47:57Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705072597","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705072597"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705072597"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705072597/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":82,"original_start_line":82,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":97,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704717566,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":90,"position":97,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074098","pull_request_review_id":3678449025,"id":2705074098,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPCey","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,311 @@\n+//! File scanning functionality for GTS documentation validation\n+\n+use std::fs;\n+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};\n+\n+use glob::Pattern;\n+use regex::Regex;\n+use walkdir::WalkDir;\n+\n+use crate::validator::{is_bad_example_context, is_wildcard_context, validate_gts_id, GtsError};\n+\n+/// File patterns to scan\n+const FILE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\"*.md\", \"*.json\", \"*.yaml\", \"*.yml\"];\n+\n+/// Directories to skip\n+const SKIP_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"target\", \"node_modules\", \".git\", \"vendor\", \".gts-spec\"];\n+\n+/// Files to skip (relative paths)\n+const SKIP_FILES: &[&str] = &[\"docs/api/api.json\"];\n+\n+/// Patterns that look like GTS but aren't (false positives)\n+const FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    r\"^gts\\.rs$\",     // Rust file named gts.rs\n+    r\"^gts\\.[a-z]+$\", // Single component like gts.rs, gts.py\n+];\n+\n+/// Pattern to find GTS-looking strings\n+/// Must have at least 2 dots after gts. to catch potential GTS IDs\n+/// Include hyphen so we can catch and report invalid hyphens\n+fn gts_pattern() -> Regex {\n+    Regex::new(r\"gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~-]+\").expect(\"Invalid regex pattern\")\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a path matches any of the exclude patterns\n+fn matches_exclude(path: &Path, exclude_patterns: &[Pattern]) -> bool {\n+    let path_str = path.to_string_lossy();\n+    for pattern in exclude_patterns {\n+        if pattern.matches(&path_str) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+        // Also try matching just the file/dir name\n+        if let Some(name) = path.file_name() {\n+            if pattern.matches(&name.to_string_lossy()) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if path contains any skip directories\n+fn in_skip_dir(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    for component in path.components() {\n+        if let std::path::Component::Normal(name) = component {\n+            if SKIP_DIRS\n+                .iter()\n+                .any(|skip| name.to_string_lossy() == *skip)\n+            {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if file matches any of the file patterns\n+fn matches_file_pattern(path: &Path) -> bool {\n+    if let Some(ext) = path.extension() {\n+        let ext_str = ext.to_string_lossy().to_lowercase();\n+        let with_dot = format!(\"*.{ext_str}\");\n+        FILE_PATTERNS.iter().any(|p| *p == with_dot)\n+    } else {\n+        false\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Find all files to scan in the given paths\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn find_files(paths: &[PathBuf], exclude: &[String], verbose: bool) -> Vec<PathBuf> {\n+    let mut files = Vec::new();\n+\n+    // Parse exclude patterns\n+    let exclude_patterns: Vec<Pattern> = exclude\n+        .iter()\n+        .filter_map(|p| match Pattern::new(p) {\n+            Ok(pat) => Some(pat),\n+            Err(e) => {\n+                if verbose {\n+                    eprintln!(\"Warning: Invalid exclude pattern '{p}': {e}\");\n+                }\n+                None\n+            }\n+        })\n+        .collect();\n+\n+    for path in paths {\n+        if path.is_file() {\n+            if matches_file_pattern(path) && !matches_exclude(path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                files.push(path.clone());\n+            }\n+        } else if path.is_dir() {\n+            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n+                .follow_links(true)\n+                .into_iter()\n+                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n+            {\n+                let file_path = entry.path();\n+\n+                // Skip directories in skip list\n+                if in_skip_dir(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Only process files\n+                if !file_path.is_file() {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check file pattern\n+                if !matches_file_pattern(file_path) {\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check exclude patterns\n+                if matches_exclude(file_path, &exclude_patterns) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Excluding: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                // Check against skip files\n+                let rel_path = file_path.to_string_lossy();\n+                if SKIP_FILES.iter().any(|skip| rel_path.contains(skip)) {\n+                    if verbose {\n+                        eprintln!(\"  Skipping: {}\", file_path.display());\n+                    }\n+                    continue;\n+                }\n+\n+                files.push(file_path.to_path_buf());\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    files.sort();\n+    files.dedup();\n+    files\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if a matched string is a false positive\n+fn is_false_positive(gts_id: &str) -> bool {\n+    for pattern in FALSE_POSITIVE_PATTERNS {\n+        if let Ok(re) = Regex::new(pattern) {\n+            if re.is_match(gts_id) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Scan a single file for GTS identifiers and validate them\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn scan_file(path: &Path, expected_vendor: Option<&str>, verbose: bool) -> Vec<GtsError> {\n+    let mut errors = Vec::new();\n+\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+        Ok(c) => c,\n+        Err(e) => {\n+            if verbose {\n+                eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n+            }\n+            return errors;\n+        }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@yoskini`, thank you for addressing this! The change to surface unreadable files as validation errors will ensure that CI properly catches file access issues instead of silently skipping them.\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.902Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/*.rs : Include at least one test case with no violations (empty or near-empty `.stderr` file) in UI tests\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: bit8shift\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 277\nFile: libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs:1198-1265\nTimestamp: 2026-01-19T10:57:35.386Z\nLearning: In libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/config/mod.rs, the render_effective_modules_config function should use lenient error handling (warn and continue) rather than strict fail-fast, to provide partial configuration dumps even when individual modules have issues.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:20Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705074098","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074098"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705074098"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":165,"original_start_line":168,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":179,"original_line":175,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704717574,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":175,"position":179,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074238","pull_request_review_id":3678449251,"id":2705074238,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPCg-","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@\n+//! GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+//!\n+//! This tool validates GTS (Global Type System) identifiers in documentation files\n+//! (.md, .json, .yaml), complementing the Rust-based DE0901 lint that validates\n+//! GTS identifiers in source code.\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! ```bash\n+//! # Validate docs with vendor filter\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x docs modules libs examples\n+//!\n+//! # With exclusions\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\" .\n+//!\n+//! # JSON output\n+//! gts-docs-validator --vendor x --json docs\n+//! ```\n+\n+// CLI tools are expected to print to stdout/stderr\n+#![allow(\n+    clippy::print_stdout,\n+    clippy::print_stderr,\n+    clippy::exit,\n+    clippy::expect_used\n+)]\n+\n+mod scanner;\n+mod validator;\n+\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+use std::process::ExitCode;\n+\n+use clap::Parser;\n+use colored::Colorize;\n+\n+use crate::scanner::{find_files, scan_file};\n+use crate::validator::ValidationResult;\n+\n+/// GTS Documentation Validator (DE0903)\n+///\n+/// Validates GTS identifiers in .md, .json, and .yaml files.\n+/// Ensures all GTS IDs follow the correct format and optionally validates\n+/// that they use a specific vendor.\n+#[derive(Parser, Debug)]\n+#[command(name = \"gts-docs-validator\")]\n+#[command(author, version, about, long_about = None)]\n+struct Cli {\n+    /// Paths to scan (files or directories)\n+    /// Defaults to: docs, modules, libs, examples\n+    #[arg(value_name = \"PATH\")]\n+    paths: Vec<PathBuf>,\n+\n+    /// Expected vendor for all GTS IDs (validates vendor matches)\n+    /// Example: --vendor x ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\"\n+    ///\n+    /// Note: Example vendors are always tolerated: acme, globex, example, demo, test, sample, tutorial\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    vendor: Option<String>,\n+\n+    /// Exclude patterns (can be specified multiple times)\n+    /// Supports glob patterns. Example: --exclude \"target/*\" --exclude \"docs/api/*\"\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'e', action = clap::ArgAction::Append)]\n+    exclude: Vec<String>,\n+\n+    /// Output results as JSON\n+    #[arg(long)]\n+    json: bool,\n+\n+    /// Show verbose output including file scanning progress\n+    #[arg(long, short = 'v')]\n+    verbose: bool,\n+}\n+\n+/// Default directories to scan if none specified\n+const DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS: &[&str] = &[\"docs\", \"modules\", \"libs\", \"examples\"];\n+\n+fn main() -> ExitCode {\n+    let cli = Cli::parse();\n+\n+    // Determine paths to scan\n+    let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n+        DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n+            .iter()\n+            .map(PathBuf::from)\n+            .filter(|p| p.exists())\n+            .collect()\n+    } else {\n+        cli.paths.clone()\n+    };","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@yoskini`, thank you for addressing this! The fail-fast check will ensure the tool provides clear feedback when there are no paths to scan. ✨\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n```\n  ／|、\n (˚ˇ​ ˇ˚)\n  >🥕\n```\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.902Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Document lint behavior in doc comments within the lint implementation\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.902Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/*.rs : Include at least one test case with no violations (empty or near-empty `.stderr` file) in UI tests\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.902Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/main.rs : If generated `main.rs` and `main.stderr` are empty, remove them from the UI test directory\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:48:23Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705074238","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074238"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705074238"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705074238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":82,"original_start_line":82,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":97,"original_line":90,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2704717566,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":90,"position":97,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089061","pull_request_review_id":3678467074,"id":2705089061,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPGIl","diff_hunk":"@@ -89,6 +89,27 @@ geiger:\n lint:\n \tRUSTFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo check --workspace --all-targets --all-features\n \n+## Validate GTS identifiers in .md and .json files (DE0903)\n+# Uses gts-docs-validator from apps/gts-docs-validator\n+# The --vendor option ensures all GTS IDs use the expected vendor (e.g., \"x\" placeholder, later \"cf\" for Cyber Fabric)\n+gts-docs:\n+\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Validate GTS docs with vendor check (ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\")\n+gts-docs-vendor:\n+\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--vendor x \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Run tests for GTS documentation validator\n+gts-docs-test:\n+\tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"a5ad52553831166705ad17e55ce7c22db7b04ddd","user":{"login":"yoskini","id":20127030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTI3MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20127030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini","html_url":"https://github.com/yoskini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Resolved","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705089061","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089061"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705089061"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089061/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":92,"original_start_line":92,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":126,"original_line":111,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2705063807,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":32,"position":57,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089818","pull_request_review_id":3678467883,"id":2705089818,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPGUa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,429 @@\n+//! GTS ID validation logic\n+\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+\n+use gts::GtsID;\n+use serde::Serialize;\n+\n+/// Represents a single GTS validation error\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize)]\n+pub struct GtsError {\n+    pub file: PathBuf,\n+    pub line: usize,\n+    pub column: usize,\n+    pub gts_id: String,\n+    pub error: String,\n+    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = \"String::is_empty\")]\n+    pub context: String,\n+}\n+\n+/// Aggregated validation results\n+#[derive(Debug, Default)]\n+pub struct ValidationResult {\n+    pub errors: Vec<GtsError>,\n+    pub files_scanned: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl ValidationResult {\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn new(files_scanned: usize) -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            errors: Vec::new(),\n+            files_scanned,\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub fn add_errors(&mut self, errors: Vec<GtsError>) {\n+        self.errors.extend(errors);\n+    }\n+\n+    #[must_use]\n+    pub fn is_ok(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.errors.is_empty()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+/// Contexts where wildcards are allowed (in documentation)\n+const WILDCARD_ALLOWED_CONTEXTS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"pattern\",\n+    \"filter\",\n+    \"query\",\n+    \"$filter\",\n+    \"starts_with\",\n+    \"with_pattern\",\n+    \"resource_pattern\",\n+    \"discovery\",\n+    \"match\",\n+    \"wildcard\",\n+    \"differs from\",\n+    \"get\",\n+    \"list\",\n+    \"todo\",\n+    \"p1 -\",\n+    \"p2 -\",\n+    \"p3 -\",\n+];\n+\n+/// Contexts that indicate \"bad example\" or intentionally invalid identifiers\n+const SKIP_VALIDATION_CONTEXTS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"invalid\",\n+    \"wrong\",\n+    \"bad\",\n+    \"reject\",\n+    \"error\",\n+    \"fail\",\n+    \"\\u{274c}\",\n+    \"\\u{2717}\",\n+    \"should not\",\n+    \"must not\",\n+    \"not allowed\",\n+    \"given**\",\n+    \"**given**\",\n+];\n+\n+/// Example vendors used in documentation that are tolerated during vendor validation.\n+/// These are placeholder/example vendors commonly used in docs and tutorials.\n+pub const EXAMPLE_VENDORS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"acme\",     // Classic example company name\n+    \"globex\",   // Another example company name\n+    \"example\",  // Generic example\n+    \"demo\",     // Demo purposes\n+    \"test\",     // Test purposes\n+    \"sample\",   // Sample code\n+    \"tutorial\", // Tutorial examples\n+];\n+\n+/// Check if a vendor is an example/placeholder vendor that should be tolerated\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn is_example_vendor(vendor: &str) -> bool {\n+    EXAMPLE_VENDORS.contains(&vendor)\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the GTS identifier is in a context where wildcards are allowed\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn is_wildcard_context(line: &str, match_start: usize) -> bool {\n+    // Use get() to safely handle potential mid-codepoint byte offsets\n+    let before = match line.get(..match_start) {\n+        Some(s) => s.to_lowercase(),\n+        None => return false, // Invalid byte offset, assume not wildcard context\n+    };\n+\n+    for ctx in WILDCARD_ALLOWED_CONTEXTS {\n+        if before.contains(ctx) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Also check for $filter anywhere in the line\n+    if line.to_lowercase().contains(\"$filter\") {\n+        return true;\n+    }\n+\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Check if the GTS identifier is in a \"bad example\" context\n+#[must_use]\n+pub fn is_bad_example_context(line: &str, prev_lines: &[&str]) -> bool {\n+    let line_lower = line.to_lowercase();\n+\n+    // Check current line\n+    for ctx in SKIP_VALIDATION_CONTEXTS {\n+        if line_lower.contains(ctx) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    // Check previous lines (last 3)\n+    for prev_line in prev_lines.iter().rev().take(3) {\n+        let prev_lower = prev_line.to_lowercase();\n+        for ctx in SKIP_VALIDATION_CONTEXTS {\n+            if prev_lower.contains(ctx) {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Validate a single GTS segment like 'x.core.modkit.plugin.v1'\n+pub fn validate_gts_segment(segment: &str) -> Result<(), String> {\n+    if segment.is_empty() {\n+        return Ok(()); // Empty segments are ok (trailing ~)\n+    }\n+\n+    // Check for invalid characters\n+    if segment.contains('-') {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Hyphen not allowed in segment: '{segment}'\"));\n+    }\n+\n+    let parts: Vec<&str> = segment.split('.').collect();\n+\n+    // Must have 5 components: vendor.org.package.type.version\n+    // But version can be v1, v1.0, v1.2.3, etc.\n+    if parts.len() < 5 {\n+        return Err(format!(\n+            \"Segment must have 5 components (vendor.org.package.type.version), got {}: '{segment}'\",\n+            parts.len()\n+        ));\n+    }\n+\n+    // The 5th component must start with 'v' (version)\n+    if !parts[4].starts_with('v') {\n+        return Err(format!(\n+            \"Version must start with 'v' (e.g., v1, v1.0): '{segment}'\"\n+        ));\n+    }\n+\n+    // Validate version format\n+    let version_part = &parts[4][1..]; // Remove 'v' prefix\n+    if version_part.is_empty() {\n+        return Err(format!(\"Version number missing after 'v': '{segment}'\"));\n+    }\n+\n+    // Version parts must be numeric\n+    let version_components: Vec<&str> = if parts.len() > 5 {\n+        // v1.2.3 case: version spans multiple dot-separated parts\n+        std::iter::once(version_part)\n+            .chain(parts[5..].iter().copied())\n+            .collect()\n+    } else {\n+        vec![version_part]\n+    };\n+\n+    for (i, vc) in version_components.iter().enumerate() {\n+        // First part must be numeric, but could be followed by more segments\n+        if vc.parse::<u32>().is_err() && i == 0 {\n+            return Err(format!(\"Version must be numeric: '{segment}'\"));\n+        }","path":"apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs","commit_id":"db935b710789d880f659e21094df1955341e2ad2","original_commit_id":"a5ad52553831166705ad17e55ce7c22db7b04ddd","user":{"login":"yoskini","id":20127030,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwMTI3MDMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20127030?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini","html_url":"https://github.com/yoskini","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yoskini/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Done","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705089818","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089818"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705089818"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705089818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":195,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":199,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2705056415,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":199,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705090753","pull_request_review_id":3678468888,"id":2705090753,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hPGjB","diff_hunk":"@@ -89,6 +89,27 @@ geiger:\n lint:\n \tRUSTFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo check --workspace --all-targets --all-features\n \n+## Validate GTS identifiers in .md and .json files (DE0903)\n+# Uses gts-docs-validator from apps/gts-docs-validator\n+# The --vendor option ensures all GTS IDs use the expected vendor (e.g., \"x\" placeholder, later \"cf\" for Cyber Fabric)\n+gts-docs:\n+\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Validate GTS docs with vendor check (ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\")\n+gts-docs-vendor:\n+\tcargo run --release -p gts-docs-validator -- \\\n+\t\t--vendor x \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"target/*\" \\\n+\t\t--exclude \"docs/api/*\" \\\n+\t\tdocs modules libs examples\n+\n+## Run tests for GTS documentation validator\n+gts-docs-test:\n+\tcargo test -p gts-docs-validator","path":"Makefile","commit_id":"e519aa9a47de2acd90fc798a7d8533feee94d5d2","original_commit_id":"a5ad52553831166705ad17e55ce7c22db7b04ddd","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@yoskini`, thank you for resolving the documentation clarification! 👍\n\n<!-- <review_comment_addressed> -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:52:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#discussion_r2705090753","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705090753"},"html":{"href