ints/validate_gts_docs.py`:\n- Around line 72-73: The GTS_PATTERN regex currently omits the hyphen character\nso strings like gts.my-vendor.x will not be matched and thus bypass validation;\nupdate the GTS_PATTERN definition to include the hyphen (e.g., add '-' to the\ncharacter classes) so the overall pattern in GTS_PATTERN matches GTS-looking\nidentifiers, then rely on validate_gts_segment to detect and report\nhyphen-related invalid segments; ensure you only change the regex character\nclasses and do not alter validate_gts_segment's validation logic.\n- Around line 169-205: In validate_gts_id enforce that non-wildcard GTS IDs must\ninclude a trailing '~' by adding a check (when allow_wildcards is False and '*'\nnot in gts_id) that the normalized gts_id endswith('~'); if it doesn't, append\nan error (use original for the message) and return errors. Place this check\nafter the wildcard handling (after the '*' checks) and before you strip the\n'gts.' prefix / split into segments (i.e., before computing rest or immediately\nafter rest = gts_id[4:]), referencing validate_gts_id, allow_wildcards, gts_id,\nrest, and original.\n- Around line 237-259: The function is_bad_example_context currently has an\nunused parameter match_start and an implicit Optional annotation for prev_lines;\nrename match_start to _match_start to signal intentional unused argument and\nchange the signature to prev_lines: Optional[List[str]] = None (import Optional\nfrom typing if not already) so the Optional is explicit, then update any\ninternal references to prev_lines as needed—no behavior changes otherwise in\nis_bad_example_context.\n- Around line 317-341: The find_files function uses f.relative_to(PROJECT_ROOT)\nwhich raises ValueError for paths outside the repo; wrap that call in a guard\n(try/except ValueError) when building rel_path so external files don’t crash the\nscan. Specifically, inside find_files where rel_path =\nstr(f.relative_to(PROJECT_ROOT)), catch ValueError and fall back to a safe value\n(e.g., str(f) or skip the SKIP_FILES check for non-repo paths) before comparing\nagainst SKIP_FILES; keep the existing SKIP_DIRS checks and ensure the function\nstill returns the correct file set.\n\nIn `@scripts/ci.py`:\n- Around line 120-141: cmd_gts_docs accesses args.verbose which doesn't exist\nwhen cmd_check calls it, causing an AttributeError; update cmd_gts_docs to read\nverbosity safely (e.g., use getattr(args, \"verbose\", False)) before appending\n\"--verbose\" so it won't crash when args lacks verbose, or alternatively ensure\nthe CLI parser that builds args for cmd_check defines a verbose flag; modify the\ncmd_gts_docs function (and only its args reading) to use a defaulted access\npattern such as getattr(args, \"verbose\", False) to fix the issue.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`68-88`: **Prefix unused `err` bindings to satisfy Ruff.**\n\nLine 70 and Line 87 unpack `err` but never use it, which triggers RUF059. Consider renaming to `_err` (or `_`) to silence the lint.  \n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        valid, err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.modkit.plugin.1\")\n+        valid, _ = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.modkit.plugin.1\")\n\n-        valid, err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.extra.modkit.plugin.v1\")\n+        valid, _ = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.extra.modkit.plugin.v1\")\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 949b3e840c1742bd1fb0de560223f63642ee935b and bc63d39aa19d93768c3a45ef5910a566431e97ea.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (7)<