ss for detecting serde/utoipa derives that must be checked before proc macros expand\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `dylint_lints/README.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🧬 Code graph analysis (1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py (6)</summary>\n\n* `validate_gts_segment` (144-166)\n* `validate_gts_id` (169-212)\n* `is_wildcard_context` (215-234)\n* `is_bad_example_context` (237-259)\n* `scan_file` (262-314)\n* `main` (415-469)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/README.md</summary>\n\n280-280: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n---\n\n287-287: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.14.11)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py</summary>\n\n237-237: Unused function argument: `match_start`\n\n(ARG001)\n\n---\n\n237-237: PEP 484 prohibits implicit `Optional`\n\nConvert to `T | None`\n\n(RUF013)\n\n---\n\n272-272: Do not catch blind exception: `Exception`\n\n(BLE001)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py</summary>\n\n70-70: Unpacked variable `err` is never used\n\nPrefix it with an underscore or any other dummy variable pattern\n\n(RUF059)\n\n---\n\n87-87: Unpacked variable `err` is never used\n\nPrefix it with an underscore or any other dummy variable pattern\n\n(RUF059)\n\n---\n\n385-385: Local variable `errors` is assigned to but never used\n\nRemove assignment to unused variable `errors`\n\n(F841)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (12)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: Agent\n* GitHub Check: CodeQL analysis (python)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=sqlite)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=pg)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (18)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/README.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-13`: **Quick-start targets are clearly documented.**  \nNice to see the new `gts-docs` and `gts-docs-test` targets surfaced alongside existing lint workflows.\n\n---\n\n`49-51`: **GTS lint catalog update looks good.**  \nThe DE090x entries are clear and align with the new validator coverage.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/2025-12-22-add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`195-200`: **Derived-type suffix correction is consistent.**  \nThe updated chained ID and expectation align with the derived type naming rule.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/types-registry/openspec/specs/types-registry/spec.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`195-202`: **Derived-type suffix correction is consistent.**  \nThe updated example ID and expected result read correctly for a derived type segment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`69-69`: **Good to mark the new targets as phony.**  \nPrevents accidental file/target collisions.\n\n---\n\n`92-98`: **New GTS doc validation targets look solid.**  \nClear entry points for running the validator and its tests locally.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`567-570`: **CLI wiring for `gts-docs` looks good.**  \nVerbose flag is a nice touch for CI troubleshooting.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`91-158`: **Solid coverage for ID normalization, chaining, and wildcard gating.**\n\n---\n\n`159-197`: **Wildcard context tests look comprehensive.**\n\n---\n\n`199-241`: **Bad-example context coverage is thorough and clear.**\n\n---\n\n`244-271`: **Regex matching cases are well-targeted.**\n\n---\n\n`431-489`: **Edge-case coverage looks good and focused.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`144-166`: **Segment validation logic is clear and well-scoped.**\n\n---\n\n`215-234`: **Wildcard context detection looks solid.**\n\n---\n\n`262-315`: **File scanning and error reporting are clean and readable.**\n\n---\n\n`344-361`: **Validation orchestration reads well.**\n\n---\n\n`364-413`: **Result formatting is user-friendly and consistent.**\n\n---\n\n`415-469`: **CLI wiring and JSON output look solid.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3671862337","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3671862337"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T17:07:53Z","commit_id":"bc63d39aa19d93768c3a45ef5910a566431e97ea"},{"id":3672024028,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7a3qPc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py`:\n- Around line 373-395: The test test_hyphen_detected currently assumes\nGTS_PATTERN will not match hyphenated segments and asserts no errors; update the\nassertions so the test reflects the intended validation behavior: if GTS_PATTERN\nhas been extended to allow '-' then change the scan_file/regex expectations to\nassert that an error is produced (e.g., replace self.assertEqual(len(errors), 0,\n...) with an assertion that len(errors) > 0 or the expected error count) and\nchange the direct regex check from self.assertIsNone(match, ...) to\nself.assertIsNotNone(match, ...) and optionally assert the found match or that\nthe error text contains the hyphenated ID; keep references to\ntest_hyphen_detected, scan_file, and GTS_PATTERN so the test adapts to the\npattern change.\n\nIn `@dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py`:\n- Around line 269-274: The current except block around path.read_text(...) is\ntoo broad; change it to catch only the file IO and decoding errors (OSError and\nUnicodeDecodeError) so other bugs bubble up: replace the generic \"except\nException as e:\" with separate handlers (or a combined except (OSError,\nUnicodeDecodeError) as e) in the code that calls path.read_text, keep the\nexisting verbose print(f\"  Warning: Could not read {path}: {e}\") and return\nerrors for those cases, and do not swallow other exception types so they\npropagate for proper failure handling; refer to the path.read_text call, the\nvariables path, verbose, and errors to locate the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`279-291`: **Add language hints to fenced blocks to satisfy MD040.**  \nThis is already flagged in prior review; still applies.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n gts.<segment>~[<segment>~]*\n \n Where each segment = vendor.org.package.type.version\n ```\n@@\n-```\n+```text\n gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~                              # Schema (type definition)\n gts.x.core.modkit.plugin.v1~vendor.pkg.module.plugin.v1~  # Instance (chained)\n gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.odata.errors.invalid.v1      # Error code\n ```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`72-73`: **Include hyphens in `GTS_PATTERN` so invalid IDs don’t bypass validation.**  \nCurrently `gts.my-vendor...` won’t match at all, so it never reaches `validate_gts_segment`. This was previously flagged and still applies.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-GTS_PATTERN = re.compile(r'gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~]+', re.IGNORECASE)\n+GTS_PATTERN = re.compile(r'gts\\.[a-z0-9_.*~\\-]+\\.[a-z0-9_.*~\\-]+', re.IGNORECASE)\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`333-337`: **Guard `relative_to(PROJECT_ROOT)` for external paths.**  \n`relative_to` raises `ValueError` when the path isn’t under the repo. This was already flagged and still applies.  \n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Suggested guard</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                    rel_path = str(f.relative_to(PROJECT_ROOT))\n-                    if rel_path in SKIP_FILES:\n+                    try:\n+                        rel_path = str(f.relative_to(PROJECT_ROOT))\n+                    except ValueError:\n+                        rel_path = \"\"\n+                    if rel_path and rel_path in SKIP_FILES:\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`120-125`: **Fix AttributeError when `check` calls `cmd_gts_docs`.**  \n`check` arguments don’t define `verbose`, so `args.verbose` crashes CI.  \n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Minimal safe fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    if args.verbose:\n+    if getattr(args, \"verbose\", False):\n         cmd_args.append(\"--verbose\")\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 140-140\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`236-258`: **Minor lint cleanup: unused arg + explicit Optional.**  \nRuff flags `match_start` unused and implicit Optional. Consider `_match_start` and `Optional[List[str]] | None`.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-from typing import List, Tuple\n+from typing import List, Tuple, Optional\n@@\n-def is_bad_example_context(line: str, match_start: int, prev_lines: List[str] = None) -> bool:\n+def is_bad_example_context(line: str, _match_start: int, prev_lines: Optional[List[str]] = None) -> bool:\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`29-90`: **Ruff: unused `err` in a couple of tests.**  \nUse `_err` to make intent explicit and silence RUF059.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested tweak</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        valid, err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.modkit.plugin.1\")\n+        valid, _err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.modkit.plugin.1\")\n@@\n-        valid, err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.extra.modkit.plugin.v1\")\n+        valid, _err = validate_gts_segment(\"x.core.extra.modkit.plugin.v1\")\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 945e51e64767c99ff4791c693b08492c2a5ab685 and a05b7d5f708952fe3911e565a5995b0550627661.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (7)</summary>\n\n* `Makefile`\n* `dylint_lints/README.md`\n* `dylint_lints/test_validate_gts_docs.py`\n* `dylint_lints/validate_gts_docs.py`\n* `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/2025-12-22-add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md`\n* `modules/system/types-registry/openspec/specs/types-registry/spec.md`\n* `scripts/ci.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (2)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/types-registry/openspec/changes/archive/2025-12-22-add-types-registry-module/specs/types-registry/spec.md\n* modules/system/types-registry/openspec/specs/types-registry/spec.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (18)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.902Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 