o just #[arg(long)] or\n#[arg(long, value_name = \"...\")] so the vendor Option<String> (symbol vendor) no\nlonger uses -V and avoids the clash with clap's version flag; update any related\ndocs/tests that referenced -V accordingly.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs`:\n- Around line 168-175: The current fs::read_to_string(path) error branch\nsilently returns the existing errors vec, skipping unreadable files; change it\nto record the read failure as a validation error instead of quietly exiting. In\nthe match arm that handles Err(e) for fs::read_to_string, push a descriptive\nvalidation failure into the errors collection (include path.display() and e) so\nunreadable files count as failures; preserve the verbose eprintln when verbose\nis true but do not return early—return errors only after recording the failure.\nTarget the match around fs::read_to_string, the variables path, e, verbose, and\nthe errors collection to implement this change.\n- Around line 207-215: The slicing uses byte offsets (context_start/context_end)\nthat may split multi-byte UTF‑8 characters and panic; adjust both context_start\nand context_end to the nearest valid UTF‑8 character boundaries before slicing\nby using String::is_char_boundary (e.g., while\n!line.is_char_boundary(context_start) { context_start += 1 } and while\n!line.is_char_boundary(context_end) { context_end -= 1 } or equivalent logic),\nthen build the context string from line[context_start..context_end] and preserve\nthe existing \"...{context}\" prefix/suffix logic; update places referencing\ncontext_start/context_end/mat/line accordingly.\n\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs`:\n- Around line 292-306: The vendor-check in the error path should mirror the\nsuccess path by skipping example vendors: when inspecting the first segment's\nvendor (using non_empty_segments, parts, vendor) ensure you call\nis_example_vendor(vendor) and do not push a \"Vendor mismatch\" error if it\nreturns true; otherwise proceed with the existing mismatch check against\nexpected_vendor. Update the block that currently compares *vendor != expected to\nfirst guard with is_example_vendor(vendor) to prevent false positives for\nexample vendors.\n\nIn `@Makefile`:\n- Line 69: Add the missing phony declaration for the gts-docs-vendor Makefile\ntarget: update the .PHONY line that currently lists clippy kani geiger safety\nlint dylint dylint-list dylint-test gts-docs gts-docs-test to also include\ngts-docs-vendor so the Makefile treats that target as phony and avoids conflicts\nwith any real files named gts-docs-vendor.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`266-268`: **LGTM on the workspace pattern implementation.**\n\nThe workspace dependencies for `glob` and `colored` are correctly defined in `[workspace.dependencies]` and properly referenced via `{ workspace = true }` in the gts-docs-validator package. However, consider updating `colored` from version 2 to 3.0.0 (released January 7, 2025) to leverage the latest improvements.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`102-112`: **Prune skipped directories during traversal to avoid unnecessary work.**  \n`in_skip_dir` is checked after entries are produced, so WalkDir still traverses skipped trees.\n\n \n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n-            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n-                .follow_links(true)\n-                .into_iter()\n-                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n+            for entry in WalkDir::new(path)\n+                .follow_links(true)\n+                .into_iter()\n+                .filter_entry(|e| !in_skip_dir(e.path()))\n+                .filter_map(Result::ok)\n             {\n                 let file_path = entry.path();\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`193-195`: **Avoid rebuilding `prev_lines` on every match.**  \nThis is O(n²) on long files; `is_bad_example_context` only needs the last 3 lines.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n+    use std::collections::VecDeque;\n+    let mut prev_lines: VecDeque<&str> = VecDeque::new();\n+    for (line_idx, line) in lines.iter().enumerate() {\n         let line_num = line_idx + 1;\n \n-        for mat in gts_re.find_iter(line) {\n+        let prev_snapshot: Vec<&str> = prev_lines.iter().copied().collect();\n+        for mat in gts_re.find_iter(line) {\n             let gts_id = mat.as_str();\n             let col = mat.start() + 1;\n@@\n-            let prev_lines: Vec<&str> = lines[..line_idx].iter().copied().collect();\n-            if is_bad_example_context(line, &prev_lines) {\n+            if is_bad_example_context(line, &prev_snapshot) {\n                 continue;\n             }\n@@\n         }\n+        prev_lines.push_back(line);\n+        if prev_lines.len() > 3 {\n+            prev_lines.pop_front();\n+        }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678032430","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678032430"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T13:09:56Z","commit_id":"30916762ea29f612e2531096a0ce3182ebc73dd8"},{"id":3678048917,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bOpKV","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs`:\n- Around line 102-119: The function is_wildcard_context currently slices the\ninput string with line[..match_start] using a byte offset (match_start) which\ncan panic on multi-byte UTF-8 characters; update is_wildcard_context to perform\na Unicode-safe slice by using line.get(..match_start) (or otherwise convert the\nbyte offset to a valid char boundary) and handle the None case (treat as empty\nprefix) before calling to_lowercase; then run the existing context checks\nagainst that safe prefix and keep the $filter check on the full lowercased line.\nEnsure you reference the existing function name is_wildcard_context and the\nWILDCARD_ALLOWED_CONTEXTS constant when applying the changes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Makefile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`69-69`: **Missing `.PHONY` entry for `gts-docs-vendor`.**\n\nThe `gts-docs-vendor` target defined on line 102 should be added to the `.PHONY` declaration.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-.PHONY: clippy kani geiger safety lint dylint dylint-list dylint-test gts-docs gts-docs-test\n+.PHONY: clippy kani geiger safety lint dylint dylint-list dylint-test gts-docs gts-docs-vendor gts-docs-test\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`293-306`: **Missing `is_example_vendor` check in error path causes inconsistent behavior.**\n\nThe vendor check in the error path (line 298) doesn't call `is_example_vendor()`, unlike the success path (line 255). Example vendors like `acme` would incorrectly trigger a vendor mismatch error when the ID has other parsing issues.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n             // Even if gts library failed, still check vendor\n             if let Some(expected) = expected_vendor {\n                 if let Some(first_seg) = non_empty_segments.first() {\n                     let parts: Vec<&str> = first_seg.split('.').collect();\n                     if let Some(vendor) = parts.first() {\n-                        if *vendor != expected {\n+                        if *vendor != expected && !is_example_vendor(vendor) {\n                             errors.push(format!(\n                                 \"Vendor mismatch: expected '{}', found '{}' in '{}'\",\n                                 expected, vendor, original\n                             ));\n                         }\n                     }\n                 }\n             }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`165-173`: **Silent skip of unreadable files may hide validation gaps.**\n\nWhen `fs::read_to_string` fails, the function returns an empty error list, which could cause CI to pass with zero validation on permission-denied or corrupted files.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n         Ok(c) => c,\n         Err(e) => {\n             if verbose {\n                 eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n             }\n-            return errors;\n+            return vec![GtsError {\n+                file: path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                gts_id: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+                context: String::new(),\n+            }];\n         }\n     };\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`204-212`: **UTF-8 slicing panic on non-ASCII input.**\n\n`context_start` and `context_end` are byte offsets that can land mid-codepoint on multi-byte UTF-8 characters, causing a panic during string slicing.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                let context_start = mat.start().saturating_sub(20);\n-                let context_end = (mat.end() + 20).min(line.len());\n-                let mut context = line[context_start..context_end].to_string();\n+                let mut context_start = mat.start().saturating_sub(20);\n+                while context_start > 0 && !line.is_char_boundary(context_start) {\n+                    context_start -= 1;\n+                }\n+                let mut context_end = (mat.end() + 20).min(line.len());\n+                while context_end < line.len() && !line.is_char_boundary(context_end) {\n+                    context_end += 1;\n+                }\n+                let mut context = line[context_start..context_end].to_string();\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`54-59`: **Clap `-V` short flag conflict with auto-generated `--version`.**\n\nWith `#[command(version)]` enabled, clap reserves `-V` for `--version`. Using `-V` as the short flag for `vendor` creates a conflict.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     /// Expected vendor for all GTS IDs (validates vendor matches)\n     /// Example: --vendor x ensures all IDs use vendor \"x\"\n     ///\n     /// Note: Example vendors are always tolerated: acme, globex, example, demo, test, sample, tutorial\n-    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    #[arg(long)]\n     vendor: Option<String>,\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`82-90`: **Add fail-fast check when no paths exist to scan.**\n\nIf all default directories are missing and no paths are provided, the tool exits successfully after scanning zero files, which could mask configuration issues.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n         DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n             .iter()\n             .map(PathBuf::from)\n             .filter(|p| p.exists())\n             .collect()\n     } else {\n         cli.paths.clone()\n     };\n+\n+    if paths.is_empty() {\n+        eprintln!(\"Error: No existing paths to scan. Provide paths explicitly or ensure default directories exist.\");\n+        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678048917","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678048917"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T13:14:21Z","commit_id":"7a74a8df39250d64c4178357b9d701079a8ff80e"},{"id":3678419431,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bQDnn","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs`:\n- Around line 185-199: The loop over version_components currently only enforces\nnumeric on the first segment; update the validation in the for loop that\niterates over version_components (the block using \"for (i, vc) in\nversion_components.iter().enumerate()\") to require every vc.parse::<u32>() to\nsucceed and return Err when any component is non-numeric, and fix the error\nmessage to include the offending component (use vc or its string) instead of the\nundefined '{segment}' placeholder so failures like \"v1.alpha\" are rejected.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`54-59`: **Avoid `-V` short-flag clash with clap’s auto `--version`.**  \n`#[command(author, version, ...)]` reserves `-V/--version`, so `short = 'V'` on `--vendor` conflicts and can break parsing. Removing the short flag is the simplest fix.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    #[arg(long, short = 'V')]\n+    #[arg(long)]\n     vendor: Option<String>,\n```\n</details>\n\n\n\n```web\nclap derive disable_version_flag short -V conflict --version\n```\n\n---\n\n`81-90`: **Fail fast when no existing paths are found.**  \nAs written, nonexistent paths can lead to a successful run with zero files scanned.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n         DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n             .iter()\n             .map(PathBuf::from)\n             .filter(|p| p.exists())\n             .collect()\n     } else {\n         cli.paths.clone()\n     };\n+\n+    if paths.is_empty() {\n+        eprintln!(\"No existing paths to scan. Provide valid paths explicitly.\");\n+        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`291-300`: **Apply example-vendor tolerance in the fallback vendor check.**  \nThe non-`gts` parse path should mirror the success path; otherwise example vendors (acme/globex/…) get flagged when parsing fails for other reasons.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                    if *vendor != expected {\n+                    if *vendor != expected && !is_example_vendor(vendor) {\n                         errors.push(format!(\n                             \"Vendor mismatch: expected '{expected}', found '{vendor}' in '{original}'\"\n                         ));\n                     }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`165-172`: **Treat unreadable files as validation failures.**  \nSkipping unreadable files allows false-success runs in CI.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n         Ok(c) => c,\n         Err(e) => {\n             if verbose {\n                 eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n             }\n-            return errors;\n+            errors.push(GtsError {\n+                file: path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                gts_id: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+                context: String::new(),\n+            });\n+            return errors;\n         }\n     };\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678419431","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678419431"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T14:41:32Z","commit_id":"5f43da0a4bacd8148cbbf65662c4a031d7220dd1"},{"id":3678437920,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bQIIg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@Makefile`:\n- Around line 92-111: The comment above the gts-docs Makefile target incorrectly\nclaims “The --vendor option ensures…” even though the gts-docs target does not\npass --vendor; update the comment to accurately reflect default behavior or move\nthat vendor-specific sentence to the gts-docs-vendor target. Specifically,\nchange the explanatory text around the gts-docs target (and/or relocate the\nvendor sentence) so that gts-docs remains documented as running the validator\nwithout --vendor while gts-docs-vendor documents the vendor x enforcement,\nreferencing the Makefile targets gts-docs and gts-docs-vendor and the --vendor\noption in the description.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/validator.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`291-303`: **Align vendor check with example-vendor tolerance in the error path.**  \nThe error-path vendor check ignores `is_example_vendor`, so placeholder vendors (e.g., `acme`) still trigger a mismatch if `gts` parsing fails. This reintroduces inconsistent behavior.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                if let Some(vendor) = parts.first() {\n-                    if *vendor != expected {\n+                if let Some(vendor) = parts.first() {\n+                    if *vendor != expected && !is_example_vendor(vendor) {\n                         errors.push(format!(\n                             \"Vendor mismatch: expected '{expected}', found '{vendor}' in '{original}'\"\n                         ));\n                     }\n                 }\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`150-200`: **Enforce numeric version components beyond the first.**  \n`validate_gts_segment` only checks the first component for numeric content, so `v1.alpha` passes despite the error message claiming all parts must be numeric.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    for (i, vc) in version_components.iter().enumerate() {\n-        // First part must be numeric, but could be followed by more segments\n-        if vc.parse::<u32>().is_err() && i == 0 {\n-            return Err(format!(\"Version must be numeric: '{segment}'\"));\n-        }\n-    }\n+    for vc in &version_components {\n+        if vc.parse::<u32>().is_err() {\n+            return Err(format!(\n+                \"Version components must be numeric: '{segment}'\"\n+            ));\n+        }\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/scanner.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`165-172`: **Surface unreadable files as validation failures.**  \nCurrently unreadable files are silently skipped, so CI can pass without actually validating those files.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n+    let content = match fs::read_to_string(path) {\n         Ok(c) => c,\n         Err(e) => {\n             if verbose {\n                 eprintln!(\"  Warning: Could not read {}: {e}\", path.display());\n             }\n-            return errors;\n+            return vec![GtsError {\n+                file: path.to_path_buf(),\n+                line: 0,\n+                column: 0,\n+                gts_id: String::new(),\n+                error: format!(\"Failed to read file: {e}\"),\n+                context: String::new(),\n+            }];\n         }\n     };\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/gts-docs-validator/src/main.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`81-90`: **Fail fast when no paths exist to scan.**  \nIf none of the default paths exist (and no explicit paths are given), the validator reports success after scanning zero files.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     let paths: Vec<PathBuf> = if cli.paths.is_empty() {\n         DEFAULT_SCAN_DIRS\n             .iter()\n             .map(PathBuf::from)\n             .filter(|p| p.exists())\n             .collect()\n     } else {\n         cli.paths.clone()\n     };\n+\n+    if paths.is_empty() {\n+        eprintln!(\"No existing paths to scan. Provide paths explicitly.\");\n+        return ExitCode::FAILURE;\n+    }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678437920","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/266#pullrequestreview-3678437920"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/266"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T14:46:09Z","commit_id":"a5ad52553831166705ad17e55ce7c22db7b04ddd"},{"id":3678470497,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bQQFh","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5