 implementation tasks for SDK + module crates covering closure-table hierarchies, REST APIs, DB schema, migrations, and authorization.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **OpenSpec / Agent Guidance** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md` | Add OpenSpec-managed block and comprehensive agent instructions (checklist, workflows, CLI quick-start, validation/troubleshooting, refresh guidance). |\n| **Project Context & Conventions** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md` | Add project overview documenting purpose, tech stack, architecture conventions, REST/error/security patterns, DB access, testing, and observability guidance. |\n| **Module Proposal** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md` | Add two-crate proposal (`resource-group-sdk`, `resource-group`) defining `ResourceGroupApi`, transport-agnostic models, local client, domain service responsibilities, ClientHub registration, and migration notes. |\n| **Specification** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md` | Add full spec: type/entity management, closure-table schema and operations, UUIDv7 IDs, CRUD rules, constraints, optional references, auth rules, REST endpoints, DB schema, and validation scenarios. |\n| **Implementation Tasks** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md` | Add granular implementation checklist spanning SDK & module scaffolding, domain layer, storage/migrations, local client, REST DTOs/routes, auth/security, testing, docs, and migrations. |\n| **Architecture & Design** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/architecture/ADR.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/architecture/BUSINESS.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/architecture/DESIGN.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/architecture/features/*` | Add ADR (closure table decision), business context, overall design, feature roadmap, and per-feature design details including algorithms, entity lifecycles, error cases, and tests. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    participant Client as Client\n    participant REST as REST API\\n(Axum handlers)\n    participant SDK as Local Client\\n(resource-group-sdk)\n    participant Domain as Domain Service\\n(resource-group)\n    participant DB as Database\\n(closure table)\n\n    rect rgba(200,230,201,0.5)\n    Client->>REST: HTTP request (create/read/move/delete)\n    end\n\n    rect rgba(187,222,251,0.5)\n    REST->>SDK: Call ResourceGroupApi (includes SecurityCtx)\n    end\n\n    rect rgba(255,224,178,0.5)\n    SDK->>Domain: Invoke domain operation (validate, business rules)\n    end\n\n    rect rgba(255,205,210,0.5)\n    Domain->>DB: Read/write resource_group, closure, references\n    DB-->>Domain: Persisted result / query results\n    end\n\n    Domain-->>SDK: Operation result or error\n    SDK-->>REST: DTO / Problem Details\n    REST-->>Client: HTTP response (201/200/204/error)\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hopped through specs with eager cheer,  \n> > I mapped the trees both far and near,  \n> > Types and routes in tidy rows,  \n> > Tasks and docs where structure grows,  \n> > A happy rabbit stamps its paws — the module's here!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------