rectory\necho \"=== Contents of guidelines/DNA ===\"\nls -la guidelines/DNA/ 2>&1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check if there's a .gitkeep or other marker ===\"\nfind guidelines/DNA/ -type f 2>&1\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Verify the project.md is in openspec ===\"\nls -la modules/system/resource-group/openspec/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 599\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix broken documentation references before approval.**\n\nThe document references 4 non-existent files that must be created or replaced before this can be approved:\n\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md` (missing)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md` (missing)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md` (missing)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` (missing)\n\nThe `guidelines/DNA/` directory exists but is empty. Either create these documentation files or update the project.md to remove/replace these references with valid paths (only 6 of 10 referenced files currently exist in the repository).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md` around lines 1 - 138, The\ndocument references four missing guideline files (`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`,\n`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`, and\n`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`) causing broken links in\nmodules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md; either create those markdown\nfiles with the expected content (matching the referenced subjects and naming) or\nedit project.md to replace/remove those invalid references and point to existing\ndocs in the repo; update the references in project.md (search for the exact\ntokens `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`,\n`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`)\nso the file contains only valid paths before approving.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit c698c5e\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T16:50:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T16:05:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699246845","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699246845"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699246845"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699246845/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":138,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":138,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256218","pull_request_review_id":3671802768,"id":2699256218,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g42Ga","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: REST API Endpoints\n+\n+The system SHALL expose REST API endpoints for resource group operations.\n+\n+Endpoints SHALL include:\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/types` — Create type\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types` — List types\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Get type\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Update type\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Delete type\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups` — Create entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Get entity\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Update entity\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Delete entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors` — Get ancestors\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants` — Get descendants\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Create reference\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Delete reference\n+\n+All endpoints SHALL:\n+- Require authentication (Bearer token)\n+- Return RFC-9457 Problem Details for errors\n+- Follow HyperSpot REST API conventions\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create type via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid JSON payload with type data\n+- **WHEN** POST request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/types`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type and returns `201 Created` with location header\n+\n+#### Scenario: List entities via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n+- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- **THEN** response contains entities\n+","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"504144d9ffd7dee95e88fca15093e91805866ec6","original_commit_id":"7211cbe904eb8b63c27093f0b7695fcf667f7835","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Specify pagination and filtering for list endpoints.**\n\nThe \"List entities via REST\" scenario doesn't specify:\n- Pagination parameters (page, limit, cursor)\n- Filtering capabilities (by type, parent, etc.)\n- Sorting options\n- Response format structure\n\nList endpoints typically need these details for proper implementation.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested scenario enhancement</summary>\n\n```diff\n #### Scenario: List entities via REST\n \n - **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n-- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups`\n-- **THEN** response contains entities\n+- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups?type_code=DEPARTMENT&limit=20`\n+- **THEN** response contains paginated list of DEPARTMENT entities\n+- **AND** includes pagination metadata (total, limit, offset/cursor)\n+- **AND** supports filtering by type_code, parent_id, application_id\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n#### Scenario: List entities via REST\n\n- **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups?type_code=DEPARTMENT&limit=20`\n- **THEN** response contains paginated list of DEPARTMENT entities\n- **AND** includes pagination metadata (total, limit, offset/cursor)\n- **AND** supports filtering by type_code, parent_id, application_id\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 219 - 224, Update the \"List entities via REST\" scenario for the\n`/resource-group/v1/groups` endpoint to specify pagination, filtering, sorting,\nand response structure: describe supported query parameters (e.g., page, limit,\ncursor), filtering keys (e.g., type, parentId, status), and sorting options\n(e.g., sort_by, order), define the response payload shape including items array\nplus pagination metadata (total, page, limit, nextCursor), and add at least one\nexample request and corresponding example response to the \"List entities via\nREST\" scenario so implementers of the resource-group list handler know expected\nparameters and output.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T16:53:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T16:53:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699256218","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256218"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699256218"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":219,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":224,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":224,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256233","pull_request_review_id":3671802768,"id":2699256233,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g42Gp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: REST API Endpoints\n+\n+The system SHALL expose REST API endpoints for resource group operations.\n+\n+Endpoints SHALL include:\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/types` — Create type\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types` — List types\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Get type\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Update type\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Delete type\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups` — Create entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Get entity\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Update entity\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Delete entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors` — Get ancestors\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants` — Get descendants\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Create reference\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Delete reference\n+\n+All endpoints SHALL:\n+- Require authentication (Bearer token)\n+- Return RFC-9457 Problem Details for errors\n+- Follow HyperSpot REST API conventions\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create type via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid JSON payload with type data\n+- **WHEN** POST request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/types`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type and returns `201 Created` with location header\n+\n+#### Scenario: List entities via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n+- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- **THEN** response contains entities\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Database Schema\n+\n+The system SHALL use SeaORM with the following tables:\n+\n+**`resource_group_type`:**\n+- `code` (PK): String, unique, case-insensitive\n+- `parents`: JSON array of type codes\n+- `application_id`: UUID (owner)\n+- `allowed_app_ids`: JSON array of UUIDs\n+- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n+\n+**`resource_group`:**\n+- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n+- `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n+- `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n+- `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n+","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"7211cbe904eb8b63c27093f0b7695fcf667f7835","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**Critical: Missing `parent_id` field in database schema.**\n\nThe entity structure (line 51) specifies \"Parent ID: Optional reference to parent entity\" and scenarios reference `parent_id` (lines 66, 82), but the `resource_group` table schema doesn't include this field.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Required schema fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n **`resource_group`:**\n - `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n - `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n - `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n - `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `parent_id` (FK): Optional UUID → `resource_group.id`\n - `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\nAlso consider adding an index on `parent_id` for efficient parent-child queries.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n**`resource_group`:**\n- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n- `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n- `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n- `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n- `parent_id` (FK): Optional UUID → `resource_group.id`\n- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 238 - 244, The resource_group table definition is missing the\noptional parent_id column referenced elsewhere; add a nullable parent_id column\nof type UUIDv7 that references resource_group.id (foreign key) and update the\nentity spec for resource_group to include parent_id as Optional UUIDv7; also\ncreate an index on parent_id to optimize parent-child queries and ensure any\ninsert/update/ORM mappings (e.g., the resource_group model/entity) are updated\nto include the parent_id field.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T16:53:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T16:53:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699256233","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256233"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2699256233"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699256233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":304,"original_start_line":238,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":310,"original_line":244,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":244,"position":310,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366025","pull_request_review_id":3674339380,"id":2701366025,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hA5MJ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@\n+# Tasks: Resource Group Module\n+\n+## 1. SDK Crate Setup\n+\n+- [ ] 1.1 Create `resource-group-sdk/Cargo.toml` with minimal dependencies\n+- [ ] 1.2 Create SDK structure: `api.rs`, `models.rs`, `errors.rs`, `lib.rs`\n+- [ ] 1.3 Define `ResourceGroupApi` trait with all methods taking `&SecurityCtx`","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"7211cbe904eb8b63c27093f0b7695fcf667f7835","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"SecurityContext not SecurityCtx","created_at":"2026-01-17T19:19:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T19:21:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2701366025","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366025"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2701366025"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366025/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":7,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366675","pull_request_review_id":3674339380,"id":2701366675,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hA5WT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+# Change: Add Resource Group Module\n+\n+## Why\n+\n+HyperSpot needs a Resource Group module that provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control. This module enables applications to organize resources in a tree structure with strict type validation, permission management, and efficient hierarchy operations using the Closure Table pattern.","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"7211cbe904eb8b63c27093f0b7695fcf667f7835","user":{"login":"MikeFalcon77","id":3686170,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2ODYxNzA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3686170?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77","html_url":"https://github.com/MikeFalcon77","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/MikeFalcon77/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I thiunk we need to invent another naming. resource-group is strange name for module.\r\ngroup_manager or res_group_manager","created_at":"2026-01-17T19:21:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-17T19:21:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2701366675","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366675"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2701366675"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2701366675/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":5,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704917737","pull_request_review_id":3678260615,"id":2704917737,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hOcTp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+# Project Context\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+This module is part of **HyperSpot** — a modular, high-performance AI services platform built in Rust.\n+\n+The Resource Group module provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control, enabling applications to organize resources in tree structures with efficient hierarchy operations.\n+\n+## Tech Stack\n+\n+- **Language**: Rust (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md))\n+- **Framework**: ModKit (see [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md))\n+- **HTTP**: Axum with `tower-http` middleware\n+- **Database**: SeaORM / SQLx with secure ORM layer (see [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md))\n+- **Observability**: `tracing` + OpenTelemetry (see [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md))\n+- **OpenAPI**: `utoipa` for automatic documentation generation\n+- **IDs**: UUIDv7 for all identifiers\n+- **Time**: `chrono` with UTC timestamps\n+\n+## Project Conventions\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+Follow the architecture manifest: [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md)\n+\n+**Key principles:**\n+- **Everything is a Module** — composable, independent units\n+- **DDD-light structure** — API / Contract / Domain / Infra layers\n+- **SDK pattern** — separate `-sdk` crate for public API surface\n+- **Type-safe REST** — OperationBuilder prevents half-wired routes at compile time\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+Follow the new module guideline: [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+\n+```\n+modules/resource-group/\n+├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n+│  └─ src/\n+│     ├─ api.rs            # API trait (all methods take &SecurityCtx)\n+│     ├─ models.rs         # Transport-agnostic models\n+│     └─ errors.rs         # Transport-agnostic errors\n+└─ resource-group/               # Implementation\n+   └─ src/\n+      ├─ module.rs         # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+      ├─ local_client.rs   # Local client implementing SDK trait\n+      ├─ api/rest/         # DTOs, handlers, routes, error mapping\n+      ├─ domain/           # Business logic, events, repository traits\n+      └─ infra/storage/    # SeaORM entities, migrations\n+```\n+\n+### Code Style\n+\n+See [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md)\n+\n+- **Formatting**: `cargo fmt` with max line length 100, 4-space indentation\n+- **Linting**: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n+- **No unsafe code**: `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`\n+- **No panics**: Deny `unwrap()` and `expect()` in production code\n+- **JSON naming**: `camelCase` via `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`\n+\n+### REST API Design\n+\n+Follow the REST API guidelines: [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md)\n+\n+**Key conventions:**\n+- **Resource URLs**: Nouns, plural (`/types`, `/groups`)\n+- **Status codes**: See [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+- **Errors**: RFC-9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`)\n+- **Pagination**: Cursor-based with OData filtering (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md))\n+- **Timestamps**: ISO-8601 UTC with milliseconds (`2025-09-01T20:00:00.000Z`)\n+\n+### Error Handling\n+\n+- **Domain errors** → `src/domain/error.rs` (pure business errors)\n+- **SDK errors** → `resource-group-sdk/src/errors.rs` (transport-agnostic)\n+- **REST mapping** → `impl From<DomainError> for Problem` in `src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+- **Handler return** → `ApiResult<T>` with automatic error conversion\n+\n+### Security\n+\n+Follow security guidelines: [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+**Key requirements:**\n+- **All API methods MUST accept `&SecurityCtx`** as first parameter\n+- **Use SecureConn** for database access with automatic tenant isolation\n+- **Input validation** via `validator` crate\n+- **No secrets in code** — use environment variables\n+\n+### Database Access\n+\n+Follow secure ORM patterns: [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md)\n+\n+- **Typestate enforcement**: Unscoped queries cannot execute\n+- **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes return `WHERE 1=0`\n+- **Derive macro**: `#[derive(Scopable)]` with explicit dimension declarations\n+- **Request-scoped**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation\n+- **Closure Table**: Use closure table pattern for efficient hierarchy queries\n+\n+### Testing Strategy\n+\n+Target: **90%+ code coverage**\n+\n+- **Unit tests**: `cargo test --workspace`\n+- **Integration tests**: `make test-pg` / `make test-sqlite`\n+- **E2E tests**: `make e2e-docker` (Python/pytest)\n+- **All checks**: `make check` or `python scripts/ci.py check`\n+\n+### Observability\n+\n+Follow tracing setup: [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md)\n+\n+- **Structured logging** via `tracing` with contextual fields\n+- **Distributed tracing** with OpenTelemetry and W3C Trace Context\n+- **TracedClient** for instrumented HTTP calls\n+\n+## Important Constraints\n+\n+1. **No breaking changes** without version bump and deprecation period\n+2. **All dependencies** specified in root `Cargo.toml` (workspace inheritance)\n+3. **Feature flags** for optional functionality\n+4. **Backward compatibility**: Clients must ignore unknown fields\n+5. **Closure Table**: Must maintain closure table integrity for all hierarchy operations\n+\n+## Reference Documents\n+\n+| Document | Purpose |\n+|----------|---------|\n+| [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md) | System architecture and design principles |\n+| [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) | ModKit framework guide |\n+| [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md) | Secure database access patterns |\n+| [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md) | Observability configuration |\n+| [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) | Step-by-step module creation |\n+| [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md) | Security best practices |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md) | REST API design |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md) | HTTP status code usage |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md) | Cursor pagination spec |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) | Rust coding standards |","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md","commit_id":"5bd26c6e50dde121a95a14a891760715a1460ca7","original_commit_id":"b1d2514e3df75c96ba4d3231579b6452860a2952","user":{"login":"ffedoroff","id":1179771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk3NzE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff","html_url":"https://github.com/ffedoroff","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ffedoroff/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@/guidelines/DNA is git submodule","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:07:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:07:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704917737","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704917737"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704917737"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704917737/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":138,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2699246845,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":138,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704922394","pull_request_review_id":3678265843,"id":2704922394,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hOdca","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+# Project Context\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+This module is part of **HyperSpot** — a modular, high-performance AI services platform built in Rust.\n+\n+The Resource Group module provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control, enabling applications to organize resources in tree structures with efficient hierarchy operations.\n+\n+## Tech Stack\n+\n+- **Language**: Rust (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md))\n+- **Framework**: ModKit (see [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md))\n+- **HTTP**: Axum with `tower-http` middleware\n+- **Database**: SeaORM / SQLx with secure ORM layer (see [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md))\n+- **Observability**: `tracing` + OpenTelemetry (see [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md))\n+- **OpenAPI**: `utoipa` for automatic documentation generation\n+- **IDs**: UUIDv7 for all identifiers\n+- **Time**: `chrono` with UTC timestamps\n+\n+## Project Conventions\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+Follow the architecture manifest: [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md)\n+\n+**Key principles:**\n+- **Everything is a Module** — composable, independent units\n+- **DDD-light structure** — API / Contract / Domain / Infra layers\n+- **SDK pattern** — separate `-sdk` crate for public API surface\n+- **Type-safe REST** — OperationBuilder prevents half-wired routes at compile time\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+Follow the new module guideline: [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+\n+```\n+modules/resource-group/\n+├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n+│  └─ src/\n+│     ├─ api.rs            # API trait (all methods take &SecurityCtx)\n+│     ├─ models.rs         # Transport-agnostic models\n+│     └─ errors.rs         # Transport-agnostic errors\n+└─ resource-group/               # Implementation\n+   └─ src/\n+      ├─ module.rs         # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+      ├─ local_client.rs   # Local client implementing SDK trait\n+      ├─ api/rest/         # DTOs, handlers, routes, error mapping\n+      ├─ domain/           # Business logic, events, repository traits\n+      └─ infra/storage/    # SeaORM entities, migrations\n+```\n+\n+### Code Style\n+\n+See [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md)\n+\n+- **Formatting**: `cargo fmt` with max line length 100, 4-space indentation\n+- **Linting**: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n+- **No unsafe code**: `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`\n+- **No panics**: Deny `unwrap()` and `expect()` in production code\n+- **JSON naming**: `camelCase` via `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`\n+\n+### REST API Design\n+\n+Follow the REST API guidelines: [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md)\n+\n+**Key conventions:**\n+- **Resource URLs**: Nouns, plural (`/types`, `/groups`)\n+- **Status codes**: See [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+- **Errors**: RFC-9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`)\n+- **Pagination**: Cursor-based with OData filtering (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md))\n+- **Timestamps**: ISO-8601 UTC with milliseconds (`2025-09-01T20:00:00.000Z`)\n+\n+### Error Handling\n+\n+- **Domain errors** → `src/domain/error.rs` (pure business errors)\n+- **SDK errors** → `resource-group-sdk/src/errors.rs` (transport-agnostic)\n+- **REST mapping** → `impl From<DomainError> for Problem` in `src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+- **Handler return** → `ApiResult<T>` with automatic error conversion\n+\n+### Security\n+\n+Follow security guidelines: [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+**Key requirements:**\n+- **All API methods MUST accept `&SecurityCtx`** as first parameter\n+- **Use SecureConn** for database access with automatic tenant isolation\n+- **Input validation** via `validator` crate\n+- **No secrets in code** — use environment variables\n+\n+### Database Access\n+\n+Follow secure ORM patterns: [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md)\n+\n+- **Typestate enforcement**: Unscoped queries cannot execute\n+- **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes return `WHERE 1=0`\n+- **Derive macro**: `#[derive(Scopable)]` with explicit dimension declarations\n+- **Request-scoped**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation\n+- **Closure Table**: Use closure table pattern for efficient hierarchy queries\n+\n+### Testing Strategy\n+\n+Target: **90%+ code coverage**\n+\n+- **Unit tests**: `cargo test --workspace`\n+- **Integration tests**: `make test-pg` / `make test-sqlite`\n+- **E2E tests**: `make e2e-docker` (Python/pytest)\n+- **All checks**: `make check` or `python scripts/ci.py check`\n+\n+### Observability\n+\n+Follow tracing setup: [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md)\n+\n+- **Structured logging** via `tracing` with contextual fields\n+- **Distributed tracing** with OpenTelemetry and W3C Trace Context\n+- **TracedClient** for instrumented HTTP calls\n+\n+## Important Constraints\n+\n+1. **No breaking changes** without version bump and deprecation period\n+2. **All dependencies** specified in root `Cargo.toml` (workspace inheritance)\n+3. **Feature flags** for optional functionality\n+4. **Backward compatibility**: Clients must ignore unknown fields\n+5. **Closure Table**: Must maintain closure table integrity for all hierarchy operations\n+\n+## Reference Documents\n+\n+| Document | Purpose |\n+|----------|---------|\n+| [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md) | System architecture and design principles |\n+| [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) | ModKit framework guide |\n+| [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md) | Secure database access patterns |\n+| [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md) | Observability configuration |\n+| [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) | Step-by-step module creation |\n+| [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md) | Security best practices |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md) | REST API design |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md) | HTTP status code usage |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md) | Cursor pagination spec |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) | Rust coding standards |","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md","commit_id":"5bd26c6e50dde121a95a14a891760715a1460ca7","original_commit_id":"b1d2514e3df75c96ba4d3231579b6452860a2952","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify that guidelines/DNA is indeed configured as a git submodule\necho \"=== Checking .gitmodules file ===\"\nif [ -f .gitmodules ]; then\n  cat .gitmodules\nelse\n  echo \".gitmodules not found\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking git submodule status ===\"\ngit submodule status 2>&1 || echo \"No submodules or not in git repo\"\n```\n\nLength of output: 222\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@ffedoroff`, thank you for the clarification! You're absolutely right—I can confirm that `guidelines/DNA` is indeed configured as a git submodule pointing to `https://github.com/hypernetix/DNA`.\n\nThe empty directory I found was because the sandbox environment doesn't initialize submodules during shallow clones. All the referenced documentation paths in `project.md` are valid and will work correctly in a proper repository checkout.\n\n**My apologies for the false alarm!** The documentation references are fine and don't need any changes.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Learnings added</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: ffedoroff\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 265\nFile: modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md:1-138\nTimestamp: 2026-01-19T14:08:28.751Z\nLearning: In the hypernetix/hyperspot repository, `guidelines/DNA` is a git submodule pointing to https://github.com/hypernetix/DNA. References to files under `@/guidelines/DNA/` (such as `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`, etc.) are valid and should not be flagged as missing.\n```\n\n> Note: Learnings are effective only in the context of similar code segments. To apply general coding guidelines, please configure [review instructions](https://docs.coderabbit.ai/guides/review-instructions). You can manage existing learnings in the [app](https://app.coderabbit.ai/learnings).\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Always consult project-wide resources in `guidelines/` directory for project conventions and best practices\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md` to learn about the project's `@/lib/modkit`* unified system\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Always consult `guidelines/DNA/` for REST API design patterns and architectural principles\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always follow the guidelines specified in `@/guidelines/README.md`\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: When a request mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan), or introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work, open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Scaffold `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md` to learn about how to create a new module\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/spec.md : When using MODIFIED Requirements, paste the full, updated requirement content (header + all scenarios); partial deltas will drop previous details at archive time\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED|RENAMED Requirements` section headers in delta spec files with at least one `#### Scenario:` per requirement\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:08:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:08:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704922394","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704922394"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704922394"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704922394/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":138,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2699246845,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":138,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704925029","pull_request_review_id":3675420077,"id":2704925029,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hOeFl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"5bd26c6e50dde121a95a14a891760715a1460ca7","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The specification describes reference counting functionality (\"increments reference count for the group\") but the database schema section (lines 231-262) does not include a `reference_count` field in the `resource_group` table. This will cause implementation failure.\n\n**Fix**: Add a reference count column to the schema:\n```markdown\n**`resource_group`:**\n- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n- `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n- `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n- `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n- `reference_count`: Integer (default 0)\n- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/265?chatWithGeneratedComment=f11448a8-593d-49ee-a6b9-97540cfcbd3a\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:09:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:09:04Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704925029","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704925029"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704925029"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704925029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":175,"original_start_line":145,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":176,"original_line":146,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":146,"position":176,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704929316","pull_request_review_id":3678273848,"id":2704929316,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hOfIk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,113 @@\n+# Tasks: Resource Group Module\n+\n+## 1. SDK Crate Setup\n+\n+- [ ] 1.1 Create `resource-group-sdk/Cargo.toml` with minimal dependencies\n+- [ ] 1.2 Create SDK structure: `api.rs`, `models.rs`, `errors.rs`, `lib.rs`\n+- [ ] 1.3 Define `ResourceGroupApi` trait with all methods taking `&SecurityCtx`","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"5bd26c6e50dde121a95a14a891760715a1460ca7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for SecurityCtx vs SecurityContext usage in the codebase\necho \"=== SecurityCtx usage (Rust files) ===\"\nrg -n \"SecurityCtx\" --type rust | head -30\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== SecurityContext usage (Rust files) ===\"\nrg -n \"SecurityContext\" --type rust | head -30\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== All files containing SecurityCtx ===\"\nrg -l \"SecurityCtx\" | head -20\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== All files containing SecurityContext ===\"\nrg -l \"SecurityContext\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 9128\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check the actual SecurityContext type definition\necho \"=== SecurityContext type definition in modkit-security ===\"\nrg -A 5 \"pub (struct|type) SecurityContext\" libs/modkit-security/src/\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check if SecurityCtx is an alias ===\"\nrg \"type SecurityCtx|pub use.*SecurityCtx\" --type rust\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check imports in tenant_resolver (uses SecurityContext) ===\"\nhead -20 modules/system/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-sdk/src/plugin_api.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1773\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Change `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext` to match the actual type from the codebase.**\n\nThe actual security context type defined in `libs/modkit-security/src/context.rs` is `SecurityContext`, not `SecurityCtx`. Update line 7 to use the correct type name.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\nat line 7, Update the Task list entry that defines the ResourceGroupApi trait so\nit references the correct type name: change any occurrences of SecurityCtx to\nSecurityContext (e.g., \"Define `ResourceGroupApi` trait with all methods taking\n`&SecurityContext`\") so the task matches the actual type in\nlibs/modkit-security; ensure every method signature mention uses\n&SecurityContext consistently.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T14:09:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T14:09:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704929316","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704929316"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2704929316"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704929316/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":7,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705354233","pull_request_review_id":3678782940,"id":2705354233,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hQG35","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+# Project Context\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+This module is part of **HyperSpot** — a modular, high-performance AI services platform built in Rust.\n+\n+The Resource Group module provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control, enabling applications to organize resources in tree structures with efficient hierarchy operations.\n+\n+## Tech Stack\n+\n+- **Language**: Rust (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md))\n+- **Framework**: ModKit (see [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md))\n+- **HTTP**: Axum with `tower-http` middleware\n+- **Database**: SeaORM / SQLx with secure ORM layer (see [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md))\n+- **Observability**: `tracing` + OpenTelemetry (see [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md))\n+- **OpenAPI**: `utoipa` for automatic documentation generation\n+- **IDs**: UUIDv7 for all identifiers\n+- **Time**: `chrono` with UTC timestamps\n+\n+## Project Conventions\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+Follow the architecture manifest: [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md)\n+\n+**Key principles:**\n+- **Everything is a Module** — composable, independent units\n+- **DDD-light structure** — API / Contract / Domain / Infra layers\n+- **SDK pattern** — separate `-sdk` crate for public API surface\n+- **Type-safe REST** — OperationBuilder prevents half-wired routes at compile time\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+Follow the new module guideline: [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+\n+```\n+modules/resource-group/\n+├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n+│  └─ src/\n+│     ├─ api.rs            # API trait (all methods take &SecurityCtx)\n+│     ├─ models.rs         # Transport-agnostic models\n+│     └─ errors.rs         # Transport-agnostic errors\n+└─ resource-group/               # Implementation\n+   └─ src/\n+      ├─ module.rs         # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+      ├─ local_client.rs   # Local client implementing SDK trait\n+      ├─ api/rest/         # DTOs, handlers, routes, error mapping\n+      ├─ domain/           # Business logic, events, repository traits\n+      └─ infra/storage/    # SeaORM entities, migrations\n+```","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"c698c5e7b14d5c0ef70b66f5744468ce30fe6b6a","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Add language identifier to fenced code block.**\n\nThe fenced code block is missing a language identifier. For directory structure visualizations, use `text` or `plaintext` to improve rendering and accessibility.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n modules/resource-group/\n ├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n36-36: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md` around lines 36 - 50, The\nfenced directory listing block starting with \"modules/resource-group/\" (showing\nresource-group-sdk/, resource-group/, module.rs, local_client.rs, etc.) lacks a\nlanguage identifier; add a language tag like \"text\" (e.g., ```text) to the\nopening fence so the directory structure renders correctly and improves\naccessibility.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T16:08:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T16:08:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2705354233","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705354233"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2705354233"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2705354233/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":36,"original_start_line":36,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":50,"original_line":50,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":50,"position":50,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191917","pull_request_review_id":3679746239,"id":2706191917,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hTTYt","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Clarify case-insensitive enforcement mechanism for type codes.**\n\nThe spec states type codes are \"case-insensitive\" but doesn't specify the enforcement mechanism. Implementers need to know:\n- Should codes be normalized to lowercase on storage?\n- Should a case-insensitive unique constraint/index be used?\n- Should queries use `LOWER()` for comparison?\n\nWithout this detail, different implementations may handle `\"Department\"` vs. `\"DEPARTMENT\"` inconsistently.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\nAdd to line 8:\n```diff\n-- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace); stored in lowercase, uniqueness enforced case-insensitively\n```\n\nAnd update the schema section (line 255):\n```diff\n-**`resource_group_type`:**\n-- `code` (PK): String, unique, case-insensitive\n+**`resource_group_type`:**\n+- `code` (PK): String (lowercase, unique)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\nat line 8, The spec's \"Code: Unique identifier\" entry needs an explicit\ncase-insensitivity policy: state that type codes MUST be normalized to lowercase\nbefore storage and that implementations MUST enforce uniqueness via either a\ncase-insensitive unique index (e.g., UNIQUE INDEX on LOWER(code) or a\ncase-insensitive collation) so \"Department\" and \"DEPARTMENT\" collide; update the\nschema section to show the persisted column is stored lowercased (or include DB\nexample using UNIQUE(LOWER(code))) and add a note that queries MUST compare\ncodes using LOWER(code) (or use case-insensitive collation) so lookups and\nconstraints behave consistently across implementations.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191917","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191917"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191917"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191917/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":8,"original_line":8,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":8,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191919","pull_request_review_id":3679746239,"id":2706191919,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hTTYv","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add scenario for type deletion validation.**\n\nThe requirement states \"Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\" but no scenario demonstrates this validation.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested scenario</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Prevent deletion of type with existing entities\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with at least one entity\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete the type\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeInUse`\n\n#### Scenario: Delete type with no entities\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `ARCHIVED_TYPE` with zero entities\n- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_type` for `ARCHIVED_TYPE`\n- **THEN** the system deletes the type\n- **AND** returns success\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\nat line 18, The spec is missing scenarios validating type-deletion rules; add\ntests covering both failure and success cases: include a \"Prevent deletion of\ntype with existing entities\" scenario that creates a type (e.g., DEPARTMENT)\nwith at least one entity, calls delete_type, and expects\nResourceGroupError::TypeInUse, and a \"Delete type with no entities\" scenario\nthat ensures a type (e.g., ARCHIVED_TYPE) with zero entities is deleted\nsuccessfully when delete_type is called and returns success.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191919","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191919"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191919"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191919/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":18,"original_line":18,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":18,"position":18,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191920","pull_request_review_id":3679746239,"id":2706191920,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hTTYw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Clarify update vs. move operation boundaries.**\n\nLines 57-58 list \"Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\" and \"Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\" as separate operations, but it's unclear:\n- Can `parent_id` be updated via the generic update operation?\n- Must parent changes always use `move_entity`?\n- What happens if someone tries to update `parent_id` directly?\n\nThis ambiguity could lead to inconsistent implementations.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\nUpdate lines 57-58:\n```diff\n-- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id; parent_id is read-only)\n - Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n```\n\nAnd add a scenario:\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject direct parent_id update\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with parent `old-parent-id`\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to update `parent_id` to `new-parent-id` via `update_entity`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` indicating parent_id cannot be updated directly\n- **AND** directs user to use `move_entity` operation\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 54 - 60, Clarify that parent changes are not allowed via the\ngeneric update path: update the spec to state that update_entity only modifies\nproperties like name and external_id and must reject attempts to change\nparent_id, and add the explicit scenario rejecting direct parent_id updates;\nrequire callers to use move_entity for subtree/parent changes and specify the\nerror returned (ResourceGroupError::Validation with guidance to use move_entity)\nwhen update_entity detects a parent_id change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191920","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191920"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191920"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191920/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":54,"original_start_line":54,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":60,"original_line":60,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":60,"position":60,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191922","pull_request_review_id":3679746239,"id":2706191922,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hTTYy","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: References Plugin (Optional)\n+\n+**Condition**: This requirement applies ONLY when the **References Plugin** is enabled/connected.\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an optional plugin to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Plugin connected\n+- **GIVEN** the References Plugin is connected\n+- **WHEN** the module initializes\n+- **THEN** the `resource_group_reference` table is created via migrations\n+- **AND** reference management endpoints are registered\n+- **AND** group deletion logic checks for active references\n+\n+#### Scenario: Plugin NOT connected\n+- **GIVEN** the References Plugin is NOT connected\n+- **WHEN** the module initializes\n+- **THEN** the `resource_group_reference` table is NOT created\n+- **AND** reference management endpoints are NOT exposed\n+- **AND** API/Service has no knowledge of references\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: REST API Endpoints\n+\n+The system SHALL expose REST API endpoints for resource group operations.\n+Base path: `/resource-group/v1`\n+\n+#### Resource Group Types\n+- `POST /types` - Create a new type\n+- `GET /types` - List all types\n+- `GET /types/{code}` - Get a specific type\n+- `PUT /types/{code}` - Update a type\n+- `DELETE /types/{code}` - Delete a type\n+\n+#### Resource Group Entities\n+- `POST /groups` - Create a new entity\n+- `GET /groups/{id}` - Get a specific entity\n+- `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update an entity\n+- `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete an entity\n+- `GET /groups/{id}/ancestors` - Get all ancestors\n+- `GET /groups/{id}/descendants` - Get all descendants","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"44ee240b5140f4d19e4d60d9af9adefcfd284404","original_commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n**Critical: Missing GET /groups list endpoint definition.**\n\nThe scenario at lines 242-246 references `GET /resource-group/v1/groups` for listing entities, but the endpoint list (lines 217-223) only defines `GET /groups/{id}` for retrieving a single entity. The list endpoint is missing from the specification.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Required fix</summary>\n\nAdd the list endpoint to the entity endpoints section:\n\n```diff\n #### Resource Group Entities\n - `POST /groups` - Create a new entity\n+- `GET /groups` - List entities (with pagination and filtering)\n - `GET /groups/{id}` - Get a specific entity\n - `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update an entity\n - `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete an entity\n - `GET /groups/{id}/ancestors` - Get all ancestors\n - `GET /groups/{id}/descendants` - Get all descendants\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 217 - 223, The Resource Group Entities list is missing the list\nendpoint referenced elsewhere; update the entities section to include the\ncollection GET endpoint (e.g., add \"GET /resource-group/v1/groups\" or the\nconsistent \"GET /groups\" entry) so it matches the scenario that calls GET\n/resource-group/v1/groups; edit the Resource Group Entities block (the list\ncontaining POST /groups, GET /groups/{id}, PUT /groups/{id}, DELETE\n/groups/{id}, GET /groups/{id}/ancestors, GET /groups/{id}/descendants) and\ninsert the list endpoint with a brief description like \"List entities\" to keep\nthe spec consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191922","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191922"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191922"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191922/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":221,"original_start_line":217,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":227,"original_line":223,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":223,"position":227,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191923","pull_request_review_id":3679746239,"id":2706191923,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hTTYz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,293 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: References Plugin (Optional)\n+\n+**Condition**: This requirement applies ONLY when the **References Plugin** is enabled/connected.\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an optional plugin to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Plugin connected\n+- **GIVEN** the References Plugin is connected\n+- **WHEN** the module initializes\n+- **THEN** the `resource_group_reference` table is created via migrations\n+- **AND** reference management endpoints are registered\n+- **AND** group deletion logic checks for active references\n+\n+#### Scenario: Plugin NOT connected\n+- **GIVEN** the References Plugin is NOT connected\n+- **WHEN** the module initializes\n+- **THEN** the `resource_group_reference` table is NOT created\n+- **AND** reference management endpoints are NOT exposed\n+- **AND** API/Service has no knowledge of references\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+- **GIVEN** References Plugin is connected\n+- **AND** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: REST API Endpoints\n+\n+The system SHALL expose REST API endpoints for resource group operations.\n+Base path: `/resource-group/v1`\n+\n+#### Resource Group Types\n+- `POST /types` - Create a new type\n+- `GET /types` - List all types\n+- `GET /types/{code}` - Get a specific type\n+- `PUT /types/{code}` - Update a type\n+- `DELETE /types/{code}` - Delete a type\n+\n+#### Resource Group Entities\n+- `POST /groups` - Create a new entity\n+- `GET /groups/{id}` - Get a specific entity\n+- `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update an entity\n+- `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete an entity\n+- `GET /groups/{id}/ancestors` - Get all ancestors\n+- `GET /groups/{id}/descendants` - Get all descendants\n+\n+#### Resource Group References (Plugin-only)\n+**Condition**: Available ONLY if References Plugin is connected.\n+\n+- `POST /groups/{id}/references` - Create a reference\n+- `DELETE /groups/{id}/references` - Delete a reference\n+\n+All endpoints SHALL:\n+- Require authentication (Bearer token)\n+- Return RFC-9457 Problem Details for errors\n+- Follow HyperSpot REST API conventions\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create type via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid JSON payload with type data\n+- **WHEN** POST request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/types`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type and returns `201 Created` with location header\n+\n+#### Scenario: List entities via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n+- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- **THEN** response contains entities\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Database Schema\n+\n+The system SHALL use SeaORM with the following tables:\n+\n+**`resource_group_type`:**\n+- `code` (PK): String, unique, case-insensitive\n+- `parents`: JSON array of type codes\n+- `application_id`: UUID (owner)\n+- `allowed_app_ids`: JSON array of UUIDs\n+- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n+\n+**`resource_group`:**\n+- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n+- `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n+- `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n+- `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n+\n+**`resource_group_closure`:**\n+- `parent_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id`\n+- `child_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id`\n+- `depth`: Integer (0 for self-reference)\n+- Composite PK: `(parent_id, child_id)`\n+- Indexes on `parent_id`, `child_id`, `depth`\n+\n+**`resource_group_reference` (Plugin-only):**\n+- **Condition**: Table exists ONLY if References Plugin is connected.\n+- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n+- `group_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id`\n+- `resource_type`: String\n+- `resource_id`: String\n+- `application_id`: UUID\n+- `created_at`: Timestamp\n+- Composite index on `(resource_type, resource_id)`","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"504144d9ffd7dee95e88fca15093e91805866ec6","original_commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Specify foreign key cascade behavior.**\n\nThe schema defines multiple foreign keys but doesn't specify cascade behavior:\n- `resource_group.type_code` → `resource_group_type.code`: What happens on type deletion?\n- `resource_group_closure` foreign keys: Should they cascade delete?\n- `resource_group_reference.group_id`: Should references cascade delete?\n\nThis could lead to implementation inconsistencies or runtime errors.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested additions</summary>\n\nAdd cascade specifications:\n\n```markdown\n**Foreign Key Constraints:**\n- `resource_group.type_code` → `resource_group_type.code` (ON DELETE RESTRICT)\n- `resource_group_closure.parent_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- `resource_group_closure.child_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- `resource_group_reference.group_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE or RESTRICT based on plugin behavior)\n```\n\nNote: The type FK should RESTRICT to enforce the \"can't delete type with entities\" rule at DB level.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 254 - 283, The schema is missing explicit ON DELETE behavior for\nseveral FKs; update the spec to declare cascade rules: set\nresource_group.type_code → resource_group_type.code to ON DELETE RESTRICT\n(prevent deleting a type that still has groups), set\nresource_group_closure.parent_id → resource_group.id and\nresource_group_closure.child_id → resource_group.id to ON DELETE CASCADE (so\nclosure rows are removed when a group is deleted), and specify\nresource_group_reference.group_id → resource_group.id as either ON DELETE\nCASCADE (if plugin references should be removed with the group) or ON DELETE\nRESTRICT (if you want to prevent deletion while references exist) and document\nthe chosen behavior in the spec.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191923","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191923"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2706191923"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2706191923/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":254,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":283,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":283,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2713208507","pull_request_review_id":3687997951,"id":2713208507,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6huEa7","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,391 @@\n+# Feature Design: Resource Group\n+\n+## A. Feature Context\n+\n+**Feature ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group`\n+**Status**: IN_DESIGN\n+\n+### 1. Overview\n+The Resource Group module provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control. It enables applications to organize resources in a tree structure with strict type validation, permission management, and efficient hierarchy operations using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+### 2. Purpose\n+To allow applications to model complex organizational structures (e.g., Organization -> Department -> Team) and enforce permissions and constraints based on these structures.\n+\n+### 3. Actors\n+- `fdd-hyperspot-actor-application`\n+- `fdd-hyperspot-actor-system-admin`\n+\n+### 4. References\n+- [Overall Design](../../DESIGN.md)\n+- [ADR-0001: Closure Table](../../ADR.md)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## B. Actor Flows\n+\n+### Create Resource Group Type\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-flow-create-type`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **Actor** provides type code, allowed parents, and allowed app IDs - `inst-provide-data`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** validates type code format (no whitespace, length limit) - `inst-validate-format`\n+3. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** checks if type code already exists - `inst-check-duplicate`\n+4. [ ] - `ph-1` - **IF** type exists: - `inst-check-exists`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** returns error `TypeAlreadyExists` - `inst-err-duplicate`\n+   2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **RETURN** - `inst-ret-duplicate`\n+5. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** creates new type record with current app as owner - `inst-create-record`\n+6. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** returns created type - `inst-return-success`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### Create Resource Group Entity\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-flow-create-entity`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **Actor** provides name, type code, and optional parent ID - `inst-provide-data`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** validates actor has permission to create entity of this type - `inst-validate-perm`\n+3. [ ] - `ph-1` - **IF** parent ID is provided: - `inst-check-parent`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** fetches parent entity - `inst-fetch-parent`\n+   2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** validates parent type is allowed for this entity type - `inst-validate-parent-type`\n+   3. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** checks hierarchy depth constraints (`max_depth`) - `inst-check-depth`\n+   4. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** checks hierarchy width constraints (`max_width`) - `inst-check-width`\n+4. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** creates entity record - `inst-create-entity`\n+5. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** inserts closure table entries (self + ancestors) - `inst-insert-closure`\n+6. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** returns created entity - `inst-return-success`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### Move Entity Subtree\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-flow-move-entity`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+1. [ ] - `ph-2` - **Actor** requests to move entity `node-id` to `new-parent-id` - `inst-req-move`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** validates `new-parent-id` exists and is valid parent type - `inst-validate-parent`\n+3. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** checks for cycles (is `new-parent-id` a descendant of `node-id`?) - `inst-check-cycle`\n+4. [ ] - `ph-2` - **IF** cycle detected: - `inst-if-cycle`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** returns error `CycleDetected` - `inst-err-cycle`\n+   2. [ ] - `ph-2` - **RETURN** - `inst-ret-cycle`\n+5. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** validates new depth constraints for entire subtree - `inst-validate-depth`\n+6. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** updates closure table (delete old paths, insert new paths) - `inst-update-closure`\n+7. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** updates `parent_id` on entity - `inst-update-entity`\n+8. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** returns success - `inst-return-success`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### Manage References\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-flow-manage-refs`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+1. [ ] - `ph-3` - **Actor** links group to external resource - `inst-link-ref`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-3` - **System** stores reference and increments counter - `inst-store-ref`\n+3. [ ] - `ph-3` - **IF** **Actor** tries to delete group with refs: - `inst-check-delete`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-3` - **System** returns error `GroupHasReferences` - `inst-err-refs`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+---\n+\n+## C. Algorithms\n+\n+### Closure Table Insert\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-algo-closure-insert`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+**Input**: `node_id`, `parent_id`\n+\n+1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** inserts self-reference: `(node_id, node_id, 0)` - `inst-insert-self`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **IF** `parent_id` is NOT NULL: - `inst-check-parent`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** selects all ancestors of `parent_id` (including `parent_id` itself) - `inst-select-ancestors`\n+   2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **FOR EACH** ancestor `a` in ancestors: - `inst-loop-ancestors`\n+      1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **System** insert `(a.parent_id, node_id, a.depth + 1)` - `inst-insert-path`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### Cycle Detection\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-algo-cycle-detection`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+**Input**: `node_id`, `target_parent_id`\n+\n+1. [ ] - `ph-2` - **System** queries closure table for path from `node_id` to `target_parent_id` - `inst-query-path`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-2` - **IF** path exists (meaning `target_parent_id` is descendant of `node_id`): - `inst-check-path`\n+   1. [ ] - `ph-2` - **RETURN** `true` (Cycle Detected) - `inst-ret-true`\n+3. [ ] - `ph-2` - **RETURN** `false` - `inst-ret-false`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+---\n+\n+## D. States\n+\n+### Entity Lifecycle\n+\n+- [ ] **ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-feature-resource-group-state-entity`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+1. [ ] - `ph-1` - **WHEN** entity created -> **Active** - `inst-state-active`\n+2. [ ] - `ph-1` - **WHEN** entity deleted -> **Deleted** (removed from DB) - `inst-state-deleted`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+---\n+\n+## E. Technical Details\n+\n+### Database Schema\n+\n+**Tables**:\n+1. `resource_group_type`\n+   - `code` (PK): String\n+   - `parents`: JSON\n+   - `application_id`: UUID\n+   - `allowed_app_ids`: JSON\n+2. `resource_group`\n+   - `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n+   - `type_code` (FK): String\n+   - `parent_id`: UUID (nullable)\n+   - `name`: String\n+3. `resource_group_closure`\n+   - `parent_id` (FK): UUID\n+   - `child_id` (FK): UUID\n+   - `depth`: Integer\n+   - PK: `(parent_id, child_id)`\n+\n+**References**:\n+- [Secure ORM](../../../../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md)\n+\n+### API Endpoints\n+\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/types`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types`\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants`","path":"modules/system/resource-group/architecture/features/feature-resource-group/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"1a62e9b42e78549aa82ce21a931acad14862984f","original_commit_id":"2efe1791f65d7ad36e8603c202455bc705ad6921","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Incomplete API endpoint list in DESIGN.md.**\n\nThe API endpoints section is missing several operations that are defined in the spec.md:\n- `GET /groups` - List all entities (referenced in spec scenarios)\n- `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update entity (mentioned in requirements at line 57)\n- `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete entity (mentioned in requirements at line 59)\n- `PUT /types/{code}` - Update type (mentioned in spec line 226)\n- `DELETE /types/{code}` - Delete type (mentioned in spec line 227)\n\nThis inconsistency between DESIGN.md and the spec.md could confuse implementers.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Complete endpoint list</summary>\n\nUpdate the API Endpoints section to match spec.md:\n\n```diff\n ### API Endpoints\n \n+#### Resource Group Types\n - `POST /resource-group/v1/types`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/types`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+\n+#### Resource Group Entities\n - `POST /resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants`\n+\n+#### Resource Group References\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/architecture/features/feature-resource-group/DESIGN.md`\naround lines 149 - 156, The API endpoints list in DESIGN.md is incomplete;\nupdate the \"API Endpoints\" section to include the missing operations required by\nspec.md by adding the following routes: GET /resource-group/v1/groups (list all\nentities), PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id} (update entity), DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id} (delete entity), PUT\n/resource-group/v1/types/{code} (update type) and DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/types/{code} (delete type) so the DESIGN.md endpoint list\nmatches the spec and referenced scenarios/requirements.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-21T15:53:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T15:53:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2713208507","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2713208507"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2713208507"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2713208507/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":149,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":156,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":156,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2715931451","pull_request_review_id":3691321473,"id":2715931451,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6h4dM7","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@\n+# Overall Design: Resource Group\n+\n+## A. Architecture Overview\n+\n+**Architectural Vision**:\n+The Resource Group module is designed as a core structural component of the Hyperspot platform. It provides a flexible, type-safe way to organize resources into hierarchies, which serves as the backbone for access control, visibility, and organizational modeling.\n+\n+The architecture emphasizes read performance for hierarchy traversals, as these operations are on the critical path for every permission check. By isolating the hierarchy logic into a dedicated module with a specialized storage pattern (Closure Table), we ensure that structural queries remain performant even as the dataset grows.\n+\n+**Architecture Layers**:\n+- **API Layer**: REST/gRPC endpoints for managing groups and types.\n+- **Service Layer**: Implements business logic, type validation, and cycle detection.\n+- **Domain Layer**: Defines core entities (ResourceGroup, ResourceGroupType).\n+- **Infrastructure Layer**: Handles database persistence using Secure ORM and Closure Table operations.\n+\n+## B. Requirements & Principles\n+\n+### 1. Functional Requirements\n+\n+#### Resource Organization Management\n+\n+**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-req-resource-org`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+The system MUST provide capabilities to create, update, move, and delete resource groups within a strict type hierarchy.\n+\n+**Capabilities**: `fdd-hyperspot-capability-resource-organization`\n+**Actors**: `fdd-hyperspot-actor-application`, `fdd-hyperspot-actor-system-admin`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### 2. Non-Functional Requirements\n+\n+#### Performance\n+\n+**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-nfr-performance`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+Hierarchy queries (ancestors/descendants) MUST complete in under 10ms for trees up to 10 levels deep.\n+\n+**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-closure-table`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### 3. Design Principles\n+\n+#### Efficient Read Operations\n+\n+**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-principle-efficient-reads`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+The system architecture MUST prioritize read performance for hierarchy operations over write performance, as reads (permission checks) occur much more frequently than writes (structure changes).\n+\n+**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-closure-table`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+### 4. Constraints\n+\n+#### Database Independence\n+\n+**ID**: `fdd-hyperspot-constraint-db-independence`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+The implementation MUST NOT rely on proprietary database features (like Oracle CONNECT BY) and MUST work with standard SQL supported by SeaORM.\n+\n+**ADRs**: `fdd-hyperspot-adr-closure-table`\n+<!-- fdd-id-content -->\n+\n+## C. Technical Architecture\n+\n+### C.1: Domain Model\n+\n+**Component Diagram**:\n+```mermaid\n+graph TD\n+    API[API Layer] --> Service[Service Layer]\n+    Service --> Repo[Repository]\n+    Repo --> DB[(Database)]\n+```\n+\n+**Components**:\n+- **ResourceGroupService**: Manages group lifecycle and hierarchy operations.\n+- **TypeRegistry**: Validates type constraints and parent-child rules.\n+- **ClosureTableManager**: Low-level helper for maintaining the closure table.\n+\n+### C.2: Domain Model","path":"modules/system/resource-group/architecture/DESIGN.md","commit_id":"1a62e9b42e78549aa82ce21a931acad14862984f","original_commit_id":"1a62e9b42e78549aa82ce21a931acad14862984f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix duplicate section heading.**\n\nBoth Line 65 and Line 80 use the heading \"Domain Model\". Line 65 is labeled \"C.1: Domain Model\" but contains the component diagram, while Line 80 is labeled \"C.2: Domain Model\" and contains the actual domain model content. This creates confusion about the document structure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-### C.1: Domain Model\n+### C.1: Component Diagram\n\n **Component Diagram**:\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/architecture/DESIGN.md` around lines 65 - 80,\nThe document has duplicate \"Domain Model\" headings (C.1: Domain Model and C.2:\nDomain Model) causing confusion; rename the first heading (C.1: Domain Model) to\na distinct title such as \"C.1: Component Diagram\" or \"C.1: Architecture\nOverview\" to reflect that it contains the component diagram and list of\ncomponents (ResourceGroupService, TypeRegistry, ClosureTableManager), leaving\nC.2 as \"Domain Model\" for the actual model content so the structure is clear.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-22T08:58:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T08:58:06Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2715931451","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2715931451"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#discussion_r2715931451"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2715931451/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":65,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":80,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":80,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3671792505,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7a2xt5","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`:\n- Line 37: The \"Affected code\" path string in the proposal.md is incorrect:\nupdate the path value currently listed as `modules/resource-group/` to the\nactual location `modules/system/resource-group/` so the document reflects the\nreal module path; edit the affected line in\nmodules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md\nwhere the \"**Affected code**\" entry contains `modules/resource-group/` and\nreplace it with `modules/system/resource-group/`.\n- Around line 5-7: Update the proposal text to remove the incorrect \"symlink\"\nclaim and accurately describe the current `resource-group` directory state and\nmigration plan: replace \"The current `resource-group` directory is a symlink to\nan old repository with a different architecture.\" with a sentence that states\nthe directory is a regular directory containing the legacy implementation,\nspecify that it follows a different architecture than HyperSpot/ModKit, and\nbriefly outline that the change is to rebuild it as a proper HyperSpot/ModKit\nmodule following the SDK pattern and DDD-light architecture (reference\n`proposal.md` and the `resource-group` directory name to locate the statement).\n\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`:\n- Around line 1-138: The document references four missing guideline files\n(`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`,\n`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`, and `@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`)\ncausing broken links in modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md;\neither create those markdown files with the expected content (matching the\nreferenced subjects and naming) or edit project.md to replace/remove those\ninvalid references and point to existing docs in the repo; update the references\nin project.md (search for the exact tokens `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`,\n`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`, `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`,\n`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`) so the file contains only valid paths\nbefore approving.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`36-36`: **Clarify \"new capability\" terminology.**\n\nThe phrasing \"Affected specs: `resource-group` (new capability)\" is ambiguous. Does this mean a new spec is being created, or that the module adds a new capability to an existing spec? Consider rewording for clarity.\n\n\n\nExample:\n- If creating a new spec: \"**New specs**: `resource-group`\"\n- If adding capability: \"**Affected specs**: None (introduces new `resource-group` spec)\"\n\n---\n\n`39-39`: **Clarify database compatibility requirements.**\n\nThe proposal states \"Requires PostgreSQL/SQLite\" but doesn't clarify whether both databases are fully supported, or if there are feature differences. Consider specifying:\n- Are both databases equally supported?\n- Does the Closure Table pattern work identically on both?\n- Are there any database-specific considerations?\n\n---\n\n`1-40`: **Solid proposal foundation; consider adding implementation details.**\n\nThe proposal effectively communicates the motivation, architecture, and impact of the new Resource Group module. The technical approach (SDK/Module split, Closure Table pattern, SecurityCtx integration) is sound and follows HyperSpot conventions.\n\nBased on learnings, this aligns well with the OpenSpec workflow for change proposals.\n\nOptional enhancements to consider (can be deferred to `tasks.md` or `design.md`):\n- Timeline or implementation phases\n- Testing strategy (unit, integration, hierarchy queries)\n- API versioning approach\n- Migration strategy details for existing symlink\n- Error handling and validation rules\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 949b3e840c1742bd1fb0de560223f63642ee935b and b1d2514e3df75c96ba4d3231579b6452860a2952.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (14)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📓 Common learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Scaffold `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: When a request mentions planning or pr