.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always follow the guidelines specified in `@/guidelines/README.md`\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Always consult project-wide resources in `guidelines/` directory for project conventions and best practices\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Create design.md only when the change is cross-cutting, introduces new architecture patterns, adds external dependencies, makes significant data model changes, involves security/performance complexity, or has ambiguity\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Create proposal.md file for all changes that add features, make breaking changes, change architecture/patterns, optimize performance, or update security patterns\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: After deployment, archive changes by moving `changes/[name]/` to `changes/archive/YYYY-MM-DD-[name]/`, updating `specs/` if capabilities changed, and running `openspec validate --strict`\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Use `openspec archive <change-id> [--yes|-y]` for tooling-only changes with `--skip-specs` flag, always passing the change ID explicitly\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Use `openspec spec list --long`, `openspec list`, and ripgrep (`rg`) for searching; prefer ripgrep only for full-text search of requirements and scenarios\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 LanguageTool</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md</summary>\n\n[style] ~36-~36: You have already used this phrasing in nearby sentences. Consider replacing it to add variety to your writing.\nContext: ...\"I want to create a spec proposal\" - \"I want to create a spec\"  Loose matching guidance...\n\n(REP_WANT_TO_VB)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md</summary>\n\n36-36: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (13)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-18`: **LGTM! Clear and concise OpenSpec pointer.**\n\nThe instruction block properly directs AI assistants to the comprehensive OpenSpec documentation when working on proposals, specifications, and architectural changes. The managed block markers enable automatic updates via `openspec update`.\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, this follows the established pattern for module-level OpenSpec instruction files.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-114`: **Comprehensive implementation checklist with clear structure.**\n\nThe task breakdown is thorough and well-organized, covering all layers from SDK to REST API. The 90%+ coverage target (line 87, 101) demonstrates good testing discipline.\n\nKey strengths:\n- Granular subtasks make progress tracking straightforward\n- Security considerations integrated throughout (SecureConn, SecurityCtx validation)\n- Infrastructure tasks properly address closure table operations (lines 46-50)\n- Migration planning included (section 10)\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, this tasks.md file follows the expected scaffolding pattern for change proposals.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-461`: **Excellent comprehensive OpenSpec guide.**\n\nThis document provides thorough guidance for AI assistants working with OpenSpec, covering the full workflow from proposal creation through archiving. Key strengths:\n\n- **Clear three-stage workflow** (lines 21-70): Creating → Implementing → Archiving\n- **Critical formatting rules** well-documented (lines 246-261): `#### Scenario:` format requirement\n- **Delta operation guidance** (lines 268-294): ADDED vs MODIFIED decision tree with warnings about full content requirement\n- **Troubleshooting section** (lines 296-322): Addresses common validation errors\n- **Search guidance** (lines 87-94): Proper tool selection (CLI vs ripgrep)\n\nThe emphasis on validation (`openspec validate --strict`) and the approval gate before implementation (line 63) are excellent practices.\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, this comprehensive guide properly documents the OpenSpec workflow and conventions used across the project.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (8)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **Correct delta header format.**\n\nUsing `## ADDED Requirements` (line 1) correctly indicates this is a new capability specification.\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, this header format aligns with the required delta operation syntax.\n\n---\n\n`3-39`: **Comprehensive Type Management specification.**\n\nThe requirement clearly defines:\n- **Data model** (lines 7-12): Code, parents, application_id, allowed_app_ids\n- **Operations** (lines 13-18): CRUD with validation\n- **Scenarios** (lines 20-38): Success case, duplicate handling, validation\n\nAll scenarios follow the correct `#### Scenario:` format and include at least one test case per requirement.\n\n**Minor observation:** Line 8 specifies \"1-63 chars\" for the code field. This specific limit might be worth documenting the rationale (e.g., DNS label compatibility, database index limitations).\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, scenario formatting is correct and each requirement has proper test coverage.\n\n---\n\n`42-92`: **Well-specified Entity Management with hierarchy support.**\n\nStrong specification covering:\n- **Data model** (lines 46-52): ID, type, name, external_id, parent, timestamps\n- **Operations** (lines 54-60): CRUD with hierarchy support\n- **Critical scenarios**: Parent type validation (lines 71-76), cycle detection (lines 87-91), subtree moves (lines 78-85)\n\nThe cycle detection requirement (lines 87-91) is crucial for maintaining hierarchy integrity and properly specified.\n\n---\n\n`95-121`: **Proper Closure Table pattern documentation.**\n\nThe specification correctly defines the closure table structure:\n- **Table schema** (lines 104-107): parent_id, child_id, depth\n- **Query scenarios**: Ancestors (lines 109-113) with depth ordering, Descendants (lines 115-119)\n\nThe depth-based ordering ensures predictable hierarchy traversal.\n\n---\n\n`123-161`: **Clear Reference Management specification.**\n\nWell-defined reference lifecycle:\n- **Data model** (lines 127-131): group_id, resource_type, resource_id, application_id\n- **Operations** (lines 133-137): Create, delete, reference counting\n- **Critical constraint** (lines 148-152): Prevents deletion of groups with active references\n\nThe reference counting mechanism (lines 145, 159) enables efficient deletion validation.\n\n---\n\n`163-186`: **Application-based authorization properly specified.**\n\nAuthorization rules are clear:\n- **Type ownership** (lines 168-169): Owner can modify types\n- **Entity permissions** (line 170): Allowed apps can create/modify entities\n- **SecurityCtx requirement** (line 171): All operations require tenant isolation\n\nScenarios cover both success (lines 173-178) and rejection (lines 180-185) cases.\n\n---\n\n`189-225`: **Comprehensive REST API endpoint specification.**\n\nAll required endpoints documented:\n- **Type management** (lines 194-198): Full CRUD with code-based addressing\n- **Entity management** (lines 199-202): CRUD with UUID addressing\n- **Hierarchy queries** (lines 203-204): Ancestors and descendants\n- **Reference management** (lines 205-206): Create and delete\n\nCommon requirements properly specified (lines 208-211): Authentication, RFC-9457 errors, REST conventions.\n\n---\n\n`227-268`: **Complete database schema specification.**\n\nAll four tables properly defined:\n- **resource_group_type** (lines 231-236): Type definitions with app ownership\n- **resource_group** (lines 238-243): Entity records\n- **resource_group_closure** (lines 245-250): Hierarchy with composite PK and indexes\n- **resource_group_reference** (lines 252-259): External references with composite index\n\nThe Secure ORM requirement (line 261) ensures tenant isolation at the database layer.\n\n**Observation:** The closure table indexes (line 250) on parent_id, child_id, and depth will support efficient ancestor and descendant queries as specified in the Hierarchy Operations requirement.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`20-20`: The proposed ModKit attribute syntax matches actual framework usage throughout the codebase. The format `#[modkit::module(name = \"resource_group\", capabilities = [db, rest])]` is correct.\n\n---\n\n`38-38`: **This review comment is based on an incorrect assumption.** The `proposal.md` file is a specification document that lists dependencies by name only (`sea-orm, axum`) without specifying versions. It does not claim versions 1.1.0 or 0.8.0. The workspace Cargo.toml does specify those versions, but a markdown proposal document does not need to match specific workspace dependency versions—it describes what modules are needed at a design level. No action required on this comment.\n\n\n\n> Likely an incorrect or invalid review comment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3671792505","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3671792505"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T16:50:17Z","commit_id":"b1d2514e3df75c96ba4d3231579b6452860a2952"},{"id":3671802768,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7a20OQ","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`:\n- Around line 238-244: The resource_group table definition is missing the\noptional parent_id column referenced elsewhere; add a nullable parent_id column\nof type UUIDv7 that references resource_group.id (foreign key) and update the\nentity spec for resource_group to include parent_id as Optional UUIDv7; also\ncreate an index on parent_id to optimize parent-child queries and ensure any\ninsert/update/ORM mappings (e.g., the resource_group model/entity) are updated\nto include the parent_id field.\n- Around line 219-224: Update the \"List entities via REST\" scenario for the\n`/resource-group/v1/groups` endpoint to specify pagination, filtering, sorting,\nand response structure: describe supported query parameters (e.g., page, limit,\ncursor), filtering keys (e.g., type, parentId, status), and sorting options\n(e.g., sort_by, order), define the response payload shape including items array\nplus pagination metadata (total, page, limit, nextCursor), and add at least one\nexample request and corresponding example response to the \"List entities via\nREST\" scenario so implementers of the resource-group list handler know expected\nparameters and output.\n- Around line 54-60: The spec line \"Entity management SHALL support: ...\nDeleting entities (only if no active references exist)\" is ambiguous about\nentities with descendants; update the spec to explicitly state the chosen\ndeletion policy (prevent deletion when descendants exist OR cascade delete\ndescendants OR orphan descendants by clearing parent_id) and implement that\npolicy textually; also add a concrete scenario example titled e.g. \"Scenario:\nDeleting an entity with descendants\" that describes the initial tree, the delete\nrequest on the parent, the expected outcome (error or list of deleted IDs or\norphaned children with parent_id=null), and any validation rules (e.g. require\nrecursive flag for cascade), so readers and implementers can follow the\ndescribed behavior.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-461`: **Excellent comprehensive OpenSpec documentation!**\n\nThe documentation is thorough, well-structured, and provides clear guidance on the three-stage workflow, CLI usage, and spec format conventions. This will be valuable for contributors.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Optional: Address markdown linting issues</summary>\n\nStatic analysis tools flagged a few stylistic improvements:\n\n1. **Add language identifiers to fenced code blocks** (lines 131, 153, 357)\n2. **Replace bold emphasis with proper headings** (lines 49, 299, 303, 307)\n3. **Consider rewording line 36** to avoid repetitive phrasing\n\nThese are purely stylistic and don't affect functionality.\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`163-186`: **Verify SecurityCtx tenant isolation details.**\n\nLine 171 mentions \"All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\" but doesn't specify:\n- What tenant fields SecurityCtx contains\n- How tenant isolation is enforced at the database query level\n- Whether resource groups are tenant-scoped or application-scoped\n\nConsider adding a scenario or clarification about how tenant isolation works in practice.\n\n\n\n\nBased on learnings, ensure this aligns with project-wide authentication patterns documented in `guidelines/DNA/`.\n\n---\n\n`245-261`: **Consider additional indexes for common query patterns.**\n\nThe schema has good index coverage for the closure table, but consider adding indexes for common queries:\n\n- `resource_group.type_code` — for filtering by type\n- `resource_group.external_id` — for external ID lookups\n- `resource_group.parent_id` — for efficient parent-child queries (after adding the field)\n\nThese would optimize typical query patterns.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between b1d2514e3df75c96ba4d3231579b6452860a2952 and 7211cbe904eb8b63c27093f0b7695fcf667f7835.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (6)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (3)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md\n* modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md\n* modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (13)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📓 Common learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: mo