ad of a heading\n\n(MD036, no-emphasis-as-heading)\n\n---\n\n357-357: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-18`: **LGTM! Clean OpenSpec instruction block.**\n\nThe AGENTS.md file follows the OpenSpec pattern correctly with proper markers and clear guidance for AI assistants. The triggers and learning references are well-defined.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-39`: **Well-defined type management requirement.**\n\nThe Resource Group Type Management requirement clearly defines the type structure, CRUD operations, and validation rules. Error scenarios cover duplicate codes and invalid formats appropriately.\n\n---\n\n`95-120`: **Solid hierarchy operations using closure table pattern.**\n\nThe closure table implementation is well-defined with proper depth semantics and efficient ancestor/descendant queries.\n\n---\n\n`123-160`: **Reference management properly integrated with deletion protection.**\n\nThe reference counting mechanism and deletion prevention are well-specified. Good integration with the entity lifecycle.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3671802768","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric