\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`35-35`: **Path correction needed.**\n\nBased on past review feedback, the affected code path is listed as `modules/resource-group/` but should be `modules/system/resource-group/` to match the actual module structure.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-11`: **Resolve broken documentation references.**\n\nMultiple referenced guideline files do not exist in the repository:\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` (lines 11, 54)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md` (lines 64, 135)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md` (lines 68, 136)\n- `@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md` (lines 70, 137)\n\nThese broken references must be resolved before merging. Either create the missing documentation files or update the references to point to existing resources.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 54-54, 64-64, 68-68, 70-70, 135-138\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`238-244`: **Critical: Add missing `parent_id` column to database schema.**\n\nThe `resource_group` table schema is missing the `parent_id` field that is referenced throughout the spec (lines 51, 66, 82). This field is essential for the hierarchical structure.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Required schema addition</summary>\n\n```diff\n **`resource_group`:**\n - `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n - `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n - `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n - `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `parent_id` (FK): Optional UUID → `resource_group.id`\n - `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\nAlso add an index on `parent_id` for query performance.\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`54-60`: **Clarify deletion policy for entities with descendants.**\n\nThe deletion requirement states \"only if no active references exist\" but doesn't specify the behavior when an entity has descendants. The spec should clarify whether to prevent deletion, cascade delete, or orphan descendants.\n\n---\n\n`219-224`: **Specify pagination and filtering for list endpoint.**\n\nThe \"List entities via REST\" scenario lacks critical details for implementation: pagination parameters, filtering capabilities, sorting options, and response structure.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`131-147`: **Consider adding language specifiers to code blocks.**\n\nFor consistency and better rendering, consider adding language identifiers to the fenced code blocks showing directory structure and decision trees. While these aren't executable code, specifying `text` or `plaintext` improves markdown tooling compatibility.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested improvements</summary>\n\nLine 131:\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n openspec/\n```\n\nLine 153:\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n New request?\n```\n\nLine 357:\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n openspec/changes/add-2fa-notify/\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 153-161, 357-366\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`36-50`: **Optional: Add language specifier to directory structure block.**\n\nFor better markdown rendering and tooling compatibility, consider adding a language identifier to the directory structure code block.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested improvement</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n modules/resource-group/\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3678273848","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3678273848"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T14:09:52Z","commit_id":"5bd26c6e50dde121a95a14a891760715a1460ca7"},{"id":3678782940,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bRcXc","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`:\n- Around line 36-50: The fenced directory listing block starting with\n\"modules/resource-group/\" (showing resource-group-sdk/, resource-group/,\nmodule.rs, local_client.rs, etc.) lacks a language identifier; add a language\ntag like \"text\" (e.g., ```text) to the opening fence so the directory structure\nrenders correctly and improves accessibility.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`37-37`: **Consider using the full module path for consistency.**\n\nThe module structure shows `modules/resource-group/` but the actual path is `modules/system/resource-group/`. Using the full path would improve consistency with the actual repository structure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-modules/resource-group/\n+modules/system/resource-group/\n ├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3678782940","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3678782940"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T16:08:48Z","commit_id":"c698c5e7b14d5c0ef70b66f5744468ce30fe6b6a"},{"id":3679746239,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bVHi_","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 5**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`:\n- Line 18: The spec is missing scenarios validating type-deletion rules; add\ntests covering both failure and success cases: include a \"Prevent deletion of\ntype with existing entities\" scenario that creates a type (e.g., DEPARTMENT)\nwith at least one entity, calls delete_type, and expects\nResourceGroupError::TypeInUse, and a \"Delete type with no entities\" scenario\nthat ensures a type (e.g., ARCHIVED_TYPE) with zero entities is deleted\nsuccessfully when delete_type is called and returns success.\n- Around line 254-283: The schema is missing explicit ON DELETE behavior for\nseveral FKs; update the spec to declare cascade rules: set\nresource_group.type_code → resource_group_type.code to ON DELETE RESTRICT\n(prevent deleting a type that still has groups), set\nresource_group_closure.parent_id → resource_group.id and\nresource_group_closure.child_id → resource_group.id to ON DELETE CASCADE (so\nclosure rows are removed when a group is deleted), and specify\nresource_group_reference.group_id → resource_group.id as either ON DELETE\nCASCADE (if plugin references should be removed with the group) or ON DELETE\nRESTRICT (if you want to prevent deletion while references exist) and document\nthe chosen behavior in the spec.\n- Around line 217-223: The Resource Group Entities list is missing the list\nendpoint referenced elsewhere; update the entities section to include the\ncollection GET endpoint (e.g., add \"GET /resource-group/v1/groups\" or the\nconsistent \"GET /groups\" entry) so it matches the scenario that calls GET\n/resource-group/v1/groups; edit the Resource Group Entities block (the list\ncontaining POST /groups, GET /groups/{id}, PUT /groups/{id}, DELETE\n/groups/{id}, GET /groups/{id}/ancestors, GET /groups/{id}/descendants) and\ninsert the list endpoint with a brief description like \"List entities\" to keep\nthe spec consistent.\n- Around line 54-60: Clarify that parent changes are not allowed via the generic\nupdate path: update the spec to state that update_entity only modifies\nproperties like name and external_id and must reject attempts to change\nparent_id, and add the explicit scenario rejecting direct parent_id updates;\nrequire callers to use move_entity for subtree/parent changes and specify the\nerror returned (ResourceGroupError::Validation with guidance to use move_entity)\nwhen update_entity detects a parent_id change.\n- Line 8: The spec's \"Code: Unique identifier\" entry needs an explicit\ncase-insensitivity policy: state that type codes MUST be normalized to lowercase\nbefore storage and that implementations MUST enforce uniqueness via either a\ncase-insensitive unique index (e.g., UNIQUE INDEX on LOWER(code) or a\ncase-insensitive collation) so \"Department\" and \"DEPARTMENT\" collide; update the\nschema section to show the persisted column is stored lowercased (or include DB\nexample using UNIQUE(LOWER(code))) and add a note that queries MUST compare\ncodes using LOWER(code) (or use case-insensitive collation) so lookups and\nconstraints behave consistently across implementations.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (6)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`49-50`: **Add validation scenarios for name and external_id constraints.**\n\nThe spec defines length constraints (\"1-255 chars\" for name, \"max 255 chars\" for external_id) but includes no scenarios validating these bounds.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject empty or oversized name\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity creation request with name = \"\" or name length > 255\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to create the entity\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n\n#### Scenario: Reject oversized external_id\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity with external_id length > 255 chars\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to create or update the entity\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`78-86`: **Add error scenarios for move_entity operation.**\n\nThe move subtree scenario (lines 78-86) only covers the success case. Missing scenarios for:\n- Moving to a parent with incompatible type\n- Moving root-level entity to become a child\n- Moving with authorization failures\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested error scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject move to incompatible parent type\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n- **AND** a potential parent `parent-id` of type `DEPARTMENT`\n- **AND** type `ORGANIZATION` does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `node-id` to `parent-id`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n\n#### Scenario: Move entity to null parent (make root)\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with current parent `old-parent-id`\n- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` with `new_parent_id = null`\n- **THEN** the system moves `node-id` to root level\n- **AND** updates closure table entries\n- **AND** returns success\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`225-230`: **Add error scenario for accessing plugin endpoints when disabled.**\n\nThe spec defines that reference endpoints (lines 228-229) are available \"ONLY if References Plugin is connected\" but doesn't specify what happens if a client attempts to access them when the plugin is disabled.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested scenario</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject reference operations when plugin not connected\n\n- **GIVEN** the References Plugin is NOT connected\n- **WHEN** the user sends POST to `/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`\n- **THEN** the system returns `404 Not Found` or `501 Not Implemented`\n- **AND** indicates the References Plugin is not enabled\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`187-187`: **Consider clarifying SecurityCtx and tenant isolation.**\n\nThe spec mentions \"valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\" but doesn't explain:\n- How tenant isolation is enforced in the schema\n- Whether tables include tenant_id fields\n- How SecurityCtx integrates with queries\n\nIf this is framework-provided functionality, consider adding a note. Otherwise, specify the tenant isolation mechanism.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested addition</summary>\n\nAdd after line 187:\n```markdown\n**Note**: `SecurityCtx` is provided by the HyperSpot framework and automatically scopes all queries to the authenticated tenant. Tenant isolation is enforced at the ORM level via Secure ORM.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`287-293`: **Clarify conditional migration mechanism for plugin tables.**\n\nThe scenario states \"if References Plugin is connected, create `reference` table\" but doesn't explain the implementation mechanism:\n- Are there separate migration files for plugin tables?\n- Does the migration check a runtime flag/config?\n- How does SeaORM handle conditional migrations?\n\nThis detail is important for implementers.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\nAdd after line 292:\n\n```markdown\n**Implementation Note**: Plugin-specific migrations should be defined in separate migration files that are only applied when the plugin is enabled. The module initialization code should conditionally run plugin migrations based on plugin availability.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`268-273`: **Add index specifications for performance optimization.**\n\nThe closure table specifies \"Indexes on `parent_id`, `child_id`, `depth`\" but other tables lack index specifications:\n- `resource_group.type_code` (FK) should have an index\n- `resource_group.external_id` (if used for lookups) may need an index\n- `resource_group_reference` composite index is specified, but individual FK indexes are not\n\nConsider adding explicit index specifications for all frequently queried columns.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested additions</summary>\n\n```markdown\n**Additional Indexes:**\n- `resource_group`: Index on `type_code` for type-based queries\n- `resource_group`: Optional index on `external_id` for external lookups\n- `resource_group_reference`: Index on `group_id` for reference queries\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3679746239","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3679746239"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T22:03:56Z","commit_id":"b1a038e3024e18603a2418e84adf85e968b00135"},{"id":3687997951,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7b0mH_","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/architecture/features/feature-resource-group/DESIGN.md`:\n- Around line 149-156: The API endpoints list in DESIGN.md is incomplete; update\nthe \"API Endpoints\" section to include the missing operations required by\nspec.md by adding the following routes: GET /resource-group/v1/groups (list all\nentities), PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id} (update entity), DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id} (delete entity), PUT\n/resource-group/v1/types/{code} (update type) and DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/types/{code} (delete type) so the DESIGN.md endpoint list\nmatches the spec and referenced scenarios/requirements.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`312-318`: **CRITICAL: Missing parent_id field in resource_group schema.**\n\nThe `resource_group` table schema is missing the `parent_id` field, which is essential for the hierarchical structure. The entity definition at line 51 specifies \"Parent ID: Optional reference to parent entity\", and multiple scenarios reference parent_id (lines 64, 66, 82), but the schema doesn't include it.\n\nThis was flagged in previous reviews and remains unresolved.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Required schema fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n **`resource_group`:**\n - `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n - `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n - `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n - `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `parent_id` (FK): Optional UUID → `resource_group.id`\n - `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\nAlso add an index on `parent_id` for efficient parent-child queries.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`229-236`: **Missing GET /groups list endpoint.**\n\nThe endpoints section lists `GET /groups/{id}` for retrieving a specific entity, but doesn't include a `GET /groups` endpoint for listing entities. However, past review comments reference scenarios that would need this endpoint.\n\nThis was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Add missing list endpoint</summary>\n\n```diff\n #### Resource Group Entities\n - `POST /groups` - Create a new entity\n+- `GET /groups` - List entities (with pagination and filtering)\n - `GET /groups/{id}` - Get a specific entity\n - `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update an entity\n - `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete an entity\n```\n\nConsider adding a scenario for the list operation that specifies pagination, filtering, and response structure.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`174-176`: **Missing reference_count field in schema.**\n\nLine 175 states \"increments reference count for the group\", but the `resource_group` schema (lines 312-318) doesn't include a `reference_count` field. This was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Add reference count to schema</summary>\n\n```diff\n **`resource_group`:**\n - `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n - `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code`\n - `name`: String (1-255 chars)\n - `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n+- `parent_id` (FK): Optional UUID → `resource_group.id`\n+- `reference_count`: Integer (default 0)\n - `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n```\n\nAlternatively, clarify if reference counting will be implemented via aggregation queries instead of a denormalized counter.\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`8-8`: **Clarify case-insensitive enforcement mechanism.**\n\nThe spec states type codes are \"case-insensitive\" but doesn't specify how this is enforced. Implementers need to know whether codes should be normalized to lowercase on storage, use case-insensitive unique constraints, or use `LOWER()` in queries.\n\nThis was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace); stored in lowercase, uniqueness enforced case-insensitively\n```\n\nAnd update schema line 306:\n```diff\n-**`resource_group_type`:**\n-- `code` (PK): String, unique, case-insensitive\n+**`resource_group_type`:**\n+- `code` (PK): String (stored lowercase, unique)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`17-18`: **Add scenario for type deletion validation.**\n\nLine 18 mentions \"Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\" but no scenario demonstrates this validation. This was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested scenarios</summary>\n\nAdd after the existing type scenarios:\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Prevent deletion of type with existing entities\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with at least one entity\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete the type\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeInUse`\n\n#### Scenario: Delete type with no entities\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `ARCHIVED_TYPE` with zero entities\n- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_type` for `ARCHIVED_TYPE`\n- **THEN** the system deletes the type successfully\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`57-58`: **Clarify update vs. move operation boundaries.**\n\nLines 57-58 list updating properties and moving entities as separate operations, but it's unclear whether `parent_id` can be updated via the generic update operation or must always use `move_entity`. This was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested clarification</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id; parent_id is read-only)\n - Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n```\n\nAnd add a scenario:\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject direct parent_id update\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with parent `old-parent-id`\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to update `parent_id` via `update_entity`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation`\n- **AND** directs user to use `move_entity` operation\n```\n\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`305-333`: **Specify foreign key cascade behavior.**\n\nThe schema defines multiple foreign keys but doesn't specify cascade behavior (ON DELETE CASCADE/RESTRICT). This could lead to implementation inconsistencies. This was flagged in previous reviews.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Add cascade specifications</summary>\n\nAdd a section after the schema tables:\n\n```markdown\n**Foreign Key Constraints:**\n- `resource_group.type_code` → `resource_group_type.code` (ON DELETE RESTRICT)\n- `resource_group.parent_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE or RESTRICT - specify based on requirement)\n- `resource_group_closure.parent_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- `resource_group_closure.child_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE)\n- `resource_group_reference.group_id` → `resource_group.id` (ON DELETE CASCADE or RESTRICT - specify based on requirement)\n```\n\nNote: `type_code` should use RESTRICT to enforce the \"can't delete type with entities\" rule at the database level.\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3687997951","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3687997951"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-21T15:53:36Z","commit_id":"2efe1791f65d7ad36e8603c202455bc705ad6921"},{"id":3691321473,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7cBRiB","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/architecture/DESIGN.md`:\n- Around line 65-80: The document has duplicate \"Domain Model\" headings (C.1:\nDomain Model and C.2: Domain Model) causing confusion; rename the first heading\n(C.1: Domain Model) to a distinct title such as \"C.1: Component Diagram\" or\n\"C.1: Architecture Overview\" to reflect that it contains the component diagram\nand list of components (ResourceGroupService, TypeRegistry,\nClosureTableManager), leaving C.2 as \"Domain Model\" for the actual model content\nso the structure is clear.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/architecture/features/feature-resource-group/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`149-156`: **Incomplete API endpoint list in DESIGN.md.**\n\nThe API endpoints section is missing several operations that are mentioned in the requirements and flows throughout this document:\n- `PUT /groups/{id}` - Update entity (referenced in Entity Management requirement at line 204)\n- `DELETE /groups/{id}` - Delete entity (referenced in Manage References flow at line 78-79)\n- `PUT /types/{code}` - Update type\n- `DELETE /types/{code}` - Delete type\n- Reference management endpoints (mentioned in the References requirement at line 252-270)\n\nThis inconsistency could confuse implementers about the complete API surface.\n\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Complete endpoint list</summary>\n\n```diff\n ### API Endpoints\n \n+#### Resource Group Types\n - `POST /resource-group/v1/types`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/types`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/types/{code}`\n+\n+#### Resource Group Entities\n - `POST /resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors`\n - `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants`\n+\n+#### Resource Group References\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/architecture/DESIGN.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`102-102`: **Simplify redundant phrasing.**\n\n\"Owner-based ownership\" is redundant. Consider simplifying to \"Owner-based access control\" or \"Ownership-based authorization\".\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested alternatives</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- **Authorization**: Owner-based ownership for types; Hierarchy-based permissions for groups.\n+- **Authorization**: Owner-based access control for types; Hierarchy-based permissions for groups.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3691321473","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/265#pullrequestreview-3691321473"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/265"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-22T08:58:06Z","commit_id":"1a62e9b42e78549aa82ce21a931acad14862984f"}]},{"source_pr_number":264,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264","source_state":"closed","source_author":"ffedoroff","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #264] Feature/resource group spec