d":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-16T15:33:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T16:44:15Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds comprehensive OpenSpec documentation and a full proposal/spec/tasks set for a new Resource Group module, including SDK/module design, closure-table hierarchy, reference management, REST APIs, DB schemas, and project conventions.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **OpenSpec Guidance** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`, `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md` | New OpenSpec guidance files: consultation rules, three-stage workflow, checklists, formatting rules, tooling commands, and operational guidance for spec-driven development. |\n| **Module Proposal** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md` | Proposal describing two crates (SDK and module), API surface (ResourceGroupApi), domain responsibilities, transport-agnostic models, error types, authorization via SecurityCtx, and integration/migration notes. |\n| **Detailed Spec** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md` | Exhaustive specification for types, entities, hierarchy (closure table), reference management, authorization rules, REST endpoints, DB schema (SeaORM), scenarios, and behavioral models. |\n| **Implementation Tasks** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md` | Checklist covering SDK and module crate scaffolding, domain and infra work, local client, REST DTOs/handlers/routes, migrations, testing, auth, and documentation tasks. |\n| **Project Conventions** <br> `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md` | Project-level conventions and architecture notes: tech stack, module layout, coding style, DB patterns, testing, observability, versioning, and security guidelines. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant SDK\n    participant Module\n    participant SecurityCtx as Auth\n    participant DB\n    Client->>SDK: ResourceGroupApi request (create/read/update/delete)\n    SDK->>Module: Forward validated DTO\n    Module->>SecurityCtx: Authorize request\n    SecurityCtx-->>Module: allow/deny\n    alt allowed\n        Module->>DB: Execute domain ops (closure table, refs)\n        DB-->>Module: persist/query results\n        Module-->>SDK: return result\n        SDK-->>Client: response\n    else denied\n        Module-->>SDK: authorization error\n        SDK-->>Client: auth error\n    end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through specs, a careful guide,  \n> > Maps of groups and branches wide,  \n> > Checklists tucked beneath each leaf,  \n> > Tasks to build, then sweet relief,  \n> > Carrot trails to code — I stride 🥕\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                              |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                              |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'Feature/resource group spec' clearly summarizes the main change: adding comprehensive OpenSpec documentation and specifications for the Resource Group module implementation. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                                                                               |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Recent nitpick comments</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-40`: **Consider adding cross-references to related documentation.**\n\nFor improved navigation, consider adding references to the related OpenSpec artifacts at the end of the proposal:\n\n```markdown\n## Related Documentation\n\n- [Detailed Specification](../../specs/resource-group/spec.md)\n- [Implementation Tasks](./tasks.md)\n- [Project Context](../../project.md)\n```\n\nThis helps readers understand where to find implementation details and full requirements.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Recent review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 2d4bcdc688895a4d5943f8de1857ba6838f7a634 and b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (3)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📓 Common learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Scaffold `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn how to create and apply change proposals, spec format and conventions, and project structure and guidelines\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Before creating any task, read relevant specs in `specs/[capability]/spec.md`, check pending changes for conflicts, read `openspec/project.md`, run `openspec list` and `openspec list --specs`\n```\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Scaffold `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: When a request mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan), or introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work, open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-8`: **Clear rationale and context.**\n\nThe \"Why\" section effectively explains the need for rebuilding the Resource Group module to follow ModKit patterns and replace the legacy symlink-based implementation.\n\n---\n\n`9-33`: **Well-structured technical approach.**\n\nThe SDK/Module separation, Closure Table pattern for hierarchies, and integration with ModKit security and ClientHub demonstrate solid architectural planning.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3760615404/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001601","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001601,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338B","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+# Change: Add Resource Group Module\n+\n+## Why\n+\n+HyperSpot needs a Resource Group module that provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control. This module enables applications to organize resources in a tree structure with strict type validation, permission management, and efficient hierarchy operations using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+The current `resource-group` directory is a symlink to an old repository with a different architecture. We need to rebuild it as a proper HyperSpot/ModKit module following the SDK pattern and DDD-light architecture.\n+\n+## What Changes\n+\n+**New Crates: `resource-group-sdk` and `resource-group`**\n+\n+**SDK Crate (`resource-group-sdk`):**\n+- `ResourceGroupApi` trait with methods for types, entities, references, and hierarchy operations\n+- Transport-agnostic models (`ResourceGroupType`, `ResourceGroupEntity`, `ResourceGroupReference`)\n+- `ResourceGroupError` enum for error handling\n+- All API methods accept `&SecurityCtx` for authorization and tenant isolation\n+\n+**Module Crate (`resource-group`):**\n+- Module declaration with `#[modkit::module(name = \"resource_group\", capabilities = [db, rest])]`\n+- Domain service with business logic for type management, entity CRUD, hierarchy operations, and reference management\n+- Local client implementing `ResourceGroupApi` trait\n+- REST API handlers, routes, and DTOs following HyperSpot conventions\n+- SeaORM entities with Secure ORM for tenant isolation\n+- Closure Table pattern for efficient hierarchy queries (ancestors/descendants)\n+- ClientHub registration for inter-module access\n+\n+**Core Features:**\n+1. **Type Management**: Define resource group types with allowed parent types and application permissions\n+2. **Hierarchical Organization**: Create, update, move, and delete entities in tree structures\n+3. **Access Control**: Application-based authorization with owner vs. allowed application permissions\n+4. **Reference Management**: Link resource groups to external resources with reference counting\n+\n+## Impact\n+\n+- **Affected specs**: `resource-group` (new capability)\n+- **Affected code**: `modules/resource-group/` (new crates)\n+- **Dependencies**: modkit, modkit-db, modkit-security, sea-orm, axum\n+- **Database**: Requires PostgreSQL/SQLite with closure table pattern\n+- **Migration**: Old `resource-group` symlink will be replaced with new ModKit module","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Missing migration and rollback strategy.**\n\nThe impact section mentions replacing the old symlink (line 40) but doesn't address:\n- **Rollback plan**: What if critical issues are discovered post-deployment?\n- **Compatibility period**: Will the old and new implementations coexist temporarily?\n- **Dependency analysis**: Are there other modules or systems depending on the old implementation?\n- **Data migration**: If the old implementation persisted data, how will it be migrated?\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested additions to Impact section</summary>\n\nConsider adding a \"Migration Strategy\" subsection:\n\n```markdown\n**Migration Strategy:**\n- Verify no active dependencies on old `resource-group` symlink\n- If data exists, provide migration scripts or document manual migration steps\n- Consider feature flag to enable/disable new module during transition\n- Document rollback procedure if critical issues arise\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\naround lines 34 - 40, Add a \"Migration Strategy\" subsection under Impact that\ndefines a rollback plan, coexistence period, dependency analysis, and data\nmigration steps: explicitly state the rollback procedure if critical issues are\nfound (how to revert the new ModKit module and restore the old resource-group\nsymlink), define a compatibility period and whether both implementations will\nrun concurrently (and how to toggle via a feature flag), list how to detect and\nenumerate dependent modules/systems before switching, and include concrete data\nmigration guidance (migration scripts or manual steps, verification checks) and\ncontingency steps to restore data if migration fails; reference the existing\n\"resource-group\" symlink and the new ModKit module names to make the steps\nactionable.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001601","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001601"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001601"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001601/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":34,"original_start_line":34,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":40,"original_line":40,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":40,"position":40,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001607","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001607,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338H","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add scenarios for critical edge cases in type management.**\n\nThe type management requirement is well-structured but missing scenarios for several edge cases:\n\n1. **Case sensitivity** (line 8): The spec states codes are case-insensitive, but there's no scenario demonstrating how `DEPARTMENT` vs `department` is handled during lookup or duplicate detection.\n\n2. **Empty parents array**: Line 9 mentions parents array but doesn't specify if empty arrays are allowed for root types or what happens when a type has no valid parents.\n\n3. **Circular parent dependencies**: What prevents Type A from allowing Type B as parent while Type B allows Type A? This could create impossible hierarchy constraints.\n\n4. **Type updates with existing entities**: Line 17 mentions updating type properties, but changing `parents` after entities exist could invalidate existing hierarchies. Should this be prevented?\n\n5. **Owner vs. allowed_app_ids**: If `allowed_app_ids` is empty, can only the owner modify, or must the owner explicitly add themselves?\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested additional scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Handle case-insensitive type code lookup\n\n- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` exists\n- **WHEN** the user queries for type `department` (lowercase)\n- **THEN** the system returns the existing type\n- **AND** creation of `department` is rejected as duplicate\n\n#### Scenario: Create root type with no parents\n\n- **GIVEN** a type code `ORGANIZATION` with empty parents array `[]`\n- **WHEN** the user creates the type\n- **THEN** the system creates a root type that can have no parent entities\n\n#### Scenario: Reject circular parent type definitions\n\n- **GIVEN** Type A with parents `[\"B\"]` and Type B with parents `[\"A\"]`\n- **WHEN** the system validates the type graph\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CircularTypeReference`\n\n#### Scenario: Prevent parent changes when entities exist\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with entities already created\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to update the `parents` field\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeInUse`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 3 - 40, Add explicit edge-case scenarios to the Resource Group Type\nManagement spec: include a \"Handle case-insensitive type code lookup\" scenario\ndemonstrating lookup and duplicate rejection for codes like `DEPARTMENT` vs\n`department`; add a \"Create root type with no parents\" scenario to allow empty\nparents arrays for root types; add a \"Reject circular parent type definitions\"\nscenario and reference a new error `ResourceGroupError::CircularTypeReference`\nto validate the type graph on create/update; and add a \"Prevent parent changes\nwhen entities exist\" scenario that returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeInUse` when\nattempting to change `parents` for a type with existing entities and clarify\nowner/`allowed_app_ids` behavior when the array is empty (owner-only\nmodifications).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001607","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001607"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001607"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001607/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":3,"original_start_line":3,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":40,"original_line":40,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":40,"position":40,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001613","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001613,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338N","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add scenarios for entity lifecycle edge cases and clarify constraints.**\n\nThe entity management requirement needs additional scenarios for:\n\n1. **Root entity creation**: Line 51 states `parent_id` is optional, but there's no scenario for creating a root entity with `parent_id = null`.\n\n2. **Deletion with children**: Line 59 mentions preventing deletion if references exist, but what about child entities? Should delete cascade or be prevented?\n\n3. **external_id constraints**: Line 50 lists `external_id` as optional but doesn't specify uniqueness rules. Should it be unique per type, globally unique, or non-unique?\n\n4. **Move to root**: Line 58 mentions moving entities but doesn't cover moving to root (`parent_id = null`).\n\n5. **Move to self**: Scenario 4 handles cycles but should also explicitly reject moving an entity to be its own parent.\n\n6. **Type immutability**: Can `type_code` be changed after creation? This could violate parent type constraints.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested additional scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Create root entity\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `ORGANIZATION` with empty parents array\n- **WHEN** the user creates an entity with `parent_id = null`\n- **THEN** the system creates a root entity\n- **AND** creates only self-reference closure entry (depth = 0)\n\n#### Scenario: Prevent deletion of entity with children\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `parent-id` with child entities\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `parent-id`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::EntityHasChildren`\n- **OR** the system cascades the delete (specify which behavior is intended)\n\n#### Scenario: Reject moving entity to itself\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id`\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `node-id` to parent `node-id`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::SelfParentNotAllowed`\n\n#### Scenario: Prevent type_code modification\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `entity-id` with `type_code = \"DEPARTMENT\"`\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to update `type_code` to `\"ORGANIZATION\"`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeImmutable`\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 42 - 93, The spec is missing edge-case scenarios and constraints\nfor root creation, deletions with children, external_id uniqueness, moving to\nroot/self, and type immutability; update the resource-group spec (the\n\"Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\" section and its scenarios) to\nadd: a \"Create root entity\" scenario for parent_id = null documenting closure\nentry behavior; a clear policy for deletions (either cascade or prevent) plus a\n\"Prevent deletion of entity with children\" scenario returning\nResourceGroupError::EntityHasChildren if preventing; explicit uniqueness rules\nfor external_id (e.g., unique per type or global) and validation rules; a \"Move\nto root\" scenario allowing parent_id = null and rebuilding closure entries; a\n\"Reject moving entity to itself\" scenario returning\nResourceGroupError::SelfParentNotAllowed; and a rule/scenario that type_code is\nimmutable after creation with failures returning\nResourceGroupError::TypeImmutable. Ensure each new scenario references the\nexisting operations (create, move_entity, delete, update) and error symbols\n(ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected, ::EntityHasChildren, ::SelfParentNotAllowed,\n::TypeImmutable) so implementers can locate relevant handlers.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001613","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001613"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001613"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":42,"original_start_line":42,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":93,"original_line":93,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":93,"position":93,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001619","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001619,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338T","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Clarify reference counting implementation and add missing scenarios.**\n\nThe reference management requirement has several ambiguities:\n\n1. **Reference count storage** (lines 137, 145, 159): The spec mentions incrementing/decrementing reference counts but the database schema (lines 227-268) doesn't show a `reference_count` field on `resource_group`. Is this:\n   - A denormalized counter field (needs to be added to schema)?\n   - Computed on-the-fly with `COUNT(*)` queries?\n   - If denormalized, how are race conditions handled during concurrent creates/deletes?\n\n2. **Duplicate references**: Can the same `(group_id, resource_type, resource_id)` tuple be created multiple times? If yes, is each tracked separately or deduplicated?\n\n3. **Reference authorization**: Line 131 stores `application_id`, but can only the creator delete a reference, or can the group owner also delete it?\n\n4. **Move restrictions**: Line 152 prevents deletion with active references, but can groups with references be moved in the hierarchy?\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested additions</summary>\n\nAdd to database schema:\n```markdown\n**`resource_group` table additions:**\n- `reference_count`: Integer, default 0 (if using denormalized approach)\n```\n\nAdd scenarios:\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Reject duplicate reference\n\n- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id` exists\n- **WHEN** the user attempts to create the same reference again\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::ReferenceAlreadyExists`\n\n#### Scenario: Handle concurrent reference operations\n\n- **GIVEN** two concurrent requests to create references for `group-id`\n- **WHEN** both requests complete\n- **THEN** the reference count accurately reflects both references (no lost updates)\n\n#### Scenario: Query references for a resource\n\n- **GIVEN** multiple groups referencing `resource-type/resource-id`\n- **WHEN** the user queries references by resource\n- **THEN** the system returns all groups linking to that resource\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 123 - 160, The spec is ambiguous about how reference counts and\nduplicate/authorization semantics work; update the document and schema to\nexplicitly state whether reference_count is a denormalized integer on the\nresource_group table (add `reference_count` with default 0) or computed at query\ntime, and if denormalized, describe concurrency controls (e.g., DB\ntransactions/optimistic locking) used by create_reference and delete_reference\nto avoid lost updates; also define duplicate behavior for the (group_id,\nresource_type, resource_id) tuple (either deduplicate and return\nResourceGroupError::ReferenceAlreadyExists on duplicates or allow multiple\nentries), specify who can delete a reference (creator application_id only or\ngroup owner allowed), and add the suggested scenarios (Reject duplicate\nreference, Handle concurrent reference operations, Query references for a\nresource) and clarify that ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences blocks delete\nbut whether moves in the hierarchy are allowed when references exist.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001619","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001619"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001619"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":123,"original_start_line":123,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":160,"original_line":160,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":160,"position":160,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001625","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001625,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Incomplete authorization model - add comprehensive permission scenarios.**\n\nThe authorization requirement defines basic rules but lacks scenarios for several critical cases:\n\n1. **Permission scope ambiguity**: Line 170 states allowed apps can \"create/modify entities\" but doesn't specify:\n   - Can they delete entities?\n   - Can they move entities?\n   - Can they modify entities created by other allowed apps?\n\n2. **Type modification permissions**: Line 169 allows type owners to modify types, but:\n   - Can the owner delete a type if other allowed apps have created entities of that type?\n   - Can allowed apps modify type metadata or only the owner?\n\n3. **Hierarchy operation authorization**: Who can move entities in the tree?\n   - Only the entity creator?\n   - Any allowed app for that type?\n   - The type owner?\n\n4. **Reference authorization**: Who can create and delete references?\n   - Only the group creator?\n   - Any allowed app for the group's type?\n   - The reference creator only for delete?\n\n5. **Tenant isolation**: Line 171 mentions SecurityCtx but no scenario demonstrates rejecting cross-tenant access.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested additional scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Scenario: Enforce tenant isolation\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `entity-id` owned by tenant `tenant-A`\n- **AND** an authenticated application from tenant `tenant-B`\n- **WHEN** tenant-B attempts to access `entity-id`\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::NotFound` (leak-safe error)\n\n#### Scenario: Reject entity deletion by non-allowed application\n\n- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n- **AND** an entity created by `app1-uuid`\n- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to delete the entity\n- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n\n#### Scenario: Type owner can delete type even with entities from other apps\n\n- **GIVEN** a type owned by `app1-uuid`\n- **AND** entities created by allowed app `app2-uuid`\n- **WHEN** `app1-uuid` attempts to delete the type\n- **THEN** [specify behavior: reject or cascade delete or orphan entities]\n\n#### Scenario: Authorization for hierarchy moves\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity created by `app1-uuid` of type with `allowed_app_ids = [app1, app2]`\n- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to move the entity\n- **THEN** [specify: allowed or rejected based on permission model]\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 163 - 187, Add comprehensive authorization scenarios to the\n\"Authorization and Access Control\" section: explicitly specify permitted actions\n(create/modify/delete/move) and who may act (type owner, allowed_app_ids, entity\ncreator) by adding Scenario: Enforce tenant isolation (use\nResourceGroupError::NotFound for cross-tenant access), Scenario: Reject entity\ndeletion by non-allowed application (ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized),\nScenario: Type owner deletion behavior (define whether delete/cascade/orphan),\nScenario: Authorization for hierarchy moves (clarify allowed_app_ids vs creator\nvs type owner), and Scenario: Reference create/delete permissions (clarify who\ncan delete references); reference the existing section title and enums\nResourceGroupError::Unauthorized and ResourceGroupError::NotFound so tests and\nimplementations (authorization checks) can map scenarios to error codes.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 557d27a to 2a8c00a","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001625","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001625"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001625"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001625/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":163,"original_start_line":163,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":187,"original_line":187,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":187,"position":187,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001629","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001629,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338d","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Type Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group types that define the schema and allowed parent-child relationships for resource groups.\n+\n+A resource group type consists of:\n+- **Code**: Unique identifier (1-63 chars, no whitespace, case-insensitive)\n+- **Parents**: Array of type codes that can be parents of this type\n+- **Application ID**: Owner application that created the type\n+- **Allowed App IDs**: Applications allowed to create/modify groups of this type\n+\n+Type management SHALL support:\n+- Creating new types with validation\n+- Listing all types\n+- Retrieving a specific type by code\n+- Updating type properties (parents, allowed apps)\n+- Deleting types (only if no entities of this type exist)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create a new resource group type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid type code `DEPARTMENT` and allowed parent types `[\"ORGANIZATION\", \"DIVISION\"]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application with ID `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_type` with type data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type with the application as owner\n+- **AND** returns the created type with `application_id` set\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject duplicate type code\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type with code `DEPARTMENT` already exists\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create another type with code `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeAlreadyExists`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid type code format\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type code with whitespace `\"DEP ARTMENT\"` or length > 63\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create a type\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Validation` with field-specific error\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to manage resource group entities organized in hierarchical structures.\n+\n+A resource group entity consists of:\n+- **ID**: Unique identifier (UUIDv7)\n+- **Type Code**: Reference to resource group type\n+- **Name**: Display name (1-255 chars)\n+- **External ID**: Optional external identifier (max 255 chars)\n+- **Parent ID**: Optional reference to parent entity\n+- **Created/Modified**: Timestamps\n+\n+Entity management SHALL support:\n+- Creating entities with optional parent (validates parent type compatibility)\n+- Retrieving entities by ID\n+- Updating entity properties (name, external_id)\n+- Moving entities to new parents (subtree move)\n+- Deleting entities (only if no active references exist)\n+- Querying ancestors and descendants efficiently\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create entity with parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid parent entity `parent-id` of type `ORGANIZATION`\n+- **AND** a type `DEPARTMENT` that allows `ORGANIZATION` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user creates an entity of type `DEPARTMENT` with `parent_id = parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the entity\n+- **AND** creates closure table entries for all ancestors\n+- **AND** returns the created entity\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject invalid parent type\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a parent entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **AND** a type `ORGANIZATION` that does NOT allow `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to create an `ORGANIZATION` entity with `DEPARTMENT` as parent\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::InvalidParentType`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Move subtree to new parent\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with descendants\n+- **AND** a valid new parent `new-parent-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `move_entity` to move `node-id` to `new-parent-id`\n+- **THEN** the system moves the entire subtree\n+- **AND** rebuilds closure table entries for all affected nodes\n+- **AND** returns success\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject cycle creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with a descendant `descendant-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to move `descendant-id` to be a child of `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Hierarchy Operations\n+\n+The system SHALL provide efficient hierarchy queries using the Closure Table pattern.\n+\n+Hierarchy operations SHALL support:\n+- Querying all ancestors of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Querying all descendants of an entity (ordered by depth)\n+- Efficient subtree operations (move, delete)\n+\n+The closure table SHALL maintain:\n+- `parent_id`: Ancestor entity ID\n+- `child_id`: Descendant entity ID\n+- `depth`: Distance from parent to child (0 for self-reference)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query ancestors\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` in a hierarchy: `ROOT -> ORG -> DEPT -> node-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `node-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` ordered by depth (ascending)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Query descendants\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an entity `org-id` with descendants: `DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1` (child of DEPT1)\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `get_descendants` for `org-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns all descendants `[DEPT1, DEPT2, TEAM1]` ordered by depth\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Reference Management\n+\n+The system SHALL provide an API to link resource groups to external resources.\n+\n+A resource group reference consists of:\n+- **Group ID**: Reference to resource group entity\n+- **Resource Type**: Type of external resource (string)\n+- **Resource ID**: External resource identifier (string)\n+- **Application ID**: Application that created the reference\n+\n+Reference management SHALL support:\n+- Creating references from groups to external resources\n+- Deleting references\n+- Preventing deletion of groups with active references\n+- Reference counting for efficient deletion checks\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id`\n+- **AND** an external resource `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `create_reference` with reference data\n+- **THEN** the system creates the reference\n+- **AND** increments reference count for the group\n+- **AND** returns the created reference\n+\n+#### Scenario: Prevent deletion with active references\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a resource group entity `group-id` with active references\n+- **WHEN** the user attempts to delete `group-id`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences`\n+\n+#### Scenario: Delete reference\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a reference from `group-id` to `resource-type/resource-id`\n+- **WHEN** the user calls `delete_reference`\n+- **THEN** the system deletes the reference\n+- **AND** decrements reference count for the group\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: Authorization and Access Control\n+\n+The system SHALL enforce application-based authorization for all operations.\n+\n+Authorization rules:\n+- Only authenticated applications can modify resource groups\n+- Type owners can modify their types\n+- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n+- All operations require valid `SecurityCtx` for tenant isolation\n+\n+#### Scenario: Authorize type creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** an authenticated application `app-uuid`\n+- **WHEN** the application creates a type\n+- **THEN** the system sets `application_id = app-uuid` as owner\n+- **AND** allows the application to modify the type\n+\n+#### Scenario: Reject unauthorized entity creation\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a type `DEPARTMENT` with `allowed_app_ids = [app1-uuid]`\n+- **AND** an authenticated application `app2-uuid` not in allowed list\n+- **WHEN** `app2-uuid` attempts to create an entity of type `DEPARTMENT`\n+- **THEN** the system returns `ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized`\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Requirement: REST API Endpoints\n+\n+The system SHALL expose REST API endpoints for resource group operations.\n+\n+Endpoints SHALL include:\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/types` — Create type\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types` — List types\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Get type\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Update type\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/types/{code}` — Delete type\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups` — Create entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Get entity\n+- `PUT /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Update entity\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}` — Delete entity\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/ancestors` — Get ancestors\n+- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/descendants` — Get descendants\n+- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Create reference\n+- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — Delete reference\n+\n+All endpoints SHALL:\n+- Require authentication (Bearer token)\n+- Return RFC-9457 Problem Details for errors\n+- Follow HyperSpot REST API conventions\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create type via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** a valid JSON payload with type data\n+- **WHEN** POST request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/types`\n+- **THEN** the system creates the type and returns `201 Created` with location header\n+\n+#### Scenario: List entities via REST\n+\n+- **GIVEN** registered entities in the system\n+- **WHEN** GET request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups`\n+- **THEN** response contains entities\n+\n+---","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Incomplete REST API specification - missing endpoints, parameters, and error scenarios.**\n\nThe REST API requirement has several gaps:\n\n1. **Missing move endpoint**: Line 202 lists CRUD for entities but entity management (line 58) mentions moving entities. Where is `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/move` or similar?\n\n2. **Delete reference endpoint ambiguity** (line 207): The endpoint `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` doesn't specify how to identify which reference to delete. Should it be:\n   - `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references/{reference-id}`?\n   - `DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references?resource_type=X&resource_id=Y`?\n\n3. **Missing query references endpoint**: How do clients list all references for a group? Need `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references`.\n\n4. **No pagination specification**: Line 195 and 223 mention listing types/groups but don't specify pagination parameters for large datasets.\n\n5. **Missing error scenarios**: Only success cases are covered. Need scenarios for:\n   - 400 Bad Request (validation errors)\n   - 401 Unauthorized (missing/invalid token)\n   - 403 Forbidden (insufficient permissions)\n   - 404 Not Found\n   - 409 Conflict (cannot delete entity with children, references, or type in use)\n\n6. **RFC-9457 example missing**: Line 210 mentions RFC-9457 Problem Details but provides no example structure.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested additions</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Additional Endpoints\n\n- `POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/move` — Move entity to new parent\n  - Request body: `{\"parent_id\": \"uuid-or-null\"}`\n- `GET /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references` — List references for group\n- `DELETE /resource-group/v1/references/{reference-id}` — Delete reference by ID\n\n#### Pagination\n\nAll list endpoints SHALL support pagination:\n- Query parameters: `?page=1&page_size=100`\n- Response includes: `total_count`, `page`, `page_size`, `items[]`\n\n#### Scenario: Handle validation error with RFC-9457\n\n- **GIVEN** an invalid type code with whitespace\n- **WHEN** POST request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/types`\n- **THEN** the system returns `400 Bad Request` with Problem Details:\n  ```json\n  {\n    \"type\": \"https://hyperspot.dev/problems/validation-error\",\n    \"title\": \"Validation Error\",\n    \"status\": 400,\n    \"detail\": \"Type code must not contain whitespace\",\n    \"invalid_params\": [{\"name\": \"code\", \"reason\": \"contains whitespace\"}]\n  }\n  ```\n\n#### Scenario: Handle conflict on delete\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity with child entities\n- **WHEN** DELETE request is sent to `/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}`\n- **THEN** the system returns `409 Conflict` with Problem Details explaining children exist\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\naround lines 189 - 225, The REST API spec is incomplete: add a move endpoint\n(e.g., POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/move with body\n{\"parent_id\":\"uuid-or-null\"}) and a references query endpoint (GET\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references), disambiguate reference deletion by\nreplacing DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references with either DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/references/{reference-id} or specify query params\n(resource_type/resource_id) for DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references, and update all list endpoints (GET\n/resource-group/v1/types and GET /resource-group/v1/groups) to support\npagination (?page=&page_size=) and include total_count/page/page_size in\nresponses; finally add error scenarios (400/401/403/404/409) with RFC-9457\nProblem Details examples (include a validation error JSON) referenced where POST\n/resource-group/v1/types and DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups are described.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 557d27a to 2a8c00a","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001629","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001629"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001629"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001629/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":189,"original_start_line":189,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":225,"original_line":225,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":225,"position":225,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001635","pull_request_review_id":3671495198,"id":2699001635,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g338j","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@\n+# Project Context\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+This module is part of **HyperSpot** — a modular, high-performance AI services platform built in Rust.\n+\n+The Resource Group module provides hierarchical resource organization with type-based access control, enabling applications to organize resources in tree structures with efficient hierarchy operations.\n+\n+## Tech Stack\n+\n+- **Language**: Rust (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md))\n+- **Framework**: ModKit (see [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md))\n+- **HTTP**: Axum with `tower-http` middleware\n+- **Database**: SeaORM / SQLx with secure ORM layer (see [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md))\n+- **Observability**: `tracing` + OpenTelemetry (see [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md))\n+- **OpenAPI**: `utoipa` for automatic documentation generation\n+- **IDs**: UUIDv7 for all identifiers\n+- **Time**: `chrono` with UTC timestamps\n+\n+## Project Conventions\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+Follow the architecture manifest: [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md)\n+\n+**Key principles:**\n+- **Everything is a Module** — composable, independent units\n+- **DDD-light structure** — API / Contract / Domain / Infra layers\n+- **SDK pattern** — separate `-sdk` crate for public API surface\n+- **Type-safe REST** — OperationBuilder prevents half-wired routes at compile time\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+Follow the new module guideline: [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+\n+```\n+modules/resource-group/\n+├─ resource-group-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n+│  └─ src/\n+│     ├─ api.rs            # API trait (all methods take &SecurityCtx)\n+│     ├─ models.rs         # Transport-agnostic models\n+│     └─ errors.rs         # Transport-agnostic errors\n+└─ resource-group/               # Implementation\n+   └─ src/\n+      ├─ module.rs         # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+      ├─ local_client.rs   # Local client implementing SDK trait\n+      ├─ api/rest/         # DTOs, handlers, routes, error mapping\n+      ├─ domain/           # Business logic, events, repository traits\n+      └─ infra/storage/    # SeaORM entities, migrations\n+```\n+\n+### Code Style\n+\n+See [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md)\n+\n+- **Formatting**: `cargo fmt` with max line length 100, 4-space indentation\n+- **Linting**: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n+- **No unsafe code**: `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`\n+- **No panics**: Deny `unwrap()` and `expect()` in production code\n+- **JSON naming**: `camelCase` via `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`\n+\n+### REST API Design\n+\n+Follow the REST API guidelines: [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md)\n+\n+**Key conventions:**\n+- **Resource URLs**: Nouns, plural (`/types`, `/groups`)\n+- **Status codes**: See [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+- **Errors**: RFC-9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`)\n+- **Pagination**: Cursor-based with OData filtering (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md))\n+- **Timestamps**: ISO-8601 UTC with milliseconds (`2025-09-01T20:00:00.000Z`)\n+\n+### Error Handling\n+\n+- **Domain errors** → `src/domain/error.rs` (pure business errors)\n+- **SDK errors** → `resource-group-sdk/src/errors.rs` (transport-agnostic)\n+- **REST mapping** → `impl From<DomainError> for Problem` in `src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+- **Handler return** → `ApiResult<T>` with automatic error conversion\n+\n+### Security\n+\n+Follow security guidelines: [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+**Key requirements:**\n+- **All API methods MUST accept `&SecurityCtx`** as first parameter\n+- **Use SecureConn** for database access with automatic tenant isolation\n+- **Input validation** via `validator` crate\n+- **No secrets in code** — use environment variables\n+\n+### Database Access\n+\n+Follow secure ORM patterns: [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md)\n+\n+- **Typestate enforcement**: Unscoped queries cannot execute\n+- **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes return `WHERE 1=0`\n+- **Derive macro**: `#[derive(Scopable)]` with explicit dimension declarations\n+- **Request-scoped**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation\n+- **Closure Table**: Use closure table pattern for efficient hierarchy queries\n+\n+### Testing Strategy\n+\n+Target: **90%+ code coverage**\n+\n+- **Unit tests**: `cargo test --workspace`\n+- **Integration tests**: `make test-pg` / `make test-sqlite`\n+- **E2E tests**: `make e2e-docker` (Python/pytest)\n+- **All checks**: `make check` or `python scripts/ci.py check`\n+\n+### Observability\n+\n+Follow tracing setup: [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md)\n+\n+- **Structured logging** via `tracing` with contextual fields\n+- **Distributed tracing** with OpenTelemetry and W3C Trace Context\n+- **TracedClient** for instrumented HTTP calls\n+\n+## Important Constraints\n+\n+1. **No breaking changes** without version bump and deprecation period\n+2. **All dependencies** specified in root `Cargo.toml` (workspace inheritance)\n+3. **Feature flags** for optional functionality\n+4. **Backward compatibility**: Clients must ignore unknown fields\n+5. **Closure Table**: Must maintain closure table integrity for all hierarchy operations\n+\n+## Reference Documents\n+\n+| Document | Purpose |\n+|----------|---------|\n+| [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../../../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md) | System architecture and design principles |\n+| [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../../../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) | ModKit framework guide |\n+| [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../../../docs/SECURE-ORM.md) | Secure database access patterns |\n+| [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../../../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md) | Observability configuration |\n+| [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) | Step-by-step module creation |\n+| [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../../../guidelines/SECURITY.md) | Security best practices |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md) | REST API design |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md) | HTTP status code usage |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md) | Cursor pagination spec |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../../../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md) | Rust coding standards |","path":"modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md","commit_id":"b4bfa9cfc28554d894d046c8c12bee7d99d4965a","original_commit_id":"b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check existence of files referenced in project.md\n\necho \"=== Checking referenced files ===\"\n\n# List of explicitly mentioned files in the project.md\nfiles=(\n  \"guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\"\n  \"docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md\"\n  \"docs/SECURE-ORM.md\"\n  \"docs/TRACING_SETUP.md\"\n  \"docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md\"\n  \"guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\"\n  \"guidelines/SECURITY.md\"\n  \"guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md\"\n  \"guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md\"\n  \"guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md\"\n)\n\nmissing_files=()\nfound_files=()\n\nfor file in \"${files[@]}\"; do\n  if [ -f \"$file\" ]; then\n    echo \"✓ Found: $file\"\n    found_files+=(\"$file\")\n  else\n    echo \"✗ Missing: $file\"\n    missing_files+=(\"$file\")\n  fi\ndone\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Summary ===\"\necho \"Found: ${`#found_files`[@]}\"\necho \"Missing: ${`#missing_files`[@]}\"\n\nif [ ${`#missing_files`[@]} -gt 0 ]; then\n  echo \"\"\n  echo \"Missing files:\"\n  printf '%s\\n' \"${missing_files[@]}\"\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 657\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Create missing referenced documentation files or update project.md to remove broken references.**\n\nFour referenced files do not exist in the repository:\n- `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` (referenced for Rust code style and forbid(unsafe_code))\n- `guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md` (referenced for REST API design conventions)\n- `guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md` (referenced for HTTP status code usage)\n- `guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md` (referenced for cursor pagination spec)\n\nThe remaining six referenced files exist. Either create the missing files or remove the references from the project.md documentation to prevent broken links for developers.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md` around lines 11 - 138, The\nproject.md contains broken references to four missing guideline files\n(referenced paths \"@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\",\n\"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md\", \"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md\", and\n\"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md\"); fix by either (A) adding those files\nunder guidelines/DNA with minimal canonical contents matching the downstream\nmentions (Rust coding rules including #![forbid(unsafe_code)], REST API design\nsummary, status-code guidance, and cursor-pagination spec) and commit them, or\n(B) remove or replace the four links in project.md (look for the \"Language\" /\n\"Code Style\" and \"REST API Design\" sections referencing those paths) so they\npoint to existing documents or a generic placeholder, ensuring no other\nreferences remain; update any cross-reference links in project.md to the new\npaths and run a docs link-check to verify.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:39:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001635","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001635"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#discussion_r2699001635"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/264"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699001635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":11,"original_start_line":11,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":138,"original_line":138,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":138,"position":138,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3671495198,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7a1pIe","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 7**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`:\n- Around line 34-40: Add a \"Migration Strategy\" subsection under Impact that\ndefines a rollback plan, coexistence period, dependency analysis, and data\nmigration steps: explicitly state the rollback procedure if critical issues are\nfound (how to revert the new ModKit module and restore the old resource-group\nsymlink), define a compatibility period and whether both implementations will\nrun concurrently (and how to toggle via a feature flag), list how to detect and\nenumerate dependent modules/systems before switching, and include concrete data\nmigration guidance (migration scripts or manual steps, verification checks) and\ncontingency steps to restore data if migration fails; reference the existing\n\"resource-group\" symlink and the new ModKit module names to make the steps\nactionable.\n\nIn\n`@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`:\n- Around line 123-160: The spec is ambiguous about how reference counts and\nduplicate/authorization semantics work; update the document and schema to\nexplicitly state whether reference_count is a denormalized integer on the\nresource_group table (add `reference_count` with default 0) or computed at query\ntime, and if denormalized, describe concurrency controls (e.g., DB\ntransactions/optimistic locking) used by create_reference and delete_reference\nto avoid lost updates; also define duplicate behavior for the (group_id,\nresource_type, resource_id) tuple (either deduplicate and return\nResourceGroupError::ReferenceAlreadyExists on duplicates or allow multiple\nentries), specify who can delete a reference (creator application_id only or\ngroup owner allowed), and add the suggested scenarios (Reject duplicate\nreference, Handle concurrent reference operations, Query references for a\nresource) and clarify that ResourceGroupError::GroupHasReferences blocks delete\nbut whether moves in the hierarchy are allowed when references exist.\n- Around line 3-40: Add explicit edge-case scenarios to the Resource Group Type\nManagement spec: include a \"Handle case-insensitive type code lookup\" scenario\ndemonstrating lookup and duplicate rejection for codes like `DEPARTMENT` vs\n`department`; add a \"Create root type with no parents\" scenario to allow empty\nparents arrays for root types; add a \"Reject circular parent type definitions\"\nscenario and reference a new error `ResourceGroupError::CircularTypeReference`\nto validate the type graph on create/update; and add a \"Prevent parent changes\nwhen entities exist\" scenario that returns `ResourceGroupError::TypeInUse` when\nattempting to change `parents` for a type with existing entities and clarify\nowner/`allowed_app_ids` behavior when the array is empty (owner-only\nmodifications).\n- Around line 163-187: Add comprehensive authorization scenarios to the\n\"Authorization and Access Control\" section: explicitly specify permitted actions\n(create/modify/delete/move) and who may act (type owner, allowed_app_ids, entity\ncreator) by adding Scenario: Enforce tenant isolation (use\nResourceGroupError::NotFound for cross-tenant access), Scenario: Reject entity\ndeletion by non-allowed application (ResourceGroupError::Unauthorized),\nScenario: Type owner deletion behavior (define whether delete/cascade/orphan),\nScenario: Authorization for hierarchy moves (clarify allowed_app_ids vs creator\nvs type owner), and Scenario: Reference create/delete permissions (clarify who\ncan delete references); reference the existing section title and enums\nResourceGroupError::Unauthorized and ResourceGroupError::NotFound so tests and\nimplementations (authorization checks) can map scenarios to error codes.\n- Around line 189-225: The REST API spec is incomplete: add a move endpoint\n(e.g., POST /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/move with body\n{\"parent_id\":\"uuid-or-null\"}) and a references query endpoint (GET\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references), disambiguate reference deletion by\nreplacing DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references with either DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/references/{reference-id} or specify query params\n(resource_type/resource_id) for DELETE\n/resource-group/v1/groups/{id}/references, and update all list endpoints (GET\n/resource-group/v1/types and GET /resource-group/v1/groups) to support\npagination (?page=&page_size=) and include total_count/page/page_size in\nresponses; finally add error scenarios (400/401/403/404/409) with RFC-9457\nProblem Details examples (include a validation error JSON) referenced where POST\n/resource-group/v1/types and DELETE /resource-group/v1/groups are described.\n- Around line 42-93: The spec is missing edge-case scenarios and constraints for\nroot creation, deletions with children, external_id uniqueness, moving to\nroot/self, and type immutability; update the resource-group spec (the\n\"Requirement: Resource Group Entity Management\" section and its scenarios) to\nadd: a \"Create root entity\" scenario for parent_id = null documenting closure\nentry behavior; a clear policy for deletions (either cascade or prevent) plus a\n\"Prevent deletion of entity with children\" scenario returning\nResourceGroupError::EntityHasChildren if preventing; explicit uniqueness rules\nfor external_id (e.g., unique per type or global) and validation rules; a \"Move\nto root\" scenario allowing parent_id = null and rebuilding closure entries; a\n\"Reject moving entity to itself\" scenario returning\nResourceGroupError::SelfParentNotAllowed; and a rule/scenario that type_code is\nimmutable after creation with failures returning\nResourceGroupError::TypeImmutable. Ensure each new scenario references the\nexisting operations (create, move_entity, delete, update) and error symbols\n(ResourceGroupError::CycleDetected, ::EntityHasChildren, ::SelfParentNotAllowed,\n::TypeImmutable) so implementers can locate relevant handlers.\n\nIn `@modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`:\n- Around line 11-138: The project.md contains broken references to four missing\nguideline files (referenced paths \"@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md\",\n\"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md\", \"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md\", and\n\"@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md\"); fix by either (A) adding those files\nunder guidelines/DNA with minimal canonical contents matching the downstream\nmentions (Rust coding rules including #![forbid(unsafe_code)], REST API design\nsummary, status-code guidance, and cursor-pagination spec) and commit them, or\n(B) remove or replace the four links in project.md (look for the \"Language\" /\n\"Code Style\" and \"REST API Design\" sections referencing those paths) so they\npoint to existing documents or a generic placeholder, ensuring no other\nreferences remain; update any cross-reference links in project.md to the new\npaths and run a docs link-check to verify.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`49-49`: **Consider promoting to a heading.**\n\nThe \"**Workflow**\" text uses emphasis instead of a proper heading. For better document structure and navigation, consider using a heading level (e.g., `#### Workflow` or `**Workflow**` → `#### Workflow`).\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-**Workflow**\n+#### Workflow\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`131-147`: **Add language identifier to directory structure code block.**\n\nThe directory structure would benefit from a language identifier for proper rendering and syntax highlighting in documentation viewers.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n openspec/\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`153-161`: **Add language identifier to decision tree code block.**\n\nThe decision tree would render better with a language identifier.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n New request?\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`357-366`: **Add language identifier to file structure code block.**\n\nThe multi-capability example structure would benefit from a language identifier.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n openspec/changes/add-2fa-notify/\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`95-121`: **Clarify closure table semantics and add edge case scenarios.**\n\nThe closure table pattern is well-chosen, but the specification needs clarification:\n\n1. **Self-reference rows**: Line 107 mentions depth=0 for self-reference, but doesn't explicitly state that every entity MUST have a self-reference row. This should be clarified.\n\n2. **Ancestor ordering ambiguity**: Line 113 states \"ordered by depth (ascending)\" but this is ambiguous. Does ascending mean `[ROOT, ORG, DEPT]` (far to near) or `[DEPT, ORG, ROOT]` (near to far)? Based on the example, it appears to mean far-to-near, but this should be explicit.\n\n3. **Empty result behavior**: Missing scenarios for:\n   - Querying ancestors of a root entity (return empty list or include self?)\n   - Querying descendants of a leaf entity (return empty list or include self?)\n\n4. **Closure table maintenance**: Line 102 mentions \"efficient subtree operations\" but doesn't specify how closure entries are maintained during delete operations. Are rows cascade-deleted?\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested clarifications and scenarios</summary>\n\n```markdown\n#### Clarification: Self-reference entries\n\nEvery entity SHALL have a closure table entry with `parent_id = child_id` and `depth = 0` for itself.\n\n#### Clarification: Ancestor ordering\n\nAncestors are returned ordered by depth ascending, meaning farthest ancestors first (ROOT before immediate parent).\n\n#### Scenario: Query ancestors of root entity\n\n- **GIVEN** a root entity `root-id` with no parent\n- **WHEN** the user calls `get_ancestors` for `root-id`\n- **THEN** the system returns an empty list (self-reference excluded)\n\n#### Scenario: Closure table cleanup on delete\n\n- **GIVEN** an entity `node-id` with ancestors and descendants\n- **WHEN** the entity is deleted\n- **THEN** all closure entries where `parent_id = node-id` OR `child_id = node-id` are deleted\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 949b3e840c1742bd1fb0de560223f63642ee935b and b493aadd8a8708109bdab04e79c077a1f691d16f.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/api_gateway/assets/elements/web-components.min.js` is excluded by `!**/*.min.js`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (7)</summary>\n\n* `.gitignore`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md`\n* `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (16)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📓 Common learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Before creating any task, read relevant specs in `specs/[capability]/spec.md`, check pending changes for conflicts, read `openspec/project.md`, run `openspec list` and `openspec list --specs`\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Scaffold `proposal.md`, `tasks.md`, and optional `design.md` along with delta specs under `openspec/changes/<id>/` for change proposals\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-r