es/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Create proposal.md file for all changes that add features, make breaking changes, change architecture/patterns, optimize performance, or update security patterns\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md` to learn about the project's `@/lib/modkit`* unified system\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Always consult project-wide resources in `guidelines/` directory for project conventions and best practices\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 LanguageTool</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md</summary>\n\n[style] ~36-~36: You have already used this phrasing in nearby sentences. Consider replacing it to add variety to your writing.\nContext: ...\"I want to create a spec proposal\" - \"I want to create a spec\"  Loose matching guidance...\n\n(REP_WANT_TO_VB)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md</summary>\n\n49-49: Emphasis used instead of a heading\n\n(MD036, no-emphasis-as-heading)\n\n---\n\n131-131: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n---\n\n153-153: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n---\n\n299-299: Emphasis used instead of a heading\n\n(MD036, no-emphasis-as-heading)\n\n---\n\n303-303: Emphasis used instead of a heading\n\n(MD036, no-emphasis-as-heading)\n\n---\n\n307-307: Emphasis used instead of a heading\n\n(MD036, no-emphasis-as-heading)\n\n---\n\n357-357: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (9)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=pg)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=sqlite)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (9)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.gitignore (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`36-39`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe ignore patterns for minified frontend assets are appropriate. Build artifacts like `*.min.js` and `*.min.css` should not be committed to version control.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-18`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe OpenSpec pointer file is well-structured with clear triggers and a managed block that enables automated refresh via `openspec update`. This aligns with the project's OpenSpec workflow conventions.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-461`: **Comprehensive OpenSpec guide with excellent structure.**\n\nThis document provides thorough coverage of the OpenSpec workflow, including the three-stage process (Creating, Implementing, Archiving), spec format conventions, CLI commands, troubleshooting, and examples. The content aligns well with the retrieved learnings and establishes clear guidelines for spec-driven development.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/tasks.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-114`: **Excellent implementation checklist.**\n\nThe task breakdown is comprehensive and well-organized across 10 major sections. It properly covers all aspects of module development including SDK setup, domain/infrastructure layers, REST API, authorization, testing (with 90%+ coverage target), and documentation. The hierarchical structure with sub-tasks provides clear implementation guidance.\n\nThe tasks align well with the project conventions specified in `project.md` and follow the OpenSpec three-stage workflow from `AGENTS.md`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/project.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-138`: **Comprehensive project context document.**\n\nThis file provides excellent context covering the module's purpose, tech stack, architecture principles (DDD-light, SDK pattern), module structure, coding conventions, REST API design, security requirements, database patterns (SecureORM, closure table), testing strategy (90%+ coverage), and important constraints. The reference documents table at the end provides clear navigation to related guidelines.\n\nThe document aligns well with the OpenSpec workflow and establishes clear conventions for implementation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/proposal.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`3-8`: **LGTM! Clear motivation and context.**\n\nThe rationale for rebuilding the module is well-articulated, providing clear context about the migration from the old symlink architecture to a proper ModKit module.\n\n---\n\n`28-33`: The spec already provides comprehensive authorization coverage, including detailed requirements and concrete scenarios. No action required.\n\nThe \"Authorization and Access Control\" requirement (spec.md:163) clearly defines:\n- Type owners can modify their types\n- Applications in `allowed_app_ids` can create/modify entities of that type\n- Concrete scenarios for authorized type creation and rejection of unauthorized entity creation\n\nThe proposal's feature description is accurate and appropriately linked to the spec's detailed authorization model.\n\n---\n\n`9-33`: **Tenant isolation is properly specified; clarify data migration strategy for existing resource-group data.**\n\nThe proposal and spec adequately address tenant isolation—SecurityCtx is enforced in API methods (proposal line 17, spec line 171), and Secure ORM is required for all tables (spec lines 261, 268). However, the proposal mentions replacing the old symlink-based implementation but does not detail a strategy for migrating existing data from the old system. Clarify whether the old implementation has persisted data that needs migration, or if this is a greenfield deployment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/resource-group/openspec/changes/add-resource-group-module/specs/resource-group/spec.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`227-268`: **Critical database schema issues - missing columns, constraints, and unclear specifications.**\n\nThe database schema has several serious issues:\n\n1. **Missing `parent_id` column**: Line 238-243 defines `resource_group` table but omits the `parent_id` column that's central to the entity structure (line 51). This is a critical omission.\n\n2. **Case-insensitive code implementation unclear**: Line 232 states code is \"case-insensitive\" but doesn't specify how:\n   - PostgreSQL: Use `CITEXT` type or `LOWER(code)` index?\n   - SQLite: Use `COLLATE NOCASE`?\n   Implementation must be specified for portability.\n\n3. **Missing tenant isolation column**: Line 261 requires \"Secure ORM\" but the schema doesn't show `tenant_id` columns. How is tenant isolation enforced at the database level?\n\n4. **No referential integrity for JSON arrays**:\n   - Line 233: `parents` array of type codes - no FK to validate types exist\n   - Line 235: `allowed_app_ids` array of UUIDs - no FK to validate apps exist\n   This allows dangling references.\n\n5. **Missing foreign key cascade behaviors**:\n   - Line 240: `type_code` FK - what happens if type is deleted? Should CASCADE or SET NULL or RESTRICT?\n   - Line 247, 254: FKs to `resource_group.id` - specify cascade behavior\n\n6. **Missing `reference_count` field**: Lines 145, 159 mention incrementing/decrementing reference count, but the schema has no such column.\n\n7. **Index redundancy/gaps**:\n   - Line 250: Indexes on `parent_id, child_id` are redundant (already in composite PK)\n   - Missing index on `resource_group.parent_id` for parent-child lookups\n   - Missing index on `resource_group_reference.group_id` for reference queries\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Corrected schema</summary>\n\n```markdown\n**`resource_group_type`:**\n- `code` (PK): String, unique, `CITEXT` (PostgreSQL) or `COLLATE NOCASE` (SQLite)\n- `parents`: JSON array of type codes (consider junction table for referential integrity)\n- `application_id`: UUID (owner), NOT NULL\n- `allowed_app_ids`: JSON array of UUIDs (consider junction table for referential integrity)\n- `tenant_id`: UUID, NOT NULL (for Secure ORM isolation)\n- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n- Index on `tenant_id`\n\n**`resource_group`:**\n- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n- `type_code` (FK): String → `resource_group_type.code` ON DELETE RESTRICT\n- `name`: String (1-255 chars), NOT NULL\n- `external_id`: Optional String (max 255 chars)\n- `parent_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id` ON DELETE RESTRICT (self-reference)\n- `reference_count`: Integer, DEFAULT 0, NOT NULL\n- `tenant_id`: UUID, NOT NULL\n- `created_at`, `updated_at`: Timestamps\n- Index on `parent_id`\n- Index on `tenant_id`\n- Index on `(tenant_id, type_code)`\n\n**`resource_group_closure`:**\n- `parent_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id` ON DELETE CASCADE\n- `child_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id` ON DELETE CASCADE\n- `depth`: Integer, NOT NULL, CHECK (depth >= 0)\n- `tenant_id`: UUID, NOT NULL\n- Composite PK: `(parent_id, child_id)`\n- Index on `child_id` (for descendant queries)\n- Index on `(parent_id, depth)` (for ancestor queries)\n- Index on `tenant_id`\n\n**`resource_group_reference`:**\n- `id` (PK): UUIDv7\n- `group_id` (FK): UUID → `resource_group.id` ON DELETE CASCADE\n- `resource_type`: String, NOT NULL\n- `resource_id`: String, NOT NULL\n- `application_id`: UUID, NOT NULL\n- `tenant_id`: UUID, NOT NULL\n- `created_at`: Timestamp\n- UNIQUE constraint on `(group_id, resource_type, resource_id)` (prevent duplicates)\n- Index on `(resource_type, resource_id)` (for reverse lookups)\n- Index on `tenant_id`\n```\n</details>\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Skipped due to learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md` to learn about the project's database interactions with ORM\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/264#pullrequestreview-36714