rectory-scoped\npatterns so that styles.min.css remains version-controlled and editable.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>.gitignore (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`37-39`: **Consider reorganizing the placement of frontend asset patterns.**\n\nThe frontend asset ignore patterns are placed under the \"Code coverage reports\" section, which seems logically disconnected. Consider moving these patterns to a more appropriate location or creating a standalone section for build artifacts.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📁 Suggested reorganization</summary>\n\n```diff\n # Code coverage reports\n /coverage/\n-\n-# static frontend assets\n-*.min.js\n-*.min.css\n+\n+# Static frontend assets (build artifacts)\n+*.min.js\n+*.min.css\n```\n\nOr place it at the end of the file as a separate section to keep build artifacts grouped together.\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 949b3e840c1742bd1fb0de560223f63642ee935b and 12ab52eecb280c685024f51755aa2ea20fd865ba.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/system/api_gateway/assets/elements/web-components.min.js` is excluded by `!**/*.min.js`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `.gitignore`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (9)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=pg)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=sqlite)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/262#pullrequestreview-3670602071","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/262","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/262#pullrequestreview-3670602071"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/262"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T12:12:47Z","commit_id":"12ab52eecb280c685024f51755aa2ea20fd865ba"},{"id":3677438788,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7bMUNE","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/api_gateway/build.rs`:\n- Around line 8-12: The pinned Stoplight Elements version is invalid and causes\ndownload failures; update the const STOPLIGHT_ELEMENTS_VERSION in build.rs (the\nconstant named STOPLIGHT_ELEMENTS_VERSION) to a valid published release like\n\"9.0.6\" (or another existing npm version) so the build fetches an existing\npackage from unpkg.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/build.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`47-57`: **Add a timeout to avoid hanging builds on slow/unreachable CDNs.**\n\nThe build script performs blocking network calls; without a timeout, CI can hang indefinitely. Consider setting a reasonable timeout in `download_to`.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed change (timeout using reqwest 0.12.x)</summary>\n\n```diff\n+use std::time::Duration;\n+\n fn download_to(url: &str, dest: &Path) -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\n     println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", dest.display());\n-    let resp = reqwest::blocking::get(url)?;\n+    let client = reqwest::blocking::Client::builder()\n+        .timeout(Duration::from_secs(30))\n+        .build()?;\n+    let resp = client.get(url).send()?;\n     if !resp.status().is_success() {\n         return Err(format!(\"HTTP {} for {}\", resp.status(), url).into());\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/262#pullrequestreview-3677438788","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/262","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/262#pullrequestreview-3677438788"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/262"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-19T10:44:24Z","commit_id":"d4059a14cc1157ecc863d0dca5e44fbb277bcebf"}]},{"source_pr_number":258,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258","source_state":"closed","source_author":"ainetx","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #258] DO NOT MERGE feat(fdd-adapter): add FDD adapter with validation checklists and GTS…","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"fdd-adapter","pr_head_sha":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"ainetx","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","id":3180316415,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs69j8b_","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/258","number":258,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"DO NOT MERGE feat(fdd-adapter): add FDD adapter with validation checklists and GTS…","user":{"login":"ainetx","id":244471386,"node_id":"U_kgDODpJWWg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/244471386?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx","html_url":"https://github.com/ainetx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ainetx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"# Add FDD Adapter with Validation Framework\r\n## Description\r\nImplements FDD Adapter for HyperSpot with 14 specification files containing validation checklists, compliance criteria, and agent instructions.\r\n**Added**:\r\n- `FDD-Adapter/` with 14 specs (tech-stack, domain-model, api-contracts, patterns, conventions, linting, build-deploy, testing, project-structure, rest-api-guidelines, rust-guidelines, module-creation, security, architectural-lints)\r\n- GTS validation integration in domain-model.md\r\n- Submodules: `FDD` (ainetx/FDD), `GTS` (GlobalTypeSystem/gts-spec)\r\n- Commit rule in main [AGENTS.md](cci:7://file:///Volumes/CaseSensitive/coding/hyperspot/AGENTS.md:0:0-0:0)\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added a comprehensive suite of new specifications covering API contracts, architecture, build/deploy, conventions, domain models, linting, module creation, patterns, performance, project structure, REST/Rust/security guidelines, tech stack, and testing.\n  * Replaced and consolidated contributor/workflow guidance with a condensed AGENTS header and new commit signing/message conventions.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Registered new project submodules and added a configuration file to reference adapter/submodule locations.\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can customize this high-level summary in your review settings.</sub>\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:22:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T08:21:08Z","closed_at":"2026-02-03T08:20:17Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assi