_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Specify language for the fenced code block.**\n\nThe endpoint pattern template should specify a language identifier for proper syntax highlighting and tooling support. Since this is a URL path template, consider using `text` or `http` as the language identifier.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n ## Endpoint Pattern\n \n-```\n+```text\n /{module}/v{version}/{resource}\n ```\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on static analysis hints.\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n## Endpoint Pattern\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n20-20: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/api-contracts.md` around lines 18 - 22, The fenced code\nblock under \"Endpoint Pattern\" in FDD-Adapter/specs/api-contracts.md should\ninclude a language identifier for proper highlighting; update the block\ndelimiter from ``` to a tagged fence like ```text (or ```http) so the template\n`/ {module}/v{version}/{resource}` is fenced as ```text\n/{module}/v{version}/{resource} ```—modify the code block around the Endpoint\nPattern heading accordingly.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:18Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468576","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468576"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468576"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468576/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":18,"original_start_line":18,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":22,"original_line":22,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":22,"position":22,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468592","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468592,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBqw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,330 @@\n+# Architectural Compliance Lints\n+\n+**Source**: dylint_lints/README.md, dylint_lints/AGENTS.md\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+HyperSpot uses **custom dylint linters** to enforce architectural patterns, layer separation, and REST API conventions at **compile time**.\n+\n+**Why Custom Lints**:\n+- Prevent architectural violations before code review\n+- Enforce team conventions automatically\n+- Catch common mistakes early (compile-time, not runtime)\n+- Document architecture rules as executable code\n+\n+## Running Lints\n+\n+```bash\n+# From workspace root\n+make dylint              # Run all lints (auto-rebuilds if changed)\n+make dylint-list         # Show all available lints\n+make dylint-test         # Test UI cases\n+```\n+\n+Or with Python CI:\n+```bash\n+python scripts/ci.py dylint\n+```\n+\n+## Lint Categories\n+\n+### DE01xx: Contract Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Ensure contract layer is transport-agnostic (no HTTP/serialization concerns)\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0101**: No Serde in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`\n+  - Reason: Contracts are transport-agnostic\n+  - Use DTOs in API layer for serialization\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0102**: No ToSchema in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT derive `ToSchema` (utoipa)\n+  - Reason: OpenAPI is HTTP concern, not contract\n+  - Use DTOs with `ToSchema` in API layer\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0103**: No HTTP Types in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT use HTTP types (`axum`, `hyper`, etc.)\n+  - Reason: Contracts are protocol-independent\n+  - HTTP types belong in API handlers\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: src/contract/user.rs\n+#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]  // Serde in contract\n+pub struct User { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/contract/user.rs\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]  // No serde\n+pub struct User { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]  // Serde in DTO\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE02xx: API Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Ensure DTOs are properly isolated and have required derives\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0201**: DTOs Only in API Rest Folder\n+  - Types with `Dto` suffix MUST be in `api/rest/` folder\n+  - Prevents DTO leakage into domain/contract\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0202**: DTOs Not Referenced Outside API\n+  - DTOs MUST NOT be used outside `api/` module\n+  - Ensures clean layer separation\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0203**: DTOs Must Have Serde Derives\n+  - DTOs MUST derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize`\n+  - Required for JSON serialization\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0204**: DTOs Must Have ToSchema Derive\n+  - DTOs MUST derive `ToSchema` (utoipa)\n+  - Required for OpenAPI generation\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: src/domain/model.rs\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }  // DTO outside api/rest/\n+\n+// ❌ BAD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Debug)]  // Missing Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE05xx: Client/Gateway Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce naming conventions for plugin clients\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0503**: Plugin Client Suffix\n+  - Plugin client types MUST end with `Client` suffix\n+  - Example: `MyServiceClient`, not `MyService`\n+\n+### DE08xx: REST API Conventions\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce REST API best practices\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0801**: API Endpoint Must Have Version\n+  - All REST endpoints MUST include version in path\n+  - Pattern: `/{module}/v{version}/{resource}`\n+  - Example: `/users/v1/users`, not `/users`\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0802**: Use OData Extension Methods\n+  - Pagination handlers MUST use OData extension methods\n+  - Use `modkit_odata::ODataQueryExt` for filtering/sorting\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: No version in path\n+#[utoipa::path(get, path = \"/users\")]\n+pub async fn list_users() { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: Version included\n+#[utoipa::path(get, path = \"/users/v1/users\")]\n+pub async fn list_users() { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE09xx: GTS Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce GTS (Global Type System) patterns\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0901**: GTS String Pattern\n+  - GTS string fields MUST follow pattern conventions\n+  \n+- ✅ **DE0902**: No Schema For on GTS Structs\n+  - GTS types have their own schema system\n+  - Don't mix with utoipa `ToSchema`\n+\n+## Planned Lints (TODO)\n+\n+### DE03xx: Domain Layer\n+- Validate domain logic isolation\n+- Ensure no infrastructure dependencies\n+\n+### DE04xx: Infrastructure Layer\n+- Validate repository implementations\n+- Ensure proper entity/model separation\n+\n+### DE06xx: Module Structure\n+- Enforce module organization\n+- Validate module declaration\n+\n+### DE07xx: Security\n+- Detect potential security issues\n+- Enforce Secure ORM usage\n+\n+### DE10xx: Error Handling\n+- Validate error types\n+- Ensure proper error propagation\n+\n+### DE11xx: Testing\n+- Enforce test naming conventions\n+- Validate test coverage patterns\n+\n+### DE12xx: Documentation\n+- Ensure public items have doc comments\n+- Validate doc example compilation\n+\n+## Adding New Lints\n+\n+When architectural rules emerge, convert them to lints:\n+\n+1. **Create lint**: `cd dylint_lints && cargo dylint new de0xxx_lint_name`\n+2. **Implement check**: Define what the lint detects\n+3. **Add examples**: Create good/bad examples in `ui/`\n+4. **Test**: Run `make dylint-test`\n+5. **Document**: Add to this spec and README\n+\n+## Best Practices\n+\n+- ✅ **Fix lint violations immediately** (don't accumulate technical debt)\n+- ✅ **Run lints in CI** (fail build on violations)\n+- ✅ **Add lints for recurring code review feedback**\n+- ✅ **Keep lints simple and focused** (one rule per lint)\n+- ✅ **Provide clear error messages** with examples\n+- ❌ **Don't disable lints** without architecture team approval\n+- ❌ **Don't use `#[allow(...)]`** unless absolutely necessary\n+","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/architectural-lints.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Define criteria for \"absolutely necessary\" #[allow(...)] usage.**\n\nThe guideline states \"Don't use `#[allow(...)]` unless absolutely necessary\" but doesn't define when it is necessary. This ambiguity could lead to inconsistent application or developers avoiding legitimate suppression of false positives.\n\n\n\nConsider adding:\n- **Approved scenarios**: Code generation, external trait implementations, temporary workarounds with tracked issues, specific false positives documented with architecture team\n- **Approval process**: Require comment explaining why suppression is needed, link to issue tracking resolution\n- **False positive handling**: Process for reporting and resolving false positives in lints themselves\n\n<details>\n<summary>📋 Suggested guideline enhancement</summary>\n\n```markdown\n### When #[allow(...)] is Acceptable\n\nUse `#[allow(...)]` ONLY when:\n1. **Generated code**: Code produced by build scripts or macros (add comment explaining)\n2. **External trait impl**: Trait requirements from external crates conflict with lint\n3. **Documented false positive**: Lint incorrectly flags correct code (file issue, link in comment)\n4. **Temporary workaround**: Short-term fix with tracking issue (expires within sprint)\n\nFormat:\n```rust\n// LINT_ALLOW: DE0xxx - Brief justification\n// Issue: `#1234` - Link to tracking issue\n#[allow(clippy::lint_name)]\n```\n\nFor false positives: Open issue in `dylint_lints/` with reproduction case.\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/architectural-lints.md` around lines 187 - 196, The \"Don't\nuse #[allow(...)] unless absolutely necessary\" guideline is ambiguous—add a\nconcise \"When #[allow(...)] is Acceptable\" subsection that enumerates approved\nscenarios (generated code, external trait implementations, documented false\npositives, temporary workarounds with tracked issues), require an\napproval/process (a brief in-source justification comment and a link to an\nissue/approval ticket), and describe false-positive handling (file issue in\ndylint_lints/ with repro and link it in the comment); also include the exact\ncomment format to require (e.g., a LINT_ALLOW tag, brief justification, and\nIssue: `#nnnn`) so reviewers can validate suppressions consistently.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468592","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468592"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468592"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468592/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":187,"original_start_line":187,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":196,"original_line":196,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":196,"position":196,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468600","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468600,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBq4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,330 @@\n+# Architectural Compliance Lints\n+\n+**Source**: dylint_lints/README.md, dylint_lints/AGENTS.md\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+HyperSpot uses **custom dylint linters** to enforce architectural patterns, layer separation, and REST API conventions at **compile time**.\n+\n+**Why Custom Lints**:\n+- Prevent architectural violations before code review\n+- Enforce team conventions automatically\n+- Catch common mistakes early (compile-time, not runtime)\n+- Document architecture rules as executable code\n+\n+## Running Lints\n+\n+```bash\n+# From workspace root\n+make dylint              # Run all lints (auto-rebuilds if changed)\n+make dylint-list         # Show all available lints\n+make dylint-test         # Test UI cases\n+```\n+\n+Or with Python CI:\n+```bash\n+python scripts/ci.py dylint\n+```\n+\n+## Lint Categories\n+\n+### DE01xx: Contract Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Ensure contract layer is transport-agnostic (no HTTP/serialization concerns)\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0101**: No Serde in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT derive `Serialize`/`Deserialize`\n+  - Reason: Contracts are transport-agnostic\n+  - Use DTOs in API layer for serialization\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0102**: No ToSchema in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT derive `ToSchema` (utoipa)\n+  - Reason: OpenAPI is HTTP concern, not contract\n+  - Use DTOs with `ToSchema` in API layer\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0103**: No HTTP Types in Contract\n+  - Contract types MUST NOT use HTTP types (`axum`, `hyper`, etc.)\n+  - Reason: Contracts are protocol-independent\n+  - HTTP types belong in API handlers\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: src/contract/user.rs\n+#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]  // Serde in contract\n+pub struct User { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/contract/user.rs\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone)]  // No serde\n+pub struct User { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]  // Serde in DTO\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE02xx: API Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Ensure DTOs are properly isolated and have required derives\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0201**: DTOs Only in API Rest Folder\n+  - Types with `Dto` suffix MUST be in `api/rest/` folder\n+  - Prevents DTO leakage into domain/contract\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0202**: DTOs Not Referenced Outside API\n+  - DTOs MUST NOT be used outside `api/` module\n+  - Ensures clean layer separation\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0203**: DTOs Must Have Serde Derives\n+  - DTOs MUST derive `Serialize` and `Deserialize`\n+  - Required for JSON serialization\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0204**: DTOs Must Have ToSchema Derive\n+  - DTOs MUST derive `ToSchema` (utoipa)\n+  - Required for OpenAPI generation\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: src/domain/model.rs\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }  // DTO outside api/rest/\n+\n+// ❌ BAD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Debug)]  // Missing Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: src/api/rest/dto.rs\n+#[derive(Debug, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct UserDto { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE05xx: Client/Gateway Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce naming conventions for plugin clients\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0503**: Plugin Client Suffix\n+  - Plugin client types MUST end with `Client` suffix\n+  - Example: `MyServiceClient`, not `MyService`\n+\n+### DE08xx: REST API Conventions\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce REST API best practices\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0801**: API Endpoint Must Have Version\n+  - All REST endpoints MUST include version in path\n+  - Pattern: `/{module}/v{version}/{resource}`\n+  - Example: `/users/v1/users`, not `/users`\n+\n+- ✅ **DE0802**: Use OData Extension Methods\n+  - Pagination handlers MUST use OData extension methods\n+  - Use `modkit_odata::ODataQueryExt` for filtering/sorting\n+\n+**Example Violation**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: No version in path\n+#[utoipa::path(get, path = \"/users\")]\n+pub async fn list_users() { ... }\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: Version included\n+#[utoipa::path(get, path = \"/users/v1/users\")]\n+pub async fn list_users() { ... }\n+```\n+\n+### DE09xx: GTS Layer\n+\n+**Purpose**: Enforce GTS (Global Type System) patterns\n+\n+**Lints**:\n+- ✅ **DE0901**: GTS String Pattern\n+  - GTS string fields MUST follow pattern conventions\n+  \n+- ✅ **DE0902**: No Schema For on GTS Structs\n+  - GTS types have their own schema system\n+  - Don't mix with utoipa `ToSchema`\n+\n+## Planned Lints (TODO)\n+\n+### DE03xx: Domain Layer\n+- Validate domain logic isolation\n+- Ensure no infrastructure dependencies\n+\n+### DE04xx: Infrastructure Layer\n+- Validate repository implementations\n+- Ensure proper entity/model separation\n+\n+### DE06xx: Module Structure\n+- Enforce module organization\n+- Validate module declaration\n+\n+### DE07xx: Security\n+- Detect potential security issues\n+- Enforce Secure ORM usage\n+\n+### DE10xx: Error Handling\n+- Validate error types\n+- Ensure proper error propagation\n+\n+### DE11xx: Testing\n+- Enforce test naming conventions\n+- Validate test coverage patterns\n+\n+### DE12xx: Documentation\n+- Ensure public items have doc comments\n+- Validate doc example compilation\n+\n+## Adding New Lints\n+\n+When architectural rules emerge, convert them to lints:\n+\n+1. **Create lint**: `cd dylint_lints && cargo dylint new de0xxx_lint_name`\n+2. **Implement check**: Define what the lint detects\n+3. **Add examples**: Create good/bad examples in `ui/`\n+4. **Test**: Run `make dylint-test`\n+5. **Document**: Add to this spec and README\n+\n+## Best Practices\n+\n+- ✅ **Fix lint violations immediately** (don't accumulate technical debt)\n+- ✅ **Run lints in CI** (fail build on violations)\n+- ✅ **Add lints for recurring code review feedback**\n+- ✅ **Keep lints simple and focused** (one rule per lint)\n+- ✅ **Provide clear error messages** with examples\n+- ❌ **Don't disable lints** without architecture team approval\n+- ❌ **Don't use `#[allow(...)]`** unless absolutely necessary\n+\n+## CI Integration\n+\n+```bash\n+# In CI pipeline\n+python scripts/ci.py dylint\n+\n+# Or with Make\n+make dylint\n+\n+# Fails with exit code 1 on violations\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/architectural-lints.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify CI integration files exist\n\necho \"Checking for CI scripts...\"\nif [ -f \"scripts/ci.py\" ]; then\n    echo \"✓ Found: scripts/ci.py\"\n    echo \"  Checking for dylint command...\"\n    rg -A 5 \"def.*dylint|'dylint'|\\\"dylint\\\"\" scripts/ci.py\nelse\n    echo \"✗ Missing: scripts/ci.py\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Checking for CI configuration files...\"\nfd -t f '\\.github|\\.gitlab-ci|Jenkinsfile' -x echo \"Found: {}\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Checking Makefile for dylint targets...\"\nif [ -f \"Makefile\" ]; then\n    rg \"^dylint\" Makefile\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1943\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add CI system and pipeline integration context to the specification.**\n\nThe specification references `python scripts/ci.py dylint` which exists and is functional, but lacks critical context:\n- No CI system is documented (GitHub Actions, GitLab CI, etc. not configured)\n- No guidance on pipeline placement or execution order relative to other checks\n- The claim that it \"Fails with exit code 1 on violations\" is stated without explaining the failure mechanism or how violations are reported\n\nExpand the section to document which CI environment this integrates with and at what stage of the pipeline Dylan checks should run.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/architectural-lints.md` around lines 197 - 207, Update the\n\"CI Integration\" section to specify the CI system and pipeline placement: state\nthat the dylint step is configured for the project's GitHub Actions workflow (or\nalternative CI you use), reference the existing command \"python scripts/ci.py\ndylint\" (and \"make dylint\") as the step to execute, and indicate it should run\nin the lint/static-analysis job before build/test stages (e.g., on push and\nPRs). Also describe the failure mechanism and reporting: explain that the script\nexits with status code 1 on any dylint violations, causing the CI job to fail,\nand that violations are printed to stdout/stderr by the script (or written to a\nlog artifact) so reviewers can inspect the reported issues.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468600","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468600"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468600"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468600/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":197,"original_start_line":197,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":207,"original_line":207,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":207,"position":207,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468604","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468604,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBq8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@\n+# Domain Model Specification\n+\n+**Source**: libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs, module source code\n+\n+## Technology\n+\n+**Rust Type System** + **GTS (Global Type System)**\n+\n+## Format\n+\n+Domain models are defined as Rust `struct` and `enum` types with derives:\n+- `serde::Serialize` / `serde::Deserialize` for JSON serialization\n+- `utoipa::ToSchema` for OpenAPI schema generation\n+- Custom derives from `modkit-macros` as needed\n+\n+## Locations\n+\n+**Core Types**: `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`  \n+**Module Contracts**: `modules/{module}/src/contract/`  \n+**SDK Types**: `modules/{module}/{module}-sdk/src/`\n+\n+## Type Reference Syntax\n+\n+Use fully-qualified Rust paths when referencing domain types:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Example references\n+modkit::contracts::ModuleInfo\n+file_parser::contract::FileParserInfoDto\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Integration\n+\n+**GTS (Global Type System)** enables extensible type definitions:\n+- Custom schema extensions\n+- Plugin-provided types\n+- Tenant-specific type customizations\n+\n+**GTS Location**: Integrated in modkit framework\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+**Command**: `cargo check --workspace`  \n+**Expected**: No type errors, all contracts compile\n+\n+## Example\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use utoipa::ToSchema;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+pub enum ModuleStatus {\n+    Active,\n+    Inactive,\n+    Error,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Validation (MANDATORY)\n+\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix markdown formatting for the URL.**\n\nThe bare URL should use proper markdown link syntax for consistency with documentation standards.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust)\n```\n</details>\n\nBased on static analysis hints.\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n**Tool**: `gts` CLI from [gts-rust](https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust)\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n70-70: Bare URL used\n\n(MD034, no-bare-urls)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/domain-model.md` at line 70, The markdown currently shows a\nbare URL after the Tool description (\"gts CLI\") which should be formatted as a\nproper markdown link; update the line containing \"**Tool**: `gts` CLI from\nhttps://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\" to use markdown link syntax (e.g.,\nlink the repository URL with descriptive text such as the project name or \"gts\nCLI\") so the `gts` CLI reference and the URL are combined into a single markdown\nlink.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468604","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468604"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468604"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468604/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":70,"original_line":70,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":70,"position":70,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468609","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468609,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBrB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@\n+# Domain Model Specification\n+\n+**Source**: libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs, module source code\n+\n+## Technology\n+\n+**Rust Type System** + **GTS (Global Type System)**\n+\n+## Format\n+\n+Domain models are defined as Rust `struct` and `enum` types with derives:\n+- `serde::Serialize` / `serde::Deserialize` for JSON serialization\n+- `utoipa::ToSchema` for OpenAPI schema generation\n+- Custom derives from `modkit-macros` as needed\n+\n+## Locations\n+\n+**Core Types**: `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`  \n+**Module Contracts**: `modules/{module}/src/contract/`  \n+**SDK Types**: `modules/{module}/{module}-sdk/src/`\n+\n+## Type Reference Syntax\n+\n+Use fully-qualified Rust paths when referencing domain types:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Example references\n+modkit::contracts::ModuleInfo\n+file_parser::contract::FileParserInfoDto\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Integration\n+\n+**GTS (Global Type System)** enables extensible type definitions:\n+- Custom schema extensions\n+- Plugin-provided types\n+- Tenant-specific type customizations\n+\n+**GTS Location**: Integrated in modkit framework\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+**Command**: `cargo check --workspace`  \n+**Expected**: No type errors, all contracts compile\n+\n+## Example\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use utoipa::ToSchema;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+pub enum ModuleStatus {\n+    Active,\n+    Inactive,\n+    Error,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Validation (MANDATORY)\n+\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate GTS entities, identifiers, and schemas to ensure compliance with Global Type System standards.\n+\n+**Installation**:\n+```bash\n+cargo install gts\n+```\n+\n+**Key Commands**:\n+\n+### Validate GTS ID Format\n+```bash\n+gts validate-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Parse GTS ID Components\n+```bash\n+gts parse-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Validate Instance Against Schema\n+```bash\n+gts validate-instance --schema <schema_file> --instance <instance_file>\n+```\n+\n+### Generate Schemas from Rust Code\n+```bash\n+gts generate-from-rust --input <source_dir> --output <schema_dir>\n+```\n+\n+**Annotations for Schema Generation**:\n+```rust\n+use gts::struct_to_gts_schema;\n+\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema]\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Validation Workflow\n+\n+**Before committing domain types**:\n+1. Annotate types with `#[struct_to_gts_schema]`\n+2. Generate GTS schemas: `gts generate-from-rust --input libs/modkit/src --output gts_schemas/`\n+3. Validate IDs: `gts validate-id <entity_id>`\n+4. Validate instances: `gts validate-instance --schema gts_schemas/<type>.json --instance instances/<entity>.json`\n+\n+**CI Integration**:\n+- GTS validation MUST pass in CI pipeline\n+- Schema generation MUST be automated\n+- ID format validation MUST be enforced\n+\n+**Common Commands**:\n+```bash\n+# List all entities\n+gts list --path gts_schemas/\n+\n+# Query entities\n+gts query --path gts_schemas/ --expr \"type == 'Module'\"\n+\n+# Check schema compatibility\n+gts compatibility --schema1 v1/module.json --schema2 v2/module.json\n+\n+# Get attribute value\n+gts attr --entity <entity_file> --path \"status\"\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`gts CLI tool GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust GitHub repository`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nI couldn't find a GitHub repository named GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust. Do you mean a different repo (for example google/gts or go-gts), or should I search GitHub again for similarly named Rust projects?\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Global Type System Rust gts tool`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nDo you mean one of these?\n\n- gts (Google TypeScript Style) — TypeScript formatter/linter CLI. [1]  \n- GTS Framework (Global TCAD Solutions) — TCAD simulation framework (not Rust). [2]  \n- global type / Global Types in multiparty session types (GTS = global type system) and related Rust tools for MPST (research/tools for projecting global→local types). [3]  \n- A Rust crate implementing a global type/registry pattern (e.g., global-registry). [4]\n\nTell me which one you meant and I’ll give details (install/use instructions or links). \n\nSources: [1] GitHub google/gts, [2] Global TCAD Solutions GTS Framework, [3] survey on Multiparty Session Types / Global Types, [4] docs.rs global-registry crate.\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Remove or clarify the GTS tool reference—the repository does not exist.**\n\nThe specification references a `gts` CLI tool from `https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust`, but this repository cannot be found on GitHub or in public package registries. Web searches for \"GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\", \"Global Type System Rust\", and \"gts Rust CLI\" return no matches for this project.\n\nSince the specification mandates GTS validation in the CI pipeline (\"GTS validation MUST pass in CI pipeline\"), either:\n- Clarify which actual tool or project should be used for GTS schema validation\n- If this tool does not yet exist, defer this section or replace it with an actual schema validation approach\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n70-70: Bare URL used\n\n(MD034, no-bare-urls)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/domain-model.md` around lines 70 - 140, The doc references\na non-existent \"gts\" CLI (commands like `gts generate-from-rust`, `gts\nvalidate-id`, and the macro `#[struct_to_gts_schema]` with example `ModuleInfo`)\nwhich must be clarified or removed: either replace the bogus `gts` references\nwith the actual tool/crate name and repo URL and update example\ncommands/annotation to match that project's CLI and macro, or mark this GTS\nsection as TODO/removed and change the CI requirement (\"GTS validation MUST pass\nin CI pipeline\") to a conditional (e.g., \"If using GTS...\") or to a real\nvalidation step (e.g., link to the actual schema generator/validator used), and\nensure the example annotation (`#[struct_to_gts_schema]`, `ModuleInfo`) is\naligned with the real codegen attribute if one exists.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:16Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:04:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468609","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468609"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468609"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468609/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":70,"original_start_line":70,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":140,"original_line":140,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":140,"position":140,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468610","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468610,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBrC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,462 @@\n+# Security Guidelines\n+\n+**Source**: guidelines/SECURITY.md, docs/SECURE-ORM.md\n+\n+## Input Validation\n+\n+**Always validate user input**:\n+```rust\n+use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\n+pub struct CreateUserRequest {\n+    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\n+    pub name: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(email)]\n+    pub email: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\n+    pub password: String,\n+}\n+\n+fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\n+    if password.len() < 8 {\n+        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Secrets Management\n+\n+**Critical Rules**:\n+- ❌ **Never commit secrets** to version control\n+- ✅ **Use environment variables** for configuration\n+- ✅ **Rotate secrets regularly**\n+- ✅ **Use secure random generation** for tokens\n+\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: hardcoded secret\n+const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: environment variable\n+let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\n+    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\n+```\n+\n+## Secure ORM (Mandatory for Multi-Tenant Systems)\n+\n+HyperSpot provides a **secure-by-default ORM layer** that enforces access control at **compile time** using the typestate pattern.\n+\n+### Key Features\n+\n+1. **Compile-time enforcement**: Cannot bypass scoping via type system\n+2. **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes explicitly denied with `WHERE 1=0`\n+3. **Tenant isolation**: Automatic filtering when tenant_ids provided\n+4. **Request-scoped**: Security context tied to request lifecycle\n+5. **No SQL injection**: Uses SeaORM's parameterized queries\n+6. **Audit trail**: Raw access logs security warnings\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+```\n+API Handler (per-request)\n+    ↓ Creates SecurityCtx from auth/session\n+SecureConn (stateless wrapper)\n+    ↓ Receives SecurityCtx per-operation\n+    ↓ Enforces implicit policy\n+SeaORM\n+    ↓\n+Database\n+```\n+\n+**Key Principles**:\n+- **Request-scoped context**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation, not stored\n+- **Stateless services**: No security state in service layer\n+- **Explicit security**: Every operation requires explicit context\n+- **Safe by default**: Raw database access requires opt-in via `insecure-escape` feature\n+\n+### Define Scopable Entity\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_db_macros::Scopable;\n+\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, DeriveEntityModel, Scopable)]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"users\")]\n+#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]\n+pub struct Model {\n+    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+    pub tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    pub email: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Attributes**:\n+- `#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]` - Column for tenant isolation\n+- `#[secure(unrestricted)]` - For global system tables (no scoping)\n+\n+### Usage in API Handler\n+\n+```rust\n+pub async fn list_users_handler(\n+    Extension(auth): Extension<AuthContext>,\n+    Extension(db): Extension<DbHandle>,\n+) -> Result<Json<Vec<User>>, Problem> {\n+    // Create security context from request\n+    let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n+        vec![auth.tenant_id], \n+        auth.user_id\n+    );\n+    \n+    // Get secure connection\n+    let secure_conn = db.sea_secure();\n+    \n+    // Query with automatic tenant isolation\n+    let users = secure_conn\n+        .find::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+        .all(secure_conn.conn())\n+        .await?;\n+    \n+    Ok(Json(users))\n+}\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/security.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add tenant authorization validation before SecurityCtx creation.**\n\nThe example creates `SecurityCtx` directly from `auth.tenant_id` without validating that the authenticated user is actually authorized for that tenant. In a multi-tenant system, this could allow privilege escalation if token validation doesn't enforce tenant membership.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔒 Recommended pattern with validation</summary>\n\n```diff\n pub async fn list_users_handler(\n     Extension(auth): Extension<AuthContext>,\n     Extension(db): Extension<DbHandle>,\n ) -> Result<Json<Vec<User>>, Problem> {\n+    // Validate user has access to tenant\n+    if !auth.authorized_tenants.contains(&auth.tenant_id) {\n+        return Err(Problem::forbidden(\"Not authorized for tenant\"));\n+    }\n+    \n     // Create security context from request\n     let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n         vec![auth.tenant_id], \n         auth.user_id\n     );\n```\n</details>\n\nThis assumes `AuthContext` includes authorized tenant list. If the OAuth2/OIDC token validation already enforces tenant scoping, document that assumption explicitly in the example.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/security.md` around lines 100 - 124, The example in\nlist_users_handler creates a SecurityCtx from auth.tenant_id without checking\nthat the authenticated user is authorized for that tenant; before calling\nSecurityCtx::for_tenants, validate that AuthContext (e.g. an authorized_tenants\nlist on auth) contains auth.tenant_id and return an appropriate error\n(Problem/403) if not authorized, or document that token validation guarantees\ntenant scoping if you intend to skip the runtime check; update the handler to\nperform this explicit membership check using AuthContext before creating the\nSecurityCtx.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468610","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468610"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468610"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468610/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":100,"original_start_line":100,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":124,"original_line":124,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":124,"position":124,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468613","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468613,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBrF","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,462 @@\n+# Security Guidelines\n+\n+**Source**: guidelines/SECURITY.md, docs/SECURE-ORM.md\n+\n+## Input Validation\n+\n+**Always validate user input**:\n+```rust\n+use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\n+pub struct CreateUserRequest {\n+    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\n+    pub name: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(email)]\n+    pub email: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\n+    pub password: String,\n+}\n+\n+fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\n+    if password.len() < 8 {\n+        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Secrets Management\n+\n+**Critical Rules**:\n+- ❌ **Never commit secrets** to version control\n+- ✅ **Use environment variables** for configuration\n+- ✅ **Rotate secrets regularly**\n+- ✅ **Use secure random generation** for tokens\n+\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: hardcoded secret\n+const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: environment variable\n+let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\n+    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\n+```\n+\n+## Secure ORM (Mandatory for Multi-Tenant Systems)\n+\n+HyperSpot provides a **secure-by-default ORM layer** that enforces access control at **compile time** using the typestate pattern.\n+\n+### Key Features\n+\n+1. **Compile-time enforcement**: Cannot bypass scoping via type system\n+2. **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes explicitly denied with `WHERE 1=0`\n+3. **Tenant isolation**: Automatic filtering when tenant_ids provided\n+4. **Request-scoped**: Security context tied to request lifecycle\n+5. **No SQL injection**: Uses SeaORM's parameterized queries\n+6. **Audit trail**: Raw access logs security warnings\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+```\n+API Handler (per-request)\n+    ↓ Creates SecurityCtx from auth/session\n+SecureConn (stateless wrapper)\n+    ↓ Receives SecurityCtx per-operation\n+    ↓ Enforces implicit policy\n+SeaORM\n+    ↓\n+Database\n+```\n+\n+**Key Principles**:\n+- **Request-scoped context**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation, not stored\n+- **Stateless services**: No security state in service layer\n+- **Explicit security**: Every operation requires explicit context\n+- **Safe by default**: Raw database access requires opt-in via `insecure-escape` feature\n+\n+### Define Scopable Entity\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_db_macros::Scopable;\n+\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, DeriveEntityModel, Scopable)]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"users\")]\n+#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]\n+pub struct Model {\n+    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+    pub tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    pub email: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Attributes**:\n+- `#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]` - Column for tenant isolation\n+- `#[secure(unrestricted)]` - For global system tables (no scoping)\n+\n+### Usage in API Handler\n+\n+```rust\n+pub async fn list_users_handler(\n+    Extension(auth): Extension<AuthContext>,\n+    Extension(db): Extension<DbHandle>,\n+) -> Result<Json<Vec<User>>, Problem> {\n+    // Create security context from request\n+    let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n+        vec![auth.tenant_id], \n+        auth.user_id\n+    );\n+    \n+    // Get secure connection\n+    let secure_conn = db.sea_secure();\n+    \n+    // Query with automatic tenant isolation\n+    let users = secure_conn\n+        .find::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+        .all(secure_conn.conn())\n+        .await?;\n+    \n+    Ok(Json(users))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Implicit Security Policy\n+\n+| Scope Condition | SQL Result |\n+|----------------|------------|\n+| Empty (no tenant, no resource) | `WHERE 1=0` (deny all) |\n+| Tenants only | `WHERE tenant_col IN (...)` |\n+| Tenants only + entity has no tenant_col | `WHERE 1=0` (deny all) |\n+| Resources only | `WHERE resource_col IN (...)` |\n+| Both tenants and resources | `WHERE tenant_col IN (...) AND resource_col IN (...)` |\n+\n+### SecurityCtx Creation\n+\n+**For multi-tenant operations**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n+    vec![tenant_id1, tenant_id2],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**For resource-specific operations**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_resources(\n+    vec![resource_id1, resource_id2],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**For both**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::new(\n+    vec![tenant_id],\n+    vec![resource_id],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+### SecureConn API\n+\n+All methods require `&SecurityCtx` parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Find all (with scope)\n+let users = secure_conn\n+    .find::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .all(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Find by ID (with scope)\n+let user = secure_conn\n+    .find_by_id::<user::Entity>(&ctx, user_id)?\n+    .one(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Update (with scope)\n+let result = secure_conn\n+    .update_many::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .set(user::Column::Status.eq(\"active\"))\n+    .exec(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Delete (with scope)\n+let result = secure_conn\n+    .delete_many::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .exec(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Insert (with tenant validation)\n+let user = secure_conn\n+    .insert::<user::Entity>(&ctx, active_model)\n+    .await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Global Entities (Unrestricted)\n+\n+For system tables that don't have tenant isolation:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, DeriveEntityModel, Scopable)]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"global_config\")]\n+#[secure(unrestricted)]  // ← No scoping\n+pub struct Model {\n+    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+    pub key: String,\n+    pub value: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Authentication & Authorization\n+\n+**Authentication**:\n+- Use OAuth2/OIDC Bearer tokens\n+- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n+- Never include secrets in URLs\n+\n+**Authorization**:\n+- Check permissions per operation\n+- Use scopes/roles from token\n+- Return 403 Forbidden for insufficient permissions\n+\n+## HTTPS & Transport Security\n+\n+**Requirements**:\n+- HTTPS only (no HTTP in production)\n+- HSTS enabled\n+- TLS 1.2+ minimum\n+- Certificate validation\n+\n+## CORS Configuration\n+\n+```yaml\n+# config/server.yaml\n+modules:\n+  api_gateway:\n+    cors_enabled: true\n+    cors_allowed_origins:\n+      - \"https://app.example.com\"\n+      - \"https://admin.example.com\"\n+```\n+\n+**Never use wildcards** (`*`) in production.\n+\n+## SQL Injection Prevention\n+\n+**Secure ORM automatically prevents SQL injection**:\n+- Uses SeaORM's parameterized queries\n+- Never builds raw SQL strings\n+- Compile-time query validation\n+\n+**If raw SQL is absolutely required**:\n+```rust\n+// Requires insecure-escape feature flag\n+db.sqlx_pool().execute(\n+    sqlx::query(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\")\n+        .bind(user_id)  // ← Parameterized\n+).await?;\n+```\n+\n+## Rate Limiting\n+\n+**Implement per endpoint**:\n+- Standard: 100 requests/hour\n+- Sensitive ops: Lower limits\n+- Return 429 with `Retry-After` header","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/security.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Review rate limiting thresholds for production viability.**\n\nThe standard rate limit of 100 requests/hour (~1.67 req/min) is extremely restrictive and may break legitimate use cases such as paginated list operations, dashboard loading, or batch operations. Most production APIs set standard limits at 1,000-10,000 requests/hour for authenticated users.\n\nAdditionally, the specification should clarify:\n- Per-user vs. per-IP rate limiting strategy\n- Specific thresholds for \"sensitive ops\" \n- Whether limits apply per-endpoint or globally\n- Burst allowances for short-term spikes\n\n\n\nConsider revising to production-appropriate values and adding more specific guidance on rate limiting strategies.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/security.md` around lines 265 - 270, Update the \"Rate\nLimiting\" section to use production-appropriate thresholds (recommend standard:\n1,000–10,000 requests/hour for authenticated users instead of 100/hour),\nexplicitly define whether limits are per-user or per-IP and how to treat\nunauthenticated requests, specify concrete lower thresholds for \"sensitive ops\"\n(e.g., 100–1,000/hour) and whether those apply per-endpoint or globally, and add\nguidance on burst handling (e.g., token-bucket/leaky-bucket with short-term\nburst allowance and smoothing) while retaining the requirement to return 429\nwith a Retry-After header; ensure you update the bullets under \"Rate Limiting\"\n(Standard, Sensitive ops, Return 429 with `Retry-After`) to reflect these values\nand strategies.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468613","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468613"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468613"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468613/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":265,"original_start_line":265,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":270,"original_line":270,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":270,"position":270,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468616","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468616,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBrI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,462 @@\n+# Security Guidelines\n+\n+**Source**: guidelines/SECURITY.md, docs/SECURE-ORM.md\n+\n+## Input Validation\n+\n+**Always validate user input**:\n+```rust\n+use validator::{Validate, ValidationError};\n+\n+#[derive(Deserialize, Validate)]\n+pub struct CreateUserRequest {\n+    #[validate(length(min = 1, max = 100))]\n+    pub name: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(email)]\n+    pub email: String,\n+    \n+    #[validate(custom = \"validate_password\")]\n+    pub password: String,\n+}\n+\n+fn validate_password(password: &str) -> Result<(), ValidationError> {\n+    if password.len() < 8 {\n+        return Err(ValidationError::new(\"Password too short\"));\n+    }\n+    Ok(())\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Secrets Management\n+\n+**Critical Rules**:\n+- ❌ **Never commit secrets** to version control\n+- ✅ **Use environment variables** for configuration\n+- ✅ **Rotate secrets regularly**\n+- ✅ **Use secure random generation** for tokens\n+\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: hardcoded secret\n+const API_KEY: &str = \"sk-1234567890abcdef\";\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: environment variable\n+let api_key = std::env::var(\"API_KEY\")\n+    .context(\"API_KEY environment variable not set\")?;\n+```\n+\n+## Secure ORM (Mandatory for Multi-Tenant Systems)\n+\n+HyperSpot provides a **secure-by-default ORM layer** that enforces access control at **compile time** using the typestate pattern.\n+\n+### Key Features\n+\n+1. **Compile-time enforcement**: Cannot bypass scoping via type system\n+2. **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes explicitly denied with `WHERE 1=0`\n+3. **Tenant isolation**: Automatic filtering when tenant_ids provided\n+4. **Request-scoped**: Security context tied to request lifecycle\n+5. **No SQL injection**: Uses SeaORM's parameterized queries\n+6. **Audit trail**: Raw access logs security warnings\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+```\n+API Handler (per-request)\n+    ↓ Creates SecurityCtx from auth/session\n+SecureConn (stateless wrapper)\n+    ↓ Receives SecurityCtx per-operation\n+    ↓ Enforces implicit policy\n+SeaORM\n+    ↓\n+Database\n+```\n+\n+**Key Principles**:\n+- **Request-scoped context**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation, not stored\n+- **Stateless services**: No security state in service layer\n+- **Explicit security**: Every operation requires explicit context\n+- **Safe by default**: Raw database access requires opt-in via `insecure-escape` feature\n+\n+### Define Scopable Entity\n+\n+```rust\n+use modkit_db_macros::Scopable;\n+\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, DeriveEntityModel, Scopable)]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"users\")]\n+#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]\n+pub struct Model {\n+    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+    pub tenant_id: Uuid,\n+    pub email: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Attributes**:\n+- `#[secure(tenant_col = \"tenant_id\")]` - Column for tenant isolation\n+- `#[secure(unrestricted)]` - For global system tables (no scoping)\n+\n+### Usage in API Handler\n+\n+```rust\n+pub async fn list_users_handler(\n+    Extension(auth): Extension<AuthContext>,\n+    Extension(db): Extension<DbHandle>,\n+) -> Result<Json<Vec<User>>, Problem> {\n+    // Create security context from request\n+    let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n+        vec![auth.tenant_id], \n+        auth.user_id\n+    );\n+    \n+    // Get secure connection\n+    let secure_conn = db.sea_secure();\n+    \n+    // Query with automatic tenant isolation\n+    let users = secure_conn\n+        .find::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+        .all(secure_conn.conn())\n+        .await?;\n+    \n+    Ok(Json(users))\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Implicit Security Policy\n+\n+| Scope Condition | SQL Result |\n+|----------------|------------|\n+| Empty (no tenant, no resource) | `WHERE 1=0` (deny all) |\n+| Tenants only | `WHERE tenant_col IN (...)` |\n+| Tenants only + entity has no tenant_col | `WHERE 1=0` (deny all) |\n+| Resources only | `WHERE resource_col IN (...)` |\n+| Both tenants and resources | `WHERE tenant_col IN (...) AND resource_col IN (...)` |\n+\n+### SecurityCtx Creation\n+\n+**For multi-tenant operations**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_tenants(\n+    vec![tenant_id1, tenant_id2],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**For resource-specific operations**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::for_resources(\n+    vec![resource_id1, resource_id2],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**For both**:\n+```rust\n+let ctx = SecurityCtx::new(\n+    vec![tenant_id],\n+    vec![resource_id],\n+    user_id\n+);\n+```\n+\n+### SecureConn API\n+\n+All methods require `&SecurityCtx` parameter:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Find all (with scope)\n+let users = secure_conn\n+    .find::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .all(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Find by ID (with scope)\n+let user = secure_conn\n+    .find_by_id::<user::Entity>(&ctx, user_id)?\n+    .one(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Update (with scope)\n+let result = secure_conn\n+    .update_many::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .set(user::Column::Status.eq(\"active\"))\n+    .exec(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Delete (with scope)\n+let result = secure_conn\n+    .delete_many::<user::Entity>(&ctx)?\n+    .exec(secure_conn.conn())\n+    .await?;\n+\n+// Insert (with tenant validation)\n+let user = secure_conn\n+    .insert::<user::Entity>(&ctx, active_model)\n+    .await?;\n+```\n+\n+### Global Entities (Unrestricted)\n+\n+For system tables that don't have tenant isolation:\n+\n+```rust\n+#[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, DeriveEntityModel, Scopable)]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"global_config\")]\n+#[secure(unrestricted)]  // ← No scoping\n+pub struct Model {\n+    #[sea_orm(primary_key)]\n+    pub id: Uuid,\n+    pub key: String,\n+    pub value: String,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Authentication & Authorization\n+\n+**Authentication**:\n+- Use OAuth2/OIDC Bearer tokens\n+- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`\n+- Never include secrets in URLs\n+\n+**Authorization**:\n+- Check permissions per operation\n+- Use scopes/roles from token\n+- Return 403 Forbidden for insufficient permissions\n+\n+## HTTPS & Transport Security\n+\n+**Requirements**:\n+- HTTPS only (no HTTP in production)\n+- HSTS enabled\n+- TLS 1.2+ minimum\n+- Certificate validation\n+\n+## CORS Configuration\n+\n+```yaml\n+# config/server.yaml\n+modules:\n+  api_gateway:\n+    cors_enabled: true\n+    cors_allowed_origins:\n+      - \"https://app.example.com\"\n+      - \"https://admin.example.com\"\n+```\n+\n+**Never use wildcards** (`*`) in production.\n+\n+## SQL Injection Prevention\n+\n+**Secure ORM automatically prevents SQL injection**:\n+- Uses SeaORM's parameterized queries\n+- Never builds raw SQL strings\n+- Compile-time query validation\n+\n+**If raw SQL is absolutely required**:\n+```rust\n+// Requires insecure-escape feature flag\n+db.sqlx_pool().execute(\n+    sqlx::query(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\")\n+        .bind(user_id)  // ← Parameterized\n+).await?;\n+```\n+\n+## Rate Limiting\n+\n+**Implement per endpoint**:\n+- Standard: 100 requests/hour\n+- Sensitive ops: Lower limits\n+- Return 429 with `Retry-After` header\n+\n+## Audit Logging\n+\n+**Log security events**:\n+```rust\n+tracing::warn!(\n+    user_id = %user_id,\n+    tenant_id = %tenant_id,\n+    action = \"delete_user\",\n+    target_id = %target_user_id,\n+    \"User deleted another user\"\n+);\n+```\n+\n+**Log**:\n+- Authentication attempts\n+- Authorization failures\n+- Resource access (especially sensitive data)\n+- Configuration changes\n+- Security policy violations","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/security.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Include trace_id in audit logging example for consistency.**\n\nThe security implementation checklist (line 452) requires logging security events with `trace_id`, but the example code doesn't demonstrate this. Including trace_id is critical for correlating security events across distributed systems.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Enhanced example with trace_id</summary>\n\n```diff\n tracing::warn!(\n+    trace_id = %trace_id,\n     user_id = %user_id,\n     tenant_id = %tenant_id,\n     action = \"delete_user\",\n     target_id = %target_user_id,\n     \"User deleted another user\"\n );\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\ntracing::warn!(\n    trace_id = %trace_id,\n    user_id = %user_id,\n    tenant_id = %tenant_id,\n    action = \"delete_user\",\n    target_id = %target_user_id,\n    \"User deleted another user\"\n);\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/security.md` around lines 272 - 290, The audit logging\nexample using tracing::warn! must include the trace_id field to match the\nsecurity checklist; update the tracing::warn! call that currently sets user_id,\ntenant_id, action, and target_id (and the message \"User deleted another user\")\nto also include trace_id = %trace_id so security events can be correlated across\nservices; ensure the variable name trace_id matches the surrounding context\nwhere traces are created/passed.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468616","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468616"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468616"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468616/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":272,"original_start_line":272,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":290,"original_line":290,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":290,"position":290,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468620","pull_request_review_id":3669526673,"id":2697468620,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gyBrM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,268 @@\n+# Testing Specification\n+\n+**Source**: README.md, testing/requirements.txt, test files\n+\n+## Testing Strategy\n+\n+**Coverage Target**: 90%+\n+\n+**Test Pyramid**:\n+1. Unit Tests (majority)\n+2. Integration Tests (module interactions)\n+3. E2E Tests (full system)\n+\n+## Unit Tests\n+\n+**Framework**: Rust built-in test framework + tokio-test for async\n+\n+**Location**: \n+- Same file: `#[cfg(test)] mod tests { ... }`\n+- Separate: `tests/` directory in each crate\n+\n+**Run Command**:\n+```bash\n+cargo test\n+```\n+\n+**Specific Module**:\n+```bash\n+cargo test -p {module_name}\n+```\n+\n+**With Output**:\n+```bash\n+cargo test -- --nocapture\n+```\n+\n+**Example**:\n+```rust\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::*;\n+\n+    #[tokio::test]\n+    async fn test_parse_when_valid_pdf_then_success() {\n+        let result = parse_file(\"test.pdf\").await;\n+        assert!(result.is_ok());\n+    }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## Integration Tests\n+\n+**Framework**: Rust integration tests (`tests/` directory)\n+\n+**Location**: `{crate}/tests/*.rs`\n+\n+**Run Command**:\n+```bash\n+cargo test --test integration\n+```\n+\n+**Example**:\n+```rust\n+// tests/integration_test.rs\n+use hyperspot_server::app::App;\n+\n+#[tokio::test]\n+async fn test_module_integration() {\n+    let app = App::new().await.unwrap();\n+    // Test module interactions\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## E2E Tests\n+\n+**Framework**: pytest + httpx (Python)\n+\n+**Location**: `testing/e2e/`\n+\n+**Dependencies**:\n+```\n+pytest\n+pytest-asyncio\n+httpx\n+```\n+\n+**Install**:\n+```bash\n+pip install -r testing/requirements.txt\n+```\n+\n+**Run Commands**:\n+```bash\n+make e2e-local      # Against running server\n+make e2e-docker     # In Docker container\n+```\n+\n+**Example Test** (`testing/e2e/test_file_parser.py`):\n+```python\n+import httpx\n+import pytest\n+\n+@pytest.mark.asyncio\n+async def test_parser_info():\n+    async with httpx.AsyncClient() as client:\n+        response = await client.get(\n+            \"http://127.0.0.1:8087/file-parser/v1/info\"\n+        )\n+        assert response.status_code == 200\n+        data = response.json()\n+        assert \"supported_formats\" in data\n+```\n+\n+## Test Configuration\n+\n+**Config File**: `testing/e2e/conftest.py` (pytest fixtures)\n+\n+**Test Data**: `testing/e2e/fixtures/` (if needed)","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/testing.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind testing -type f -o -type d 2>/dev/null | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 184\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nls -la testing/e2e/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"Directory does not exist\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 654\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nls -la testing/e2e/ | grep -E \"fixtures|testdata\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 121\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat testing/e2e/conftest.py | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 549\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Update documentation to reference correct test data directory.**\n\nThe documentation references `testing/e2e/fixtures/`, but the actual directory is `testing/e2e/testdata/`. The `conftest.py` file exists and is properly configured, but the test data directory name is incorrect.\n\nChange `testing/e2e/fixtures/` to `testing/e2e/testdata/` in the documentation.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/testing.md` around lines 114 - 118, Update the docs section\nthat lists test data to reference the actual directory name: replace the\nincorrect path \"testing/e2e/fixtures/\" with \"testing/e2e/testdata/\" in\nFDD-Adapter/specs/testing.md (the Test Configuration block that references the\npytest config file testing/e2e/conftest.py).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:17Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:27:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468620","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468620"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697468620"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697468620/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":114,"original_start_line":114,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":118,"original_line":118,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":118,"position":118,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622516","pull_request_review_id":3669709233,"id":2697622516,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gynP0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+# FDD Adapter: HyperSpot\n+\n+**Extends**: `/FDD/AGENTS.md`\n+\n+**ALWAYS open and follow**: `/FDD/requirements/core.md` WHEN editing this file","path":".fdd-adapter/AGENTS.md","commit_id":"82c11e73c235c1946abd87da4ab283cc8fc926e2","original_commit_id":"ec698ae0ff131e5e07b39275f2750ee0fa5cb3a7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify FDD submodule files exist\n\necho \"=== Checking FDD directory structure ===\"\nls -la FDD 2>/dev/null || echo \"FDD directory not found\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking for FDD/AGENTS.md ===\"\nif [ -f \"FDD/AGENTS.md\" ]; then\n  echo \"✓ FDD/AGENTS.md exists\"\n  wc -l FDD/AGENTS.md\nelse\n  echo \"✗ FDD/AGENTS.md NOT found\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking for FDD/requirements/core.md ===\"\nif [ -f \"FDD/requirements/core.md\" ]; then\n  echo \"✓ FDD/requirements/core.md exists\"\n  wc -l FDD/requirements/core.md\nelse\n  echo \"✗ FDD/requirements/core.md NOT found\"\nfi\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== FDD directory contents (first level) ===\"\nfind FDD -maxdepth 2 -type f -name \"*.md\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 407\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md and search for referenced files\n\necho \"=== FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md (lines 1-15) ===\"\nhead -15 FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Search for AGENTS.md files anywhere in repo ===\"\nfd -t f \"AGENTS.md$\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Search for core.md files anywhere in repo ===\"\nfd -t f \"core.md$\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check if FDD is a git submodule ===\"\ncat .gitmodules 2>/dev/null | grep -A 3 \"FDD\" || echo \"No FDD entry in .gitmodules\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1395\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Initialize the FDD submodule or remove references to non-existent files.**\n\nLines 3 and 5 reference `/FDD/AGENTS.md` and `/FDD/requirements/core.md`, but the FDD submodule directory is empty. Either initialize the FDD submodule (via `git submodule update --init`), provide these files in the FDD directory, or clarify that these are external references not yet integrated into the repository.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md` around lines 3 - 5, The AGENTS.md references missing\nFDD submodule files (/FDD/AGENTS.md and /FDD/requirements/core.md); either\ninitialize and populate the submodule or remove/update these references: run git\nsubmodule update --init and add the referenced files into the FDD directory, or\nedit FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md to point to existing/internal docs or add a clear\nnote stating these are external/not-yet-integrated resources; ensure the file\npaths in FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md (the referenced /FDD/AGENTS.md and\n/FDD/requirements/core.md) are correct after the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T09:17:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T09:17:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697622516","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622516"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697622516"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622516/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":3,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622528","pull_request_review_id":3669709233,"id":2697622528,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gynQA","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@\n+# FDD Adapter: HyperSpot\n+\n+**Extends**: `/FDD/AGENTS.md`\n+\n+**ALWAYS open and follow**: `/FDD/requirements/core.md` WHEN editing this file\n+\n+**Version**: 1.1  \n+**Last Updated**: 2025-01-16  \n+**Tech Stack**: Rust (Edition 2021) / ModKit / Axum / Multi-DB","path":".fdd-adapter/AGENTS.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"ec698ae0ff131e5e07b39275f2750ee0fa5cb3a7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Correct the date to match the PR creation date.**\n\nThe \"Last Updated\" date is \"2025-01-16\" but the PR was created on 2026-01-16. Update to the correct year.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📅 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n **Version**: 1.1  \n-**Last Updated**: 2025-01-16  \n+**Last Updated**: 2026-01-16  \n **Tech Stack**: Rust (Edition 2021) / ModKit / Axum / Multi-DB\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/AGENTS.md` around lines 7 - 9, Update the \"Last Updated\" metadata\nin AGENTS.md by changing the date string \"Last Updated: 2025-01-16\" to the\ncorrect PR creation date \"2026-01-16\"; locate the \"Last Updated\" line in the\nfile (the literal text \"Last Updated\") and replace the year accordingly so the\nheader block under Version/Tech Stack reflects 2026-01-16.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T09:17:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T09:17:42Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697622528","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622528"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697622528"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697622528/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":7,"original_start_line":7,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":9,"original_line":9,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":9,"position":9,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697676178","pull_request_review_id":3669784953,"id":2697676178,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gy0WS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,510 @@\n+# Performance Specification\n+\n+**Source**: Cargo.toml, README.md, ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md, libs/modkit-db/\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+HyperSpot is designed as a **high-performance platform** built in Rust with explicit focus on optimization at multiple levels: compile-time, runtime, and architectural. Performance is not an afterthought but a core design principle enabling \"whole subsystem locally\" workflows and efficient resource utilization.\n+\n+**Performance Philosophy**:\n+- **Compile-time optimization** via Rust's zero-cost abstractions and profile-guided settings\n+- **Async-first architecture** with tokio runtime for high concurrency\n+- **Resource efficiency** enabling local development and testing of large subsystems\n+- **Measured optimization** - profile before optimizing, benchmark after changes\n+- **Quality enables performance** - 90%+ test coverage target prevents performance regressions\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 1. Compilation Performance\n+\n+### Profile Configuration\n+\n+**Release Profile** (production):\n+```toml\n+[profile.release]\n+codegen-units = 1        # Maximum optimization, slower builds\n+lto = false              # Can enable for smaller binaries (much slower builds)\n+opt-level = 3            # Maximum optimization (default)\n+```\n+\n+**Development Profile** (fast iteration):\n+```toml\n+[profile.dev]\n+incremental = true       # Incremental compilation\n+codegen-units = 16       # Parallel codegen for faster builds\n+opt-level = 0            # No optimization (default)\n+```\n+\n+**Test Profile** (test performance):\n+```toml\n+[profile.test]\n+incremental = true\n+codegen-units = 16\n+opt-level = 0            # Fast compilation for tests\n+```\n+\n+### Optimization Strategies\n+\n+**For production builds**:\n+- Use `cargo build --release` (applies release profile)\n+- Consider `lto = \"thin\"` for moderate binary size reduction\n+- Consider `strip = true` to remove debug symbols (smaller binaries)\n+\n+**For development**:\n+- Use `cargo check` for fast feedback (no codegen)\n+- Use `cargo build` with dev profile (incremental, parallel)\n+- Profile in release mode, not debug mode\n+\n+### Clippy Performance Lints\n+\n+Performance-related clippy lints are **denied** at workspace level:\n+\n+```toml\n+[workspace.lints.clippy]\n+perf = \"deny\"                    # Performance lint group\n+clone_on_copy = \"deny\"           # Avoid unnecessary clones\n+cast_precision_loss = \"deny\"     # Catch lossy casts\n+```\n+\n+**Command**:\n+```bash\n+cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D clippy::perf\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 2. Runtime Performance\n+\n+### Async Runtime\n+\n+**Framework**: Tokio (multi-threaded runtime)\n+\n+**Patterns**:\n+- All I/O operations are `async`\n+- Use `tokio::spawn` for concurrent tasks\n+- Use `CancellationToken` for graceful shutdown\n+- Avoid blocking operations in async context\n+\n+**Example**:\n+```rust\n+use tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken;\n+\n+async fn handler(ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<Response> {\n+    // Non-blocking async operations\n+    let data = fetch_data().await?;\n+    process_async(data).await\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Anti-patterns**:\n+```rust\n+// ❌ BAD: Blocking operation in async context\n+async fn bad_handler() {\n+    std::thread::sleep(Duration::from_secs(1));  // Blocks entire thread\n+}\n+\n+// ✅ GOOD: Async sleep\n+async fn good_handler() {\n+    tokio::time::sleep(Duration::from_secs(1)).await;  // Yields to runtime\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Database Optimizations\n+\n+**Connection Pooling**:\n+- DbManager caches database handles per module\n+- Uses `DashMap` for concurrent cache access\n+- Connection pool configuration per module\n+\n+**Configuration**:\n+```yaml\n+modules:\n+  my_module:\n+    database:\n+      server: \"postgres_main\"\n+      pool:\n+        max_conns: 10              # Max connections per pool\n+        acquire_timeout: \"30s\"     # Connection acquisition timeout\n+```\n+\n+**SQLite Optimizations**:\n+```yaml\n+database:\n+  servers:\n+    sqlite_db:\n+      params:\n+        WAL: \"true\"                # Write-Ahead Logging (better concurrency)\n+        synchronous: \"NORMAL\"      # Balance safety/performance\n+        busy_timeout: \"5000\"       # Retry on lock contention\n+      pool:\n+        max_conns: 5               # SQLite benefits from fewer connections\n+```\n+\n+**Best Practices**:\n+- Use prepared statements (automatic with sqlx)\n+- Batch operations where possible\n+- Use transactions for multiple writes\n+- Index frequently queried columns\n+- Use advisory locks for distributed coordination\n+\n+### Caching Strategies\n+\n+**Static Data**:\n+```rust\n+use std::sync::LazyLock;\n+\n+static CACHED_CONFIG: LazyLock<Config> = LazyLock::new(|| {\n+    load_expensive_config()\n+});\n+```\n+\n+**Module-level Caching**:\n+```rust\n+// DbManager caches database handles\n+let handle = db_manager.get(\"my_module\").await?;  // Cached after first call\n+```\n+\n+**OData Query Caching**:\n+- Query parsing results can be cached\n+- Filter node trees are reusable\n+- Consider caching for expensive calculations\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 3. Architectural Performance\n+\n+### Modular Design Benefits\n+\n+**Selective Compilation**:\n+- Modules are separate crates\n+- Only modified modules need recompilation\n+- Feature flags enable conditional compilation\n+\n+**In-Process vs Out-of-Process**:\n+- **In-process**: Direct function calls, zero serialization overhead\n+- **Out-of-process (OoP)**: gRPC communication, process isolation\n+- Choose based on requirements (isolation vs performance)\n+\n+**Example Decision Matrix**:\n+| Module Type | Deployment | Rationale |\n+|-------------|-----------|-----------|\n+| Core business logic | In-process | Maximum performance |\n+| Third-party integrations | OoP | Fault isolation |\n+| Compute-intensive tasks | OoP | Resource isolation |\n+| High-frequency APIs | In-process | Low latency |\n+\n+### Resource Management\n+\n+**Memory Efficiency**:\n+- Rust's ownership prevents memory leaks\n+- Zero-copy patterns where possible\n+- Use `Arc<T>` for shared ownership\n+- Use `&str` instead of `String` when borrowing\n+\n+**Concurrency**:\n+- Lock-free structures (`DashMap`) for shared state\n+- Minimize lock contention\n+- Use async channels for message passing\n+- Prefer `tokio::sync` primitives\n+\n+---\n+\n+## 4. Profiling & Benchmarking\n+\n+### Profiling Tools\n+\n+**CPU Profiling**:\n+```bash\n+# Install flamegraph\n+cargo install flamegraph\n+\n+# Profile release build\n+cargo flamegraph --release -- <args>\n+\n+# Output: flamegraph.svg (interactive visualization)\n+```\n+\n+**Memory Profiling**:\n+```bash\n+# Using valgrind (Linux/macOS)\n+valgrind --tool=massif target/release/hyperspot-server\n+\n+# Using heaptrack (Linux)\n+heaptrack target/release/hyperspot-server\n+```\n+\n+**tokio-console** (async runtime inspection):\n+```bash\n+# Enable console in Cargo.toml\n+tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\", \"tracing\"] }\n+console-subscriber = \"0.1\"\n+\n+# Run tokio-console\n+tokio-console\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/performance.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"bdfbdecebd2c45fdc63dd67b47c556bee123669d","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`console-subscriber crate latest version crates.io`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nThe latest console-subscriber version is 0.5.0 (released Oct 30, 2025). [1][2]\n\nSources:\n[1] docs.rs changelog for console-subscriber 0.5.0.  \n[2] deps.rs page for console-subscriber 0.5.0.\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Update `console-subscriber` version.**\n\nThe example shows `console-subscriber = \"0.1\"`, which is significantly outdated. The latest version is 0.5.0, which includes recent features and bug fixes.\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested update</summary>\n\n```diff\n # Enable console in Cargo.toml\n tokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\", \"tracing\"] }\n-console-subscriber = \"0.1\"\n+console-subscriber = \"0.5\"\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# Enable console in Cargo.toml\ntokio = { version = \"1\", features = [\"full\", \"tracing\"] }\nconsole-subscriber = \"0.5\"\n\n# Run tokio-console\ntokio-console\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@FDD-Adapter/specs/performance.md` around lines 238 - 244, Update the outdated\ndependency declaration for console-subscriber in the example Cargo.toml snippet:\nreplace the line `console-subscriber = \"0.1\"` with `console-subscriber =\n\"0.5.0\"` (keeping the surrounding tokio dependency line and the `tokio-console`\nrun instruction unchanged) so the example uses the current console-subscriber\nversion.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T09:29:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T09:29:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697676178","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697676178"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697676178"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697676178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":238,"original_start_line":238,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":244,"original_line":244,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":244,"position":244,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697824759","pull_request_review_id":3669982954,"id":2697824759,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzYn3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@\n+# Domain Model Specification\n+\n+**Source**: libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs, module source code\n+\n+## Technology\n+\n+**Rust Type System** + **GTS (Global Type System)**\n+\n+## Format\n+\n+Domain models are defined as Rust `struct` and `enum` types with derives:\n+- `serde::Serialize` / `serde::Deserialize` for JSON serialization\n+- `utoipa::ToSchema` for OpenAPI schema generation\n+- Custom derives from `modkit-macros` as needed\n+\n+## Locations\n+\n+**Core Types**: `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`  \n+**Module Contracts**: `modules/{module}/src/contract/`  \n+**SDK Types**: `modules/{module}/{module}-sdk/src/`\n+\n+## Type Reference Syntax\n+\n+Use fully-qualified Rust paths when referencing domain types:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Example references\n+modkit::contracts::ModuleInfo\n+file_parser::contract::FileParserInfoDto\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Integration\n+\n+**GTS (Global Type System)** enables extensible type definitions:\n+- Custom schema extensions\n+- Plugin-provided types\n+- Tenant-specific type customizations\n+\n+**GTS Location**: Integrated in modkit framework\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+**Command**: `cargo check --workspace`  \n+**Expected**: No type errors, all contracts compile\n+\n+## Example\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use utoipa::ToSchema;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+pub enum ModuleStatus {\n+    Active,\n+    Inactive,\n+    Error,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Validation (MANDATORY)\n+\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate GTS entities, identifiers, and schemas to ensure compliance with Global Type System standards.\n+\n+**Installation**:\n+```bash\n+cargo install gts\n+```\n+\n+**Key Commands**:\n+\n+### Validate GTS ID Format\n+```bash\n+gts validate-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Parse GTS ID Components\n+```bash\n+gts parse-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Validate Instance Against Schema\n+```bash\n+gts validate-instance --schema <schema_file> --instance <instance_file>\n+```\n+\n+### Generate Schemas from Rust Code\n+```bash\n+gts generate-from-rust --input <source_dir> --output <schema_dir>\n+```\n+\n+**Annotations for Schema Generation**:\n+```rust\n+use gts::struct_to_gts_schema;\n+\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema]\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Validation Workflow\n+\n+**Before committing domain types**:\n+1. Annotate types with `#[struct_to_gts_schema]`\n+2. Generate GTS schemas: `gts generate-from-rust --input libs/modkit/src --output gts_schemas/`\n+3. Validate IDs: `gts validate-id <entity_id>`\n+4. Validate instances: `gts validate-instance --schema gts_schemas/<type>.json --instance instances/<entity>.json`\n+\n+**CI Integration**:\n+- GTS validation MUST pass in CI pipeline\n+- Schema generation MUST be automated\n+- ID format validation MUST be enforced\n+\n+**Common Commands**:\n+```bash\n+# List all entities\n+gts list --path gts_schemas/\n+\n+# Query entities\n+gts query --path gts_schemas/ --expr \"type == 'Module'\"\n+\n+# Check schema compatibility\n+gts compatibility --schema1 v1/module.json --schema2 v2/module.json\n+\n+# Get attribute value\n+gts attr --entity <entity_file> --path \"status\"\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No, it's a glitch, the https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust exists","created_at":"2026-01-16T10:04:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:04:13Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697824759","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697824759"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697824759"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697824759/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":70,"original_start_line":70,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":140,"original_line":140,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2697468609,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":140,"position":140,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697826981","pull_request_review_id":3669985792,"id":2697826981,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzZKl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@\n+# Domain Model Specification\n+\n+**Source**: libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs, module source code\n+\n+## Technology\n+\n+**Rust Type System** + **GTS (Global Type System)**\n+\n+## Format\n+\n+Domain models are defined as Rust `struct` and `enum` types with derives:\n+- `serde::Serialize` / `serde::Deserialize` for JSON serialization\n+- `utoipa::ToSchema` for OpenAPI schema generation\n+- Custom derives from `modkit-macros` as needed\n+\n+## Locations\n+\n+**Core Types**: `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`  \n+**Module Contracts**: `modules/{module}/src/contract/`  \n+**SDK Types**: `modules/{module}/{module}-sdk/src/`\n+\n+## Type Reference Syntax\n+\n+Use fully-qualified Rust paths when referencing domain types:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Example references\n+modkit::contracts::ModuleInfo\n+file_parser::contract::FileParserInfoDto\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Integration\n+\n+**GTS (Global Type System)** enables extensible type definitions:\n+- Custom schema extensions\n+- Plugin-provided types\n+- Tenant-specific type customizations\n+\n+**GTS Location**: Integrated in modkit framework\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+**Command**: `cargo check --workspace`  \n+**Expected**: No type errors, all contracts compile\n+\n+## Example\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use utoipa::ToSchema;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+pub enum ModuleStatus {\n+    Active,\n+    Inactive,\n+    Error,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Validation (MANDATORY)\n+\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate GTS entities, identifiers, and schemas to ensure compliance with Global Type System standards.\n+\n+**Installation**:\n+```bash\n+cargo install gts\n+```\n+\n+**Key Commands**:\n+\n+### Validate GTS ID Format\n+```bash\n+gts validate-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Parse GTS ID Components\n+```bash\n+gts parse-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Validate Instance Against Schema\n+```bash\n+gts validate-instance --schema <schema_file> --instance <instance_file>\n+```\n+\n+### Generate Schemas from Rust Code\n+```bash\n+gts generate-from-rust --input <source_dir> --output <schema_dir>\n+```\n+\n+**Annotations for Schema Generation**:\n+```rust\n+use gts::struct_to_gts_schema;\n+\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema]\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Validation Workflow\n+\n+**Before committing domain types**:\n+1. Annotate types with `#[struct_to_gts_schema]`\n+2. Generate GTS schemas: `gts generate-from-rust --input libs/modkit/src --output gts_schemas/`\n+3. Validate IDs: `gts validate-id <entity_id>`\n+4. Validate instances: `gts validate-instance --schema gts_schemas/<type>.json --instance instances/<entity>.json`\n+\n+**CI Integration**:\n+- GTS validation MUST pass in CI pipeline\n+- Schema generation MUST be automated\n+- ID format validation MUST be enforced\n+\n+**Common Commands**:\n+```bash\n+# List all entities\n+gts list --path gts_schemas/\n+\n+# Query entities\n+gts query --path gts_schemas/ --expr \"type == 'Module'\"\n+\n+# Check schema compatibility\n+gts compatibility --schema1 v1/module.json --schema2 v2/module.json\n+\n+# Get attribute value\n+gts attr --entity <entity_file> --path \"status\"\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"f68547173d29283c630d98c8de1999e7221d4728","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n```\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if the GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust repository exists on GitHub\ngh repo view GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust --json name,url,description,isPrivate,createdAt\n```\n\nLength of output: 203\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n`@Artifizer`, you're absolutely right, and I apologize for the incorrect review comment. The repository **does exist** at https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust. \n\nI've confirmed it's a public repository created on September 30, 2025, with the description \"Rust implementation of GTS (Global Type System) specification\". The GTS CLI tool reference in the specification is valid.\n\nThank you for the correction!\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Create design.md only when the change is cross-cutting, introduces new architecture patterns, adds external dependencies, makes significant data model changes, involves security/performance complexity, or has ambiguity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/spec.md : Use `## ADDED|MODIFIED|REMOVED|RENAMED Requirements` section headers in delta spec files with at least one `#### Scenario:` per requirement\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Applies to modules/system/types-registry/openspec/openspec/changes/**/specs/**/spec.md : When using MODIFIED Requirements, paste the full, updated requirement content (header + all scenarios); partial deltas will drop previous details at archive time\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T10:04:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:04:43Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697826981","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697826981"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2697826981"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697826981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":70,"original_start_line":70,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":140,"original_line":140,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2697468609,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":140,"position":140,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697868105","pull_request_review_id":3670040719,"id