in":false},"body":"ok, now FDD in .fdd, FDD Adapter in .fdd-adapter","created_at":"2026-01-16T16:41:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T16:41:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2699221586","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699221586"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2699221586"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699221586/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2697868105,"author_association":"NONE","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699233775","pull_request_review_id":3671777346,"id":2699233775,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g4wnv","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,219 @@\n+# Domain Model Specification\n+\n+**Source**: libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs, module source code\n+\n+## Technology\n+\n+**Rust Type System** + **GTS (Global Type System)**\n+\n+## Format\n+\n+Domain models are defined as Rust `struct` and `enum` types with derives:\n+- `serde::Serialize` / `serde::Deserialize` for JSON serialization\n+- `utoipa::ToSchema` for OpenAPI schema generation\n+- Custom derives from `modkit-macros` as needed\n+\n+## Locations\n+\n+**Core Types**: `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`  \n+**Module Contracts**: `modules/{module}/src/contract/`  \n+**SDK Types**: `modules/{module}/{module}-sdk/src/`\n+\n+## Type Reference Syntax\n+\n+Use fully-qualified Rust paths when referencing domain types:\n+\n+```rust\n+// Example references\n+modkit::contracts::ModuleInfo\n+file_parser::contract::FileParserInfoDto\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Integration\n+\n+**GTS (Global Type System)** enables extensible type definitions:\n+- Custom schema extensions\n+- Plugin-provided types\n+- Tenant-specific type customizations\n+\n+**GTS Location**: Integrated in modkit framework\n+\n+## Validation\n+\n+**Command**: `cargo check --workspace`  \n+**Expected**: No type errors, all contracts compile\n+\n+## Example\n+\n+```rust\n+use serde::{Deserialize, Serialize};\n+use utoipa::ToSchema;\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n+pub enum ModuleStatus {\n+    Active,\n+    Inactive,\n+    Error,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+## GTS Validation (MANDATORY)\n+\n+**Tool**: `gts` CLI from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\n+\n+**Purpose**: Validate GTS entities, identifiers, and schemas to ensure compliance with Global Type System standards.\n+\n+**Installation**:\n+```bash\n+cargo install gts\n+```\n+\n+**Key Commands**:\n+\n+### Validate GTS ID Format\n+```bash\n+gts validate-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Parse GTS ID Components\n+```bash\n+gts parse-id <GTS_ID>\n+```\n+\n+### Validate Instance Against Schema\n+```bash\n+gts validate-instance --schema <schema_file> --instance <instance_file>\n+```\n+\n+### Generate Schemas from Rust Code\n+```bash\n+gts generate-from-rust --input <source_dir> --output <schema_dir>\n+```\n+\n+**Annotations for Schema Generation**:\n+```rust\n+use gts::struct_to_gts_schema;\n+\n+#[struct_to_gts_schema]\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Serialize, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n+pub struct ModuleInfo {\n+    pub name: String,\n+    pub version: String,\n+    pub status: ModuleStatus,\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Validation Workflow\n+\n+**Before committing domain types**:\n+1. Annotate types with `#[struct_to_gts_schema]`\n+2. Generate GTS schemas: `gts generate-from-rust --input libs/modkit/src --output gts_schemas/`\n+3. Validate IDs: `gts validate-id <entity_id>`\n+4. Validate instances: `gts validate-instance --schema gts_schemas/<type>.json --instance instances/<entity>.json`\n+\n+**CI Integration**:\n+- GTS validation MUST pass in CI pipeline\n+- Schema generation MUST be automated\n+- ID format validation MUST be enforced\n+\n+**Common Commands**:\n+```bash\n+# List all entities\n+gts list --path gts_schemas/\n+\n+# Query entities\n+gts query --path gts_schemas/ --expr \"type == 'Module'\"\n+\n+# Check schema compatibility\n+gts compatibility --schema1 v1/module.json --schema2 v2/module.json\n+\n+# Get attribute value\n+gts attr --entity <entity_file> --path \"status\"\n+```","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"82c11e73c235c1946abd87da4ab283cc8fc926e2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check GTS repo info via GitHub CLI\ngh repo view GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust --json releases,description,createdAt,updatedAt 2>/dev/null || echo \"GitHub CLI not available; will use alternative approach\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 119\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for existing GTS schemas in the repo\nfd -e json . | grep -i 'gts_schema\\|schema.*gts' || echo \"No GTS schema files found\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 89\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check for GTS CLI references in CI and scripts\nrg -n 'gts\\s+(validate|generate|parse|list|query|compatibility|attr)' .github/ scripts/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No GTS integration found in CI/scripts\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 102\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if gts is referenced in package management files (Cargo.toml, etc.)\nfd -t f '(Cargo.toml|package.json|requirements.txt)' | xargs rg -l 'gts' 2>/dev/null || echo \"GTS not found in dependency files\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 619\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if the gts-rust repository is mentioned anywhere in the codebase\nrg -n 'GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust\\|gts-rust' . 2>/dev/null || echo \"GTS repo reference not found\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 92\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`GlobalTypeSystem gts-rust production ready stable release maturity`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nI couldn't find a published Rust project named \"GlobalTypeSystem\" or \"gts-rust\" (no matching GitHub repo or crates.io package). The only nearby hits are unrelated crates using the \"gts\" prefix (example: gts-transport) and a couple of global-type/registry crates — see gts-transport and a global_registry crate. [1][2]\n\nIf you meant a specific repo or crate, please paste its GitHub or crates.io link. If you want a quick checklist to judge production readiness/maturity for a Rust project, I can run it against the repo you point to; typical checks are:\n- published on crates.io with recent semver-stable releases and changelog\n- GitHub releases/tags, CI (tests, clippy, fmt), code coverage\n- number of open vs closed issues and PR activity\n- documentation (docs.rs, README, examples)\n- dependents/usage in other projects and community adoption\n- license and security/maintenance policy\n\nTell me the exact repo or crate URL and I’ll evaluate its maturity and production-readiness with citations. \n\nSources:\n[1] gts-transport (docs.rs / lib.rs).  \n[2] global_registry (docs.rs).\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**The GTS tool referenced in the specification does not appear to exist or is not publicly available—this is a critical blocker.**\n\nThe specification mandates validation using `gts-rust` from https://github.com/GlobalTypeSystem/gts-rust, but this repository does not exist on GitHub or crates.io. Additionally, the codebase currently has:\n- No GTS schema files\n- No GTS CLI integration in CI/scripts\n- No references to the `gts-rust` tool\n\nThe custom GTS-related linters in `dylint_lints/` (e.g., `de09_gts_layer`) are unrelated to this external tool.\n\nBefore mandating GTS validation in the specification, clarify:\n- Is `gts-rust` an internal tool that needs to be made available? \n- Should the specification reference a different, existing tool?\n- Does the external GTS repository have a different name or location?\n\nWithout resolving this, the MUST requirements for GTS validation cannot be implemented.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n70-70: Bare URL used\n\n(MD034, no-bare-urls)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.fdd-adapter/specs/domain-model.md around lines 68 - 140, The spec mandates\na non-existent external tool \"gts-rust\" and lacks schemas/CI integration; either\nprovide the actual repository (or internal location) and add generated schemas\nand CI hooks, or update the spec to reference an existing tool and remove the\nunreachable MUSTs: locate occurrences in domain-model.md (GTS Validation\nsection), any gts_schemas/ references, and the custom linters in dylint_lints/\n(e.g., de09_gts_layer) to: 1) if gts-rust is internal, add its repo URL and\ninstallation instructions and commit generated schemas under gts_schemas/, plus\nadd CI steps to run the CLI commands shown; or 2) if a different tool should be\nused, change the spec to name that tool, update the example commands and CI\nscripts accordingly, and remove/soften MUST requirements until tooling and\nschemas exist.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T16:45:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T16:45:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2699233775","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699233775"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2699233775"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699233775/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":68,"original_start_line":68,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":140,"original_line":140,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":140,"position":140,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2699233784","pull_request_review_id":3671777346,"id":2699233784,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g4wn4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@\n+# Architecture Patterns Specification\n+\n+**Source**: docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md, README.md, code analysis\n+\n+## Core Pattern: Modular Architecture\n+\n+**Description**: Everything is a Module - composable, independent units\n+\n+**Implementation**:\n+- Every logical component is a Rust package (crate)\n+- Each module has a library crate (`lib.rs`) with module declaration\n+- Optional binary crate (`main.rs`) for out-of-process modules\n+- Modules discovered automatically via `inventory` crate\n+\n+**Module Structure**:\n+```\n+modules/{module}/\n+├── src/\n+│   ├── lib.rs              # Module declaration\n+│   ├── module.rs           # Module implementation\n+│   ├── contract/           # Public contracts\n+│   ├── api/rest/           # REST API routes\n+│   ├── domain/             # Business logic\n+│   └── infra/              # Infrastructure\n+├── tests/                  # Integration tests\n+└── Cargo.toml\n+```\n+\n+## Gateway Pattern\n+\n+**Description**: Gateway modules with pluggable worker modules\n+\n+**When to Use**: When you need:\n+- Multiple implementations of same capability\n+- Runtime plugin selection\n+- Tenant-specific customization\n+- Dynamic module loading\n+\n+**Example**: `tenant_resolver` (gateway) + tenant resolver plugins\n+\n+## In-Process vs Out-of-Process Modules\n+\n+**In-Process**: Default, linked into main binary  \n+**Out-of-Process**: Separate process, gRPC communication\n+\n+**OoP Benefits**:\n+- Language independence\n+- Fault isolation\n+- Independent scaling\n+- Security boundaries\n+\n+**Reference**: `docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`\n+\n+## Layered Architecture (within modules)\n+\n+```\n+api/rest/           → REST API endpoints (DTOs)\n+domain/             → Business logic\n+infra/              → Infrastructure (DB, external services)\n+```\n+\n+**Rules**:\n+- API layer uses DTOs (not domain entities)\n+- Domain layer is DB-agnostic\n+- Infrastructure layer handles external concerns\n+\n+## Configuration Pattern\n+\n+**Hierarchical YAML**:\n+```yaml\n+server:              # Global config\n+database:            # Global DB config\n+modules:             # Per-module config\n+  module_name:\n+    config: {...}\n+    database: {...}\n+```\n+\n+**Environment Overrides**: `HYPERSPOT_` prefix\n+\n+## Error Handling Pattern\n+\n+**RFC 7807 Problem Details** for HTTP APIs  ","path":".fdd-adapter/specs/patterns.md","commit_id":"5af4e5c8aba34608a80924f9b5c849bf21b5c68f","original_commit_id":"82c11e73c235c1946abd87da4ab283cc8fc926e2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update RFC reference for consistency.**\n\nThis file references \"RFC 7807 Problem Details\" while `.fdd-adapter/specs/rust-guidelines.md` consistently references \