blic","site_admin":false},"body":"Path reference inconsistency will cause file resolution failure. The reference `/FDD/AGENTS.md` uses an absolute path starting with `/FDD/`, but the submodule is actually located at `.fdd/` (relative path from project root) as defined in `.fdd-config.json` and `.gitmodules`. This is inconsistent with how `.fdd-adapter/AGENTS.md` references the same file using relative path `../.fdd/AGENTS.md`. \n\nThe path should be:\n```markdown\nALWAYS open and follow `.fdd/AGENTS.md`\n```\n\nOr if using a special workspace notation:\n```markdown\nALWAYS open and follow `@/.fdd/AGENTS.md`\n```\n\nThe current absolute path `/FDD/AGENTS.md` will fail to resolve on most systems as it assumes a root-level `/FDD/` directory that doesn't exist.\n```suggestion\nALWAYS open and follow `.fdd/AGENTS.md`\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/258?chatWithGeneratedComment=a96fff9f-0388-4934-9727-c82dae008a64\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-18T11:37:25Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:37:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/258#discussion_r2702342930","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/258","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702342930"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyber