ure addition. The commit message documents all changes comprehensively, including the new FDD-Adapter specifications with 180+ agent instructions and the integration of GTS validation. No compatibility concerns are indicated.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>.gitmodules (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`4-9`: **LGTM! Submodule additions are properly configured.**\n\nThe FDD and GTS submodules are correctly specified with HTTPS URLs and appropriate paths.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>FDD-Adapter/specs/build-deploy.md (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`139-144`: **Good practice: Environment variables properly documented.**\n\nThe use of the `HYPERSPOT_` prefix for environment variables provides clear namespacing, and the examples use placeholder values rather than hardcoded secrets.\n\n---\n\n`210-225`: **Comprehensive agent instructions cover critical deployment practices.**\n\nThe agent instructions appropriately enforce zero-warning policies, security checks, and configuration best practices.\n\n---\n\n`29-49`: All referenced configuration files (`config/quickstart.yaml`, `config/no-db.yaml`, `config/e2e-local.yaml`) are present in the repository. No action needed.\n\n---\n\n`51-81`: All documented CI commands and Makefile targets exist and are accurately described. The Python script `scripts/ci.py` contains all referenced commands (fmt, clippy, test, dylint, audit, deny, all) with proper flag support (--fix for fmt and clippy), and the Makefile contains all documented targets (check, fmt, dev-fmt, clippy, test, dylint, deny).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>AGENTS.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-11`: **Good practice: Mandatory DCO and conventional commit format.**\n\nThe commit rules enforce Developer Certificate of Origin (DCO) and follow conventional commit format, which improve project governance and commit history clarity.\n\n---\n\n`3-3`: **Initialize the FDD submodule or update the reference.**\n\nThe directive on line 3 references `/FDD/AGENTS.md`, but the FDD submodule is not initialized. The FDD directory exists but is empty. Either initialize the submodule (via `git submodule update --init FDD`) or update the reference if this dependency is optional.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>FDD-Adapter/specs/conventions.md (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`71-76`: **Sound error handling practices documented.**\n\nThe guidelines correctly mandate `Result<T, E>`, prohibit panics in library code, and reference RFC 7807 for API error responses.\n\n---\n\n`163-178`: **Comprehensive agent instructions enforce Rust best practices.**\n\nThe ALWAYS/NEVER rules appropriately cover formatting, linting, naming conventions, documentation, and error handling.\n\n---\n\n`25-25`: **Reference is valid.** The file `specs/linting.md` exists in the repository at the referenced path.\n\n---\n\n`111-116`: **Remove or fix references to non-existent guideline files.**\n\nTwo of the four referenced guideline files do not exist:\n- `guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md` (missing)\n- `guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md` (missing)\n\nThe `guidelines/DNA/` directory structure does not exist. Either create these guideline files or remove/update the references to them in the Guidelines section.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Skipped due to learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Always consult `guidelines/DNA/` for REST API design patterns and architectural principles\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md` to learn about how to create a new module\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always follow the guidelines specified in `@/guidelines/README