e crate's new location at `modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/`:\n- `../../../../libs/modkit` navigates up 4 levels to root, then into libs\n- `../nodes_registry-sdk` correctly references the sibling SDK crate\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk/src/api.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`4-21`: **Well-designed async trait for the SDK public API.**\n\nThe trait is appropriately bounded with `Send + Sync` for thread-safe async usage, and the method signatures are clear and consistent. The rename from `NodesRegistryApi` to `NodesRegistryClient` follows common SDK naming conventions.\n\n---\n\n`1-2`: **All SDK imports are properly exported.**\n\nThe types imported on lines 1-2 (`NodesRegistryError`, `Node`, `NodeSysCap`, `NodeSysInfo`) are correctly re-exported in the SDK's `lib.rs`. No action needed.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`43-43`: **Path correctly updated for the restructured crate location.**\n\nThe dependency path now points to the implementation crate at the new nested location. This is the correct approach since the server should depend on the full implementation, which re-exports SDK types.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-node-info/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-19`: **Feature additions enable required functionality.**\n\n- `chrono` \"clock\" feature: enables `Utc::now()` for timestamp operations (used in collector.rs, sysinfo_collector.rs, syscap_collector.rs)\n- `uuid` \"v4\" feature: enables random UUID generation via `Uuid::new_v4()` (used in hardware_uuid.rs)\n\nBoth features are actively used and necessary for the crate to compile.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-17`: **SDK crate manifest is properly structured and registered.**\n\nBoth `nodes_registry-sdk` and `nodes_registry` crates are correctly registered in the workspace `members` list. The manifest correctly uses workspace-scoped metadata and dependencies, with the path to `modkit-node-info` properly resolving to the existing workspace crate.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`40-41`: **LGTM! Workspace members correctly updated for the SDK split.**\n\nThe new structure aligns with the existing SDK pattern used by `module_orchestrator` and `types-registry` modules in the workspace.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1745-1746`: **LGTM! Path and example correctly updated.**\n\nThe updated path correctly reflects the new nested directory structure for `nodes_registry`, and the example line provides clear guidance for developers adding new modules.\n\n---\n\n`2495-2498`: **LGTM! Plugin dependency documentation correctly simplified.**\n\nThe change from `deps = [\"types_registry\", \"plugin_a\", \"plugin_b\"]` to `deps = [\"types_registry\"]` accurately reflects that plugins are resolved indirectly via GTS, avoiding tight coupling between gateways and plugin modules.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/api/rest/mapper.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-8`: **LGTM! Import correctly migrated to SDK crate.**\n\nThe import path change from `crate::contract` to `nodes_registry_sdk` correctly reflects the SDK extraction. All model types are properly re-exported from the SDK crate.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-13`: **LGTM! Clean SDK crate structure with proper hygiene attributes.**\n\nThe SDK crate correctly:\n- Enforces `unsafe_code` prohibition and Rust 2018 idioms\n- Exposes a minimal public API surface (`NodesRegistryClient`, `NodesRegistryError`, model types)\n- Re-exports types at crate root for ergonomic consumer usage\n\nThe `api` module defines `NodesRegistryClient` as a well-designed async trait with proper bounds (`Send + Sync`) and consistent error handling across all node registry operations.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **LGTM: SDK type import update.**\n\nAligns the service with the new SDK public surface; no functional impact.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/tests/domain_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-7`: **LGTM: SysCap import path updated.**\n\nMatches the new crate-root re-export.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/tests/service_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`7-7`: **LGTM: SysCap import path updated.**\n\nConsistent with the new SDK-based re-exports.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/domain/node_storage.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **LGTM: SDK type import update.**\n\nKeeps storage aligned with the new SDK surface.\n\n---\n\n`266-266`: **LGTM: Test import updated to SDK path.**\n\nConsistent with crate re-exports.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/gateways/local.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **SDK import swap looks correct.**  \nPulling the public types from `nodes_registry_sdk` aligns with the new public contract split.\n\n---\n\n`18-38`: **Trait rename applied consistently.**  \nThe local client cleanly implements `NodesRegistryClient` with unchanged behavior.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`19-22`: **Crate-root re-exports are clear and consistent.**  \nThis keeps the public surface aligned with the new SDK crate.\n\n</blockquote><