cept `&SecurityCtx` as the first parameter for authorization and tenant isolation. However, `NodesRegistryClient` currently has no `SecurityCtx` parameters.\n\nThis is a **valid concern IF nodes_registry is tenant-scoped**, but the design suggests it is not:\n- **types_registry** explicitly exempts itself from SecurityCtx with: *\"GTS schemas and instances are global resources, so no security context is required\"*\n- **nodes_registry** appears to follow the same pattern—providing **system-level node information** accessible globally, not tenant-scoped data\n- Recent refactoring (commit cefc6b0) extracted nodes_registry-sdk without adding SecurityCtx, and the README (lines 262–277) documents usage without it\n\n**Recommendation:** Either (1) confirm that nodes_registry is indeed a global system service and add an explicit comment in `api.rs` stating why SecurityCtx is not required (mirroring types_registry's documentation), or (2) if node data IS tenant-aware, add `ctx: &SecurityCtx` as the first parameter to all trait methods.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/tests/service_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-9`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import path update from `nodes_registry::contract::SysCap` to `nodes_registry::SysCap` correctly aligns with the SDK restructuring where types are now re-exported at the crate root.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/README.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`16-42`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe architecture diagram accurately reflects the new dual-crate structure with the SDK separation. The directory layout clearly shows the public contract in `nodes_registry-sdk/` and implementation in `nodes_registry/`.\n\n---\n\n`58-70`: **LGTM!**\n\nAPI endpoint paths consistently updated to `/nodes-registry/v1/nodes`.\n\n---\n\n`260-277`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe \"Usage from Other Modules\" section correctly demonstrates the new SDK import pattern with `nodes_registry_sdk::NodesRegistryClient`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/lib.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-22`: **LGTM!**\n\nClean re-export surface that forwards all SDK types at the crate root. This maintains a consistent public API while delegating the actual type definitions to the SDK crate.\n\n---\n\n`24-36`: **LGTM!**\n\nModule structure is well organized with clear separation between public (`module::NodesRegistry`) and internal (`#[doc(hidden)]`) modules.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/nodes_registry/nodes_registry/src/gateways/local.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-3`: **LGTM!**\n\nImport paths correctly updated to use the SDK crate directly.\n\n---\n\n`17-38`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe trait implementation correctly updated from `NodesRegistryApi` to `NodesRegistryClient`. The error conversion using `.map_err(Into::into)` is clean and relies on the `From<DomainError> for NodesRegistryError` implementation in the domain layer, which properly maps all domain error variants to the SDK error type.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/256#pullrequestreview-3668215713","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/256","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/256#pullrequestreview-3668215713"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/256"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T00:26:54Z","commit_id":"cefc6b0f1cd71428b99dddf63272ff51ec571229"}]},{"source_pr_number":254,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pu