},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3756577953","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#issuecomment-3756577953","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/254","id":3756577953,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7f6NSh","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T19:46:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:43:05Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nUpdated API gateway port to 8087, made proto path resolution dynamic in a build script, bumped Docker base image and added libprotoc, increased CI health-check timeout and added local server lifecycle handling, and marked several E2E tests as skipped.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **API Gateway Port Configuration** <br> `config/e2e-local.yaml` | Changed API gateway bind address from `127.0.0.1:8086` to `127.0.0.1:8087`. |\n| **Build System Proto Resolution** <br> `modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs` | Replaced hard-coded proto paths with workspace-root resolution, added proto existence checks and improved error messaging; updated cargo:rerun-if-changed directives. |\n| **CI / Local E2E Orchestration** <br> `scripts/ci.py` | Increased health-check timeout (1s→2s), expanded exception handling (ConnectionResetError, OSError), updated default E2E base URL to `http://localhost:8087`, and added local server startup/logging/process lifecycle management. |\n| **Docker Image / Protobuf Packaging** <br> `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` | Switched base image to `debian:trixie-slim`, added `libprotoc-dev` install, and copied `proto` directory into the image. |\n| **Skipped E2E Tests** <br> `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_list_tenants_pagination.py`, `.../test_parents_children.py`, `.../test_root.py`, `.../test_select_projection.py`, `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_get.py`, `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_sysinfo.py` | Added `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Test is failing\")` to multiple failing tests across tenant_resolver and nodes_registry E2E suites. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 3 (Moderate) | ⏱️ ~20 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 A port hopped softly to eight-oh-seven,  \n> Protos now wander to the workspace heaven,  \n> Docker wears Trixie for glibc delight,  \n> CI tends servers through day and night,  \n> Skipping a few tests — the rabbit winks, all right!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 1 | ❌ 2</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning, 1 inconclusive)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status         | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | Resolution                                                                                                                                                            |\n| :----------------: | :------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ⚠️ Warning     | Docstring coverage is 56.25% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                                                        | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold.                                                                                    |\n|     Title check    | ❓ Inconclusive | The title is vague and generic, referencing 'DRAFT' status and using the phrase 'make all now works' without clearly conveying the specific changes in the changeset, which include port changes, build script improvements, test skips, and Docker updates. | Replace with a more descriptive title that captures the main change, such as 'Fix E2E local build and tests' or 'Update API gateway port and skip failing E2E tests'. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (1 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name    | Status   | Explanation                                                 |\n| :---------------: | :------- | :---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3756577953/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744792","pull_request_review_id":3667309922,"id":2695744792,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6grc0Y","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,13 +1,43 @@\n+use std::env;\n+use std::path::PathBuf;\n+\n fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\n-    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed=../../../../proto/directory/v1/directory.proto\");\n-    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed=../../../../proto\");\n+    let manifest_dir = PathBuf::from(env::var(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")?);\n+    // From module_orchestrator-grpc, go up 4 levels to workspace root:\n+    // grpc -> module_orchestrator -> system -> modules -> root\n+    let workspace_root = manifest_dir\n+        .parent()\n+        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n+        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n+        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n+        .ok_or(\"Could not find workspace root\")?;\n+\n+    let proto_dir = workspace_root.join(\"proto\");\n+    let proto_file = proto_dir.join(\"directory/v1/directory.proto\");\n+\n+    // Verify paths exist\n+    if !proto_file.exists() {\n+        return Err(format!(\n+            \"Proto file not found: {} (workspace root: {})\",\n+            proto_file.display(),\n+            workspace_root.display()\n+        )\n+        .into());\n+    }\n+\n+    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", proto_file.display());\n+    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", proto_dir.display());","path":"modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","original_commit_id":"a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`cargo rerun-if-changed directory watch files subdirectories behavior`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: Cargo's official docs say cargo:rerun-if-changed=PATH will scan a directory for any modifications (i.e. recursive) when PATH is a directory. However, some tooling/docs and macros note differing behavior on some platforms/versions — in those descriptions a directory only checks the directory's own mtime (not all files), and they recommend emitting rerun-if-changed lines for each file (or recursively) to be safe. To be robust, emit explicit rerun-if-changed for the files you need (or walk the tree in build.rs and print a line per file). [1][2][3]\n\nSources:\n- Cargo reference — rerun-if-changed (directory scanned for modifications). [1]\n- cargo_emit/docs.rs note (directory may only check directory mtime; recommend printing entries recursively). [2]\n- Rust Internals discussion about path/depfile resolution quirks (practical issues across versions). [3]\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find and examine the actual build.rs file\nfind . -name \"build.rs\" -path \"*/module_orchestrator-grpc/*\" -type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 134\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat ./modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1604\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Directory watch reliability and hardcoded proto file limitation.**\n\n`cargo:rerun-if-changed` on a directory has platform-dependent behavior—while official Cargo docs claim recursive scanning, practical experience shows it may only detect directory metadata changes on some versions/platforms. More significantly, the build only compiles a single hardcoded proto file (`directory/v1/directory.proto`), so new proto files in the directory won't be compiled regardless. Consider either: (1) walking the proto directory in build.rs and printing `rerun-if-changed` for each `.proto` file, or (2) iterating over proto files when calling `compile_protos()`, or (3) document that developers must explicitly add new proto files to the build script.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs` around\nlines 28 - 29, The current build.rs only emits cargo:rerun-if-changed for\nproto_file and proto_dir and compiles a single hardcoded proto, which misses new\n.proto files and is unreliable; modify build.rs to walk the proto_dir (e.g.,\nusing std::fs::read_dir or walkdir) and for each discovered *.proto emit\nprintln!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", proto_path.display()) and collect the\npaths into a Vec to pass into compile_protos() (or call\ntonic_build::compile_protos() for each file), replacing the single hardcoded\nproto_file usage; ensure compile_protos() (or the call site that invokes\ntonic_build) accepts the list of proto paths so all proto files are compiled and\nwatched individually.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744792","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744792"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744792"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":28,"original_start_line":28,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":29,"original_line":29,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":31,"position":31,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744796","pull_request_review_id":3667309922,"id":2695744796,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6grc0c","diff_hunk":"@@ -19,13 +20,15 @@ COPY libs ./libs\n COPY modules ./modules\n COPY examples ./examples\n COPY config ./config\n+COPY proto ./proto\n \n # Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\n # Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n RUN cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --features users-info-example","path":"testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","original_commit_id":"a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Comment says \"release mode\" but builds in debug mode.**\n\nThe comment on line 25-26 states \"Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\" but the command omits `--release`, producing a debug binary. Line 36 correctly copies from `target/debug/`, so this appears intentional for faster E2E builds. Update the comment to match the actual behavior.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# Build the hyperspot-server binary in release mode\n-# Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n+# Build the hyperspot-server binary in debug mode (faster for E2E tests)\n+# Using --bin to build only the specific binary\n RUN cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --features users-info-example\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# Build the hyperspot-server binary in debug mode (faster for E2E tests)\n# Using --bin to build only the specific binary\nRUN cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --features users-info-example\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` around lines 25 - 27, The Dockerfile\ncomment claiming \"release mode\" is incorrect for the build step; update the\ncomment above the RUN cargo build --bin hyperspot-server --features\nusers-info-example to state that it builds a debug/development binary (matching\nthe subsequent COPY from target/debug/) or explicitly change the command to\ninclude --release if you intend a release build; ensure the comment references\nthe RUN cargo build line and the COPY from target/debug/ so they are consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744796","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744796"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744796"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744796/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":25,"original_start_line":25,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":27,"original_line":27,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":19,"position":19,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744801","pull_request_review_id":3667309922,"id":2695744801,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6grc0h","diff_hunk":"@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@\n )\n \n \n+@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Test is failing\")\n @pytest.mark.asyncio","path":"testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","original_commit_id":"a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**All tests in this file are now skipped, leaving parent/children endpoints without E2E coverage.**\n\nSkipping an entire test suite is a significant gap in test coverage. The tenant hierarchy traversal (`/parents`, `/children`) endpoints will have no automated E2E validation.\n\nConsider:\n1. Creating a tracking issue to investigate and fix these failures\n2. Adding a comment explaining the root cause (e.g., is this related to the port change, a backend issue, or environment configuration?)\n3. If failures are environment-specific, consider using `pytest.mark.skipif` with a condition instead\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 38-39, 62-63, 91-92, 125-126\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py`\naround lines 16 - 17, The entire test file is being skipped via blanket\n`@pytest.mark.skip` which removes E2E coverage for the tenant hierarchy endpoints\n(/parents and /children); remove the global skip and instead create a tracking\nissue (and add its ID in a comment at the top of test_parents_children.py)\ndocumenting the root cause, then replace the unconditional skip with\npytest.mark.skipif guarded by a clear condition (e.g., an environment variable\nor CI flag) so tests run normally in supported environments, or mark individual\nfailing tests as xfail if only some tests are unstable; ensure the top-of-file\ncomment references the tracking issue and describes whether the failure is due\nto port changes, backend, or environment so future devs know how to re-enable\nthese tests.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744801","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744801"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2695744801"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695744801/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":16,"original_start_line":16,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":17,"original_line":17,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697439012","pull_request_review_id":3669484272,"id":2697439012,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gx6ck","diff_hunk":"@@ -86,7 +86,7 @@ modules:\n   api_gateway:\n     # No database needed for api_gateway\n     config:\n-      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8086\"\n+      bind_addr: \"127.0.0.1:8087\"","path":"config/e2e-local.yaml","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","original_commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It was intentional, the idea was to build and run server for e2e on 8086, not on 8087.\nThe reason is:\n\n1. Developers sometimes have already normal server running on 8087 (e.g. as part of smoke testing or IDE agentic flow commands or when use UI+Backend locally), so we would have port conflict. When we use 8086 it's always for e2e so e2e scrip can kill a server safely if it's running on 8086\n \n2. We want to run server with special config / CLI options when we run e2e. For example it can have something like `-mock` CLI parameter or load special mock modules that would simulate certain behavior, etc. We do not want this server on 8086 keep running or be used accidentally by UI or other API clients on the dev machine\n\n3. We need to test if bind_addr option works anyway ","created_at":"2026-01-16T08:16:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:17:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2697439012","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697439012"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2697439012"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697439012/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":89,"original_line":89,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697440154","pull_request_review_id":3669484272,"id":2697440154,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gx6ua","diff_hunk":"@@ -205,14 +206,15 @@ def kill_existing_server(port):\n \n \n def cmd_e2e(args):\n-    base_url = os.environ.get(\"E2E_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8086\")\n+    base_url = os.environ.get(\"E2E_BASE_URL\", \"http://localhost:8087\")","path":"scripts/ci.py","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","original_commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.