"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697975835"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#discussion_r2697975835"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697975835/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":57,"original_line":57,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2697441690,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3667309922,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7alrVi","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs`:\n- Around line 28-29: The current build.rs only emits cargo:rerun-if-changed for\nproto_file and proto_dir and compiles a single hardcoded proto, which misses new\n.proto files and is unreliable; modify build.rs to walk the proto_dir (e.g.,\nusing std::fs::read_dir or walkdir) and for each discovered *.proto emit\nprintln!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", proto_path.display()) and collect the\npaths into a Vec to pass into compile_protos() (or call\ntonic_build::compile_protos() for each file), replacing the single hardcoded\nproto_file usage; ensure compile_protos() (or the call site that invokes\ntonic_build) accepts the list of proto paths so all proto files are compiled and\nwatched individually.\n\nIn `@testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile`:\n- Around line 25-27: The Dockerfile comment claiming \"release mode\" is incorrect\nfor the build step; update the comment above the RUN cargo build --bin\nhyperspot-server --features users-info-example to state that it builds a\ndebug/development binary (matching the subsequent COPY from target/debug/) or\nexplicitly change the command to include --release if you intend a release\nbuild; ensure the comment references the RUN cargo build line and the COPY from\ntarget/debug/ so they are consistent.\n\nIn `@testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py`:\n- Around line 16-17: The entire test file is being skipped via blanket\n`@pytest.mark.skip` which removes E2E coverage for the tenant hierarchy endpoints\n(/parents and /children); remove the global skip and instead create a tracking\nissue (and add its ID in a comment at the top of test_parents_children.py)\ndocumenting the root cause, then replace the unconditional skip with\npytest.mark.skipif guarded by a clear condition (e.g., an environment variable\nor CI flag) so tests run normally in supported environments, or mark individual\nfailing tests as xfail if only some tests are unstable; ensure the top-of-file\ncomment references the tracking issue and describes whether the failure is due\nto port changes, backend, or environment so future devs know how to re-enable\nthese tests.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_select_projection.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-11`: **Single test file effectively disabled.**\n\nSame concern as other skipped tests - this leaves the `$select` projection functionality without E2E coverage. The earlier feedback about tracking issues and descriptive reasons applies here as well.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_list_tenants_pagination.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-9`: **Same generic skip reason concern as other test files.**\n\nAs noted in `test_root.py`, consider adding context to help track when these tests should be re-enabled. A tracking issue or brief root cause description would improve maintainability.\n\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 21-21\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_sysinfo.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`100-102`: **Consider adding a more descriptive skip reason or tracking issue.**\n\nThe generic \"Test is failing\" reason doesn't help future maintainers understand why this test fails or when it should be re-enabled. Consider:\n1. Adding a more specific reason (e.g., \"CPU info not populated in CI environment\")\n2. Linking to a tracking issue (e.g., `reason=\"Failing due to `#123`\"`)\n\nThis applies to multiple skipped tests across this PR.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_root.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-9`: **Consider adding more context to the skip reason.**\n\nThe generic \"Test is failing\" message doesn't help future maintainers understand when this test should be re-enabled. Consider linking to a tracking issue or describing the root cause (e.g., `\"Test is failing due to port migration - see `#XXX`\"`).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-13`: **Workspace root resolution is fragile.**\n\nThe 4-level parent traversal assumes a fixed directory structure. If the crate is moved or the hierarchy changes, this will fail with a generic \"Could not find workspace root\" error. Consider using `CARGO_WORKSPACE_DIR` (available since Cargo 1.70 in build scripts when set) or locating the root `Cargo.toml` by searching upward.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ More robust alternative</summary>\n\n```diff\n+fn find_workspace_root(start: &std::path::Path) -> Option<std::path::PathBuf> {\n+    let mut current = start.to_path_buf();\n+    loop {\n+        let cargo_toml = current.join(\"Cargo.toml\");\n+        if cargo_toml.exists() {\n+            // Check if this is a workspace root (has [workspace] section)\n+            if let Ok(contents) = std::fs::read_to_string(&cargo_toml) {\n+                if contents.contains(\"[workspace]\") {\n+                    return Some(current);\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+        if !current.pop() {\n+            return None;\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\n     let manifest_dir = PathBuf::from(env::var(\"CARGO_MANIFEST_DIR\")?);\n-    // From module_orchestrator-grpc, go up 4 levels to workspace root:\n-    // grpc -> module_orchestrator -> system -> modules -> root\n-    let workspace_root = manifest_dir\n-        .parent()\n-        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n-        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n-        .and_then(|p| p.parent())\n-        .ok_or(\"Could not find workspace root\")?;\n+    let workspace_root = find_workspace_root(&manifest_dir)\n+        .ok_or(\"Could not find workspace root (no Cargo.toml with [workspace])\")?;\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`161-163`: **Remove unused exception variable.**\n\nThe variable `e` is captured but never used. Replace with `_` to indicate intentional discard.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError) as e:\n+        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError):\n             # Connection errors are expected while server is starting\n             pass\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`266-266`: **Redundant reassignment.**\n\n`server_process` is already initialized to `None` on line 217. This reassignment is unnecessary.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n     else:\n         step(\"Running E2E tests in local mode\")\n         # Start local server automatically\n-        server_process = None\n         try:\n             wait_for_health(base_url, timeout_secs=5)\n         except SystemExit:\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between ed0d1dad6e96cecd9d3d12824003d1fddd755bab and a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (10)</summary>\n\n* `config/e2e-local.yaml`\n* `modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs`\n* `scripts/ci.py`\n* `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_list_tenants_pagination.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_root.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_select_projection.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_get.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_sysinfo.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧬 Code graph analysis (1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/conftest.py (1)</summary>\n\n* `base_url` (12-14)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.14.11)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py</summary>\n\n157-157: Audit URL open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of `file:` or custom schemes is often unexpected.\n\n(S310)\n\n---\n\n161-161: Local variable `e` is assigned to but never used\n\nRemove assignment to unused variable `e`\n\n(F841)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>config/e2e-local.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`89-89`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe port change from 8086 to 8087 is consistent with the PR objectives and aligns with the corresponding E2E_BASE_URL update in the CI scripts.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_get.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`57-58`: **Potential inconsistency: `test_get_node_with_force_refresh` also uses `details=true` but isn't skipped.**\n\n`test_get_node_by_id_with_details` is skipped while `test_get_node_with_force_refresh` (lines 127-167) also fetches nodes with `details=true` and remains active. If the `details=true` endpoint is broken, both tests should fail. If only specific assertions in this test are problematic, consider narrowing the skip or fixing those assertions rather than skipping the entire test.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`30-31`: **Using Debian testing release for GLIBC compatibility.**\n\n`debian:trixie-slim` is the Debian testing release, which may have stability considerations. For E2E testing this is acceptable, but be aware that trixie packages can change. Once trixie becomes stable (Debian 13), consider pinning to the stable release name.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`35-41`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe tonic_prost_build configuration correctly uses the dynamically resolved paths with proper error handling for path conversion.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`209-209`: **Port change consistent with other files.**\n\nThe default URL update to port 8087 aligns with `testing/e2e/conftest.py` and the config changes mentioned in the PR objectives.\n\n---\n\n`157-157`: **LGTM!**\n\nIncreasing timeout to 2s and expanding exception handling for `ConnectionResetError` and `OSError` improves robustness during server startup when transient connection errors are expected.\n\n---\n\n`296-303`: The pattern shown is actually correct and widely used. When passing a file object to `subprocess.Popen`, Python extracts the underlying file descriptor and the child process inherits it independently. Closing the parent's file object reference does not invalidate the child's inherited file descriptor—they are separate references in separate process file descriptor tables. The subprocess successfully writes to the inherited descriptor even after the with block closes the parent's file object.\n\n\n\n> Likely an incorrect or invalid review comment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#pullrequestreview-3667309922","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#pullrequestreview-3667309922"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T19:52:38Z","commit_id":"a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10"},{"id":3667343043,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7alzbD","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 0**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `296-303`: **File handles may close prematurely when server process is backgrounded.**\n> \n> The `with` statement exits immediately after `subprocess.Popen()` returns, closing both file handles while the subprocess continues running in the background. This can lead to lost log output or broken pipe errors.\n> \n> Open the files without `with` and rely on cleanup when the process terminates:\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -            with open(server_log_file, \"w\") as out_file, open(\n> -                server_error_file, \"w\"\n> -            ) as err_file:\n> -                server_process = subprocess.Popen(\n> -                    server_cmd,\n> -                    stdout=out_file,\n> -                    stderr=err_file,\n> -                )\n> +            out_file = open(server_log_file, \"w\")\n> +            err_file = open(server_error_file, \"w\")\n> +            server_process = subprocess.Popen(\n> +                server_cmd,\n> +                stdout=out_file,\n> +                stderr=err_file,\n> +            )\n> +            # Note: File handles intentionally left open for the subprocess.\n> +            # They will be closed when the process terminates.\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`28-29`: **Directory watch reliability concern (previously flagged).**\n\nThe `cargo:rerun-if-changed` on `proto_dir` has platform-dependent behavior and may only detect directory metadata changes rather than file modifications on some platforms. Additionally, the build still compiles only a single hardcoded proto file (`directory/v1/directory.proto`).\n\nAs noted in a previous review, consider walking the proto directory and emitting `rerun-if-changed` for each `.proto` file individually if you expect to add more proto files.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`16-17`: **All five tests skipped with a generic reason, removing E2E coverage for tenant hierarchy endpoints.**\n\nThis concern was already raised in a previous review. The blanket `@pytest.mark.skip(reason=\"Test is failing\")` decorators:\n1. Leave `/parents` and `/children` endpoints without any automated E2E validation\n2. Provide no actionable information about the root cause\n3. Lack a tracking issue reference for follow-up\n\nConsider using `pytest.mark.xfail` if failures are expected but you want visibility, or `pytest.mark.skipif` with a condition (e.g., environment flag) to allow tests to run in supported environments.\n\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 38-39, 62-63, 91-92, 125-126\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_sysinfo.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`100-102`: **Consider adding more context to the skip reason and tracking the issue.**\n\nThe generic reason \"Test is failing\" doesn't help future maintainers understand what's broken or when to revisit. Consider:\n1. Adding specifics about the failure (e.g., `\"CPU frequency_mhz returns 0 in CI environment\"`)\n2. Linking to a tracking issue or adding a TODO comment with the root cause\n\nThis applies to the other skipped tests in this PR as well.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_get.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`57-59`: **Acknowledged: Test skipped to unblock CI.**\n\nSame recommendation as the other skipped tests - consider documenting the specific failure reason and tracking resolution in an issue.\n\n\n\nWould you like me to open an issue to track re-enabling these skipped tests?\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`157-163`: **Health check improvements look good.**\n\nThe timeout increase to 2s and expanded exception handling for `ConnectionResetError` and `OSError` improve robustness during server startup.\n\nMinor: The caught exception `e` is unused (flagged by Ruff F841). You can simplify to just `except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError):` without the `as e`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Remove unused variable</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError) as e:\n-            # Connection errors are expected while server is starting\n-            pass\n+        except (URLError, HTTPError, ConnectionResetError, OSError):\n+            # Connection errors are expected while server is starting\n+            pass\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a0d6a7f5dfd66b30d501eeff666d34e777c4be10 and f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (10)</summary>\n\n* `config/e2e-local.yaml`\n* `modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs`\n* `scripts/ci.py`\n* `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_list_tenants_pagination.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_parents_children.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_root.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_select_projection.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_get.py`\n* `testing/e2e/modules/nodes_registry/test_nodes_registry_sysinfo.py`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (4)</summary>\n\n* testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_select_projection.py\n* testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile\n* testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_list_tenants_pagination.py\n* testing/e2e/modules/examples/tenant_resolver_gw/test_root.py\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧬 Code graph analysis (1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/conftest.py (1)</summary>\n\n* `base_url` (12-14)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 Ruff (0.14.11)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py</summary>\n\n157-157: Audit URL open for permitted schemes. Allowing use of `file:` or custom schemes is often unexpected.\n\n(S310)\n\n---\n\n161-161: Local variable `e` is assigned to but never used\n\nRemove assignment to unused variable `e`\n\n(F841)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>config/e2e-local.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`89-89`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe port change to 8087 is consistent with the corresponding updates in `scripts/ci.py` (default `E2E_BASE_URL`) and `testing/e2e/conftest.py` (base_url fixture default).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/module_orchestrator/module_orchestrator-grpc/build.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-13`: **Dynamic workspace root resolution is a good improvement.**\n\nThis approach correctly resolves proto paths relative to the workspace root rather than relying on relative paths that break in different build contexts.\n\nOne caveat: the hardcoded 4-level traversal (`parent().parent().parent().parent()`) is fragile if the crate moves within the workspace. Consider adding a comment documenting the expected path structure, or using a more robust approach like searching upward for `Cargo.toml` with `[workspace]`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>scripts/ci.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`209-209`: **Port update is consistent with config changes.**\n\nThe default `E2E_BASE_URL` now matches `config/e2e-local.yaml` and `testing/e2e/conftest.py`.\n\n---\n\n`263-316`: **Server auto-start in local mode is a nice usability improvement.**\n\nThe automatic server lifecycle management with proper log redirection and cleanup makes local E2E testing more convenient.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#pullrequestreview-3667343043","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/254#pullrequestreview-3667343043"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/254"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T20:00:21Z","commit_id":"f5387c155fe090efd112e36c5a0f72e0c80c1e7c"}]},{"source_pr_number":253,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253","source_state":"closed","source_author":"KvizadSaderah","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #253] feat(dylint): add core domain and security lints (DE0301, DE0308, DE0706)","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"feature/dylint-core-lints","pr_head_sha":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"KvizadSaderah","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","id":3178299785,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs69cQGJ","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/253","number":253,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"feat(dylint): add core domain and security lints (DE0301, DE0308, DE0706)","user":{"login":"KvizadSaderah","id":14391797,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzkxNzk3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14391797?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah","html_url":"https://github.com/KvizadSaderah","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KvizadSaderah/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Overview\n\nAdd three new dylint rules for architectural enforcement.\n\n**Relates to #68** (DyLint Top-10 Implementation)\n\n### New Lints\n\n| Lint | Name | Purpose |\n|------|------|---------|\n| DE0301 | no_infra_in_domain | Prohibits infrastructure imports in domain layer |\n| DE0308 | no_http_in_domain | Prohibits HTTP types in domain layer |\n| DE0706 | no_direct_sqlx | Prohibits direct sqlx usage, enforces Sea-ORM/SecORM |\n\n### Changes\n\n- Added `de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/`\n- Added `de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/`\n- Added `de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/`\n- Updated `lint_utils/src/lib.rs` with helper functions\n- Updated `Cargo.toml` with new workspace members\n\n### Testing\n\n- `make dylint-test` ✅\n- `make dylint` ✅\n\n---\n\n*This is a clean PR from upstream/main, replacing #224 which had merge conflicts.*\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added three new lints to enforce architecture best practices: DE0301 (prevent infrastructure dependencies in domain modules), DE0308 (prevent HTTP types in domain modules), and DE0706 (prevent direct sqlx usage in favor of ORM abstractions).\n  * Introduced `DomainModel` and `DomainErrorMarker` traits for compile-time domain layer enforcement.\n\n* **Chores**\n  * Removed the Types system module and associated SDK.\n  * Removed unused workspace dependencies.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:18:50Z","updated_at":"2026-02-12T19:49:19Z","closed_at":"2026-02-12T19:49:18Z","merged_at":"2026-02-12T19:49:18Z","merge_commit_sha":"a6864d838a75217433e0b65fcb5a7494ed230988","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_ev