a/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-21T10:29:45Z","body":"We stop the PR for now until we discuss a proper implementation of safeguards by using traits, generics and macros. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3777344603/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801631969","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#issuecomment-3801631969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/253","id":3801631969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7imEzh","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T20:34:04Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T20:34:04Z","body":"> We stop the PR for now until we discuss a proper implementation of safeguards by using traits, generics and macros.\r\n\r\n@Bechma , can we do opposite - first we implement Dylint rule (as it's very simple) and have needed guards in place. And then, when we have better idea we replace given Dylint to something else?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801631969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801788902","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#issuecomment-3801788902","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/253","id":3801788902,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7imrHm","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T21:14:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T21:14:55Z","body":"@Artifizer The problem that I still see with these kind of lints is, as andrew mention in https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/253#pullrequestreview-3678164876 , as we go restrictive, we limit people of creating utils methods, or certain use cases we didn't think about it. I don't like to play the cat-mouse game with the lints.\r\n\r\nThere's a work done here https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/247 where we are starting to apply the idea of: \"The struct that you are going to use in REST, need to have certain compilation check\".\r\nThus, my idea is to extend that concept if it's well received, to the 3 lints, for infra/http in domain and sqlx. This is why it's on draft mode.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3801788902/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3805419641","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#issuecomment-3805419641","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/253","id":3805419641,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7i0hh5","user":{"login":"mergify[bot]","id":37929162,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90Mzc5MjkxNjI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/10562?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/mergify","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mergify%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url"