admin":false},"name":"GitHub Actions","description":"Automate your workflow from idea to production","external_url":"https://help.github.com/en/actions","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","created_at":"2018-07-30T09:30:17Z","updated_at":"2026-05-05T14:51:38Z","permissions":{"actions":"write","administration":"read","artifact_metadata":"write","attestations":"write","checks":"write","code_quality":"write","contents":"write","copilot_requests":"write","deployments":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","merge_queues":"write","metadata":"read","models":"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3823351788","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#issuecomment-3823351788","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/253","id":3823351788,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7j47fs","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-30T11:59:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T11:59:52Z","body":"> @Bechma Regarding the two traits question:\r\n> \r\n> Current design rationale:\r\n> \r\n> * DomainSafe is needed for blanket impls on types that are not Send+Sync (like &str, &T)\r\n> * DomainModel = DomainSafe + Send + Sync — for actual domain entities\r\n> \r\n> To align with api_dto pattern, there are two options:\r\n> \r\n> Option A: Add flags like api_dto #[domain_model(entity)] for entities with identity #[domain_model(value_object)] for immutable value objects This gives proper validation in macro (like validate_flags) plus we hide DomainSafe with doc(hidden).\r\n> \r\n> Option B: Simplify without flags Keep one trait, make DomainSafe doc(hidden), validation stays via trait bounds.\r\n> \r\n> Which approach would you prefer?\r\n\r\nThere's no need for that Send + Sync, you achieve that by using Arc<T> . So we don't really need these two traits.\r\n\r\nPlease, check the macro api_dto and implement a similar solution for the domain model while having the validation inside of the macro. When doing a transformation between dto and domain model, the generic trait must have the constraint of DomainModel(DomainSafe naming is weird to me)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3823351788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cybe