t Started\r\nSimply sign into Github and click the \"Configure\" button. Check out our documentation for more info: https://docs.qodo.ai/get-started.\r\n\r\n## Overview\r\nQodo automatically reviews every GitHub pull request, identifies logic bugs, edge cases, security issues, and code quality problems, and provides actionable suggestions your team can apply immediately.\r\n\r\nInstall in minutes. Integrates seamlessly into your existing workflows.\r\n\r\n## Qodo is designed for developers who:\r\n- Handle frequent pull requests and need reliable review coverage\r\n- Balance code quality with fast delivery\r\n- Work in complex, multi-repo systems\r\n- Use AI-generated code and need stronger guardrails\r\n- Build production software where reliability matters\r\n\r\n## Qodo Capabilities\r\n- ## Automated PR Analysis\r\n  - Reviews every pull request automatically\r\n  - No manual trigger required\r\n\r\n- ## Context-Aware Code Review\r\n  - Understands cross-file changes\r\n  - Detects architectural inconsistencies\r\n\r\n- ## Actionable Suggestions\r\n  - Concrete code fixes\r\n  - Clear explanations\r\n  - Prioritized feedback\r\n\r\n- ## Security & Reliability Checks\r\n  - Identifies risky patterns\r\n  - Reduces attack surface area","external_url":"https://www.qodo.ai/","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/qodo-code-review","created_at":"2023-11-16T16:18:38Z","updated_at":"2026-05-06T15:53:40Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"read","contents":"write","discussions":"write","issues":"write","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write"},"events":["check_run","check_suite","discussion_comment","issue_comment","pull_request","pull_request_review_comment","push"]}}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695483972","pull_request_review_id":3666988457,"id":2695483972,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqdJE","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@\n+# DE0706: No Direct sqlx Usage\n+\n+### What it does\n+\n+Prohibits direct usage of the `sqlx` crate in the codebase.\n+\n+### Why is this bad?\n+\n+Direct sqlx usage bypasses important architectural layers:\n+- **Skips security enforcement**: SecureConn and AccessScope are not applied\n+- **Bypasses query building**: Loses type-safe query construction\n+- **Inconsistent patterns**: Makes codebase harder to maintain\n+- **No audit logging**: Loses automatic operation tracking\n+- **No tenant isolation**: Multi-tenant security controls are bypassed\n+\n+### Example\n+\n+```rust\n+// ❌ Bad - direct sqlx usage\n+use sqlx::PgPool;\n+use sqlx::query;\n+\n+let pool = PgPool::connect(&db_url).await?;\n+let users = sqlx::query(\"SELECT * FROM users\")\n+    .fetch_all(&pool)\n+    .await?;\n+```\n+\n+```rust\n+// ❌ Bad - sqlx query macros\n+use sqlx::query_as;\n+\n+let user = query_as!(User, \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\", id)\n+    .fetch_one(&pool)\n+    .await?;\n+```\n+\n+Use instead:\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ Good - sea-orm with type-safe queries\n+use sea_orm::{EntityTrait, QueryFilter, ColumnTrait};\n+use crate::infra::storage::entity::user::{Entity as UserEntity, Column};\n+\n+let users = UserEntity::find()\n+    .all(&conn)\n+    .await?;\n+\n+let user = UserEntity::find()\n+    .filter(Column::Id.eq(id))\n+    .one(&conn)\n+    .await?;\n+```\n+\n+```rust\n+// ✅ Good - SecureConn with access scope\n+use modkit_db::secure::SecureEntityExt;\n+use modkit_security::AccessScope;\n+\n+let users = UserEntity::find()\n+    .secure()                    // Enable security layer\n+    .scope_with(&scope)          // Apply tenant/access control\n+    .all(conn)\n+    .await\n+    .map_err(db_err)?;\n+```\n+\n+### Configuration\n+\n+This lint is configured to **deny** by default.\n+\n+It detects:\n+- `use sqlx::*` imports\n+- `use sqlx::{...}` nested imports\n+- `extern crate sqlx` declarations\n+\n+### See Also\n+\n+- [DE0705](../de0705_no_prebuild_sql_queries) - No Prebuilt SQL Queries\n+- [DE0407](../../de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings) - No Hardcoded Connection Strings","path":"dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/README.md","commit_id":"bfa85efde9203c80a25c3ab58d5c97e06a97dab4","original_commit_id":"bfa85efde9203c80a25c3ab58d5c97e06a97dab4","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify referenced lint directories exist\necho \"Checking DE0705:\"\nfd -t d \"de0705\" dylint_lints/\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Checking DE0407:\"\nfd -t d \"de0407\" dylint_lints/\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Listing directory structure to understand relative paths:\"\necho \"From de0706 parent directory:\"\nls -la dylint_lints/de07_security/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Infrastructure directory:\"\nls -la dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/ 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 396\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# More thorough search for these lint directories\necho \"Search for all de07 and de04 directories:\"\nfind dylint_lints -maxdepth 2 -type d -name \"de07*\" -o -name \"de04*\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Complete listing of de07_security contents:\"\nfind dylint_lints/de07_security -type d\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Check if de04_infrastructure exists:\"\nls -la dylint_lints/ | grep -i de04\n\necho \"\"\necho \"All lint categories present:\"\nls -d dylint_lints/de* 2>/dev/null\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 748\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Double-check by looking at the README file itself to understand the context\necho \"Current README.md content around lines 79-80:\"\nsed -n '75,85p' dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/README.md\n\necho \"\"\necho \"Check if there are any DE07xx or DE04xx lints anywhere in the repo:\"\nfind dylint_lints -maxdepth 2 -type d | grep -E \"de070[0-9]|de040[0-9]\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 460\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Remove or fix broken \"See Also\" links to non-existent lints.**\n\nThe \"See Also\" section references DE0705 and DE0407, but neither lint exists in the codebase. Either remove these references or update them to point to actual lints.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/README.md` around lines 79 -\n80, The \"See Also\" section contains broken references to lint IDs \"[DE0705]\" and\n\"[DE0407]\"; either remove those two link lines or replace them with correct\nexisting lint IDs/links. Locate the \"See Also\" block in the README (the lines\nstarting with \"- [DE0705]\" and \"- [DE0407]\") and update each entry to point to\nan actual lint in the codebase or delete the lines if no appropriate\nreplacements exist; ensure link text and relative path match the target lint's\nreal ID.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 65d0abd","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:22:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T08:45:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2695483972","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695483972"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2695483972"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695483972/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":79,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":80,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":80,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695503146","pull_request_review_id":3667011848,"id":2695503146,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqh0q","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+\n+use rustc_ast::{Item, ItemKind, UseTree, UseTreeKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{EarlyLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+use lint_utils::is_in_domain_path;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_early_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that domain modules do not import infrastructure dependencies.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Domain modules should contain pure business logic and depend only on abstractions (ports),\n+    /// not concrete implementations. Importing infrastructure code (database, HTTP, external APIs)\n+    /// violates the Dependency Inversion Principle and makes domain logic harder to test.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust\n+    /// // Bad - infrastructure imports in domain\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use crate::infra::storage::UserRepository;  // ❌ concrete implementation\n+    ///     use sea_orm::*;  // ❌ database framework\n+    ///     use sqlx::*;     // ❌ database driver\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust\n+    /// // Good - domain depends on abstractions\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use std::sync::Arc;\n+    ///     \n+    ///     pub trait UsersRepository: Send + Sync {\n+    ///         async fn find_by_id(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<User, DomainError>;\n+    ///     }\n+    ///     \n+    ///     pub struct Service {\n+    ///         repo: Arc<dyn UsersRepository>,  // ✅ trait object\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0301_NO_INFRA_IN_DOMAIN,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"domain modules should not import infrastructure dependencies (DE0301)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// Forbidden import patterns for domain layer\n+const INFRA_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    // Infrastructure layer\n+    \"crate::infra\",","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"bfa85efde9203c80a25c3ab58d5c97e06a97dab4","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"we also have these references:\r\n- modkit_db\r\n- modkit_db_macros\r\n- modkit_transport_grpc","created_at":"2026-01-15T18:28:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T18:39:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2695503146","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695503146"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2695503146"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695503146/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":56,"original_line":57,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":57,"position":56,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695517931","pull_request_review_id":3667011848,"id":2695517931,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqlbr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+\n+use rustc_ast::{Item, ItemKind, UseTree, UseTreeKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{EarlyLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+use lint_utils::is_in_domain_path;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_early_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that domain modules do not reference HTTP types or status codes.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Domain modules should be transport-agnostic. HTTP is just one possible\n+    /// transport layer. Referencing HTTP types in domain code couples the business\n+    /// logic to a specific transport mechanism.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - HTTP types in domain\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use http::StatusCode;\n+    ///     \n+    ///     pub fn check_result() -> StatusCode {\n+    ///         StatusCode::OK  // ❌ HTTP-specific\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - domain errors converted in API layer\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     pub enum DomainResult {\n+    ///         Success,\n+    ///         NotFound,\n+    ///         InvalidData,\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"domain modules should not reference HTTP types or status codes (DE0308)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// HTTP-related patterns forbidden in domain code\n+const HTTP_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"http::\",\n+    \"http::StatusCode\",\n+    \"http::Method\",\n+    \"http::HeaderMap\",\n+    \"http::Request\",\n+    \"http::Response\",\n+    \"axum::http\",\n+    \"hyper::StatusCode\",\n+    \"hyper::Method\",\n+    \"actix_web::http\",","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"bfa85efde9203c80a25c3ab58d5c97e06a97dab4","original_commit_id":"bfa85efde9203c80a25c3ab58d5c97e06a97dab4","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com