e_args in DE0308\nrg \"check_angle_args|angle_args\" dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 210\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the rustc_ast enum definitions to confirm AssocType and Constraint are real variants\nrg \"enum AngleBracketedArg|enum GenericArg\" --type rust --max-count 5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for any existing tests that check associated type constraints in either DE0308 or DE0301\nfind dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer -name \"*.rs\" -type f -exec rg \"Item\\s*=\" {} + | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if DE0301 test files have any trait bound tests at all\ncat -n dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/ui/good_domain_0301.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 804\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# See the full DE0308 implementation to check if trait bounds walk their generic args\nwc -l dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs\nsed -n '160,260p' dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs | cat -n\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 5003\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any stderr files that show expected lint output for trait bounds\nfind dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer -name \"*.stderr\" -type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 747\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the trait bounds test for DE0308 to see what cases are covered\ncat -n dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/ui/trait_bounds_http.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 633\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the corresponding stderr to see what's expected\ncat -n dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/ui/trait_bounds_http.stderr\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1010\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if DE0301 has a corresponding trait bounds test\nls -la dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/ui/ | grep -i trait\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search the entire DE0301 codebase to see if associated types or constraints are mentioned anywhere\nrg \"AssocType|assoc_type|Item\\s*=|Response\\s*=\" dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the actual structure of the rustc_ast crate to understand AngleBracketedArg variants\npython3 << 'EOF'\n# Try to understand what AngleBracketedArg variants exist by searching Rust documentation\nimport subprocess\nresult = subprocess.run(\n  ['rg', 'AngleBracketedArg::', '--type', 'rust', '-A', '2'],\n  capture_output=True,\n  text=True,\n  cwd='.'\n)\n# Get unique variants\nlines = result.stdout.split('\\n')\nvariants = set()\nfor line in lines:\n  if 'AngleBracketedArg::' in line:\n    # Extract the variant name\n    parts = line.split('AngleBracketedArg::')\n    if len(parts) > 1:\n      variant = parts[1].split('(')[0].split('[')[0].split('{')[0].split(';')[0].split(',')[0].strip()\n      if variant:\n        variants.add(variant)\n\nfor v in sorted(variants):\n  print(f\"  AngleBracketedArg::{v}\")\nEOF\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 150\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Trait-bound generic arguments and associated-type constraints aren't checked recursively.**\n\nThe lint only checks trait paths directly but skips walking the generic arguments within trait bounds. This means `impl Iterator<Item = sqlx::PgPool>` or `dyn Service<Response = http::Response>` would not be caught. Additionally, within `TyKind::Path` generic args, only `AngleBracketedArg::Arg(Type)` is handled—`AssocType` and `Constraint` cases are missing.\n\nExtract a helper to walk all angle-bracketed argument variants and apply it consistently to trait bounds:\n\n<details>\n<summary>Fix details</summary>\n\n```diff\n+fn check_angle_args(\n+    cx: &rustc_lint::EarlyContext<'_>,\n+    angle_args: &rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArgs,\n+) {\n+    for arg in &angle_args.args {\n+        match arg {\n+            rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArg::Arg(rustc_ast::GenericArg::Type(inner_ty)) => {\n+                check_type_in_domain(cx, inner_ty);\n+            }\n+            rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArg::AssocType(assoc) => {\n+                check_type_in_domain(cx, &assoc.ty);\n+            }\n+            rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArg::Constraint(constraint) => {\n+                check_type_in_domain(cx, &constraint.ty);\n+            }\n+            _ => {}\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n```\n\nThen use it in `TyKind::Path` and recursively within `TyKind::TraitObject` and `TyKind::ImplTrait` trait bounds to check their generic arguments.\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/src/lib.rs` around\nlines 148 - 232, The lint misses checking trait-bound generic/associated-type\narguments (e.g., impl Iterator<Item = sqlx::PgPool> or dyn Service<Response =\nhttp::Response>) because TyKind::Path only inspects AngleBracketedArg::Arg(Type)\nand trait bounds in TyKind::TraitObject / TyKind::ImplTrait aren't recursing\ninto their generic args; add a helper (e.g., walk_angle_bracketed_args) that\naccepts an &rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArgs and calls check_type_in_domain for\nevery GenericArg::Type and also recursively visits associated-type bindings and\nconstraint types (handle AssocType/Constraint/binding variants), then call this\nhelper from check_type_in_domain when handling TyKind::Path segments' args and\nwhen iterating trait_ref.trait_ref.path in TyKind::TraitObject and\nTyKind::ImplTrait so INFRA_PATTERNS matching and DE0301_NO_INFRA_IN_DOMAIN\ndiagnostics cover those cases too.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:13:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:13:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2698900299","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900299"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2698900299"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900299/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":140,"original_start_line":148,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":231,"original_line":232,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":232,"position":231,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900304","pull_request_review_id":3671358874,"id":2698900304,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g3fNQ","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,44 @@\n+[package]\n+name = \"de0308_no_http_in_domain\"\n+version = \"0.1.0\"\n+authors = [\"Hypernetix\"]\n+description = \"Domain modules should not reference HTTP types or status codes (DE0308)\"\n+edition = \"2024\"\n+publish = false\n+\n+[lib]\n+crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]\n+\n+[[example]]\n+name = \"bad_http_import\"\n+path = \"ui/bad_http_import.rs\"\n+\n+[[example]]\n+name = \"good_domain_0308\"\n+path = \"ui/good_domain_0308.rs\"\n+\n+[[example]]\n+name = \"bad_http_type_in_struct\"\n+path = \"ui/bad_http_type_in_struct.rs\"\n+\n+[[example]]\n+name = \"nested_generic_http_type\"\n+path = \"ui/nested_generic_http_type.rs\"\n+\n+[[example]]\n+name = \"trait_bounds_http\"\n+path = \"ui/trait_bounds_http.rs\"\n+\n+[dependencies]\n+clippy_utils.workspace = true\n+dylint_linting.workspace = true\n+lint_utils.workspace = true\n+\n+[dev-dependencies]\n+dylint_testing.workspace = true\n+http = \"1.0\"\n+axum.workspace = true\n+anyhow.workspace = true\n+\n+[package.metadata.rust-analyzer]\n+rustc_private = true","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"544c3d0d3f498a5f1023874578df5ab762f78cc1","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check editions in other lint crates\necho \"=== Editions used in other dylint lint crates ===\"\nfind dylint_lints -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f | head -10 | while read file; do\n  edition=$(grep \"^edition\" \"$file\" 2>/dev/null | head -1)\n  if [ -n \"$edition\" ]; then\n    echo \"$file: $edition\"\n  fi\ndone\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking workspace root Cargo.toml for http dependency ===\"\ngrep -A20 \"\\[dependencies\\]\" Cargo.toml | grep -E \"^(http|axum)\" || echo \"No http or axum in root [dependencies]\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking workspace members in root Cargo.toml ===\"\ngrep -A30 \"members = \\[\" Cargo.toml | head -40\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking if de0308_no_http_in_domain is registered ===\"\ngrep \"de0308_no_http_in_domain\" Cargo.toml || echo \"Not found in root Cargo.toml\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2478\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if 2024 edition is valid and how it's used in the workspace\necho \"=== Checking for 'edition.workspace = true' pattern in workspace ===\"\nfind . -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f -exec grep -l \"edition.workspace = true\" {} \\; 2>/dev/null | head -5\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Full context of de0503 edition configuration ===\"\ncat dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0503_plugin_client_suffix/Cargo.toml | head -15\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking workspace definition in root Cargo.toml ===\"\nhead -50 Cargo.toml | grep -A5 \"\\[workspace\\]\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Full members list to confirm de0308 absence ===\"\ngrep \"de0308\" Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 955\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add lint crate to workspace `members` list and use workspace-inherited edition.**\n\nThe Cargo.toml is missing two critical elements:\n\n1. **Missing workspace registration**: The lint crate `de0308_no_http_in_domain` is not registered in the workspace root `Cargo.toml` `members` list. Per coding guidelines, new lint crates must be added to the workspace members.\n\n2. **Edition not workspace-inherited**: Use `edition.workspace = true` instead of hardcoding `edition = \"2024\"`. The crate `de0503_plugin_client_suffix` demonstrates this pattern and provides consistency across the workspace.\n\nThe example targets and `.workspace = true` dependencies are correctly configured, but these two issues must be resolved.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/Cargo.toml` around\nlines 1 - 44, The crate de0308_no_http_in_domain Cargo.toml currently hardcodes\nedition and isn't registered in the workspace; update it to use\nworkspace-inherited edition by replacing the edition = \"2024\" entry with\nedition.workspace = true in the [package] table, and register the crate in the\nworkspace root by adding \"de0308_no_http_in_domain\" to the workspace members\nlist so the workspace builds and inherits edition and other workspace settings.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-16T15:13:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T15:13:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2698900304","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900304"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2698900304"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900304/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":44,"original_line":44,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":44,"position":44,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698900308","pull_request_review_id":3671358874,"id":2698900308,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g3fNU","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,287 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+\n+use rustc_ast::{Item, ItemKind, UseTree, UseTreeKind, Ty, TyKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{EarlyLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+use lint_utils::is_in_domain_path;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_early_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that domain modules do not reference HTTP types or status codes.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Domain modules should be transport-agnostic. HTTP is just one possible\n+    /// transport layer. Referencing HTTP types in domain code couples the business\n+    /// logic to a specific transport mechanism.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - HTTP types in domain\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use http::StatusCode;\n+    ///     \n+    ///     pub fn check_result() -> StatusCode {\n+    ///         StatusCode::OK  // ❌ HTTP-specific\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - domain errors converted in API layer\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     pub enum DomainResult {\n+    ///         Success,\n+    ///         NotFound,\n+    ///         InvalidData,\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"domain modules should not reference HTTP types or status codes (DE0308)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// HTTP-related patterns forbidden in domain code\n+/// Only includes frameworks actually used in the project: axum, hyper, http\n+const HTTP_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"http::\",\n+    \"http::StatusCode\",\n+    \"http::Method\",\n+    \"http::HeaderMap\",\n+    \"http::Request\",\n+    \"http::Response\",\n+    \"axum::http\",\n+    \"hyper::StatusCode\",\n+    \"hyper::Method\",\n+    \"reqwest::StatusCode\",\n+];\n+\n+fn use_tree_to_strings(tree: &UseTree) -> Vec<String> {\n+    match &tree.kind {\n+        UseTreeKind::Simple(..) | UseTreeKind::Glob => {\n+            vec![tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n+                .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                .join(\"::\")]\n+        }\n+        UseTreeKind::Nested { items, .. } => {\n+            let prefix = tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n+                .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                .join(\"::\");\n+            \n+            let mut paths = Vec::new();\n+            for (nested_tree, _) in items {\n+                for nested_str in use_tree_to_strings(nested_tree) {\n+                    if nested_str.is_empty() {\n+                        paths.push(prefix.clone());\n+                    } else if prefix.is_empty() {\n+                        paths.push(nested_str);\n+                    } else {\n+                        paths.push(format!(\"{}::{}\", prefix, nested_str));\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            }\n+            if paths.is_empty() { vec![prefix] } else { paths }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn check_use_in_domain(cx: &rustc_lint::EarlyContext<'_>, item: &Item) {\n+    let ItemKind::Use(use_tree) = &item.kind else {\n+        return;\n+    };\n+\n+    for path_str in use_tree_to_strings(use_tree) {\n+        for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n+            if path_str.starts_with(pattern) {\n+                cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, item.span, |diag| {\n+                    diag.primary_message(\n+                        \"domain module imports HTTP type (DE0308)\"\n+                    );\n+                    diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n+                });\n+                return;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+fn check_type_in_domain(cx: &rustc_lint::EarlyContext<'_>, ty: &Ty) {\n+    match &ty.kind {\n+        TyKind::Path(_, path) => {\n+            // Check the path itself\n+            let path_str = path.segments.iter()\n+                .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                .join(\"::\");\n+            \n+            for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n+                if path_str.starts_with(pattern) {\n+                    cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, ty.span, |diag| {\n+                        diag.primary_message(\n+                            format!(\"domain module uses HTTP type `{}` (DE0308)\", path_str)\n+                        );\n+                        diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n+                    });\n+                    return;\n+                }\n+            }\n+            \n+            // Recursively check generic arguments (e.g., Option<http::StatusCode>)\n+            for segment in &path.segments {\n+                if let Some(args) = &segment.args {\n+                    if let rustc_ast::GenericArgs::AngleBracketed(ref angle_args) = **args {\n+                        for arg in &angle_args.args {\n+                            if let rustc_ast::AngleBracketedArg::Arg(rustc_ast::GenericArg::Type(inner_ty)) = arg {\n+                                check_type_in_domain(cx, inner_ty);\n+                            }\n+                        }\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+        // Handle references: &http::Request\n+        TyKind::Ref(_, mut_ty) => {\n+            check_type_in_domain(cx, &mut_ty.ty);\n+        }\n+        // Handle slices: [http::StatusCode]\n+        TyKind::Slice(inner_ty) => {\n+            check_type_in_domain(cx, inner_ty);\n+        }\n+        // Handle arrays: [http::StatusCode; 10]\n+        TyKind::Array(inner_ty, _) => {\n+            check_type_in_domain(cx, inner_ty);\n+        }\n+        // Handle raw pointers: *const http::Request\n+        TyKind::Ptr(mut_ty) => {\n+            check_type_in_domain(cx, &mut_ty.ty);\n+        }\n+        // Handle tuples: (http::Request, String)\n+        TyKind::Tup(types) => {\n+            for inner_ty in types {\n+                check_type_in_domain(cx, inner_ty);\n+            }\n+        }\n+        // Handle trait objects: dyn http::Service\n+        TyKind::TraitObject(bounds, _) => {\n+            for bound in bounds {\n+                if let rustc_ast::GenericBound::Trait(trait_ref) = bound {\n+                    // Check the trait path itself\n+                    let path = &trait_ref.trait_ref.path;\n+                    let path_str = path.segments.iter()\n+                        .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                        .join(\"::\");\n+                    \n+                    for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n+                        if path_str.starts_with(pattern) {\n+                            cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, ty.span, |diag| {\n+                                diag.primary_message(\n+                                    format!(\"domain module uses HTTP trait `{}` (DE0308)\", path_str)\n+                                );\n+                                diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n+                            });\n+                            return;\n+                        }\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }\n+        // Handle impl Trait: impl http::Service\n+        TyKind::ImplTrait(_, bounds) => {\n+            for bound in bounds {\n+                if let rustc_ast::GenericBound::Trait(trait_ref) = bound {\n+                    // Check the trait path itself\n+                    let path = &trait_ref.trait_ref.path;\n+                    let path_str = path.segments.iter()\n+                        .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                        .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                        .join(\"::\");\n+                    \n+                    for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n+                        if path_str.starts_with(pattern) {\n+                            cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, ty.span, |diag| {\n+                                diag.primary_message(\n+                                    format!(\"domain module uses HTTP trait `{}` (DE0308)\", path_str)\n+                                );\n+                                diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n+                            });\n+                            return;\n+                        }\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            }\n+        }","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"544c3d0d3f498a5f1023874578df5ab762f78cc1","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.gi