ructs with bounds in the codebase that use domain_model\necho \"=== Searching for struct definitions with bounds ===\"\nrg \"struct\\s+\\w+<\\w+\\s*:\" libs/ --type rust -C 1 | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1685\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# More importantly: does the ui/domain_model_valid.rs test actually get compiled and run?\necho \"=== Checking if domain_model_valid.rs would compile the generated code ===\"\nhead -5 libs/modkit/tests/ui/domain_model_valid.rs\necho \"---\"\necho \"This test uses trybuild's .pass() which means it compiles and verifies it works\"\necho \"But there's NO generic struct in this test\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 420\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Final verification: can we find any documentation or TODOs about generic handling?\necho \"=== Searching for TODOs or comments about generics ===\"\nrg -i \"todo|fixme|generic\" libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 437\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Field assertions for generic types will fail to compile due to out-of-scope type parameters.**\n\nFor a generic struct like `Container<T>`, the generated validation function references `T` without declaring it as a generic parameter:\n\n```rust\nfn __validate_domain_model_fields() {\n    __assert_field_is_domain_safe::<T>();  // Error: T is not in scope\n}\n```\n\nThis causes compilation to fail whenever `#[domain_model]` is applied to a generic struct. The fix is to propagate generic parameters and where clauses to the validation function:\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed fix to handle generic types</summary>\n\n```diff\n     // Build the compile-time field validation\n     let field_assertions = if field_types.is_empty() {\n         quote! {}\n     } else {\n+        let (_, ty_generics, where_clause) = input.generics.split_for_impl();\n         quote! {\n             const _: () = {\n                 #[allow(dead_code)]\n                 fn __assert_field_is_domain_safe<T: ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe>() {}\n \n                 #[allow(dead_code)]\n-                fn __validate_domain_model_fields() {\n+                fn __validate_domain_model_fields `#ty_generics` () `#where_clause` {\n                     #(\n                         __assert_field_is_domain_safe::<#field_types>();\n                     )*\n                 }\n             };\n         }\n     };\n```\n</details>\n\nAdd a test case with a generic struct to verify the fix works:\n\n```rust\n#[test]\nfn test_expand_generic_struct_with_bounds() {\n    let input: DeriveInput = parse_quote! {\n        pub struct Container<T: ::modkit::domain::DomainSafe> {\n            pub value: T,\n        }\n    };\n    let output = expand_domain_model(&input);\n    let output_str = output.to_string();\n    assert!(output_str.contains(\"DomainSafe\"));\n}\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs` around lines 46 - 63, The generated\nfield assertions currently reference type parameters out of scope; update the\nfield_assertions generation so the helper validation function includes the\noriginal item's generic parameters and where-clauses (i.e., propagate generics\nand where predicates) so generic types compile; modify the quoted block that\ndefines __validate_domain_model_fields (and keeps __assert_field_is_domain_safe\nand uses #(`#field_types`)*) to declare the same generics and where-clause as the\ninput (so T and bounds are in scope), and add the suggested unit test for a\ngeneric struct to verify DomainSafe bounds are preserved.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 47fb289","created_at":"2026-01-29T08:42:53Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T14:08:30Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740547256","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740547256"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740547256"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740547256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":46,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":63,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":63,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740547261","pull_request_review_id":3721386173,"id":2740547261,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jWW69","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,200 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainSafe` and `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Verify at compile-time that all fields are also `DomainSafe`\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain-safe types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!     \n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+\n+use std::collections::{BTreeMap, BTreeSet, HashMap, HashSet};\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+/// Marker trait for types that are safe to use in the domain layer.\n+///\n+/// Types implementing this trait are guaranteed to be free of infrastructure\n+/// dependencies such as:\n+/// - Database types (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`)\n+/// - HTTP types (http, axum, hyper)\n+/// - Framework-specific types\n+///\n+/// # Implementing\n+///\n+/// Do NOT implement this trait manually. Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro\n+/// which performs compile-time validation that all fields are also `DomainSafe`.\n+///\n+/// # Blanket Implementations\n+///\n+/// Common standard library and third-party types have blanket implementations:\n+/// - Primitives: `bool`, `i8`..`i128`, `u8`..`u128`, `f32`, `f64`, `char`, `String`, `&str`\n+/// - Collections: `Vec<T>`, `Option<T>`, `Result<T, E>`, `HashMap<K, V>`, etc.\n+/// - Common crates: `uuid::Uuid`, `chrono::DateTime`, `rust_decimal::Decimal`","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"a634384a3b43f6964ec935caf04f7444fac03412","original_commit_id":"a634384a3b43f6964ec935caf04f7444fac03412","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscript