>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs` around lines 54 - 59, The docblock claims\nblanket implementations for chrono::DateTime and rust_decimal::Decimal but those\nimpls are missing; either add the missing impls or remove them from the\ndocumentation. Fix by locating the blanket-impl module in mod.rs (the \"Blanket\nImplementations\" section) and either (A) add the corresponding impl blocks for\nchrono::DateTime<Tz> and rust_decimal::Decimal matching the pattern used for\nuuid::Uuid (implement the same trait(s)/From/Into/Serialize/Deserialize or the\nproject's custom trait names used elsewhere), or (B) if you don’t intend to\nsupport them, remove the chrono::DateTime and rust_decimal::Decimal lines from\nthe doc comment so the list only contains actually implemented types like\nuuid::Uuid; ensure the identifiers chrono::DateTime and rust_decimal::Decimal\nare referenced exactly when adding impls so reviewers can find them.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit d2ca80a","created_at":"2026-01-29T08:42:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T08:50:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740547261","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740547261"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740547261"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740547261/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":54,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":59,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":59,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740602650","pull_request_review_id":3721452163,"id":2740602650,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jWkca","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainSafe` and `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Verify at compile-time that all fields are also `DomainSafe`\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain-safe types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!     \n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"d2ca80a6fd91a4672c0be9ba5ac53622dcfc1806","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# First, locate the file and view its full content\nfd -a \"mod.rs\" libs/modkit/src/domain\nwc -l libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs\ncat -n libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 8443\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if ModKit unified system README exists\nfd -a \"README.md\" docs/modkit_unified_system 2>/dev/null || echo \"Not found at docs/modkit_unified_system\"\n# Try alternative locations\nfd -a \"README.md\" docs/ | grep -i modkit || echo \"No modkit readme found\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 175\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for HashMap/HashSet DomainSafe implementations\nrg \"impl.*DomainSafe.*HashMap|impl.*DomainSafe.*HashSet\" libs/modkit/src/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 299\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Read ModKit unified system README\nhead -100 /home/jailuser/git/docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3446\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for chrono examples in documentation\nrg \"DateTime<Utc>\" docs/ -A 2 -B 2 | head -40\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3219\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are guidelines about fully qualified chrono types\nrg \"chrono::\" docs/ -A 1 -B 1 | head -30\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1746\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Consider adding domain marker trait design to ModKit documentation, or confirm its architectural independence.**\n\nThis module introduces `DomainSafe`, `DomainModel`, and `DomainErrorMarker` as core infrastructure. The ModKit unified system documentation exists but does not currently document expected patterns for domain marker traits. Either add guidance to `docs/modkit_unified_system/` (perhaps a new section in `01_overview.md` or `05_errors_rfc9457.md`), or document why domain markers operate independently from ModKit's core invariants (SDK pattern, ClientHub, lifecycle, etc.).\n\nAdditionally, the `HashMap` and `HashSet` implementations accept `S: std::hash::BuildHasher` without requiring `S: DomainSafe`, which allows custom hashers with infrastructure dependencies to bypass the domain safety guarantee. Constrain these with `S: DomainSafe`:\n\n```rust\nimpl<K: DomainSafe, V: DomainSafe, S: DomainSafe + std::hash::BuildHasher> DomainSafe for HashMap<K, V, S> {}\nimpl<T: DomainSafe, S: DomainSafe + std::hash::BuildHasher> DomainSafe for HashSet<T, S> {}\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs` around lines 1 - 37, Document or justify the\nDomain marker traits (DomainSafe, DomainModel, DomainErrorMarker) in the ModKit\ndocs by adding a short section to the modkit_unified_system docs (e.g.,\n01_overview.md or 05_errors_rfc9457.md) explaining their intended architectural\nindependence or how they integrate with SDK/ClientHub/lifecycle patterns; and\ntighten the DomainSafe impls for collection types by requiring the hasher type\nparameter to also be DomainSafe so custom hashers cannot introduce infra\ndeps—update the HashMap and HashSet impl blocks (the impl for HashMap<K, V, S>\nand the impl for HashSet<T, S>) to add S: DomainSafe alongside\nstd::hash::BuildHasher.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-29T08:58:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T08:58:10Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740602650","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740602650"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2740602650"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740602650/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":49,"original_line":37,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":37,"position":49,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740602661","pull_request_review_id":3721452163,"id":2740602661,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jWkcl","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,202 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"d2ca80a6fd91a4672c0be9ba5ac53622dcfc1806","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if the file exists and verify the content at lines 11-19\ncat -n libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs | sed -n '1,25p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 967\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for other documentation examples using DateTime or chrono types\nrg -A 5 -B 2 \"DateTime\" libs/modkit/src --type rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 90\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for documentation examples with DateTime or chrono patterns\nrg \"DateTime|chrono::\" libs/modkit/src --type-add 'rust:*.rs' -A 3 -B 1 | head