tusCode\",\n    \"Request\",\n    \"Response\",\n    \"HeaderMap\",\n    \"Method\",\n]\n\n# Check if T matches any forbidden pattern\nmatches_pattern = any(pattern in path_str or path_str.startswith(pattern) for pattern in FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS)\nprint(f\"path_str = '{path_str}'\")\nprint(f\"Matches forbidden pattern? {matches_pattern}\")\n\n# Check if T matches any forbidden type name\nmatches_name = path_str in FORBIDDEN_TYPE_NAMES\nprint(f\"Matches forbidden type name? {matches_name}\")\n\nprint(\"\\nConclusion: Bare generic parameter 'T' passes validation\")\nprint(\"Result: struct Wrapper<T> { inner: T } is allowed by macro\")\nprint(\"But Wrapper<sqlx::PgPool> can be instantiated at the call site!\")\nEOF\npython /tmp/analyze_generic.py\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 327\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Double-check: look for any existing validation of generic params in expand_domain_model\nrg -B 5 -A 5 \"generics\\|type_param\" libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify: does the current macro expansion allow instantiation with infra types?\n# Check the generated impl - it uses split_for_impl which is the standard way\ncat -n libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs | sed -n '68,96p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1437\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for any other validation of generic params elsewhere in the macro system\nrg -n \"type_param\\|generic\" libs/modkit-macros/src/ --type=rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there's any documentation about expected generic param behavior\nrg -B 5 -A 5 \"generic\\|type parameter\" libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check what FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS actually contains to understand the scope\ncat -n libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs | sed -n '12,56p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1624\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look for any integration tests or real-world usage with generics\nfind ./libs -name \"*.rs\" -path \"*/tests/*\" -o -path \"*/src/*\" | xargs grep -l \"#\\[domain_model\\].*<\" | head -5\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1033\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Final verification: check if there's any bound-checking infrastructure we missed\nrg -n \"DomainModel\\|DomainSafe\" libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Confirm the generated impl has no bounds on T\ncat -n libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs | sed -n '90,96p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 371\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# One more check: see if there's anywhere that validates struct definition params\nrg -B 10 -A 10 \"input.generics\" libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1126\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Bare generic type parameters can bypass infra-type validation.**\n\n`#[domain_model] struct Wrapper<T> { inner: T }` passes validation because the macro doesn't check struct-level generic parameters. Since `DomainModel` is implemented unconditionally for all `T`, `Wrapper<sqlx::PgPool>` compiles, undermining boundary enforcement.\n\nAdd validation to track and reject bare generic parameters unless explicitly bounded to `DomainModel` or `DomainSafe`. Include a UI test verifying that `struct Wrapper<T>` with an infra type is rejected at compile time.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested enforcement approach</summary>\n\nTrack generic parameters during macro expansion and reject unbound type parameters in fields. Add bounds check before generating the impl blocks.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-macros/src/domain_model.rs` around lines 175 - 259, The macro\ncurrently misses validation for bare struct generic parameters, allowing\npatterns like struct Wrapper<T>{inner:T} and then impl DomainModel for\nWrapper<T> to accept infra types; update the macro expansion to collect generic\ntype parameters from the struct (e.g., from the TypeGenerics / Generics on the\ninput) and treat unbounded TypeParam idents as forbidden when they appear as\nfield types unless the param has a bound like DomainModel or DomainSafe; modify\nor extend validate_field_type/validate_type_path to detect syn::Type::Path\npointing to a single-segment Ident that matches one of the struct's generic\nparams and then emit a syn::Error requiring an explicit DomainModel/DomainSafe\nbound, and add a compile-fail UI test that defines struct Wrapper<T>{ inner: T }\nand attempts Wrapper<sqlx::PgPool> to ensure the macro rejects it at compile\ntime.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T17:01:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T17:01:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2755353365","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2755353365"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2755353365"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2755353365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":161,"original_start_line":175,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":253,"original_line":259,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":259,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2755353370","pull_request_review_id":3740766395,"id":2755353370,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kO1sa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Validate at macro-expansion time that all fields are free of infrastructure types\n+//! - Generate clear error messages if forbidden types are detected\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!\n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! # Validation Strategy\n+//!\n+//! The `#[domain_model]` macro performs validation by checking field type names against\n+//! a list of forbidden patterns (e.g., `sqlx::`, `http::`, `sea_orm::`). This provides\n+//! clear error messages at macro expansion time, similar to how `#[api_dto]` validates\n+//! its arguments.\n+//!\n+//! Additional enforcement is provided by Dylint lints:\n+//! - `DE0301`: Prohibits infrastructure imports in domain layer\n+//! - `DE0308`: Prohibits HTTP types in domain layer\n+\n+// Re-export uuid for use in domain models\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","original_commit_id":"dbce7ec4cd3d467293062543a2330fcdb0613496","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs | sed -n '45,55p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 502\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for imports of Uuid from the domain module\nrg \"domain::Uuid|from.*domain.*import.*Uuid\" --type rust -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Also check if Uuid is used in other domain files\nrg \"use.*uuid::Uuid|pub use.*uuid::Uuid\" libs/modkit/src/domain/ --type rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 109\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check what this mod.rs file exports and its structure\nrg \"pub use|pub mod|pub struct|pub trait\" libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs -A 1\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 360\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add `pub` to make the import a true re-export as the comment states.**\n\nThe comment explicitly says \"Re-export uuid for use in domain models,\" but the code only imports it privately (`use uuid::Uuid;`). To match the stated intent and allow domain models to reference `domain::Uuid`, change it to a public re-export.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n // Re-export uuid for use in domain models\n-use uuid::Uuid;\n+pub use uuid::Uuid;\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n// Re-export uuid for use in domain models\npub use uuid::Uuid;\n\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs` around lines 50 - 52, The current import \"use\nuuid::Uuid\" is private but the comment says it should be re-exported; change it\nto a public re-export by replacing the private import with \"pub use uuid::Uuid\"\nso other modules can refer to domain::Uuid (locate this in mod.rs where Uuid is\nimported).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-02T17:01:01Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T17:01:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2755353370","pu