lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs | sed -n '190,220p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1247\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check how is_in_contract_module_ast is used elsewhere in the codebase\nrg -n \"is_in_contract_module_ast\" -B 2 -A 2 -g '*.rs' | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1524\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Exclude contract modules to comply with coding guidelines.**\n\nThe lint is missing a contract-module check required by the coding guidelines. Currently only `is_in_domain_path` gates the lint, so contract modules will be incorrectly flagged. Add the `is_in_contract_module_ast` guard to skip them.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Suggested guard</summary>\n\n```diff\n-use lint_utils::{is_in_domain_path, use_tree_to_strings};\n+use lint_utils::{is_in_contract_module_ast, is_in_domain_path, use_tree_to_strings};\n\n ...\n-        if !is_in_domain_path(cx.sess().source_map(), item.span) {\n+        if !is_in_domain_path(cx.sess().source_map(), item.span)\n+            || is_in_contract_module_ast(cx, item)\n+        {\n             return;\n         }\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAs per coding guidelines: \"Use `is_in_contract_module_ast()` helper from `lint_utils` crate to check if an AST item is in a contract/ directory\".\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs` around\nlines 200 - 205, The lint currently only checks is_in_domain_path in\nDe0308NoHttpInDomain::check_item and thus flags contract modules; update\ncheck_item to early-return when the AST item is in a contract module by calling\nlint_utils::is_in_contract_module_ast (e.g., if\nis_in_contract_module_ast(cx.sess().source_map(), item.span) { return; }) before\nperforming the domain-path check so contract/ items are skipped.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit cec5300","created_at":"2026-02-02T19:22:21Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T19:27:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2755864575","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2755864575"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2755864575"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2755864575/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":205,"original_start_line":200,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":213,"original_line":205,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":205,"position":213,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756134863","pull_request_review_id":3741708995,"id":2756134863,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kR0fP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Validate at macro-expansion time that all fields are free of infrastructure types\n+//! - Generate clear error messages if forbidden types are detected\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!\n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! # Validation Strategy\n+//!\n+//! The `#[domain_model]` macro performs validation by checking field type names against\n+//! a list of forbidden patterns (e.g., `sqlx::`, `http::`, `sea_orm::`). This provides\n+//! clear error messages at macro expansion time, similar to how `#[api_dto]` validates\n+//! its arguments.\n+//!\n+//! Additional enforcement is provided by Dylint lints:\n+//! - `DE0301`: Prohibits infrastructure imports in domain layer\n+//! - `DE0308`: Prohibits HTTP types in domain layer\n+\n+// Re-export uuid for use in domain models\n+use uuid::Uuid;","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","original_commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this is not a re-export, it's not public","created_at":"2026-02-02T21:11:18Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:41:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756134863","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756134863"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756134863"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756134863/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":51,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":51,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756135895","pull_request_review_id":3741708995,"id":2756135895,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kR0vX","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Validate at macro-expansion time that all fields are free of infrastructure types\n+//! - Generate clear error messages if forbidden types are detected\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!\n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! # Validation Strategy\n+//!\n+//! The `#[domain_model]` macro performs validation by checking field type names against\n+//! a list of forbidden patterns (e.g., `sqlx::`, `http::`, `sea_orm::`). This provides\n+//! clear error messages at macro expansion time, similar to how `#[api_dto]` validates\n+//! its arguments.\n+//!\n+//! Additional enforcement is provided by Dylint lints:\n+//! - `DE0301`: Prohibits infrastructure imports in domain layer\n+//! - `DE0308`: Prohibits HTTP types in domain layer\n+\n+// Re-export uuid for use in domain models\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+/// Marker trait for domain models (business entities).\n+///\n+/// Domain models represent core business concepts and should:\n+/// - Contain only business-relevant data\n+/// - Be independent of persistence mechanisms\n+/// - Be free of infrastructure dependencies\n+///\n+/// # Usage\n+///\n+/// Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to implement this trait:\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// #[domain_model]\n+/// pub struct Order {\n+///     pub id: Uuid,\n+///     pub customer_id: Uuid,\n+///     pub total: Decimal,\n+///     pub status: OrderStatus,\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+///\n+/// The macro validates field types at expansion time and generates clear error\n+/// messages if forbidden types (e.g., `sqlx::PgPool`, `http::StatusCode`) are detected.\n+///\n+/// # Thread Safety\n+///\n+/// This trait does not require `Send + Sync`. If you need thread-safe domain models,\n+/// wrap them in `Arc<T>` at the point of use.\n+pub trait DomainModel {}\n+\n+/// Internal marker trait (deprecated).\n+///\n+/// This trait is kept for backward compatibility but should not be used directly.\n+/// Use `DomainModel` instead.\n+#[doc(hidden)]\n+#[deprecated(since = \"0.1.6\", note = \"Use DomainModel instead\")]","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","original_commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"remove it completely, it was not even merged","created_at":"2026-02-02T21:11:45Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:41:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756135895","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756135895"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756135895"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756135895/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":88,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":88,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756137375","pull_request_review_id":3741708995,"id":2756137375,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kR1Gf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,126 @@\n+//! Domain Layer Marker Traits\n+//!\n+//! This module provides marker traits for enforcing domain-driven design boundaries\n+//! at compile time. Types marked with these traits are guaranteed to be free of\n+//! infrastructure dependencies (`sqlx`, `sea_orm`, `http`, `axum`, etc.).\n+//!\n+//! # Usage\n+//!\n+//! Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to mark domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! use modkit_macros::domain_model;\n+//!\n+//! #[domain_model]\n+//! pub struct User {\n+//!     pub id: Uuid,\n+//!     pub email: String,\n+//!     pub created_at: DateTime<Utc>,\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! The macro will:\n+//! - Implement `DomainModel` for the type\n+//! - Validate at macro-expansion time that all fields are free of infrastructure types\n+//! - Generate clear error messages if forbidden types are detected\n+//!\n+//! # Enforcement\n+//!\n+//! Domain services can use trait bounds to ensure they only work with domain types:\n+//!\n+//! ```rust,ignore\n+//! pub trait UserRepository: Send + Sync {\n+//!     type Model: DomainModel;\n+//!\n+//!     async fn find(&self, id: Uuid) -> Result<Option<Self::Model>>;\n+//! }\n+//! ```\n+//!\n+//! # Validation Strategy\n+//!\n+//! The `#[domain_model]` macro performs validation by checking field type names against\n+//! a list of forbidden patterns (e.g., `sqlx::`, `http::`, `sea_orm::`). This provides\n+//! clear error messages at macro expansion time, similar to how `#[api_dto]` validates\n+//! its arguments.\n+//!\n+//! Additional enforcement is provided by Dylint lints:\n+//! - `DE0301`: Prohibits infrastructure imports in domain layer\n+//! - `DE0308`: Prohibits HTTP types in domain layer\n+\n+// Re-export uuid for use in domain models\n+use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+/// Marker trait for domain models (business entities).\n+///\n+/// Domain models represent core business concepts and should:\n+/// - Contain only business-relevant data\n+/// - Be independent of persistence mechanisms\n+/// - Be free of infrastructure dependencies\n+///\n+/// # Usage\n+///\n+/// Use the `#[domain_model]` attribute macro to implement this trait:\n+///\n+/// ```rust,ignore\n+/// #[domain_model]\n+/// pub struct Order {\n+///     pub id: Uuid,\n+///     pub customer_id: Uuid,\n+///     pub total: Decimal,\n+///     pub status: OrderStatus,\n+/// }\n+/// ```\n+///\n+/// The macro validates field types at expansion time and generates clear error\n+/// messages if forbidden types (e.g., `sqlx::PgPool`, `http::StatusCode`) are detected.\n+///\n+/// # Thread Safety\n+///\n+/// This trait does not require `Send + Sync`. If you need thread-safe domain models,\n+/// wrap them in `Arc<T>` at the point of use.\n+pub trait DomainModel {}\n+\n+/// Internal marker trait (deprecated).\n+///\n+/// This trait is kept for backward compatibility but should not be used directly.\n+/// Use `DomainModel` instead.\n+#[doc(hidden)]\n+#[deprecated(since = \"0.1.6\", note = \"Use DomainModel instead\")]\n+pub trait DomainSafe {}\n+\n+/// Marker trait for domain errors.\n+///\n+/// Domain errors represent business rule violations and should not\n+/// contain infrastructure-specific error types.\n+pub trait DomainErrorMarker: std::error::Error + Send + Sync {}\n+\n+// =============================================================================\n+// Backward compatibility implementations for DomainSafe (deprecated)\n+// =============================================================================\n+\n+#[allow(deprecated)]\n+mod compat {","path":"libs/modkit/src/domain/mod.rs","commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","original_commit_id":"1a7988cf25d027b7bb84d79950dddb0d73e604d7","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"you can remove it, no need of these implements","created_at":"2026-02-02T21:12:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:41:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756137375","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756137375"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756137375"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756137375/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":n