ps://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"this modifications are incorrect","created_at":"2026-02-02T21:41:16Z","updated_at":"2026-02-02T21:41:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756205496","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756205496"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2756205496"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2756205496/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"file"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806836","pull_request_review_id":3743738397,"id":2757806836,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kYMr0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,255 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+\n+use lint_utils::{is_in_contract_module_ast, is_in_domain_path, use_tree_to_strings};\n+use rustc_ast::{Item, ItemKind, Ty, TyKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{EarlyContext, EarlyLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_early_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that domain modules do not reference HTTP types or status codes.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Domain modules should be transport-agnostic. HTTP is just one possible\n+    /// transport layer. Referencing HTTP types in domain code couples the business\n+    /// logic to a specific transport mechanism.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - HTTP types in domain\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use http::StatusCode;\n+    ///\n+    ///     pub fn check_result() -> StatusCode {\n+    ///         StatusCode::OK  // ❌ HTTP-specific\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - domain errors converted in API layer\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     pub enum DomainResult {\n+    ///         Success,\n+    ///         NotFound,\n+    ///         InvalidData,\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"domain modules should not reference HTTP types or status codes (DE0308)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// HTTP-related patterns forbidden in domain code\n+/// Only includes frameworks actually used in the project: axum, hyper, http\n+const HTTP_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"http\",\n+    \"axum\",\n+    \"hyper\",\n+];","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"db886828e584356ee5ed658949981916611c663c","original_commit_id":"e2e7dd7f22be7f7f45fe8a0450085ffd2f497a7c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**`starts_with` matching causes false positives on `http`-prefixed modules.**\n\nThe pattern `\"http\"` with `starts_with()` will incorrectly match internal modules or crates like `http_client`, `http_utils`, or `httpbin`. The check should ensure the match is either an exact crate name or followed by `::`.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n+/// Returns true if the path matches a forbidden HTTP pattern.\n+/// Matches exact crate name or crate::subpath (avoids matching http_client, etc.)\n+fn matches_http_pattern(path_str: &str) -> bool {\n+    for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n+        if path_str == *pattern || path_str.starts_with(&format!(\"{}::\", pattern)) {\n+            return true;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n fn check_use_item(cx: &EarlyContext<'_>, item: &Item, tree: &rustc_ast::UseTree) {\n     for path_str in use_tree_to_strings(tree) {\n-        for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS {\n-            if path_str.starts_with(pattern) {\n-                cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, item.span, |diag| {\n-                    diag.primary_message(\"domain module imports HTTP type (DE0308)\");\n-                    diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n-                });\n-                return;\n-            }\n+        if matches_http_pattern(&path_str) {\n+            cx.span_lint(DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN, item.span, |diag| {\n+                diag.primary_message(\"domain module imports HTTP type (DE0308)\");\n+                diag.help(\"domain should be transport-agnostic; handle HTTP in api/ layer\");\n+            });\n+            return;\n         }\n     }\n }\n```\n\nThen replace all other `for pattern in HTTP_PATTERNS { if path_str.starts_with(pattern) ... }` blocks with calls to `matches_http_pattern(&path_str)`.\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 84-85\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs` around\nlines 53 - 57, The current matching using HTTP_PATTERNS with starts_with causes\nfalse positives (e.g., \"http_client\"); implement a helper fn\nmatches_http_pattern(path: &str) -> bool that iterates HTTP_PATTERNS and returns\ntrue only if path == pattern or path.starts_with(&format!(\"{}::\", pattern));\nthen replace the existing starts_with checks (where code examines path_str\nagainst HTTP_PATTERNS) with calls to matches_http_pattern(&path_str) (also\nupdate the other occurrences noted around lines 84-85) so that only exact\ncrate/module names or those followed by \"::\" are matched.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit e8d0003","created_at":"2026-02-03T08:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T08:25:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2757806836","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806836"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2757806836"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806836/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":53,"original_start_line":53,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":57,"original_line":57,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":57,"position":57,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806842","pull_request_review_id":3743738397,"id":2757806842,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6kYMr6","diff_hunk":"@@ -8,8 +8,7 @@ use tracing::{debug, info};\n use crate::config::FileParserConfig;\n use crate::domain::service::{FileParserService, ServiceConfig};\n use crate::infra::parsers::{\n-    DocxParser, HtmlParser, ImageParser, PdfParser, PlainTextParser, PptxParser, StubParser,\n-    XlsxParser,\n+    DocxParser, HtmlParser, ImageParser, PdfParser, PlainTextParser, StubParser,\n };","path":"modules/file-parser/src/module.rs","commit_id":"ee431900a707660626da1a50e6d9c9de1295869e","original_commit_id":"e2e7dd7f22be7f7f45fe8a0450085ffd2f497a7c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if there are any references to XlsxParser or PptxParser usage in the codebase\necho \"=== Searching for XlsxParser/PptxParser references ===\"\nrg -n -C2 'XlsxParser|PptxParser' --type rust\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking if parser modules still exist ===\"\nfd -t f -e rs | xargs grep -l 'xlsx_parser\\|pptx_parser' 2>/dev/null || echo \"No module files found\"\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking for .xlsx or .pptx test fixtures ===\"\nfd -e xlsx -e pptx\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Checking current state of modules/file_parser/src/module.rs lines 50-65 ===\"\nsed -n '50,65p' modules/file_parser/src/module.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1317\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check if e2e tests reference the PPTX or XLSX fixtures\necho \"=== Searching for references to pptx test fixtures ===\"\nrg -n 'pptx' --type rust --type python --type yaml\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Searching for references to xlsx test fixtures ===\"\nrg -n 'xlsx' --type rust --type python --type yaml\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Listing e2e test files ===\"\nfd -e rs -e py -e yaml testing/e2e | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 635\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Fix the search for test files\necho \"=== Listing files in testing/e2e directory ===\"\nfind testing/e2e -type f 2>/dev/null | head -30\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Searching all file types for pptx/xlsx references ===\"\nrg -i 'pptx|xlsx' --no-types --max-count=20\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check if there's a parser.rs file that might reference these parsers ===\"\nfind . -name 'parser.rs' -o -name 'parsers.rs' 2>/dev/null | head -10\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Look at the struct definition to see what parsers should be available ===\"\nrg -n 'FileParserBackend' -A 10 --type rust | head -40\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 5492\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Found a critical test file - let's examine it\necho \"=== Content of test_file_parser_xlsx_pptx.py ===\"\ncat testing/e2e/modules/file_parser/test_file_parser_xlsx_pptx.py\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check if xlsx/pptx parser implementations exist ===\"\nfind . -name '*xlsx*' -o -name '*pptx*' | grep -v testdata | grep -v '.hypothesis'\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Check the infra/parsers directory structure ===\"\nls -la modules/file_parser/src/infra/parsers/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 8202\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**This change breaks XLSX and PPTX parsing tests — these parsers appear to have been entirely removed but comprehensive e2e tests still exist.**\n\nThe removal of `XlsxParser` and `PptxParser` eliminates support for Excel and PowerPoint files entirely. This creates a critical issue: the e2e test file `testing/e2e/modules/file_parser/test_file_parser_xlsx_pptx.py` contains six tests that validate XLSX/PPTX upload, parsing, and the info endpoint. These tests will fail because:\n- Parser implementations no longer exist (no xlsx_parser.rs or pptx_parser.rs in the parsers directory)\n- Parsers are not instantiated in the parsers vector (module.rs lines 56-63)\n- The info endpoint tests expect xlsx/pptx to be in supported_extensions\n\nEither restore the XLSX/PPTX parser implementations and re-register them in module.rs, or remove the corresponding e2e tests and fixtures. Verify which approach aligns with the PR intent.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/file_parser/src/module.rs` around lines 10 - 12, The XLSX and PPTX\nparser implementations were removed causing e2e failures; restore XlsxParser and\nPptxParser implementations (create xlsx_parser.rs and pptx_parser.rs matching\nother parsers) and re-register them in the parsers vector inside module.rs where\nother parsers (DocxParser, PdfParser, etc.) are instantiated, and ensure the\nmodule's supported_extensions list includes \"xlsx\" and \"pptx\"; alternatively, if\nthe PR intent is to drop XLSX/PPTX support, delete the corresponding tests and\nany references to XlsxParser/PptxParser from module.rs and supported_extensions\nso the code and tests remain consistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-02-03T08:17:00Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T08:17:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2757806842","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806842"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/253#discussion_r2757806842"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/253"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2757806842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":10,"original_start_line":10,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":13,"original_line":12,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":7,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2790460383","pull_request_review_id":3781821951,"id":2790460383,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6mUwvf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,92 @@\n+# DE0308: No HTTP in Domain\n+\n+### What it does\n+\n+Checks that domain modules do not r