modifications.\n\n## Changes\n\n|Cohort / File(s)|Summary|\n|---|---|\n|**Top-level guide** <br> `docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md`|New concise quickstart covering server start/stop commands (`make example`, `make quickstart`), server URL, health and OpenAPI endpoints, interactive docs, per-module quickstarts, troubleshooting, and further reading.|\n|**Module quickstart template** <br> `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`|Added required `QUICKSTART.md` guidance for REST-enabled modules: one-line description, interactive docs link, minimal curl examples, \"More Examples\" section, and a lightweight template referencing the central QUICKSTART_GUIDE.|\n|**File Parser module** <br> `modules/file_parser/QUICKSTART.md`|New quickstart documenting `/info`, `/parse-local`, `/parse-url`, `/upload`, and markdown parsing endpoints with curl examples and sample JSON outputs.|\n|**System modules** <br> `modules/system/nodes_registry/QUICKSTART.md`, `modules/system/tenant_resolver/QUICKSTART.md`, `modules/system/types-registry/QUICKSTART.md`|New quickstarts for Nodes Registry, Tenant Resolver, and Types Registry: overviews, links to interactive API docs, example curl commands for listing/retrieval, and sample JSON responses.|\n|**Subproject pointer** <br> `docs/DNA`|Added a subproject commit hash line (submodule pointer) with no functional changes.|\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n(Skipped — documentation-only changes; no runtime control-flow changes to visualize.)\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 2 (Simple) | ⏱️ ~12 minutes\n\n## Possibly related issues\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#356 — Adds overlapping comprehensive Quickstart and per-module QUICKSTART docs; likely duplicates or complements this PR's documentation additions.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- MikeFalcon77  \n- Artifizer\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hopped through folders, pen in paw,  \n> Quickstarts sprouted, tidy and raw.  \n> Curl and health checks, examples to see,  \n> Start the server, come hop with me! ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                           |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                           |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately summarizes the main change: adding comprehensive quickstart documentation for the HyperSpot server. It is clear, concise, and directly reflects the changeset content across all modified files. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | No functions found in the changed files to evaluate docstring coverage. Skipping docstring coverage check.                                                                                                            |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\nThanks for using [CodeRabbit](https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=oss&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=hypernetix/hyperspot&utm_content=251)! It's free for OSS, and your support helps us grow. If you like it, consider giving us a shout-out.\n\n<details>\n<summary>❤️ Share</summary>\n\n- [X](https://twitter.com/intent/tweet?text=I%20just%20used%20%40coderabbitai%20for%20