on covering server startup, API exploration, and troubleshooting\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n💡 <a href=\"/hypernetix/hyperspot/new/main/.github/instructions?filename=*.instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add Copilot custom instructions</a> for smarter, more guided reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn how to get started</a>.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/251#pullrequestreview-3666646302","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/251","author_association":"NONE","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/251#pullrequestreview-3666646302"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/251"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T16:55:53Z","commit_id":"b32cf10c21eff7840fa4fceab6aaed458bbc26c7"},{"id":3666650006,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7ajKOW","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md`:\n- Line 32: The bare URL on the \"**Interactive docs:**\" line should be formatted\nas either an angle-bracketed URL or a proper Markdown link; update the line in\nQUICKSTART_GUIDE.md (the \"**Interactive docs:**\" entry) to use either\n\"<http://127.0.0.1:8087/docs>\" or \"[Interactive\ndocs](http://127.0.0.1:8087/docs)\" so the link renders correctly.\n- Around line 66-68: Replace the placeholder URL in the curl example in\nQUICKSTART_GUIDE.md (the POST to /file-parser/v1/parse-url) with a real,\npublicly accessible PDF URL or add a concise note immediately above the example\ntelling users to replace \"https://example.com/document.pdf\" with a valid PDF\nURL; ensure the example command remains runnable and mention that the URL must\npoint to a downloadable PDF.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`130-131`: **Add error handling for NODE_ID extraction.**\n\nThe command assumes the API returns at least one node and that Python successfully parses the JSON. If the nodes list is empty or the request fails, the subsequent curl command will fail with a confusing error.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Proposed improvement with error handling</summary>\n\n```diff\n # Get node by ID\n-NODE_ID=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8087/nodes-registry/v1/nodes | python3 -c \"import sys,json; print(json.load(sys.stdin)[0]['id'])\")\n+NODE_ID=$(curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8087/nodes-registry/v1/nodes | python3 -c \"import sys,json; nodes=json.load(sys.stdin); print(nodes[0]['id']) if nodes else sys.exit('No nodes found')\")\n+if [ -z \"$NODE_ID\" ]; then\n+  echo \"Error: Could not retrieve NODE_ID. Ensure the server is running and has registered nodes.\"\n+  exit 1\n+fi\n curl -s \"http://127.0.0.1:8087/nodes-registry/v1/nodes/$NODE_ID\" | python3 -m json.tool\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`234-234`: **Add safety guidance for the pkill command.**\n\nThe `pkill -f` command matches against the full command line and will kill all processes matching the pattern. While appropriate for this use case, consider adding a note to help users verify what will be killed before executing the command.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested enhancement</summary>\n\n```diff\n+# Preview what will be killed (optional)\n+pgrep -f hyperspot-server\n+\n+# Stop the server\n pkill -f hyperspot-server\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between ed0d1dad6e96cecd9d3d12824003d1fddd755bab and b32cf10c21eff7840fa4fceab6aaed458bbc26c7.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md</summary>\n\n32-32: Bare URL used\n\n(MD034, no-bare-urls)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>docs/QUICKSTART_GUIDE.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-11`: **No action required.** The file `config/quickstart.yaml` exists in the repository at the path referenced in the documentation, so the command on lines 9-11 is correct and will function as documented.\n\n\n> Likely an incorrect or invalid review comment.\n\n---\n\n`251-2