omment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None#diff-bW9kdWxlcy9zeXN0ZW0vZ3JwY19odWIvc3JjL21vZHVsZS5ycw==) | 50.00% | [1 Missing :warning: ](https://app.codecov.io/gh/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/249?src=pr&el=tree&utm_medium=referral&utm_source=github&utm_content=comment&utm_campaign=pr+comments&utm_term=None) |\n\n:loudspeaker: Thoughts on this report? [Let us know!](https://github.com/codecov/feedback/issues/255)","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3754926842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[],"source_reviews":[{"id":3665697645,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7afhtt","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 0**\n\n> [!CAUTION]\n> Some comments are outside the diff and can’t be posted inline due to platform limitations.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>⚠️ Outside diff range comments (8)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `10-10`: **Doc comment references outdated API name.**\n> \n> The doc comment on line 10 still references `TypesRegistryApi` but the re-export on line 18 is `TypesRegistryClient`. Update for consistency.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -//! - **`ClientHub` registration**: Other modules access via `hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?`\n> +//! - **`ClientHub` registration**: Other modules access via `hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?`\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-17`: **Documentation references outdated trait name.**\n> \n> The module doc comment on line 1 and the code example on line 15 still reference `TypesRegistryApi` instead of `TypesRegistryClient`. This creates an inconsistency with the renamed trait.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -//! `TypesRegistryApi` trait definition.\n> +//! `TypesRegistryClient` trait definition.\n>  //!\n>  //! This trait defines the public API for the `types-registry` module.\n>  //! GTS schemas and instances are global resources, so no security context is required.\n> \n>  use async_trait::async_trait;\n> \n>  use crate::error::TypesRegistryError;\n>  use crate::models::{GtsEntity, ListQuery, RegisterResult};\n> \n>  /// Public API trait for the `types-registry` module.\n>  ///\n>  /// This trait can be consumed by other modules via `ClientHub`:\n>  /// ```ignore\n> -/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n> +/// let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n>  /// let entity = client.get(\"gts.acme.core.events.user_created.v1~\").await?;\n>  /// ```\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-27`: **Update documentation to reflect the new trait name.**\n> \n> The doc comment still references the old name `TypesRegistryApi` on lines 4, 13, and 16, while the actual export is now `TypesRegistryClient`. This inconsistency could confuse consumers of the SDK.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested documentation fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  //! Types Registry SDK\n>  //!\n>  //! This crate provides the public API for the `types-registry` module:\n> -//! - `TypesRegistryApi` trait for inter-module communication\n> +//! - `TypesRegistryClient` trait for inter-module communication\n>  //! - `GtsEntity` model representing registered GTS entities\n>  //! - `ListQuery` for filtering entity listings\n>  //! - `TypesRegistryError` for error handling\n>  //!\n>  //! ## Usage\n>  //!\n>  //! Consumers obtain the client from `ClientHub`:\n>  //! ```ignore\n> -//! use types_registry_sdk::TypesRegistryApi;\n> +//! use types_registry_sdk::TypesRegistryClient;\n>  //!\n>  //! // Get the client from ClientHub\n> -//! let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryApi>()?;\n> +//! let client = hub.get::<dyn TypesRegistryClient>()?;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `553-570`: **Inconsistent renaming: import updated but parameter types still reference `DirectoryApi`.**\n> \n> Line 553 correctly imports `DirectoryClient`, but the function signatures on lines 557 and 566 still use `&dyn DirectoryApi` as parameter types. This creates an inconsistency that would cause compilation errors.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  // my_module-sdk/src/wiring.rs\n>  use std::sync::Arc;\n>  use anyhow::Result;\n>  use modkit::client_hub::ClientHub;\n>  use module_orchestrator_sdk::DirectoryClient;\n>  use crate::{MyModuleApi, MyModuleGrpcClient, SERVICE_NAME};\n> \n>  /// Wire the gRPC client into ClientHub\n> -pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryApi) -> Result<()> {\n> +pub async fn wire_client(hub: &ClientHub, resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<()> {\n>      let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;\n>      let client = MyModuleGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;\n>      hub.register::<dyn MyModuleApi>(Arc::new(client));\n>      tracing::info!(service = SERVICE_NAME, \"client wired into ClientHub\");\n>      Ok(())\n>  }\n> \n>  /// Build client directly (without registering in hub)\n> -pub async fn build_client(resolver: &dyn DirectoryApi) -> Result<Arc<dyn MyModuleApi>> {\n> +pub async fn build_client(resolver: &dyn DirectoryClient) -> Result<Arc<dyn MyModuleApi>> {\n>      let endpoint = resolver.resolve_grpc_service(SERVICE_NAME).await?;\n>      let client = MyModuleGrpcClient::connect(&endpoint.uri).await?;\n>      Ok(Arc::new(client))\n>  }\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> \n> `579-589`: **Consumer example still references `DirectoryApi`.**\n> \n> The usage example on line 580 should use `DirectoryClient` to match the updated import.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  // Consumer module\n>  use my_module_sdk::{MyModuleApi, wire_client};\n> \n>  async fn init(&self, ctx: &ModuleCtx) -> Result<()> {\n> -    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n> +    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n> \n>      // Wire the client into ClientHub\n>      wire_client(ctx.client_hub(), directory.as_ref()).await?;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> \n> `1457-1480`: **Documentation still references `DirectoryApi` in the Typed ClientHub section.**\n> \n> Lines 1461 and 1479 mention `DirectoryApi` for remote client resolution. These should be updated to `DirectoryClient` for consistency with the renaming.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  ## Typed ClientHub\n>  \n>  The **ClientHub** provides type-safe client resolution for inter-module communication. It supports both in-process and\n>  remote clients:\n>  \n>  * **In-process clients** — direct function calls within the same process\n> -* **Remote clients** — gRPC clients for OoP modules (resolved via DirectoryApi)\n> +* **Remote clients** — gRPC clients for OoP modules (resolved via DirectoryClient)\n>  * **Scoped clients** — multiple implementations of the same interface keyed by scope (for plugins)\n> ```\n> \n> And in the table on line 1479:\n> \n> ```diff\n> -| Registration | `expose_*_client()`     | DirectoryApi + gRPC client |\n> +| Registration | `expose_*_client()`     | DirectoryClient + gRPC client |\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/domain/local_client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `1-1`: **Doc comments reference outdated trait name `TypesRegistryApi`.**\n> \n> The module-level doc comment (line 1) and struct doc comment (lines 13-15) still reference `TypesRegistryApi`, but the trait has been renamed to `TypesRegistryClient`.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -//! Local client implementing the `TypesRegistryApi` trait.\n> +//! Local client implementing the `TypesRegistryClient` trait.\n> ```\n> \n> ```diff\n>  /// Local client for the Types Registry module.\n>  ///\n> -/// This client implements the `TypesRegistryApi` trait and delegates\n> +/// This client implements the `TypesRegistryClient` trait and delegates\n>  /// to the domain service. It is registered in the `ClientHub` for\n>  /// inter-module communication.\n>  pub struct TypesRegistryLocalClient {\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> Also applies to: 12-16\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `2238-2248`: **Inconsistent reference: `DirectoryApi` should be `DirectoryClient`.**\n> \n> Line 2244 still references `DirectoryApi` in the example code:\n> \n> ```rust\n> let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n> ```\n> \n> This should be updated to `DirectoryClient` to align with the PR's renaming objective.\n> \n> \n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n> -    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryApi>()?;\n> +    let directory = ctx.client_hub().get::<dyn DirectoryClient>()?;\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/types-registry/types-registry/src/infra/storage/in_memory_repo.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`288-289`: **Good refactor for test maintainability.**\n\nThis constant is also defined in `handlers.rs` tests (Line 91). If more test files need this value, consider extracting it to a shared test utilities module (e.g., `#[cfg(test)] mod test_constants`) to avoid duplication. For now, the current approach is acceptable.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/wiring.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`22-28`: **Nitpick: Consider updating the variable name in the doc example for consistency.**\n\nThe example at line 26 still uses `directory_api` as the variable name. For consistency with the `DirectoryClient` rename, consider updating it to `directory_client`.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested change</summary>\n\n```diff\n /// # Example\n /// ```ignore\n /// use calculator_sdk::{wire_client, CalculatorClient};\n ///\n-/// wire_client(&hub, &directory_api).await?;\n+/// wire_client(&hub, &directory_client).await?;\n /// let client = hub.get::<dyn CalculatorClient>()?;\n /// ```\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/src/infra/audit/http_audit_client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-15`: **Consider the naming inconsistency between struct name and documentation.**\n\nThe documentation now suggests HTTPS URLs, but the struct is named `HttpAuditClient`. While this is a minor inconsistency, it might cause confusion about whether the client specifically supports HTTP or HTTPS. Consider either:\n- Renaming to `HttpsAuditClient` if HTTPS is the expected protocol\n- Keeping the name generic (e.g., `AuditClient`) since the URL scheme is determined by the caller\n- Updating documentation to clarify that both HTTP and HTTPS are supported\n\nNote that the code doesn't validate the URL scheme, so both protocols would work regardless of the name.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 5eb9825aee0c7cc3bcdde27897b7b393ad483918 and 6f3b9a62d1bf0b1e3343f8fb0f947e7ca1543915.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (45)</summary>\n\n* `apps/hyperspot-server/src/main.rs`\n* `docs/MODKIT_PLUGINS.md`\n* `docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`\n* `examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/src/infra/audit/http_audit_client.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/wiring.rs`\n* `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/plugins/contoso_tr_plugin/src/module.rs`\n* `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/plugins/fabrikam_tr_plugin/src/module.rs`\n* `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-gw/src/domain/service.rs`\n* `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-gw/src/module.rs`\n* `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`\n* `libs/modkit-db/memdb`\n* `libs/modkit-macros/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/bootstrap/oop.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/client_hub.rs`\n* `libs/modkit/src/direct