src/lib.rs`, `examples/modkit/users_info/.../mod.rs` | `DummyPolicyEngine` renamed to `NoopPolicyEngine`; Default and PolicyEngine impls updated; re-exports and example initialization changed. |\n| **Replace SecurityCtx/Subject with SecurityContext** <br> `libs/modkit-security/src/security_ctx.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/src/subject.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/src/prelude.rs`, `examples/...` | Deleted legacy `SecurityCtx` and `Subject` modules/types; public prelude and re-exports updated to expose `SecurityContext` instead. |\n| **Auth middleware / extractor updates** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/lib.rs` | Replaced `SecurityCtx` with `SecurityContext` in extractor `Authz` and FromRequestParts; `AuthPolicyLayer::new` signature simplified (removed `ScopeBuilder` param); removed `pub mod scope_builder`. |\n| **Remove ScopeBuilder and impl** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/src/traits.rs`, `libs/modkit-auth/src/scope_builder.rs` | `ScopeBuilder` trait and `SimpleScopeBuilder` implementation removed; related imports and AccessScope usage trimmed. |\n| **Auth tests updated** <br> `libs/modkit-auth/tests/*`, `libs/modkit-auth/tests/middleware_integration_test.rs` | Tests updated to drop `ScopeBuilder` and use new `AuthPolicyLayer::new` signature; removed test helpers implementing `ScopeBuilder`. |\n| **DB secure module adjustments** <br> `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/mod.rs`, `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/db_ops.rs`, `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/tests.rs` | Public re-exports reduced to `AccessScope`; docs/examples updated to use `SecurityContext`; two unit tests referencing `SecurityCtx` removed. |\n| **API gateway auth updates** <br> `modules/system/api_gateway/src/auth.rs`, `modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs` | Removed `scope_builder` from `AuthState`; use `NoopPolicyEngine`; disabled-auth flow now builds/injects `SecurityContext`; AuthPolicyLayer initialization updated. |\n| **API gateway auth tests** <br> `modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs` | Tests migrated from `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext::builder()` and use prepared scope checks; handler signatures and assertions updated. |\n| **Security tests simplified** <br> `libs/modkit-security/tests/policy.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/tests/root_constants.rs` | Legacy `SecurityCtx` tests removed; root constants tests adjusted to assert `AccessScope` behavior directly. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#241 — Parallel migration replacing `SecurityCtx` with `SecurityContext` and updating imports/signatures across related crates.\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hopped through code at break of dawn,  \n> NoopPolicyEngine yawns and carries on.  \n> Old Scopes folded, Subjects gone astray,  \n> SecurityContext leads the way.  \n> A carrot cheers: clean changes made today!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                        |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'Drop SecurityCtx' directly and clearly summarizes the main objective of this changeset, which is to remove the deprecated SecurityCtx type and replace it with SecurityContext throughout the codebase. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                               |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3754182691/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cod