lone)]\npub struct Authz(pub SecurityContext);\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs` around lines 24 - 26, Update the doc\ncomment for the Authz struct to reference the current type name: replace\n\"Extractor for `SecurityCtx`\" with \"Extractor for `SecurityContext`\" (or similar\nwording) so the documentation matches the wrapped SecurityContext type and\nreflects that it validates auth middleware has run.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit adecd14","created_at":"2026-01-15T11:03:37Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T11:34:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#discussion_r2693942945","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2693942945"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#discussion_r2693942945"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2693942945/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":24,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":26,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":23,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2693942961","pull_request_review_id":3665078527,"id":2693942961,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gkk6x","diff_hunk":"@@ -14,35 +14,35 @@ use crate::secure::{AccessScope, ScopableEntity, Scoped, Unscoped};\n ///\n /// # Responsibilities\n ///\n-/// - Does **not** inspect the `SecurityCtx` or enforce tenant scoping rules.\n+/// - Does **not** inspect the `SecurityContext` or enforce tenant scoping rules.\n /// - Does **not** automatically populate any entity fields.\n /// - Callers are responsible for:\n ///   - Setting all required fields before calling.\n ///   - Validating that the operation is authorized within the current\n-///     `SecurityCtx` (e.g., verifying `tenant_id` or resource ownership).\n+///     `SecurityContext` (e.g., verifying `tenant_id` or resource ownership).\n ///\n /// # Behavior by Entity Type\n ///\n /// ## Tenant-scoped entities (have `tenant_col`)\n /// - Must have a valid, non-empty `tenant_id` set in the `ActiveModel` before insert.\n /// - The `tenant_id` should come from the request payload or be validated against\n-///   `SecurityCtx` by the service layer before calling this helper.\n+///   `SecurityContext` by the service layer before calling this helper.\n ///\n /// ## Global entities (no `tenant_col`)\n /// - May be inserted freely without tenant validation.\n /// - Typical examples include system-wide configuration or audit logs.\n ///\n /// # Recommended Field Population\n ///\n-/// When inserting entities, populate these fields from `SecurityCtx` in service code:\n+/// When inserting entities, populate these fields from `SecurityContext` in service code:\n /// - `tenant_id`: from payload or validated via `ctx.scope()`\n /// - `owner_id`: from `ctx.subject_id()`\n /// - `created_by`: from `ctx.subject_id()` if applicable\n ///\n /// # Example\n ///\n /// ```ignore\n-/// use modkit_db::secure::{secure_insert, SecurityCtx};\n+/// use modkit_db::secure::{secure_insert, SecurityContext};","path":"libs/modkit-db/src/secure/db_ops.rs","commit_id":"690abbe87aca49f5f6db509fc46436e5ff472a3d","original_commit_id":"7d639f1148157000398b1c1c256b38453b8accf2","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","