`\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `77-80`: **Outdated doc comment example.**\n> \n> The example in the doc comment still references `scope_builder` which was removed from the `AuthPolicyLayer::new` signature.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>  /// # Example\n>  /// ```ignore\n> -/// router = router.layer(AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, scope_builder, authorizer, policy));\n> +/// router = router.layer(AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, authorizer, policy));\n>  /// ```\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `91-94`: **Test assertion references removed field - test will fail.**\n> \n> The assertion checks `json[\"is_denied\"]` but this field was removed from the `test_handler` JSON response (lines 35-40). This will cause the test to fail since `json[\"is_denied\"]` will be `null`, not `false`.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>🐛 Proposed fix - remove the stale assertion</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>      assert_eq!(\n>          json[\"tenant_count\"], 1,\n>          \"Should have exactly one tenant (the default)\"\n>      );\n> -    assert_eq!(\n> -        json[\"is_denied\"], false,\n> -        \"Default tenant context should not be denied\"\n> -    );\n>      assert_eq!(\n>          json[\"subject_id\"],\n>          TEST_DEFAULT_SUBJECT_ID.to_string(),\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs`:\n- Around line 24-26: Update the doc comment for the Authz struct to reference\nthe current type name: replace \"Extractor for `SecurityCtx`\" with \"Extractor for\n`SecurityContext`\" (or similar wording) so the documentation matches the wrapped\nSecurityContext type and reflects that it validates auth middleware has run.\n\nIn `@libs/modkit-db/src/secure/db_ops.rs`:\n- Line 45: Doc example imports SecurityContext from modkit_db::secure but that\nmodule only re-exports AccessScope; update the example to import SecurityContext\nfrom modkit_security (e.g. use modkit_security::SecurityContext) or add a\nre-export in secure/mod.rs (pub use modkit_security::SecurityContext) so\nsecure_insert and SecurityContext resolve correctly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-17`: **Consider renaming `SecCtx*` exports for consistency.**\n\nThe `bin_codec` exports still use `SecCtx` naming (`SecCtxDecodeError`, `SecCtxEncodeError`, `SECCTX_BIN_VERSION`) while the rest of the codebase has migrated to `SecurityContext`. If these names are part of a stable binary protocol or public API, keeping them may be intentional for backward compatibility. Otherwise, consider renaming them to align with the new naming convention.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 2478dc56ba562d42ba31f9988db976022b4c9170 and 7d639f1148157000398b1c1c256b38453b8accf2.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (20)</summary>\n\n* `examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/src/domain/service/mod.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/lib.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/scope_builder.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/traits.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/tests/auth_integration.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/tests/middleware_integration_test.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/db_ops.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/mod.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/