/summary>\n\n* `is_empty` (30-32)\n* `tenant_ids` (17-19)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/context.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `builder` (18-20)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (9)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=pg)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (22)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/src/secure/db_ops.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`17-41`: **Documentation updates look correct.**\n\nThe references to `SecurityContext` in the documentation accurately reflect the new API naming convention. The explanations of field population and responsibilities are clear and helpful.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/prelude.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **Public API surface change looks correct.**\n\nThe prelude now exports `AccessScope` and `SecurityContext`, removing the deprecated `SecurityCtx` and `Subject`. This aligns with the PR's objective to migrate to the modern security context API.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/tests/root_constants.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-21`: **Tests correctly validate AccessScope semantics.**\n\nThe tests verify the deny-all default behavior and tenant scoping. The assertions are clear and cover the essential properties of `AccessScope`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/src/domain/service/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`139-139`: **Policy engine rename applied correctly.**\n\nThe change from `DummyPolicyEngine` to `NoopPolicyEngine` aligns with the PR's renaming convention. The instantiation pattern is correct.\n\nNote: This example hardcodes `NoopPolicyEngine`, which permits all operations. If this example is meant to demonstrate a production-like setup, consider documenting that a real application should inject a proper policy engine implementation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-db/src/secure/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`126-126`: **Re-export reduction is consistent with the API migration.**\n\nRemoving `SecurityCtx` and `Subject` from re-exports aligns with the broader deprecation. Only `AccessScope` is needed for the secure ORM operations exposed by this module.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/src/auth.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-9`: **LGTM! Import updates align with the security API migration.**\n\nThe imports correctly reflect the removal of `ScopeBuilder` and `SimpleScopeBuilder`, replacing them with `NoopPolicyEngine` and `PolicyEngineRef` from `modkit_security`. This is consistent with the PR objective.\n\n---\n\n`257-261`: **LGTM! NoopPolicyEngine correctly used as the default policy engine.**\n\nThe `AuthState` construction uses `NoopPolicyEngine` which always permits access. This is appropriate since actual authorization is performed by the `authorizer` component and route-level policy via `GatewayRoutePolicy`. This pattern is consistent with the usage in other modules (e.g., `examples/modkit/users_info/users_info/src/domain/service/mod.rs`).\n\n---\n\n`272-285`: **LGTM! NoopValidator is a well-documented defensive fallback.**\n\nThe `NoopValidator` intentionally panics to catch misconfiguration where `auth_with_policy` is accidentally wired while `auth_disabled=true`. The documentation at lines 153-164 clearly explains this design decision.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/policy_engine.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-23`: **LGTM! Clean rename from DummyPolicyEngine to NoopPolicyEngine.**\n\nThe rename to `NoopPolicyEngine` improves clarity - \"Noop\" (No-operation) is a standard naming convention that better conveys the intent of this implementation. The behavior remains unchanged: it always returns `true` for all policy checks.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-32`: **LGTM! Import updated to use SecurityContext.**\n\nThe import correctly switches from the deprecated `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext`, along with `PolicyEngineRef`.\n\n---\n\n`209-213`: **LGTM! SecurityContext builder pattern correctly used.**\n\nThe `SecurityContext::builder()` with explicit `tenant_id` and `subject_id` is a clean replacement for the previous `SecurityCtx` construction.\n\n---\n\n`235-237`: **LGTM! AuthPolicyLayer::new call updated to match new signature.**\n\nThe call correctly removes the `scope_builder` parameter, matching the updated `AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, authorizer, policy)` signature shown in `libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/tests/auth_integration.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`18-22`: **LGTM! Imports updated to reflect the security API migration.**\n\nThe imports correctly remove `ScopeBuilder` and switch to `SecurityContext` from `modkit_security`.\n\n---\n\n`113-122`: **LGTM! Test handler correctly uses SecurityContext.**\n\nThe handler now extracts `SecurityContext` via `axum::Extension<SecurityContext>` and properly checks for anonymous context using `Uuid::default()` comparison.\n\n---\n\n`125-135`: **LGTM! build_test_router updated with new AuthPolicyLayer signature.**\n\nThe function correctly constructs `AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, authorizer, policy)` without the removed `scope_builder` parameter.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/tests/middleware_integration_test.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-18`: **LGTM! Imports updated to reflect the removal of ScopeBuilder.**\n\nThe imports correctly include only `PrimaryAuthorizer` and `TokenValidator` traits, with `ScopeBuilder` removed.\n\n---\n\n`76-84`: **LGTM! create_app function updated with new AuthPolicyLayer signature.**\n\nThe function correctly constructs `AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, authorizer, policy)` without the `scope_builder` parameter.\n\n---\n\n`175-177`: **LGTM! Inline AuthPolicyLayer construction also updated.**\n\nThe inline layer construction in the optional auth test correctly uses the new three-parameter signature.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **LGTM on the rename from `DummyPolicyEngine` to `NoopPolicyEngine`.**\n\nThe naming is clearer and follows the common \"Noop\" pattern for no-operation implementations.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`178-186`: **LGTM on the SecurityContext builder usage.**\n\nThe migration correctly uses `SecurityContext::builder()` with the builder pattern to construct the context from validated claims.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`23-41`: **Migration to SecurityContext with scope preparation looks correct.**\n\nThe handler correctly extracts `Extension<SecurityContext>` and uses the new pattern to prepare the scope via `ctx.scope(Arc::new(NoopPolicyEngine)).prepare().await`. This aligns with the `scope` method signature in `libs/modkit-security/src/context.rs`.\n\n---\n\n`44-53`: **LGTM on the builder pattern usage.**\n\nThe middleware correctly uses `SecurityContext::builder().tenant_id(...).subject_id(...).build()` to construct the context, matching the builder API from the security module.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#pullrequestreview-3665078527","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#pullrequestreview-3665078527"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T11:03:37Z","commit_id":"7d639f1148157000398b1c1c256b38453b8accf2"},{"id":3665193156,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7admjE","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot