uote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `215-219`: **Inconsistent terminology in warning message.**\n> \n> The warning message references \"SecurityCtx\" but the code now uses `SecurityContext`. Update for consistency.\n> \n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n> \n> ```diff\n>             tracing::warn!(\n> -                \"API Gateway auth is DISABLED: all requests will run with default tenant SecurityCtx. \\\n> +                \"API Gateway auth is DISABLED: all requests will run with default tenant SecurityContext. \\\n>                  This mode bypasses authentication and is intended ONLY for single-user on-premises deployments without an IdP. \\\n>                  Permission checks and secure ORM still apply. DO NOT use this mode in multi-tenant or production environments.\"\n>             );\n> ```\n> </details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> <details>\n> <summary>modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n> \n> `18-21`: **Use production constants from `modkit_security::constants` in tests.**\n> \n> The test constants do not match the production values:\n> - `TEST_DEFAULT_TENANT_ID` is `00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001` but production `DEFAULT_TENANT_ID` is `00000000-df51-5b42-9538-d2b56b7ee953`\n> - `TEST_DEFAULT_SUBJECT_ID` is `11111111-0000-0000-0000-000000000001` but production `DEFAULT_SUBJECT_ID` is `11111111-6a88-4768-9dfc-6bcd5187d9ed`\n> \n> The comment at line 20 claims the test subject ID \"matches `api_gateway` constant,\" but it does not. Update these test constants to use the actual production values from `modkit_security::constants` to ensure the test accurately reflects production behavior.\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n> \n> </blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\