ibs/modkit-auth/src/claims.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `builder` (32-34)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (10)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=sqlite)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: modkit-db integration (backend=pg)\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (13)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/policy_engine.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`11-11`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe rename from `DummyPolicyEngine` to `NoopPolicyEngine` improves clarity—\"Noop\" is standard terminology for no-operation implementations.\n\n---\n\n`19-23`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe `PolicyEngine` implementation correctly provides no-op behavior. The unused parameter naming convention (`_ctx`, `_resource`, `_action`) is appropriate.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/tests/auth_integration.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-28`: **LGTM! Clean migration to SecurityContext and simplified imports.**\n\nThe imports are correctly updated: `ScopeBuilder` is removed from the traits import, and `SecurityContext` replaces `SecurityCtx`. The handler at line 114 correctly extracts and uses `SecurityContext`.\n\n---\n\n`124-135`: **LGTM! Correct AuthPolicyLayer::new signature.**\n\nThe `build_test_router` function correctly uses the new 3-argument signature for `AuthPolicyLayer::new(validator, authorizer, policy)`, matching the updated API that no longer requires a `scope_builder` parameter.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **LGTM! Public exports updated correctly.**\n\nThe export now includes `NoopPolicyEngine` (renamed from `DummyPolicyEngine`), and the removal of `SecurityCtx` and `Subject` exports aligns with the PR's objective to consolidate on `SecurityContext`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`24-26`: **LGTM! Doc comment and type updated correctly.**\n\nThe doc comment now correctly references `SecurityContext`, and the `Authz` struct wraps the new type. The past review comment has been addressed.\n\n---\n\n`86-99`: **LGTM! Simplified AuthPolicyLayer::new signature.**\n\nThe constructor now takes only three parameters (`validator`, `authorizer`, `policy`), removing the `scope_builder` dependency as intended by this PR.\n\n---\n\n`178-186`: **LGTM! SecurityContext built from claims using builder pattern.**\n\nThe builder pattern correctly extracts `tenant_id` and `subject_id` from the validated claims to construct the `SecurityContext`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`32-32`: **LGTM! Import updated to SecurityContext.**\n\nThe import correctly brings in `SecurityContext` from `modkit_security`.\n\n---\n\n`235-237`: **LGTM! AuthPolicyLayer::new uses updated signature.**\n\nThe call correctly passes the three required arguments (`validator`, `authorizer`, `policy`) without the removed `scope_builder` parameter.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-14`: **LGTM! Imports updated for new types.**\n\nCorrectly imports `NoopPolicyEngine` and `SecurityContext` from `modkit_security`, and adds `Arc` for wrapping the policy engine.\n\n---\n\n`23-41`: **LGTM! Test handler correctly migrated to SecurityContext.**\n\nThe handler extracts `SecurityContext` and derives the scope using the `NoopPolicyEngine`. The async scope preparation pattern (`ctx.scope(...).prepare().await`) is correctly applied.\n\n---\n\n`44-53`: **LGTM! Middleware correctly builds SecurityContext.**\n\nThe `inject_default_tenant_context` middleware uses the builder pattern to construct a `SecurityContext` with the test tenant and subject IDs, matching the pattern used in the actual API gateway code.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#pullrequestreview-3665260719","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/248#pullrequestreview-3665260719"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/248"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T11:56:49Z","commit_id":"690abbe87aca49f5f6db509fc46436e5ff472a3d"}]},{"source_pr_number":247,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247","source_state":"closed","source_author":"nanoandrew4","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #247] Add new lint to enforce snake-case usage with new api_dto macro","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"snake-case-enforcement","pr_head_sha":"2686d00b2004648d3fbd1bf68419c111f1f362e6","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"nanoandrew4","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","id":3176748485,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs69WVXF","html_url":"https://github.