},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/2686d00b2004648d3fbd1bf68419c111f1f362e6"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3753992864","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#issuecomment-3753992864","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/247","id":3753992864,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fwWKg","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T10:13:31Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T11:34:22Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a proc-macro for API DTOs, marker traits and blanket impls for request/response DTOs, and multiple lints (de0104, de0203, de0803) enforcing DTO placement, macro usage, and snake_case serde naming. Migrates many DTOs to use the macro and updates manifests and tests accordingly.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace manifest updates** <br> `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml`, various `*/Cargo.toml` (many) | Added/renamed workspace members; added workspace dependencies (serde, serde_json, utoipa, modkit, modkit-macros); standardized authors and linker config |\n| **Macro library** <br> `libs/modkit-macros/src/api_dto.rs`, `libs/modkit-macros/src/lib.rs` | Added `#[proc_macro_attribute] api_dto` implementation and helpers (flag validation, expansion) with unit tests |\n| **Core API traits & wiring** <br> `libs/modkit/src/api/api_dto.rs`, `libs/modkit/src/api/mod.rs`, `libs/modkit/src/api/operation_builder.rs`, `libs/modkit/src/lib.rs` | Added `RequestApiDto` / `ResponseApiDto` traits, blanket impls for containers, updated OperationBuilder generic bounds to require DTO traits, test updates |\n| **Lint utilities** <br> `dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs`, `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml` | Added AST helpers for api_dto detection and ApiDtoArgs parsing; adjusted lint-utils dependencies |\n| **New lints: de0803 (snake_case)** <br> `dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/*` | New lint implementation enforcing snake_case in serde rename/rename_all for API DTOs, README, rust-toolchain, many UI tests/examples |\n| **New/changed lints: de0203 (api_dto requirement) & de0104 (no api_dto in contract)** <br> `dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0203_dtos_must_use_api_dto/*`, `dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0104_no_api_dto_in_contract/*` | Replaced old serde-derive lint with api_dto-enforcement; added contract-layer prohibition lint with UI tests |\n| **Removed old DE0203 implementation & examples** <br> `dylint_lints/de02_api_layer/de0203_dtos_must_have_serde_derives/*` | Deleted previous serde-derive lint and its UI fixtures (migrated to new lint) |\n| **DTO migrations across codebase** <br> examples and modules: `examples/.../src/api/rest/dto.rs`, `modules/.../src/api/rest/dto.rs`, `modules/system/.../tests/*` (many) | Replaced explicit `Serialize`/`Deserialize`/`ToSchema` derives with `#[modkit_macros::api_dto(...)]`, adjusted field naming (snake_case) and conversions/tests where applicable |\n| **New example crates & lints** <br> `dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0104_no_api_dto_in_contract/*`, `dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0104_no_api_dto_in_contract/Cargo.toml` | Added new crate and examples demonstrating forbidden api_dto usage in contract layer |\n| **UI test artifacts** <br> `dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/ui/*.rs` and `.stderr` | Many new pass/fail UI cases exercising snake_case lint (fields, variants, nested rename_all, etc.) |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\nmermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n  participant Source as \"Source crate (DTOs)\"\n  participant Macro as \"modkit_macros::api_dto (proc-macro)\"\n  participant Compiler as \"rustc (expansion)\"\n  participant Lint as \"dylint lints (de0203/de0104/de0803)\"\n  participant Runtime as \"libs/modkit (traits/OperationBuilder)\"\n  Source->>Macro: apply attribute #[api_dto(...)] on types\n  Macro->>Compiler: emit expanded item with serde attrs, trait impls or compile_error\n  Compiler->>Lint: run pre-expansion/early lints on AST (detect api_dto misuse, snake_case issues)\n  Lint-->>Source: emit diagnostics (DE0203 / DE0104 / DE0803)\n  Compiler->>Runtime: require Request/Response marker traits on OperationBuilder generics\n  Runtime-->>Source: type-check errors if DTOs missing marker traits\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#284 — workspace dependency and workspace member changes overlap (modkit, modkit-macros, serde, file_parser) and likely related to manifest and module migration here.  \n- hypernetix/hyperspot#223 — changes to simple-user-settings DTOs and Cargo.toml which align with this PR's macro-driven DTO migration.  \n- hypernetix/hyperspot#256 — modifications to nodes_registry DTOs and crate surface that match DTO migrations in this PR.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- MikeFalcon77  \n- Bechma\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 I hop through crates, a macro bright,  \n> > I stitch API DTOs just right.  \n> > Snake_case dances, lints in tow,  \n> > Contracts kept pure, layouts grow.  \n> > Hooray for clean types — hop, hop, go! 🥕\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                   |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                                                   |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'Add new lint to enforce snake-case usage with new api_dto macro' accurately and clearly summarizes the main change in the changeset—introducing a new lint rule for snake-case enforcement with the api_dto macro. |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                                                          |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3753992864/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3754031453","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#issuecomment-3754031453","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/247","id":3754031453,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fwfld","user":{"login":"codecov-commenter","id":65553080,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTUzMDgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65553080?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov-commenter","html_url":"https://github.com/codecov-commenter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov-commenter/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov-commenter/following{/other_user}