 in test files\nfind dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/ui -type f -name \"*.rs\" -exec grep -l \"serialize\\|deserialize\" {} \\;\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1745\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's check if any existing lints handle nested attribute lists similarly\nrg \"meta_item_list\\(\\)\" dylint_lints -B 5 -A 10 | grep -A 15 \"meta_item_list()\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4828\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Verify Serde attribute syntax - check if serialize/deserialize forms exist in their own tests or examples\nrg \"rename\\(\" --type rs | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 90\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Serde rename_all serialize deserialize attribute forms nested list`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nSummary — what forms exist and how they behave (with examples)\n\n- Valid rename_all values: \"lowercase\", \"UPPERCASE\", \"PascalCase\", \"camelCase\", \"snake_case\", \"SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE\", \"kebab-case\", \"SCREAMING-KEBAB-CASE\". Use either #[serde(rename_all = \"...\")] or split for directions: #[serde(rename_all(serialize = \"...\", deserialize = \"...\"))]. [1][2]\n\n- Scope: rename_all is a container attribute that renames the container’s immediate field names (for structs) or variant names (for enums). It does NOT automatically recurse into the fields’ own types — nested structs/enums must be annotated themselves (or inherit via their own derives/attributes). Example: #[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")] on struct Outer renames Outer’s fields; if a field is Vec<Inner>, Inner’s fields are unaffected unless Inner also has #[serde(...)] applied. [1][2]\n\n- Lists/Vecs: rename_all affects the name of the field that holds the list (the JSON key). It does not change how elements inside the list are serialized beyond the element type’s own serde behavior. Example:\n  - Rust:\n    #[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    #[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]\n    struct Outer { my_list: Vec<Inner>, }\n    #[derive(Serialize, Deserialize)]\n    #[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n    struct Inner { inner_field: i32, }\n  - JSON produced: { \"myList\": [ { \"inner_field\": 1 }, ... ] } — note myList came from Outer’s rename_all and inner_field from Inner’s rename_all. [1][5]\n\n- Per-field overrides: you can override rename_all with per-field attributes like #[serde(rename = \"...\")] or set separate serialize/deserialize rules with #[serde(rename(serialize = \"...\", deserialize = \"...\"))] or #[serde(rename_all(serialize = \"...\", deserialize = \"...\"))]. [1]\n\nReferences\n- Serde container attributes (rename_all, rename, rename_all split, scope notes). [1]\n- Serde rename examples (camelCase example). [2]\n\nReferences used:\n[1] Serde container attributes — serde.rs/container-attrs.  \n[2] Serde rename examples — serde.rs/attr-rename.\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let me check one of the test files with more detail to understand current coverage\ncat dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/ui/pass.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 373\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the README for DE0803 to understand the lint's scope\ncat dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/README.md\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1360\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Let's verify by creating a test case with the nested form to see if it would be caught\n# First, check if there are any such test cases already\nfind dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_snake_case/ui -name \"*.rs\" -exec grep -l \"serialize\\s*=\" {} \\;\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check the exact structure of test files to understand format\ncat dylint_lints/de08_rest_api_conventions/de0803_api_sna