8b","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@nanoandrew4`, you're absolutely right—my apologies for the confusion. The comments are correctly placed immediately before the attribute lines where the errors are reported. Since this lint specifically flags the `#[modkit_macros::api_dto(...)]` attribute usage in contract code, placing the annotations right before the attribute (lines 4, 11, 18) is the appropriate pattern here. Thank you for the clarification!\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Select pre-expansion lint pass for detecting serde/utoipa derives that must be checked before proc macros expand\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Use `ui_test_examples` when tests need external dependencies (serde, utoipa) or have logically distinct scenarios with explicit test organization\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Use `is_in_contract_module_ast()` helper from `lint_utils` crate to check if an AST item is in a contract/ directory\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/*.rs : Place test comment annotations (`// Should trigger DEXXX - description` or `// Should not trigger DEXXX - description`) on the line immediately before where the error is reported, not on attribute lines\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/*.rs : For struct/enum/function multiline spans in UI tests, place error comments on the first line of the item declaration (e.g., `pub struct Name`), not on the `#[derive(...)]` attribute line\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Document lint behavior in doc comments within the lint implementation\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/**/src/lib.rs : Every lint crate MUST include a `test_comment_annotations_match_stderr` test using `lint_utils::test_comment_annotations_match_stderr` to validate comment/stderr alignment\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: dylint_lints/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:31.912Z\nLearning: Applies to dylint_lints/ui/*.stderr : Ensure `.stderr` files have comment annotations describing what triggers the lint and include `help:` and `note:` sections\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-22T10:22:58Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T10:22:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2716254390","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716254390"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2716254390"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716254390/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":4,"original_start_line":4,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":23,"original_line":23,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2716240018,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":23,"position":23,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716288679","pull_request_review_id":3691740918,"id":2716288679,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6h50an","diff_hunk":"@@ -87,6 +94,98 @@ pub fn is_serde_trait(segments: &[&str], trait_name: &str) -> bool {\n     }\n }\n \n+/// Check if an item has the `#[modkit_macros::api_dto(...)]` attribute.\n+///\n+/// The `api_dto` macro automatically adds:\n+/// - `#[derive(serde::Serialize)]` (if `response` is specified)\n+/// - `#[derive(serde::Deserialize)]` (if `request` is specified)\n+/// - `#[derive(utoipa::ToSchema)]` (always)\n+/// - `#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]` (always)\n+///\n+/// Lints checking for these derives/attributes should skip items with this attribute.\n+pub fn has_api_dto_attribute(item: &rustc_ast::Item) -> bool {\n+    for attr in &item.attrs {\n+        // Check for modkit_macros::api_dto or just api_dto\n+        if let rustc_ast::AttrKind::Normal(attr_item) = &attr.kind {\n+            let path = &attr_item.item.path;\n+            let segments: Vec<&str> = path.segments.iter().map(|s| s.ident.name.as_str()).collect();\n+\n+            // Match: api_dto, modkit_macros::api_dto\n+            if segments.last() == Some(&\"api_dto\") {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+/// Returns the api_dto arguments (request, response) if present.\n+/// Returns None if the attribute is not present.\n+/// Returns Some with flags indicating which modes are enabled.\n+pub fn get_api_dto_args(item: &rustc_ast::Item) -> Option<ApiDtoArgs> {\n+    for attr in &item.attrs {\n+        if let rustc_ast::AttrKind::Normal(attr_item) = &attr.kind {\n+            let path = &attr_item.item.path;\n+            let segments: Vec<&str> = path.segments.iter().map(|s| s.ident.name.as_str()).collect();\n+\n+            if segments.last() != Some(&\"api_dto\") {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            // Parse the arguments\n+            let mut has_request = false;\n+            let mut has_response = false;\n+\n+            if let Some(args) = attr_item.item.meta_item_list() {\n+                for arg in args {\n+                    if let Some(ident) = arg.ident() {\n+                        match ident.name.as_str() {\n+                            \"request\" => has_request = true,\n+                            \"response\" => has_response = true,\n+                            _ => {}\n+                        }\n+                    }\n+                }\n+            }\n+\n+            return Some(ApiDtoArgs {\n+                has_request,\n+                has_response,\n+            });\n+        }\n+    }\n+    None\n+}\n+\n+/// Arguments parsed from `#[api_dto(request, response)]`\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy)]\n+pub struct ApiDtoArgs {\n+    pub has_request: bool,\n+    pub has_response: bool,\n+}\n+\n+impl ApiDtoArgs {\n+    /// Returns true if the macro will add Serialize derive (response mode)\n+    pub fn adds_serialize(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.has_response\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns true if the macro will add Deserialize derive (request mode)\n+    pub fn adds_deserialize(&self) -> bool {\n+        self.has_request\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns true if the macro will add ToSchema derive (always)\n+    pub fn adds_toschema(&self) -> bool {\n+        true\n+    }\n+\n+    /// Returns true if the macro will add serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\") (always)\n+    pub fn adds_snake_case_rename(&self) -> bool {\n+        true\n+    }","path":"dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"89c8b5b38072738da08174f74906b276b081e2c8","original_commit_id":"44b6d8b6cd61add0a5a3d33872468ea254914d6f","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Find api_dto macro file and inspect its behavior\nfd -a \"api_dto.rs\" . --type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 469\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Inspect the proc-macro implementation to see defaults\nwc -l /home/jailuser/git/libs/modkit-macros/src/api_dto.rs\nhead -100 /home/jailuser/git/libs/modkit-macros/src/api_dto.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2993\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Read the rest of the file to see complete implementation\nsed -n '70,150p' /home/jailuser/git/libs/modkit-macros/src/api_dto.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2593\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Fix `adds_snake_case_rename()` to match macro behavior: only return true if request or response is present.**\n\nThe `api_dto` macro only adds `serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")` when at least one of `request` or `response` flags is provided (see `has_serde` condition in macro). However, `adds_snake_case_rename()` unconditionally returns `true`, causing the lint to misclassify items when neither flag is present.\n\nCorrected logic should be:\n```rust\npub fn adds_snake_case_rename(&self) -> bool {\n    self.has_request || self.has_response\n}\n```\n\nAdditionally, `get_api_dto_args()` can return `{request:false, response:false}`, but the macro requires at least one flag and rejects this case with a compile error. Consider whether the lint should validate this precondition or document that returned `false`/`false` represents an invalid (unparseable or empty) attribute.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs` around lines 122 - 186, The\nadds_snake_case_rename() method in ApiDtoArgs currently always returns true,\nwhich contradicts the macro behavior that only applies serde(rename_all =\n\"snake_case\") when request or response is present; update\nadds_snake_case_rename() to return self.has_request || self.has_response; also\ncheck get_api_dto_args() (which can produce ApiDtoArgs { has_request:false,\nhas_response:false }) and either add a validation step in the lint to treat the\nempty/invalid attribute as absent/error or document that a false/false result\nrepresents an invalid/empty attribute so callers know this case must be rejected\nsimilarly to the macro.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 04d391a","created_at":"2026-01-22T10:32:29Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T10:41:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2716288679","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716288679"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2716288679"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716288679/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":122,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":186,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":114,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2716347499","pull_request_review_id":3691807979,"id":2716347499,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6h6Cxr","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@\n+[package]\n+name = \"de0104_no_api_dto_in_contract\"\n+version = 