ipt executed:\n\n```shell\n# Examine the actual .cargo/config.toml file\ncd dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0101_no_serde_in_contract && cat -n .cargo/config.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 328\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo config.toml linker setting scope target table vs top-level documentation`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: put linker in a target triple table (e.g. [target.aarch64-unknown-none]).\n\nDetails:\n- The [target.'cfg(...)'] sections in config.toml only affect rustflags (they do not support the linker key). Use a literal target triple table for linker and runner settings. [1][2]\n- Behavior around host vs cross target (whether target.* applies to host-built artifacts) is governed by the unstable target-applies-to-host option and related host-config behavior. If you pass --target or build host artifacts, read that section for nuances. [3]\n\nSources:\n- Cargo config target/cfg explanation (note: cfg syntax only applies to rustflags). [1]\n- Examples / discussion recommending setting linker under [target.<triple>]. [2]\n- target-applies-to-host / host-config discussion (affects when target.* settings are applied). [3]\n\nReferences:\n[1] ([users.rust-lang.org](https://users.rust-lang.org/t/about-target-triple-target-cfg-in-cargo-config/33707?utm_source=openai))\n[2] ([internals.rust-lang.org](https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/we-need-configurably-additive-rustflags/19851?utm_source=openai))\n[3] ([dev-doc.rust-lang.org](https://dev-doc.rust-lang.org/beta/cargo/reference/unstable.html?utm_source=openai))\n\nWould you like an example config showing linker under a triple and rustflags under a cfg block?\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://users.rust-lang.org/t/about-target-triple-target-cfg-in-cargo-config/33707?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/we-need-configurably-additive-rustflags/19851?utm_source=openai\n- 3: https://dev-doc.rust-lang.org/beta/cargo/reference/unstable.html?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Move `linker` to a literal target triple table—top-level and `[target.'cfg(all())']` are both unsupported.**\n\nCargo's `config.toml` does not support the `linker` key at the top level or within `[target.'cfg(...)']` sections. The `cfg` syntax only applies to `rustflags`. Move the linker setting to a literal target triple (e.g., `[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]`):\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛠️ Correct config</summary>\n\n```diff\n-# [target.'cfg(all())']\n-# rustflags = [\"-C\", \"linker=dylint-link\"]\n-\n-# For Rust versions 1.74.0 and onward, the following alternative can be used\n-# (see https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/pull/12535):\n-linker = \"dylint-link\"\n+[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n+linker = \"dylint-link\"\n```\n\nAdjust the target triple to match your build target(s).\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\nlinker = \"dylint-link\"\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0101_no_serde_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml`\naround lines 1 - 6, The config.toml currently places the linker key at top-level\nand comments a [target.'cfg(all())'] block which is invalid; move the linker =\n\"dylint-link\" entry into a literal target table such as\n[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu] (or whatever target triple you build for)\ninstead of top-level or [target.'cfg(all())'], ensuring the linker key lives\nunder that literal target table in config.toml so Cargo recognizes it.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-22T21:17:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-22T21:17:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2718669773","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2718669773"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2718669773"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2718669773/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":6,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":9,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2718669778","pull_request_review_id":3694636422,"id":2718669778,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iC5vS","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@\n-[target.'cfg(all())']\n-rustflags = [\"-C\", \"linker=dylint-link\"]\n+# [target.'cfg(all())']\n+# rustflags = [\"-C\", \"linker=dylint-link\"]\n \n # For Rust versions 1.74.0 and onward, the following alternative can be used\n # (see https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo/pull/12535):\n-# linker = \"dylint-link\"\n+linker = \"dylint-link\"","path":"dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0102_no_toschema_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml","commit_id":"a29e99b0cc1e53d28f65a3fb2b9b5bc36d67fc6a","original_commit_id":"a29e99b0cc1e53d28f65a3fb2b9b5bc36d67fc6a","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Find and read the actual .cargo/config.toml file\nfind . -path \"*de0102_no_toschema_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml\" -type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 148\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Also search for other .cargo/config.toml files to understand project patterns\nfind . -name \"config.toml\" -path \"*/.cargo/*\" -type f\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 929\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo .cargo/config.toml linker setting format root level vs [build] section`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer\n- Put linker settings under [target.<triple>] in .cargo/config.toml (e.g. [target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu] linker = \"/path/to/ld\"). That's the supported, usual place Cargo reads for per-target linkers. [1]\n\nDetails / behavior\n- Per-target linker config belongs in [target.<triple>]. Settings there apply when building for that target triple. [1]  \n- There is an unstable host-config mechanism ([host] / [host.<triple>]) and a top-level target-applies-to-host toggle that change how host vs target tables are applied when cross-compiling; those are behind Cargo unstable flags and not the normal stable config flow. Use them only with nightly and the -Z flags. [1][2]  \n- Common mistake: putting linker in Cargo.toml (package manifest) does nothing; the linker must be in .cargo/config(.toml) under the target table (or set via environment variable CARGO_TARGET_<TRIPLE>_LINKER). Community threads/answers confirm this. [2]\n\nSources\n1. Cargo reference — unstable features / config file (host/target behavior). [1]  \n2. Practical advice / examples (StackOverflow / community threads) showing linker belongs in .cargo/config and not Cargo.toml. [2]\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0102_no_toschema_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 328\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check another similar config file for pattern comparison\ncat -n ./dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0101_no_serde_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 328\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for documentation or comments about the Rust 1.74.0 change mentioned in the config\nrg -i \"rust.*1\\.74\" --max-count=20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Rust cargo PR 12535 linker config 1.74.0`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nYes — Pull Request `#12535` added support for target.'cfg(..)'.linker, and it shipped in Cargo included with Rust 1.74.0. [1][2]\n\nReferences:\n- Rust 1.74.0 release notes (Cargo section) listing \"Add support for `target.'cfg(..)'.linker`.\" [1]\n- Rust toolchain diff / changelog that also lists the Cargo PR `#12535` entry. [2]\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo config.toml target.'cfg(...)'.linker syntax Rust 1.74 format example`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: Cargo does not support setting linker under a [target.'cfg(...)'] table — the cfg(...) form only applies to rustflags/runner; linker is only valid for a concrete target triple. Use [target.<triple>]. Example config.toml (Rust/Cargo 1.74):\n\n- Invalid / not supported:\n  [target.'cfg(target_arch = \"arm\")']\n  linker = \"arm-none-eabi-gcc\"  # <-- NOT applied by Cargo\n\n- Supported / correct:\n  [target.armv7-unknown-linux-gnueabihf]\n  linker = \"arm-none-eabi-gcc\"\n  rustflags = [\"-C\", \"link-arg=-Tlink.ld\"]\n\nDocs: Cargo config reference (cfg form only affects rustflags; linker is per-triple). [1][2]\n\nSources:\n[1] Cargo configuration reference — target tables. doc.rust-lang.org. ([doc.rust-lang.org](https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html?utm_source=openai))  \n[2] Discussion / notes showing cfg in .cargo/config doesn't apply to linker/features. ([users.rust-lang.org](https://users.rust-lang.org/t/about-target-triple-target-cfg-in-cargo-config/33707?utm_source=openai))\n\nCitations:\n\n- 1: https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/reference/config.html?utm_source=openai\n- 2: https://users.rust-lang.org/t/about-target-triple-target-cfg-in-cargo-config/33707?utm_source=openai\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`\"cargo\" \"PR 12535\" \"target.'cfg\" linker implementation what did it add`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: PR rust-lang/cargo#12535 added support for specifying the linker inside cfg-based target tables in Cargo config — i.e. you can now set target.'cfg(...)'.linker in .cargo/config(.toml) so a cfg() expression (not just a concrete triple) can choose the linker used for that target. [1][2]\n\nSources:\n- Cargo changelog (notes the addition “Add support for `target.'cfg(..)'.linker`”). [1]\n- Cargo config reference / repo mentions cfg-based target settings (including linker behavior). [2]\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo config.toml root level linker setting without section`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nShort answer: No — the linker setting must go under a target (or host) table in Cargo config, not as a top-level key. See Cargo's config reference and the unstable host/target behavior docs.\n\nExample (in .cargo/config.toml):\n[target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\nlinker = \"/path/to/linker\"\n\nThere is also an unstable [host] table for host-specific linker configuration and the target-applies-to-host behavior (requires nightly -Z flags). [1][2]\n\nSources:\n[1] Cargo configuration reference.  \n[2] Cargo unstable: target-applies-to-host / host configuration.\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Move `linker` under the `[target.'cfg(all())']` section.**\n\nThe `linker = \"dylint-link\"` setting at line 6 is at the root level without a section header. In Cargo config, the `linker` key must be placed under a target table. Since Rust 1.74.0 added support for `target.'cfg(...)'` syntax, the correct format is:\n\n```toml\n[target.'cfg(all())']\nlinker = \"dylint-link\"\n```\n\nThis matches the pattern of the commented-out section above (lines 1-2) and follows Cargo's configuration requirements.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@dylint_lints/de01_contract_layer/de0102_no_toschema_in_contract/.cargo/config.toml`\naround lines 1 - 6, The linker = \"dylint-link\" entry is at the root level but\nmust live under a target table; move that key into the [target.'cfg(all())']\nsection so the file contains a target.'cfg(all())' table with linker =\n\"dylint-link\" (i.e., restore/enable the commented [target.'cfg(all())'] block\nand place the linker setting inside it), referencing the linker key and the\n[target.'cfg(all())'] table to locate where to change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit ca12fa2","created_at":"2026-01-22T21:17:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:56:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2718669778","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","_links