er_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Find all .cargo/config.toml files in dylint_lints directory\necho \"=== .cargo/config.toml files in dylint_lints ===\"\nfd -t f 'config\\.toml' dylint_lints/ --exec echo \"File: {}\" \\; --exec cat {} \\; --exec echo \"\" \\;\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 112\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`Cargo PR 12535 linker setting config.toml syntax top-level`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nPR `#12535` added support for conditional target tables in config.toml using the TOML table key form target.'cfg(...)'.linker — i.e. you can put a cfg(...) expression in the target table name. Example usages:\n\n- simple target table (existing style)\n  [target.x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu]\n  linker = \"/path/to/linker\"\n\n- conditional/cfg table (added by PR `#12535`)\n  [target.'cfg(target_arch = \"aarch64\")']\n  linker = \"/usr/bin/aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc\"\n\nYou can also use other cfg predicates inside the quoted table key. See the Cargo changelog entry for the PR and the Cargo config docs for related linker/target settings. [1][2]\n\nSources:\n[1] Cargo changelog (mentions \"Added support for target.'cfg(..)'.linker. `#12535`\"). [2] Cargo reference / unstable features (config.toml target/host/linker examples).\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for the specific file mentioned in the review\necho \"=== Search for specific config.toml file ===\"\nfind . -path \"*/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/.cargo/config.toml\" 2>/dev/null\n\necho -e \"\\n=== All .cargo directories in repo ===\"\nfd -t d '.cargo' \n\necho -e \"\\n=== Search for any config.toml files ===\"\nfd -t f 'config\\.toml' \n\necho -e \"\\n=== Search for de0901_gts_string_pattern directory ===\"\nfd -t d 'de0901_gts_string_pattern'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 376\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\ncat -n ./dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/.cargo/config.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 328\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Move `linker` setting into a section header.**\n\nThe `linker = \"dylint-link\"` key at line 6 is at the top level without a section header, which is invalid Cargo config syntax. Cargo will silently ignore it. Cargo PR `#12535` added support for conditional target tables (e.g., `[target.'cfg(...)']`), but linker settings must always be within a section. Use:\n\n```toml\n[build]\nlinker = \"dylint-link\"\n```\n\nOr keep it in the target-specific section if conditioning is needed.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de09_gts_layer/de0901_gts_string_pattern/.cargo/config.toml`\naround lines 1 - 6, The top-level setting linker = \"dylint-link\" is invalid in\nCargo config and will be ignored; move this key into a proper section header\n(for example add a [build] section or place it inside an existing target table\nlike [target.'cfg(all())']) so the linker directive is recognized; update the\nconfig so the unique symbol linker = \"dylint-link\" is nested under a section\nheader (e.g., [build] or [target.'cfg(all())']) rather than at top level.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit ca12fa2","created_at":"2026-01-22T21:17:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T10:50:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2718669791","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/247","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2718669791"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/247#discussion_r2718669791"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/