//api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd add Role based access check (ensure the client is allowed to communicate to any LLM / or particular LLM)","created_at":"2026-01-18T11:43:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:44:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702347037","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702347037"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702347037"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702347037/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":25,"original_line":25,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":25,"position":25,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702348705","pull_request_review_id":3675431417,"id":2702348705,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hEpGh","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1098 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Format\n+\n+Message content is an array of typed blocks:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+content: [\n+  { type: \"text\", text: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"image\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"audio\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"video\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"document\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"tool_call\", id: \"...\", tool_id: \"...\", arguments: {...} },\n+  { type: \"tool_result\", tool_call_id: \"...\", result: {...} }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+| Type | Fields | Direction |\n+|------|--------|-----------|\n+| text | text | input/output |\n+| image | url | input/output |\n+| audio | url | input/output |\n+| video | url | input/output |\n+| document | url | input/output |\n+| tool_call | id, tool_id, arguments | output |\n+| tool_result | tool_call_id, result | input |\n+\n+**Media input**:\n+- FileStorage URL — Gateway fetches content before sending to provider\n+- Data URL (`data:<mime>;base64,...`) — Gateway passes directly to provider\n+\n+**Media output**: Gateway stores via FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools Format\n+\n+Consumer defines tools via reference or inline GTS schema:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+tools: [\n+  // Option 1: Reference to Type Registry\n+  { schema_id: \"gts.hx.core.faas.func.v1~acme.crm.contacts.search.v1\" },","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","original_commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Right now we use `gts.x`, not `gts.hx`, because `x` is generic (and can become a part of any other platform) while `hx` is Hypernetix vendor ID","created_at":"2026-01-18T11:46:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:46:40Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702348705","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702348705"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702348705"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702348705/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":51,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":51,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702350529","pull_request_review_id":3675432709,"id":2702350529,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hEpjB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1098 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Format\n+\n+Message content is an array of typed blocks:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+content: [\n+  { type: \"text\", text: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"image\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"audio\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"video\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"document\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"tool_call\", id: \"...\", tool_id: \"...\", arguments: {...} },\n+  { type: \"tool_result\", tool_call_id: \"...\", result: {...} }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+| Type | Fields | Direction |\n+|------|--------|-----------|\n+| text | text | input/output |\n+| image | url | input/output |\n+| audio | url | input/output |\n+| video | url | input/output |\n+| document | url | input/output |\n+| tool_call | id, tool_id, arguments | output |\n+| tool_result | tool_call_id, result | input |\n+\n+**Media input**:\n+- FileStorage URL — Gateway fetches content before sending to provider\n+- Data URL (`data:<mime>;base64,...`) — Gateway passes directly to provider\n+\n+**Media output**: Gateway stores via FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools Format\n+\n+Consumer defines tools via reference or inline GTS schema:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+tools: [\n+  // Option 1: Reference to Type Registry\n+  { schema_id: \"gts.hx.core.faas.func.v1~acme.crm.contacts.search.v1\" },\n+\n+  // Option 2: Inline GTS schema\n+  {\n+    $id: \"dynamic_search\",\n+    title: \"Dynamic Search\",\n+    description: \"Search with dynamic parameters\",\n+    params: {\n+      type: \"object\",\n+      properties: {\n+        query: { type: \"string\" }\n+      },\n+      required: [\"query\"]\n+    },\n+    returns: {\n+      type: \"array\",\n+      items: { type: \"object\" }\n+    }\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+| Format | When to use |\n+|--------|-------------|\n+| `schema_id` | Registered tools, governance required |\n+| Inline schema | Ad-hoc tools, dynamic generation, testing |\n+\n+**Gateway behavior**:\n+- `schema_id` → resolve from Type Registry, convert to provider format\n+- Inline schema → use directly, convert to provider format\n+\n+**Response `tool_call.tool_id`**: Returns `schema_id` or inline `$id` (whichever was used in request).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Response Format\n+\n+Gateway fully normalizes `chat_completion` responses to a unified format. Other endpoints (`embed`, `list_models`, `get_job`) have endpoint-specific response structures.\n+\n+```plaintext\n+response: {\n+  content: [...],           // normalized content blocks\n+  usage: {                  // normalized usage\n+    prompt_tokens: 100,\n+    completion_tokens: 50,\n+    total_tokens: 150\n+  },\n+  metadata: {               // normalized metadata\n+    model: \"gpt-4\",\n+    provider: \"openai\",\n+    latency_ms: 234,\n+    request_id: \"req_abc123\"\n+  },\n+  extensions: {             // provider-specific data (optional)\n+    \"openai\": { ... },\n+    \"anthropic\": { ... }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Normalization Guarantees\n+\n+| Field | Guarantee |\n+|-------|-----------|\n+| `content` | Always present, unified block format |\n+| `usage` | Always present, consistent field names |\n+| `metadata.model` | Always present, model ID used |\n+| `metadata.provider` | Always present, identifies source |\n+| `metadata.latency_ms` | Always present, request duration |\n+| `metadata.request_id` | Always present, for tracing |\n+| `metadata.fallback_used` | Optional, true if fallback was triggered |\n+| `metadata.original_model` | Optional, requested model before fallback |\n+| `extensions` | Optional, provider-keyed |\n+\n+### Extensions\n+\n+Provider-specific data that doesn't fit the normalized schema goes into `extensions`. Consumers should not depend on extensions for core functionality.\n+\n+**Response extensions** (examples):\n+```plaintext\n+extensions: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    stop_reason: \"end_turn\",\n+    cache_creation_input_tokens: 1000,\n+    cache_read_input_tokens: 500\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    system_fingerprint: \"fp_abc123\",\n+    logprobs: [...]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Request extensions** (provider hints):\n+```plaintext\n+provider_hints: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    cache_control: { type: \"ephemeral\" }\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    logprobs: true,\n+    top_logprobs: 5\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Principles**:\n+- Extensions are optional — consumers can ignore them\n+- Extensions are type-safe — keyed by provider name\n+- Extensions don't affect Gateway logic — pass-through only\n+- Model Discovery (S1.12) advertises available extensions per model\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Streaming Format\n+\n+Gateway normalizes streaming events to a unified SSE format.\n+\n+**Event types**:\n+\n+| Event | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| `delta` | Content chunk (text, tool_call) |\n+| `usage` | Final usage metrics (last event before done) |\n+| `done` | Stream completion |\n+| `error` | Error occurred |\n+\n+**Delta event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: delta\n+data: {\n+  type: \"text_delta\" | \"tool_call_delta\",\n+  index: 0,           // content block index\n+  text?: \"...\",       // for text_delta\n+  tool_call?: {...}   // for tool_call_delta\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Usage event** (always emitted before done):\n+```plaintext\n+event: usage\n+data: {\n+  prompt_tokens: 100,\n+  completion_tokens: 50,\n+  total_tokens: 150\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Done event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: done\n+data: {\n+  finish_reason: \"stop\" | \"tool_calls\" | \"length\" | \"content_filter\",\n+  metadata: { model: \"gpt-4\", provider: \"openai\", latency_ms: 234, request_id: \"...\" },\n+  extensions: { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Normalization**:\n+- All providers mapped to same event types\n+- `tool_calls` always streamed after text (consistent ordering)\n+- `usage` always in final chunk (not deltas)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| FileStorage | Fetch input media by URL, store generated content |\n+| Credential Resolver | API keys for providers |\n+| Type Registry | Read GTS schemas by ID (tool definitions) |\n+| Usage Tracker | Token/cost reporting |\n+| Hook System | `llm.pre_call`, `llm.post_response` interceptors |\n+| Audit | Request/response logging |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","original_commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Need to add License Resolver to dependencies","created_at":"2026-01-18T11:49:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:49:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702350529","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702350529"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702350529"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702350529/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":225,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":225,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702350995","pull_request_review_id":3675432953,"id":2702350995,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hEpqT","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,1098 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Format\n+\n+Message content is an array of typed blocks:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+content: [\n+  { type: \"text\", text: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"image\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"audio\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"video\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"document\", url: \"...\" },\n+  { type: \"tool_call\", id: \"...\", tool_id: \"...\", arguments: {...} },\n+  { type: \"tool_result\", tool_call_id: \"...\", result: {...} }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+| Type | Fields | Direction |\n+|------|--------|-----------|\n+| text | text | input/output |\n+| image | url | input/output |\n+| audio | url | input/output |\n+| video | url | input/output |\n+| document | url | input/output |\n+| tool_call | id, tool_id, arguments | output |\n+| tool_result | tool_call_id, result | input |\n+\n+**Media input**:\n+- FileStorage URL — Gateway fetches content before sending to provider\n+- Data URL (`data:<mime>;base64,...`) — Gateway passes directly to provider\n+\n+**Media output**: Gateway stores via FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools Format\n+\n+Consumer defines tools via reference or inline GTS schema:\n+\n+```plaintext\n+tools: [\n+  // Option 1: Reference to Type Registry\n+  { schema_id: \"gts.hx.core.faas.func.v1~acme.crm.contacts.search.v1\" },\n+\n+  // Option 2: Inline GTS schema\n+  {\n+    $id: \"dynamic_search\",\n+    title: \"Dynamic Search\",\n+    description: \"Search with dynamic parameters\",\n+    params: {\n+      type: \"object\",\n+      properties: {\n+        query: { type: \"string\" }\n+      },\n+      required: [\"query\"]\n+    },\n+    returns: {\n+      type: \"array\",\n+      items: { type: \"object\" }\n+    }\n+  }\n+]\n+```\n+\n+| Format | When to use |\n+|--------|-------------|\n+| `schema_id` | Registered tools, governance required |\n+| Inline schema | Ad-hoc tools, dynamic generation, testing |\n+\n+**Gateway behavior**:\n+- `schema_id` → resolve from Type Registry, convert to provider format\n+- Inline schema → use directly, convert to provider format\n+\n+**Response `tool_call.tool_id`**: Returns `schema_id` or inline `$id` (whichever was used in request).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Response Format\n+\n+Gateway fully normalizes `chat_completion` responses to a unified format. Other endpoints (`embed`, `list_models`, `get_job`) have endpoint-specific response structures.\n+\n+```plaintext\n+response: {\n+  content: [...],           // normalized content blocks\n+  usage: {                  // normalized usage\n+    prompt_tokens: 100,\n+    completion_tokens: 50,\n+    total_tokens: 150\n+  },\n+  metadata: {               // normalized metadata\n+    model: \"gpt-4\",\n+    provider: \"openai\",\n+    latency_ms: 234,\n+    request_id: \"req_abc123\"\n+  },\n+  extensions: {             // provider-specific data (optional)\n+    \"openai\": { ... },\n+    \"anthropic\": { ... }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Normalization Guarantees\n+\n+| Field | Guarantee |\n+|-------|-----------|\n+| `content` | Always present, unified block format |\n+| `usage` | Always present, consistent field names |\n+| `metadata.model` | Always present, model ID used |\n+| `metadata.provider` | Always present, identifies source |\n+| `metadata.latency_ms` | Always present, request duration |\n+| `metadata.request_id` | Always present, for tracing |\n+| `metadata.fallback_used` | Optional, true if fallback was triggered |\n+| `metadata.original_model` | Optional, requested model before fallback |\n+| `extensions` | Optional, provider-keyed |\n+\n+### Extensions\n+\n+Provider-specific data that doesn't fit the normalized schema goes into `extensions`. Consumers should not depend on extensions for core functionality.\n+\n+**Response extensions** (examples):\n+```plaintext\n+extensions: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    stop_reason: \"end_turn\",\n+    cache_creation_input_tokens: 1000,\n+    cache_read_input_tokens: 500\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    system_fingerprint: \"fp_abc123\",\n+    logprobs: [...]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Request extensions** (provider hints):\n+```plaintext\n+provider_hints: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    cache_control: { type: \"ephemeral\" }\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    logprobs: true,\n+    top_logprobs: 5\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Principles**:\n+- Extensions are optional — consumers can ignore them\n+- Extensions are type-safe — keyed by provider name\n+- Extensions don't affect Gateway logic — pass-through only\n+- Model Discovery (S1.12) advertises available extensions per model\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Streaming Format\n+\n+Gateway normalizes streaming events to a unified SSE format.\n+\n+**Event types**:\n+\n+| Event | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| `delta` | Content chunk (text, tool_call) |\n+| `usage` | Final usage metrics (last event before done) |\n+| `done` | Stream completion |\n+| `error` | Error occurred |\n+\n+**Delta event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: delta\n+data: {\n+  type: \"text_delta\" | \"tool_call_delta\",\n+  index: 0,           // content block index\n+  text?: \"...\",       // for text_delta\n+  tool_call?: {...}   // for tool_call_delta\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Usage event** (always emitted before done):\n+```plaintext\n+event: usage\n+data: {\n+  prompt_tokens: 100,\n+  completion_tokens: 50,\n+  total_tokens: 150\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Done event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: done\n+data: {\n+  finish_reason: \"stop\" | \"tool_calls\" | \"length\" | \"content_filter\",\n+  metadata: { model: \"gpt-4\", provider: \"openai\", latency_ms: 234, request_id: \"...\" },\n+  extensions: { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Normalization**:\n+- All providers mapped to same event types\n+- `tool_calls` always streamed after text (consistent ordering)\n+- `usage` always in final chunk (not deltas)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| FileStorage | Fetch input media by URL, store generated content |\n+| Credential Resolver | API keys for providers |\n+| Type Registry | Read GTS schemas by ID (tool definitions) |\n+| Usage Tracker | Token/cost reporting |\n+| Hook System | `llm.pre_call`, `llm.post_response` interceptors |\n+| Audit | Request/response logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full message history with each request. Conversation state is managed by a separate component (Chat Engine). Exception: async job state (ID mappings and cached results for sync providers) is stored temporarily until retrieval/expiry.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes requests/responses but does not interpret content. Tool execution, response parsing — consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Errors\n+\n+All errors follow RFC 9457 Problem Details format with GTS error codes.\n+\n+**Code pattern**: `gts.hx.core.errors.err.v1~hx.llm_gateway.<error>.v1`","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","original_commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"http