nified format. Other endpoints (`embed`, `list_models`, `get_job`) have endpoint-specific response structures.\n+\n+```plaintext\n+response: {\n+  content: [...],           // normalized content blocks\n+  usage: {                  // normalized usage\n+    prompt_tokens: 100,\n+    completion_tokens: 50,\n+    total_tokens: 150\n+  },\n+  metadata: {               // normalized metadata\n+    model: \"gpt-4\",\n+    provider: \"openai\",\n+    latency_ms: 234,\n+    request_id: \"req_abc123\"\n+  },\n+  extensions: {             // provider-specific data (optional)\n+    \"openai\": { ... },\n+    \"anthropic\": { ... }\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+### Normalization Guarantees\n+\n+| Field | Guarantee |\n+|-------|-----------|\n+| `content` | Always present, unified block format |\n+| `usage` | Always present, consistent field names |\n+| `metadata.model` | Always present, model ID used |\n+| `metadata.provider` | Always present, identifies source |\n+| `metadata.latency_ms` | Always present, request duration |\n+| `metadata.request_id` | Always present, for tracing |\n+| `metadata.fallback_used` | Optional, true if fallback was triggered |\n+| `metadata.original_model` | Optional, requested model before fallback |\n+| `extensions` | Optional, provider-keyed |\n+\n+### Extensions\n+\n+Provider-specific data that doesn't fit the normalized schema goes into `extensions`. Consumers should not depend on extensions for core functionality.\n+\n+**Response extensions** (examples):\n+```plaintext\n+extensions: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    stop_reason: \"end_turn\",\n+    cache_creation_input_tokens: 1000,\n+    cache_read_input_tokens: 500\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    system_fingerprint: \"fp_abc123\",\n+    logprobs: [...]\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Request extensions** (provider hints):\n+```plaintext\n+provider_hints: {\n+  \"anthropic\": {\n+    cache_control: { type: \"ephemeral\" }\n+  },\n+  \"openai\": {\n+    logprobs: true,\n+    top_logprobs: 5\n+  }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Principles**:\n+- Extensions are optional — consumers can ignore them\n+- Extensions are type-safe — keyed by provider name\n+- Extensions don't affect Gateway logic — pass-through only\n+- Model Discovery (S1.12) advertises available extensions per model\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Streaming Format\n+\n+Gateway normalizes streaming events to a unified SSE format.\n+\n+**Event types**:\n+\n+| Event | Description |\n+|-------|-------------|\n+| `delta` | Content chunk (text, tool_call) |\n+| `usage` | Final usage metrics (last event before done) |\n+| `done` | Stream completion |\n+| `error` | Error occurred |\n+\n+**Delta event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: delta\n+data: {\n+  type: \"text_delta\" | \"tool_call_delta\",\n+  index: 0,           // content block index\n+  text?: \"...\",       // for text_delta\n+  tool_call?: {...}   // for tool_call_delta\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Usage event** (always emitted before done):\n+```plaintext\n+event: usage\n+data: {\n+  prompt_tokens: 100,\n+  completion_tokens: 50,\n+  total_tokens: 150\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Done event**:\n+```plaintext\n+event: done\n+data: {\n+  finish_reason: \"stop\" | \"tool_calls\" | \"length\" | \"content_filter\",\n+  metadata: { model: \"gpt-4\", provider: \"openai\", latency_ms: 234, request_id: \"...\" },\n+  extensions: { ... }\n+}\n+```\n+\n+**Normalization**:\n+- All providers mapped to same event types\n+- `tool_calls` always streamed after text (consistent ordering)\n+- `usage` always in final chunk (not deltas)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| FileStorage | Fetch input media by URL, store generated content |\n+| Credential Resolver | API keys for providers |\n+| Type Registry | Read GTS schemas by ID (tool definitions) |\n+| Usage Tracker | Token/cost reporting |\n+| Hook System | `llm.pre_call`, `llm.post_response` interceptors |\n+| Audit | Request/response logging |\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"As we discussed, here could be also LLM Registry, that tells LLM Gateway if model is present (and loaded). If a mode not loaded, we can support JIT (Just-in-time) model load like in LM Studio, in this case LLM Gateway will need to wait and report client some model load progress.. need to think about it","created_at":"2026-01-18T11:58:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-18T11:58:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702355721","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702355721"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2702355721"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2702355721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":68,"original_line":226,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":226,"position":68,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788800","pull_request_review_id":3678114777,"id":2704788800,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hN81A","diff_hunk":"@@ -102,18 +102,19 @@ Provide conversational capabilities (chat messages, conversation history) as a c\n - TODO: API link\n - TODO: SDK link\n \n-### Models Registry\n+### Model Registry\n #### Responsibility\n-Maintain a catalog of available models (local/remote), including metadata, capabilities, and compatibility for runtime selection.\n+Maintain a catalog of available models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.","path":"docs/MODULES.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"835ed5bc25cbbdd8c804f325fd3d9f4a87f1061c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Hyphenate compound adjectives for consistency.**\n\nThese read as compound modifiers; hyphenation improves clarity in documentation.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Proposed edits</summary>\n\n```diff\n-#### Responsibility\n-Maintain a catalog of available models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+#### Responsibility\n+Maintain a catalog of available models with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n\n-Provide unified access to multiple LLM providers with multimodal support, tool calling, and enterprise governance.\n+Provide unified access to multiple LLM providers with multimodal support, tool calling, and enterprise-governance controls.\n\n-Store and retrieve files and media for LLM Gateway (input media, generated content).\n+Store and retrieve files and media for LLM Gateway (input-media assets, generated content).\n\n-GTS schema storage service for tool definitions and contracts.\n+GTS schema-storage service for tool definitions and contracts.\n\n-Centralized gateway for external API calls with credentials injection, reliability, and observability.\n+Centralized gateway for external-API calls with credentials injection, reliability, and observability.\n```\n</details>\n\n\nAlso applies to: 139-139, 262-262, 436-436, 641-641\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@docs/MODULES.md` around lines 106 - 107, Hyphenate compound adjectives in the\nsentence \"Maintain a catalog of available models with tenant-level availability\nand approval workflow\" (e.g., change to \"tenant-level availability and\napproval-workflow\" or better \"approval-workflow\" -> \"approval-workflow\"\ndepending on preferred noun usage) and apply the same hyphenation pattern to the\nother similar lines mentioned (the sentences at the other occurrences that use\ncompound modifiers), ensuring compound modifiers like \"tenant level\" and\n\"approval workflow\" are consistently written as \"tenant-level\" and\n\"approval-workflow\" (or adjust to \"approval workflow\" -> \"approval-workflow\"\nwhere it functions as a modifier).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:30:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T13:31:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2704788800","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788800"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2704788800"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788800/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":106,"original_start_line":106,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":107,"original_line":107,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":8,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788802","pull_request_review_id":3678114777,"id":2704788802,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hN81C","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@\n+# Type Registry\n+\n+GTS schema storage service.\n+\n+## LLM Gateway Usage\n+\n+- Resolve tool schemas by ID for function calling\n+\n+## Documentation\n+\n+- [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) — Scenarios for LLM Gateway","path":"modules/type_registry/README.md","commit_id":"835ed5bc25cbbdd8c804f325fd3d9f4a87f1061c","original_commit_id":"835ed5bc25cbbdd8c804f325fd3d9f4a87f1061c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix PRD link description to match Type Registry.**\n\nLine 11 labels the PRD as “Scenarios for LLM Gateway,” but this README is for Type Registry. Suggest updating the description to avoid confusion.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-- [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) — Scenarios for LLM Gateway\n+- [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) — Scenarios for Type Registry\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) — Scenarios for Type Registry\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/type_registry/README.md` at line 11, Update the link description for\n[PRD.md] in the README to refer to the Type Registry rather than “Scenarios for\nLLM Gateway” — replace the current label with something like “PRD — Type\nRegistry” or “PRD: Type Registry” so the README correctly describes the linked\ndocument.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:30:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T13:31:00Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2704788802","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788802"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2704788802"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704788802/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":11,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":11,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2708216904","pull_request_review_id":3682031449,"id":2708216904,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hbBxI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>HP: pre_call(request)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: request_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor\n+\n+After receiving response, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify response.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW->>HP: post_response(response)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: response_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.6 Per-Tenant Budget Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway checks budget before execution via Usage Plugin. Rejects if exhausted, reports actual usage after completion.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant UP as Usage Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>UP: check_budget\n+    alt Budget exhausted\n+        UP-->>GW: denied\n+        GW-->>C: budget_exceeded\n+    else Budget available\n+        UP-->>GW: ok\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW->>UP: report_usage\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.7 Request Cancellation\n+\n+Consumer can cancel in-progress request. Gateway propagates cancellation to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    C->>GW: cancel(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Cancel\n+    OB->>P: Cancel\n+    GW-->>C: cancelled\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.8 Rate Limiting\n+\n+Gateway enforces rate limits at tenant and user levels. Rejects requests exceeding limits.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>GW: Check rate limits\n+    alt Limit exceeded\n+        GW-->>C: rate_limited\n+    else Within limits\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P3 — Optimization\n+\n+### [ ] S3.1 Cost-Aware Routing\n+\n+When multiple providers can serve request, Gateway selects based on cost and latency optimization.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.2 Embeddings Batching\n+\n+Gateway batches embedding requests within time window for efficiency. No cross-tenant batching. Supports partial failure reporting.\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"3b93f215ebe50c5fb6b437fc065298a011ccd8f0","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Specify partial batch failure response format.**\n\nLine 661 mentions \"Supports partial failure reporting\" but doesn't define the response structure. A past review requested specification of:\n- HTTP status code for partial failures (200 with mixed results, or 207 Multi-Status?)\n- Response structure: array with successful embeddings and error objects?\n- Error object format: RFC 9457 within array elements?\n- Request-to-response ordering preservation\n\nExample structure might be:\n```\n{\n  \"results\": [\n    { \"index\": 0, \"embedding\": [...] },\n    { \"index\": 1, \"error\": {...} },\n    { \"index\": 2, \"embedding\": [...] }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": { \"succeeded\": 2, \"failed\": 1 }\n}\n```\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 659 - 662, The \"S3.2 Embeddings\nBatching\" section must explicitly define the partial-failure response: state the\nchosen HTTP status (recommend 207 Multi-Status or note if using 200 with mixed\nresults), define a top-level response object with a \"results\" array where each\nelement preserves request ordering and contains an \"index\" (original request\nposition) and either an \"embedding\" (on success) or an \"error\" object (on\nfailure), reference RFC 9457 for the error object shape and required fields, and\ninclude a \"summary\" object with succeeded/failed counts; update the prose in the\nS3.2 section to list these field names (\"results\", \"index\", \"embedding\",\n\"error\", \"summary\") and explicitly state ordering preservation and\npartial-success semantics.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-20T12:49:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-20T12:49:16Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2708216904","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2708216904"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2708216904"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2708216904/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":659,"original_start_line":659,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":662,"original_line":662,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":662,"position":662,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038870","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038870,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8IW","diff_hunk":"@@ -33,3 +33,4 @@ logs\n \n # Code coverage reports\n /coverage/\n+CLAUDE.local.md","path":".gitignore","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Clarify scope of `CLAUDE.local.md` ignore pattern.**\n\nLine 36 ignores a root-level `CLAUDE.local.md`, not `coverage/CLAUDE.local.md`. If the intent is to ignore the coverage artifact, scope it under `/coverage/`; otherwise, please confirm that a root-level file is intended.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested adjustment (if coverage-scoped)</summary>\n\n```diff\n /coverage/\n-CLAUDE.local.md\n+/coverage/CLAUDE.local.md\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n/coverage/\n/coverage/CLAUDE.local.md\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn @.gitignore around lines 35 - 36, The .gitignore currently has\n\"CLAUDE.local.md\" which ignores a root-level file; if you meant to ignore the\nfile inside the coverage folder, update the pattern to\n\"coverage/CLAUDE.local.md\" (or \"/coverage/CLAUDE.local.md\" to anchor to repo\nroot) so it's scoped to the coverage artifact; otherwise, confirm the root-level\nignore is intentional and add a short comment above the line explaining why the\ntop-level CLAUDE.local.md should be ignored.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038870","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038870"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038870"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038870/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":35,"original_start_line":35,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":36,"original_line":36,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":4,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038876","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038876,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8Ic","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Document the normalized API contract specification.**\n\nThe PRD states Gateway provides \"unified access\" and lists core capabilities, but the actual normalized request/response schemas aren't documented. Past reviews requested this specification.\n\nAdd a dedicated section defining:\n- Request format (message structure, content types, parameters like `model`, `temperature`, `max_tokens`, `streaming`)\n- Response format (completion structure, choices, metadata fields)\n- Streaming event format (SSE event types, data payloads for partial/completion/error)\n- Tool call/result schema (normalized invocation format)\n- Usage metadata structure (token counts, cost, latency)\n- Error response format (structured error object with code, type, message, details)\n\nThis contract is essential for consumers to implement against the Gateway independently of provider differences.\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 10 - 20, Add a dedicated\n\"Normalized API Contract\" section to the PRD that defines the canonical\nrequest/response/streaming/tool/error/usage schemas so consumers can implement\nagainst the Gateway; explicitly document the request format (message array,\ncontent types, and parameters like model, temperature, max_tokens, streaming),\nthe response format (completion object, choices array, metadata fields), the\nstreaming SSE event types and payloads for partial/completion/error, the\nnormalized tool invocation/result schema, the usage metadata structure (token\ncounts, cost, latency), and the structured error response (code, type, message,\ndetails) and include small examples for each to make the contract unambiguous\nfor implementers.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038876","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038876"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038876"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038876/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":10,"original_start_line":10,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038880","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038880,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8Ig","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add FileStorage error handling specifications.**\n\nLines reference FileStorage for media input/output but don't specify error handling. Past reviews flagged this gap across multiple scenarios (S1.4, S1.6, S1.8, S1.13).\n\nDocument error cases:\n- Service unavailable (503): Gateway response code, retry behavior\n- File not found / invalid URL (404): Error code and message structure\n- File size exceeds limits (413): Error code, max allowed size\n- Network fetch failures (502): Error code, retry policy\n\nSpecify:\n- HTTP status codes returned to consumer for each failure mode\n- Response structure (`error`, `code`, `message` fields)\n- Retry behavior (e.g., exponential backoff with jitter for transient 503/502, no retry for 404/413)\n- Maximum retry attempts\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 23 - 33, The PRD's Content\nModel references FileStorage but lacks explicit error-handling specs; update the\ndocument to enumerate failure modes for FileStorage interactions (service\nunavailable 503, file not found/invalid URL 404, payload too large 413, network\nfetch failures 502) and for each state specify the HTTP status the Gateway will\nreturn, the consumer response schema containing fields error, code and message,\nthe retry policy (no retry for 404/413, exponential backoff with jitter for\ntransient 502/503) and a concrete maximum retry attempts value (e.g., 3);\nreference the Gateway/FileStorage integration and scenarios S1.4, S1.6, S1.8,\nS1.13 so readers can map each error case to existing requirements.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038880","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038880"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038880"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038880/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":23,"original_start_line":23,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":33,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":33,"position":33,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038883","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038883,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8Ij","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add License Resolver to dependencies table.**\n\nPast review comments indicate License Resolver should be listed as a dependency. Without it, the PRD doesn't reflect the complete dependency graph.\n\nAdd License Resolver to the table with its role specification.\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 60 - 67, Update the\nDependencies table under the \"Dependencies\" section by adding a new row for\n\"License Resolver\" (alongside the existing entries like \"Model Registry\",\n\"Outbound API Gateway\", \"FileStorage\", \"Type Registry\"); set its role to a short\ndescriptive phrase such as \"License resolution and enforcement\" so the PRD\nreflects the complete dependency graph and previous review feedback.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038883","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038883"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038883"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":60,"original_start_line":60,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":67,"original_line":67,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":67,"position":67,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038884","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038884,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8Ik","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add FileStorage error handling to S1.4 Vision scenario.**\n\nThe scenario shows only the happy path. When `GW->FS: Fetch images` fails (service unavailable, not found, network error), the handling is unspecified.\n\nDocument:\n- Error cases: 503 (FileStorage unavailable), 404 (image not found), network failures\n- Gateway response to consumer for each error case\n- Retry behavior (if any)\n- Whether Gateway returns partial results if some images fetch successfully\n\nReference the FileStorage error handling specification added in the Content Model section.\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 148 - 168, Update the S1.4\nVision (Image Analysis) scenario to include FileStorage error handling:\nenumerate specific error cases (503 Service Unavailable, 404 Not Found,\nnetwork/timeouts) for the GW->FS: Fetch images step, define the Gateway's\nconsumer responses for each (HTTP status/code or chat error message), specify\nretry behavior (number of retries, backoff, idempotency rules) and whether GW\nreturns partial results when some images fetch successfully, and add a\ncross-reference to the FileStorage error handling spec in the Content Model;\nensure the section title \"S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\" and the sequence line\n\"GW->FS: Fetch images\" are updated accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038884","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038884"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038884"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":148,"original_start_line":148,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":168,"original_line":168,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":168,"position":168,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038887","pull_request_review_id":3697300998,"id":2721038887,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6iL8In","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Add FileStorage error handling to S1.6 Speech-to-Text scenario.**\n\nThe scenario shows only the happy path. When `GW->FS: Fetch audio` fails, the handling is unspecified.\n\nDocument:\n- Error cases: 503 (FileStorage unavailable), 404 (audio not found), 413 (file too large), network failures\n- Gateway response to consumer for each error case\n- Retry behavior\n- Audio-specific limits (max file size, supported formats)\n\nReference the FileStorage error handling specification added in the Content Model section.\n\nBased on past review comments.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md` around lines 196 - 216, Update the S1.6\nSpeech-to-Text scenario to include FileStorage error handling: enumerate\nspecific error cases (503 Service Unavailable, 404 Not Found, 413 Payload Too\nLarge, and generic network failures), state the Gateway's consumer-facing\nresponse for each case (HTTP status/code and user-friendly message), describe\nretry behavior (which errors are retriable and backoff policy) and reference the\nFileStorage error handling specification from the Content Model; also add\naudio-specific limits (max file size and supported formats) so the GW->FS: Fetch\naudio step and the overall S1.6 flow clearly show how the gateway handles\nfailures and limits.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:triton:puma -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-23T12:39:05Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038887","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038887"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2721038887"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038887/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":196,"original_start_line":196,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":216,"original_line":216,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":216,"position":216,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2721038890","pull_request