user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"what about statistics fetch and normalization? e.g. used tokens for model X on provider Y, etc\nOr will it be OAGW responsibility? If OAGW, then how OAGW would know how to extract stats metadata from the LLM request/response?","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:33:21Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729680873","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729680873"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729680873"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729680873/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":19,"original_line":19,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":19,"position":19,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729682782","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729682782,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is6de","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"What about callback / hooks invocation? If supported, how they will be called? I believe it must be a call to FaaS module ... but maybe in `ph-2`","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:34:22Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729682782","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729682782"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729682782"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729682782/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729684401","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729684401,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is62x","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please confirm it will be a FaaS call, or you have other ideas?","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:35:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729684401","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729684401"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729684401"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729684401/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":42,"original_line":42,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":42,"position":42,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729686904","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729686904,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is7d4","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd maybe consider to call Hook, Usage and Audit modules directly using Rust SDK, but these modules would have their own plugins. Otherwise many modules will have an \"audit\" plugin or \"usage\" plugin ...","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:36:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729686904","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729686904"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729686904"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729686904/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":56,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":56,"position":56,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729688283","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729688283,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is7zb","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"We can mention just \"add resolvers dependency\" - license resolver, tenant resolver, auth resolver","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:36:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729688283","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729688283"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729688283"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729688283/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":60,"original_start_line":60,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":67,"original_line":67,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038883,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":67,"position":67,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729689878","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729689878,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is8MW","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe we need to check LLM quota, license and user role first","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:37:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729689878","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729689878"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729689878"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729689878/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":92,"original_line":92,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":92,"position":92,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729690702","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729690702,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is8ZO","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Agree, valid comment","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:38:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729690702","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729690702"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729690702"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729690702/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":148,"original_start_line":148,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":168,"original_line":168,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038884,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":168,"position":168,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729691346","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729691346,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is8jS","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"agree","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:38:36Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729691346","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729691346"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729691346"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729691346/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":23,"original_start_line":23,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":33,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038880,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":33,"position":33,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729696572","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729696572,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is908","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Are we going to support local FaaS function calls?","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:41:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729696572","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729696572"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729696572"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729696572/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":319,"original_line":319,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":319,"position":319,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729698862","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729698862,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is-Yu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"can we please also explicit prefix for a feature like:\n\n```\n[ ] `ph-1` S1.1 Chat Completion\n```\n\nJust to avoid problems with content reshuffling and increase visibility for the long lists","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:42:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729698862","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729698862"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729698862"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729698862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":81,"original_line":81,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":81,"position":81,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729702723","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729702723,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is_VD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Should we have jobs executor right inside LLM gateway or we can use separate/standalone job executor? ","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:44:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729702723","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729702723"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729702723"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729702723/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":407,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":407,"position":407,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703235","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729703235,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is_dD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"agree, timeouts should be briefly covered","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:44:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729703235","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703235"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729703235"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703235/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":389,"original_start_line":389,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":418,"original_line":418,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038899,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":418,"position":418,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703860","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729703860,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6is_m0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Usage module, not plugin ...","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:45:08Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729703860","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703860"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729703860"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729703860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":453,"original_line":453,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":453,"position":453,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729705677","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729705677,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itADN","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Hook module...","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:45:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729705677","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729705677"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729705677"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729705677/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":521,"original_line":521,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":521,"position":521,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729708599","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729708599,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itAw3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>HP: pre_call(request)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: request_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor\n+\n+After receiving response, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify response.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW->>HP: post_response(response)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: response_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.6 Per-Tenant Budget Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway checks budget before execution via Usage Plugin. Rejects if exhausted, reports actual usage after completion.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant UP as Usage Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>UP: check_budget\n+    alt Budget exhausted\n+        UP-->>GW: denied\n+        GW-->>C: budget_exceeded\n+    else Budget available\n+        UP-->>GW: ok\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW->>UP: report_usage\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.7 Request Cancellation\n+\n+Consumer can cancel in-progress request. Gateway propagates cancellation to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    C->>GW: cancel(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Cancel\n+    OB->>P: Cancel\n+    GW-->>C: cancelled\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.8 Rate Limiting\n+\n+Gateway enforces rate limits at tenant and user levels. Rejects requests exceeding limits.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Can we add also provider limits in `ph-2`? Because there can be some terms in the contract from provider to vendor , not for individual tenants","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:47:18Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729708599","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729708599"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729708599"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729708599/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":627,"original_line":627,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":627,"position":627,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709219","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729709219,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itA6j","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>HP: pre_call(request)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: request_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor\n+\n+After receiving response, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify response.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW->>HP: post_response(response)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: response_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.6 Per-Tenant Budget Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway checks budget before execution via Usage Plugin. Rejects if exhausted, reports actual usage after completion.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant UP as Usage Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>UP: check_budget\n+    alt Budget exhausted\n+        UP-->>GW: denied\n+        GW-->>C: budget_exceeded\n+    else Budget available\n+        UP-->>GW: ok\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW->>UP: report_usage\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.7 Request Cancellation\n+\n+Consumer can cancel in-progress request. Gateway propagates cancellation to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    C->>GW: cancel(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Cancel\n+    OB->>P: Cancel\n+    GW-->>C: cancelled\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.8 Rate Limiting\n+\n+Gateway enforces rate limits at tenant and user levels. Rejects requests exceeding limits.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>GW: Check rate limits\n+    alt Limit exceeded\n+        GW-->>C: rate_limited\n+    else Within limits\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P3 — Optimization\n+\n+### [ ] S3.1 Cost-Aware Routing\n+\n+When multiple providers can serve request, Gateway selects based on cost and latency optimization.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.2 Embeddings Batching\n+\n+Gateway batches embedding requests within time window for efficiency. No cross-tenant batching. Supports partial failure reporting.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.3 Batch Processing\n+\n+Consumer submits batch of requests for async processing at reduced cost.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider batch APIs (OpenAI Batch API, Anthropic Message Batches).\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: create_batch(requests[])\n+    GW->>OB: Submit batch\n+    OB->>P: Provider batch API\n+    P-->>OB: batch_id\n+    OB-->>GW: batch_id\n+    GW-->>C: batch_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_batch(batch_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll batch\n+    P-->>OB: status + results[]\n+    OB-->>GW: status + results[]\n+    GW-->>C: status + results[]\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P4 — Enterprise\n+\n+### [ ] S4.1 Audit Events\n+\n+Gateway emits audit events via Audit Plugin for compliance: request started, completed, failed, blocked, fallback triggered.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Audit module","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:47:41Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729709219","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709219"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729709219"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709219/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":699,"original_line":699,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":699,"position":699,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709602","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729709602,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itBAi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>HP: pre_call(request)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: request_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor\n+\n+After receiving response, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify response.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW->>HP: post_response(response)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: response_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.6 Per-Tenant Budget Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway checks budget before execution via Usage Plugin. Rejects if exhausted, reports actual usage after completion.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant UP as Usage Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>UP: check_budget\n+    alt Budget exhausted\n+        UP-->>GW: denied\n+        GW-->>C: budget_exceeded\n+    else Budget available\n+        UP-->>GW: ok\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW->>UP: report_usage\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.7 Request Cancellation\n+\n+Consumer can cancel in-progress request. Gateway propagates cancellation to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    C->>GW: cancel(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Cancel\n+    OB->>P: Cancel\n+    GW-->>C: cancelled\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.8 Rate Limiting\n+\n+Gateway enforces rate limits at tenant and user levels. Rejects requests exceeding limits.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>GW: Check rate limits\n+    alt Limit exceeded\n+        GW-->>C: rate_limited\n+    else Within limits\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P3 — Optimization\n+\n+### [ ] S3.1 Cost-Aware Routing\n+\n+When multiple providers can serve request, Gateway selects based on cost and latency optimization.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.2 Embeddings Batching\n+\n+Gateway batches embedding requests within time window for efficiency. No cross-tenant batching. Supports partial failure reporting.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.3 Batch Processing\n+\n+Consumer submits batch of requests for async processing at reduced cost.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider batch APIs (OpenAI Batch API, Anthropic Message Batches).\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: create_batch(requests[])\n+    GW->>OB: Submit batch\n+    OB->>P: Provider batch API\n+    P-->>OB: batch_id\n+    OB-->>GW: batch_id\n+    GW-->>C: batch_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_batch(batch_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll batch\n+    P-->>OB: status + results[]\n+    OB-->>GW: status + results[]\n+    GW-->>C: status + results[]\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P4 — Enterprise\n+\n+### [ ] S4.1 Audit Events\n+\n+Gateway emits audit events via Audit Plugin for compliance: request started, completed, failed, blocked, fallback triggered.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Errors\n+\n+Gateway returns errors for:\n+- Model not found / not approved\n+- Validation errors\n+- Capability not supported\n+- Budget exceeded\n+- Rate limited\n+- Request/response blocked by hook\n+- Provider errors and timeouts\n+- Job not found / expired","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"agree","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:47:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729709602","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709602"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729709602"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729709602/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"start_line":703,"original_start_line":703,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":713,"original_line":713,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038905,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":713,"position":713,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729712092","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729712092,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itBnc","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@\n+# LLM Gateway\n+\n+Unified interface for LLM inference across providers. Stateless, pass-through design.\n+\n+## Capabilities\n+\n+### P1 — Core\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Chat completion (sync and streaming) |\n+| [ ] | Embeddings generation |\n+| [ ] | Vision (image analysis) |\n+| [ ] | Image generation |\n+| [ ] | Speech-to-text (transcription) |\n+| [ ] | Text-to-speech (synthesis) |\n+| [ ] | Video understanding |\n+| [ ] | Video generation |\n+| [ ] | Document understanding |\n+| [ ] | Tool/function calling |\n+| [ ] | Structured output (JSON mode) |\n+| [ ] | Model discovery |\n+| [ ] | Async jobs (long-running operations) |\n+| [ ] | Realtime audio (WebSocket) |\n+| [ ] | Usage tracking |\n+\n+### P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Provider fallback |\n+| [ ] | Retry with backoff |\n+| [ ] | Timeout enforcement |\n+| [ ] | Pre-call interceptor |\n+| [ ] | Post-response interceptor |\n+| [ ] | Per-tenant budget enforcement |\n+| [ ] | Request cancellation |\n+| [ ] | Rate limiting (tenant/user) |\n+\n+### P3 — Optimization\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Cost-aware routing |\n+| [ ] | Embeddings batching |\n+\n+### P4 — Enterprise\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Audit events |\n+\n+## Module Structure\n+\n+```plaintext\n+modules/llm_gateway/\n+├── llm_gateway-sdk/         # Public API traits, models, errors\n+├── llm_gateway-gw/          # Gateway implementation\n+└── plugins/\n+    ├── providers/\n+    │   ├── openai_plugin/       # OpenAI-compatible providers\n+    │   ├── anthropic_plugin/    # Claude API\n+    │   └── ollama_plugin/       # Local models via Ollama\n+    ├── hooks/","path":"modules/llm_gateway/README.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe we only need providers plugins","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:49:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729712092","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729712092"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729712092"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729712092/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":64,"original_line":64,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":64,"position":64,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729713681","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729713681,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itCAR","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,97 @@\n+# LLM Gateway\n+\n+Unified interface for LLM inference across providers. Stateless, pass-through design.\n+\n+## Capabilities\n+\n+### P1 — Core\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Chat completion (sync and streaming) |\n+| [ ] | Embeddings generation |\n+| [ ] | Vision (image analysis) |\n+| [ ] | Image generation |\n+| [ ] | Speech-to-text (transcription) |\n+| [ ] | Text-to-speech (synthesis) |\n+| [ ] | Video understanding |\n+| [ ] | Video generation |\n+| [ ] | Document understanding |\n+| [ ] | Tool/function calling |\n+| [ ] | Structured output (JSON mode) |\n+| [ ] | Model discovery |\n+| [ ] | Async jobs (long-running operations) |\n+| [ ] | Realtime audio (WebSocket) |\n+| [ ] | Usage tracking |\n+\n+### P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Provider fallback |\n+| [ ] | Retry with backoff |\n+| [ ] | Timeout enforcement |\n+| [ ] | Pre-call interceptor |\n+| [ ] | Post-response interceptor |\n+| [ ] | Per-tenant budget enforcement |\n+| [ ] | Request cancellation |\n+| [ ] | Rate limiting (tenant/user) |\n+\n+### P3 — Optimization\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Cost-aware routing |\n+| [ ] | Embeddings batching |\n+\n+### P4 — Enterprise\n+\n+| Done | Capability |\n+|------|------------|\n+| [ ] | Audit events |\n+\n+## Module Structure\n+\n+```plaintext\n+modules/llm_gateway/\n+├── llm_gateway-sdk/         # Public API traits, models, errors\n+├── llm_gateway-gw/          # Gateway implementation\n+└── plugins/\n+    ├── providers/\n+    │   ├── openai_plugin/       # OpenAI-compatible providers\n+    │   ├── anthropic_plugin/    # Claude API\n+    │   └── ollama_plugin/       # Local models via Ollama\n+    ├── hooks/\n+    │   ├── noop_hook_plugin/    # Default no-op (passthrough)\n+    │   └── ...                  # Custom hook plugins\n+    ├── usage/\n+    │   ├── noop_usage_plugin/   # Default no-op\n+    │   └── ...                  # Custom usage tracking\n+    └── audit/\n+        ├── noop_audit_plugin/   # Default no-op\n+        └── ...                  # Custom audit logging\n+```\n+\n+## Documentation\n+\n+- [PRD.md](docs/PRD.md) — Product requirements, scenarios with sequence diagrams\n+- ARCHITECTURE.md — Gateway + Plugin design, component interactions `TODO`\n+- API.md — SDK traits, request/response models, errors `TODO`\n+- PROVIDERS.md — Provider abstraction, capability matrix `TODO`\n+- CONFIGURATION.md — Gateway and plugin configuration `TODO`\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Module | Role |\n+|--------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Fetch input media, store generated content |\n+| Type Registry | Read GTS schemas by ID (tool definitions) |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/README.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followi