0221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"JFYI, we'll have a full spec in few days","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:51:15Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729716143","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729716143"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729716143"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729716143/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729717443","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729717443,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itC7D","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@\n+# Model Registry — PRD\n+\n+Model catalog with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Get Tenant Model","path":"modules/model_registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"No checkbox and phase prefix","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:51:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729717443","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729717443"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729717443"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729717443/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":7,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729720095","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729720095,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itDkf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@\n+# Model Registry — PRD\n+\n+Model catalog with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Get Tenant Model\n+\n+LLM Gateway resolves model availability for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: get_tenant_model(ctx, model_id)\n+    MR-->>LLM: model info + provider\n+```\n+\n+### S2 List Tenant Models\n+\n+LLM Gateway queries available models for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: list_tenant_models(ctx, filter)\n+    MR-->>LLM: models[]\n+```\n+\n+### S3 Model Discovery\n+\n+Registry polls providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider API\n+\n+    MR->>OB: GET /models\n+    OB->>P: Request (with credentials)\n+    P-->>OB: models[]\n+    OB-->>MR: models[]\n+    MR->>MR: Upsert + create pending approvals\n+```\n+\n+### S4 Model Approval\n+\n+New models require tenant admin approval before becoming available.","path":"modules/model_registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I believe we'll also need an upper-level tenant models whitelist/blacklist in `ph-2`, to support scenarios when a head office do not want departments to consume expensive models","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:53:28Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729720095","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729720095"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729720095"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729720095/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":52,"original_line":52,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":52,"position":52,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729722269","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729722269,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itEGd","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@\n+# Model Registry — PRD\n+\n+Model catalog with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Get Tenant Model\n+\n+LLM Gateway resolves model availability for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: get_tenant_model(ctx, model_id)\n+    MR-->>LLM: model info + provider\n+```\n+\n+### S2 List Tenant Models\n+\n+LLM Gateway queries available models for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: list_tenant_models(ctx, filter)\n+    MR-->>LLM: models[]\n+```\n+\n+### S3 Model Discovery\n+\n+Registry polls providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider API\n+\n+    MR->>OB: GET /models\n+    OB->>P: Request (with credentials)\n+    P-->>OB: models[]\n+    OB-->>MR: models[]\n+    MR->>MR: Upsert + create pending approvals\n+```\n+\n+### S4 Model Approval\n+\n+New models require tenant admin approval before becoming available.\n+\n+**Statuses**: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected` | `revoked`\n+\n+**Auto-approval**: configurable per tenant/provider\n+\n+### S5 Provider Health Monitoring\n+\n+Registry tracks provider health metrics for LLM Gateway routing decisions.","path":"modules/model_registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Is it going to be a periodic job or some inline method before some chat session start?","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:54:40Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729722269","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729722269"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729722269"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729722269/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":60,"original_line":60,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":60,"position":60,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729723029","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729723029,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itESV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@\n+# Model Registry — PRD\n+\n+Model catalog with tenant-level availability and approval workflow.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Get Tenant Model\n+\n+LLM Gateway resolves model availability for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: get_tenant_model(ctx, model_id)\n+    MR-->>LLM: model info + provider\n+```\n+\n+### S2 List Tenant Models\n+\n+LLM Gateway queries available models for current tenant.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant LLM as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    LLM->>MR: list_tenant_models(ctx, filter)\n+    MR-->>LLM: models[]\n+```\n+\n+### S3 Model Discovery\n+\n+Registry polls providers for available models via Outbound API Gateway.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider API\n+\n+    MR->>OB: GET /models\n+    OB->>P: Request (with credentials)\n+    P-->>OB: models[]\n+    OB-->>MR: models[]\n+    MR->>MR: Upsert + create pending approvals\n+```\n+\n+### S4 Model Approval\n+\n+New models require tenant admin approval before becoming available.\n+\n+**Statuses**: `pending` → `approved` | `rejected` | `revoked`\n+\n+**Auto-approval**: configurable per tenant/provider\n+\n+### S5 Provider Health Monitoring\n+\n+Registry tracks provider health metrics for LLM Gateway routing decisions.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider API\n+\n+    loop Health check interval\n+        MR->>OB: Health probe\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response / timeout / error\n+        OB-->>MR: latency, status\n+        MR->>MR: Update provider health state\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+Metrics: latency, error rate, availability status.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Module | Role |\n+|--------|------|\n+| Outbound API Gateway | Provider API calls |\n+| Tenant Resolver | Tenant context |","path":"modules/model_registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I'd mention settings service for hierarchical settings (e.g. whitelists/blacklists)","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:55:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729723029","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729723029"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729723029"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729723029/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":86,"original_line":86,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":86,"position":86,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729724162","pull_request_review_id":3708498723,"id":2729724162,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itEkC","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@\n+# Type Registry — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)","path":"modules/type_registry/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"@alizid10 , you'll need to build a spec, btw","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:55:47Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729724162","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729724162"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729724162"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729724162/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725533","pull_request_review_id":3708554949,"id":2729725533,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itE5d","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, good point! Grouping the resolvers together makes the dependencies table cleaner. Here's how you can add it:\n\n| Dependency | Role |\n|------------|------|\n| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n| **Resolvers** | **License, tenant, and auth resolution** |\n\nThis keeps the table concise while covering all three resolver types (License Resolver, Tenant Resolver, Auth Resolver) in a single entry.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.723Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.806Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:34.527Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725533","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725533"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725533"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725533/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":60,"original_start_line":60,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":67,"original_line":67,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038883,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":67,"position":67,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725540","pull_request_review_id":3708554962,"id":2729725540,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itE5k","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for confirming! Let me know if you'd like assistance documenting those error cases.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.723Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.806Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:34.527Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:32Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725540","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725540"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725540"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725540/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":23,"original_start_line":23,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":33,"original_line":33,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038880,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":33,"position":33,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725561","pull_request_review_id":3708554983,"id":2729725561,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itE55","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P2 — Reliability & Governance\n+\n+### [ ] S2.1 Provider Fallback\n+\n+When primary provider fails, Gateway automatically switches to fallback provider with matching capabilities.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P1 as Primary Provider\n+    participant P2 as Fallback Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P1: Request\n+    P1-->>OB: failure\n+    OB-->>GW: failure\n+    GW->>GW: Select fallback\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P2: Request\n+    P2-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Response (fallback indicated)\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.2 Retry with Backoff\n+\n+Transient failures trigger automatic retry with exponential backoff before fallback.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: transient error\n+    OB-->>GW: transient error\n+    GW->>GW: Wait (backoff)\n+    GW->>OB: Retry\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Success\n+    OB-->>GW: Success\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.3 Timeout Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway enforces timeout types:\n+- **Time-to-first-token (TTFT)**: max wait for initial response chunk\n+- **Total generation timeout**: max duration for complete response\n+\n+On timeout → retry → fallback → error.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\n+\n+Before sending to provider, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify request.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>HP: pre_call(request)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: request_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor\n+\n+After receiving response, Gateway invokes Hook Plugin. Plugin can allow, block, or modify response.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant HP as Hook Plugin\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW->>HP: post_response(response)\n+    alt Blocked\n+        HP-->>GW: blocked\n+        GW-->>C: response_blocked\n+    else Allowed/Modified\n+        HP-->>GW: proceed\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.6 Per-Tenant Budget Enforcement\n+\n+Gateway checks budget before execution via Usage Plugin. Rejects if exhausted, reports actual usage after completion.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant UP as Usage Plugin\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>UP: check_budget\n+    alt Budget exhausted\n+        UP-->>GW: denied\n+        GW-->>C: budget_exceeded\n+    else Budget available\n+        UP-->>GW: ok\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW->>UP: report_usage\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.7 Request Cancellation\n+\n+Consumer can cancel in-progress request. Gateway propagates cancellation to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    C->>GW: cancel(request_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Cancel\n+    OB->>P: Cancel\n+    GW-->>C: cancelled\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S2.8 Rate Limiting\n+\n+Gateway enforces rate limits at tenant and user levels. Rejects requests exceeding limits.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(...)\n+    GW->>GW: Check rate limits\n+    alt Limit exceeded\n+        GW-->>C: rate_limited\n+    else Within limits\n+        GW->>OB: Request\n+        OB->>P: Request\n+        P-->>OB: Response\n+        OB-->>GW: Response\n+        GW-->>C: Response\n+    end\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P3 — Optimization\n+\n+### [ ] S3.1 Cost-Aware Routing\n+\n+When multiple providers can serve request, Gateway selects based on cost and latency optimization.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.2 Embeddings Batching\n+\n+Gateway batches embedding requests within time window for efficiency. No cross-tenant batching. Supports partial failure reporting.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S3.3 Batch Processing\n+\n+Consumer submits batch of requests for async processing at reduced cost.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider batch APIs (OpenAI Batch API, Anthropic Message Batches).\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: create_batch(requests[])\n+    GW->>OB: Submit batch\n+    OB->>P: Provider batch API\n+    P-->>OB: batch_id\n+    OB-->>GW: batch_id\n+    GW-->>C: batch_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_batch(batch_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll batch\n+    P-->>OB: status + results[]\n+    OB-->>GW: status + results[]\n+    GW-->>C: status + results[]\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P4 — Enterprise\n+\n+### [ ] S4.1 Audit Events\n+\n+Gateway emits audit events via Audit Plugin for compliance: request started, completed, failed, blocked, fallback triggered.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Errors\n+\n+Gateway returns errors for:\n+- Model not found / not approved\n+- Validation errors\n+- Capability not supported\n+- Budget exceeded\n+- Rate limited\n+- Request/response blocked by hook\n+- Provider errors and timeouts\n+- Job not found / expired","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for agreeing! Looking forward to seeing the comprehensive error reference in the documentation. 🐰\n\n```\n    /)/)\n   (•ᴗ•)\n   />📋  Error docs looking good!\n```\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.723Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.806Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:34.527Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:33Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725561","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725561"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725561"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725561/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":703,"original_start_line":703,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":713,"original_line":713,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038905,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":713,"position":713,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725589","pull_request_review_id":3708555014,"id":2729725589,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itE6V","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for confirming! Adding brief timeout specifications (polling duration, intervals, and error codes) will help implementers understand the bounded behavior when Gateway polls internally. Looking forward to seeing those details in the PRD.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.723Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.806Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:34.527Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:34Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725589","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725589"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725589"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725589/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":389,"original_start_line":389,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":418,"original_line":418,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038899,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":418,"position":418,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725636","pull_request_review_id":3708555049,"id":2729725636,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6itE7E","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"`@Artifizer`, thank you for confirming! \n\nIf you'd like, I can help expand the S1.4 Vision scenario to include the FileStorage error handling details—covering the specific error cases (503, 404, network failures), Gateway responses, retry behavior, and partial result handling. Just let me know if you'd like me to draft those additions for you.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings used</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:56.723Z\nLearning: Create design.md only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, new external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance/migration complexity, or ambiguity requiring technical decisions\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types_registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:18:20.806Z\nLearning: Create `design.md` only if the change involves cross-cutting changes (multiple services/modules), new architectural patterns, external dependencies, significant data model changes, security/performance complexity, or migration complexity\n```\n\n---\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/simple_user_settings/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-26T20:17:34.527Z\nLearning: Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n```\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated reply by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:35Z","updated_at":"2026-01-26T23:56:35Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725636","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725636"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2729725636"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2729725636/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":148,"original_start_line":148,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":168,"original_line":168,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721038884,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":168,"position":168,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730756663","pull_request_review_id":3709689179,"id":2730756663,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixAo3","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# FileStorage — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)\n+\n+Media storage for LLM Gateway inputs and outputs.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Fetch Media by URL\n+\n+LLM Gateway fetches uploaded media (images, audio, video, documents) before sending to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway","path":"modules/file_storage/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"In case of using through the chat engine, we need to save the file to show it in the conversation history.  \r\nAnd llm-gw should have this file before every llm call in case of having a message with this file in the current request. \r\n\r\nI think that FE should talk about file storage and provide links to the chat engine and LLM-GW next.\r\n","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:10:24Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:10:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730756663","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730756663"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730756663"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730756663/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":13,"original_line":13,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2721597172,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":13,"position":13,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730757571","pull_request_review_id":3709690369,"id":2730757571,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixA3D","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# FileStorage — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)\n+\n+Media storage for LLM Gateway inputs and outputs.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Fetch Media by URL","path":"modules/file_storage/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, will be done when we will have a template","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:10:44Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:10:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730757571","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730757571"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730757571"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730757571/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":7,"original_line":7,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729671279,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":7,"position":7,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730767268","pull_request_review_id":3709701217,"id":2730767268,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixDOk","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# FileStorage — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)\n+\n+Media storage for LLM Gateway inputs and outputs.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Fetch Media by URL\n+\n+LLM Gateway fetches uploaded media (images, audio, video, documents) before sending to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    GW->>FS: fetch(url)\n+    FS-->>GW: content + metadata\n+```\n+\n+### S2 Store Generated Content\n+\n+LLM Gateway stores generated media (images, audio, video) and returns URL to consumer.","path":"modules/file_storage/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It may have different rules for different scenarios. This topic should be covered during the preparation of the PRD for the file storage component. Not all LLM-GW usage will come from the chat. We should support direct LLM calling as well.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:13:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:13:03Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730767268","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730767268"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730767268"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730767268/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":22,"original_line":22,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729673190,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":22,"position":22,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730770676","pull_request_review_id":3709705046,"id":2730770676,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixED0","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# FileStorage — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)\n+\n+Media storage for LLM Gateway inputs and outputs.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Fetch Media by URL\n+\n+LLM Gateway fetches uploaded media (images, audio, video, documents) before sending to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    GW->>FS: fetch(url)\n+    FS-->>GW: content + metadata\n+```\n+\n+### S2 Store Generated Content\n+\n+LLM Gateway stores generated media (images, audio, video) and returns URL to consumer.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    GW->>FS: store(content, metadata)\n+    FS-->>GW: url\n+```\n+\n+### S3 Get Metadata\n+\n+LLM Gateway checks file size before processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    GW->>FS: get_metadata(url)\n+    FS-->>GW: { size, mime_type }\n+```\n+","path":"modules/file_storage/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This topic should be covered during the preparation of the PRD for the file storage component. The TTL logic should be universal and cover not just the llm-gw scenario.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:13:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:13:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730770676","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730770676"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730770676"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730770676/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":45,"original_line":45,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729675124,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":45,"position":45,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730776792","pull_request_review_id":3709711624,"id":2730776792,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixFjY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,52 @@\n+# FileStorage — PRD (LLM Gateway Scope)\n+\n+Media storage for LLM Gateway inputs and outputs.\n+\n+## Scenarios\n+\n+### S1 Fetch Media by URL\n+\n+LLM Gateway fetches uploaded media (images, audio, video, documents) before sending to provider.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    GW->>FS: fetch(url)","path":"modules/file_storage/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The same. This PR is about llm-gw. Now we describe the requirements from llm-gw to file storage.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:15:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:15:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730776792","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730776792"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730776792"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730776792/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":16,"original_line":16,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729677011,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":16,"position":16,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730780985","pull_request_review_id":3709717571,"id":2730780985,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixGk5","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Please take a look as \"S1.16 Usage Tracking\"","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:16:09Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:16:09Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730780985","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730780985"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730780985"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730780985/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":19,"original_line":19,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729680873,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":19,"position":19,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730783862","pull_request_review_id":3709720950,"id":2730783862,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixHR2","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"please take a look\r\n### [ ] S2.4 Pre-Call Interceptor\r\n### [ ] S2.5 Post-Response Interceptor","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:16:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:16:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730783862","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730783862"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730783862"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730783862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":20,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729682782,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":20,"position":20,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730792342","pull_request_review_id":3709731113,"id":2730792342,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixJWW","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It may be a FaaS tool trought Type Registry schema.\r\nllm-gw do not call anything. It just respond to the caller, that llm wants to call the tool X with params Y.\r\n","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:18:39Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:18:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730792342","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730792342"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730792342"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730792342/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":42,"original_line":42,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729684401,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":42,"position":42,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730802908","pull_request_review_id":3709743791,"id":2730802908,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixL7c","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Yes, why not have audit, usage, and other such plugins everywhere? From my perspective, it will be more flexible if we can use NoOp plugins for such activities everywhere.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:21:01Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:21:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730802908","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730802908"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730802908"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730802908/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":56,"original_line":56,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729686904,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":56,"position":56,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730812615","pull_request_review_id":3709756184,"id":2730812615,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixOTH","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's not the responsibility of LLM-gw. I think it will be done in the agentic engine.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:22:58Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:22:58Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730812615","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730812615"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730812615"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730812615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":319,"original_line":319,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729696572,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":319,"position":319,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730831700","pull_request_review_id":3709779769,"id":2730831700,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixS9U","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It's very simple part of LLM-gw.\r\nAnd how it will works will be described in next documents.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:27:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:27:38Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730831700","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730831700"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730831700"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730831700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":407,"original_line":407,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729702723,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":407,"position":407,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730832990","pull_request_review_id":3709781569,"id":2730832990,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixTRe","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Waiting for template","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:27:53Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:27:54Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730832990","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730832990"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730832990"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730832990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":81,"original_line":81,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729698862,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":81,"position":81,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730838721","pull_request_review_id":3709789682,"id":2730838721,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ixUrB","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,713 @@\n+# LLM Gateway PRD\n+\n+## Notation\n+\n+- `[ ]` — not implemented\n+- `[x]` — implemented\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Overview\n+\n+LLM Gateway provides unified access to multiple LLM providers. Consumers interact with a single interface regardless of underlying provider.\n+\n+**Core capabilities**:\n+- Text generation (chat completion)\n+- Multimodal input/output (images, audio, video, documents)\n+- Embeddings generation\n+- Tool/function calling\n+- Structured output with schema validation\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Content Model\n+\n+Gateway supports multimodal content in messages:\n+- Text\n+- Images (input and output)\n+- Audio (input and output)\n+- Video (input and output)\n+- Documents\n+- Tool calls and results\n+\n+Media can be provided via FileStorage URL or inline data URL. Generated media is stored in FileStorage and returned as URL.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Tools\n+\n+Consumer can provide tools for function calling:\n+- Reference to Type Registry schema\n+- Inline schema definition\n+- Provider-compatible format\n+\n+Gateway resolves references, converts to provider format, and returns tool calls with preserved identifiers. Tool execution is consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Plugins\n+\n+Gateway supports configurable plugins with noop defaults:\n+\n+| Plugin | Purpose |\n+|--------|---------|\n+| Hook Plugin | Pre-call and post-response interception (moderation, PII, transformation) |\n+| Usage Plugin | Budget checks and usage reporting |\n+| Audit Plugin | Compliance event logging |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Dependencies\n+\n+| Dependency | Role |\n+|------------|------|\n+| Model Registry | Model catalog, availability checks |\n+| Outbound API Gateway | External API calls to providers |\n+| FileStorage | Media storage and retrieval |\n+| Type Registry | Tool schema resolution |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Design Principles\n+\n+**Stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history. Consumer provides full context with each request. Exception: temporary async job state.\n+\n+**Pass-through**: Gateway normalizes but does not interpret content. Tool execution and response parsing are consumer responsibility.\n+\n+---\n+\n+## P1 — Core\n+\n+### [ ] S1.1 Chat Completion\n+\n+Consumer sends messages, Gateway routes to provider based on model, returns response with usage.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(model, messages)\n+    GW->>GW: Resolve provider\n+    GW->>OB: Provider API call\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Response\n+    OB-->>GW: Response\n+    GW-->>C: Normalized response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.2 Streaming Chat Completion\n+\n+Same as S1.1, but response is streamed. Gateway normalizes provider events to unified format.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(stream=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Streaming request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    loop Content chunks\n+        P-->>OB: chunk\n+        OB-->>GW: chunk\n+        GW-->>C: normalized chunk\n+    end\n+    GW-->>C: usage + done\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.3 Embeddings Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text(s), Gateway returns vector embeddings.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: embed(model, input[])\n+    GW->>OB: Embeddings request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: vectors[]\n+    OB-->>GW: vectors[]\n+    GW-->>C: vectors[] + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.4 Vision (Image Analysis)\n+\n+Consumer sends message with image URLs. Gateway fetches from FileStorage, routes to vision-capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with image URLs)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch images\n+    FS-->>GW: image content\n+    GW->>OB: Request with images\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.5 Image Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates image, stores in FileStorage, returns URL.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(image gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated image\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated image\n+    GW->>FS: Store image\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.6 Speech-to-Text\n+\n+Consumer sends message with audio URL. Gateway fetches audio, returns transcription.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with audio URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch audio\n+    FS-->>GW: audio content\n+    GW->>OB: Transcription request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Transcription\n+    OB-->>GW: Transcription\n+    GW-->>C: Text response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.7 Text-to-Speech\n+\n+Consumer sends text. Gateway synthesizes audio, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Supports streaming mode.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(TTS model, text)\n+    GW->>OB: Synthesis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Audio\n+    OB-->>GW: Audio\n+    GW->>FS: Store audio\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.8 Video Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with video URL. Gateway fetches video, returns analysis.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with video URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch video\n+    FS-->>GW: video content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.9 Video Generation\n+\n+Consumer sends text prompt. Gateway generates video, stores in FileStorage, returns URL. Typically requires async mode due to long processing.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(video gen model, prompt)\n+    GW->>OB: Generation request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Generated video\n+    OB-->>GW: Generated video\n+    GW->>FS: Store video\n+    FS-->>GW: URL\n+    GW-->>C: Response with URL + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.10 Tool/Function Calling\n+\n+Consumer sends request with tool definitions. Gateway resolves schema references, converts to provider format. Model returns tool calls for consumer to execute.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant TR as Type Registry\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, tools)\n+    GW->>TR: Resolve schema references\n+    TR-->>GW: schemas\n+    GW->>OB: Request with tools\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: tool_calls[]\n+    OB-->>GW: tool_calls[]\n+    GW-->>C: Response with tool_calls[]\n+    Note over C: Consumer executes tools\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages + tool_results)\n+    GW->>OB: Request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Final response\n+    OB-->>GW: Final response\n+    GW-->>C: Response\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.11 Structured Output\n+\n+Consumer requests response matching JSON schema. Gateway validates response against schema. On validation failure, Gateway retries with error context.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages, response_schema)\n+    GW->>OB: Request with schema\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: JSON response\n+    OB-->>GW: JSON response\n+    GW->>GW: Validate against schema\n+    GW-->>C: Validated response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.12 Model Discovery\n+\n+Consumer queries available models and capabilities. Gateway delegates to Model Registry.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant MR as Model Registry\n+\n+    C->>GW: list_models(filter?)\n+    GW->>MR: list_tenant_models(filter)\n+    MR-->>GW: models[]\n+    GW-->>C: models[]\n+```\n+\n+Model info includes: capabilities, context limits, pricing.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.13 Document Understanding\n+\n+Consumer sends message with document URL. Gateway fetches document, routes to capable model.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant FS as FileStorage\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(messages with document URL)\n+    GW->>FS: Fetch document\n+    FS-->>GW: document content\n+    GW->>OB: Analysis request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: Analysis\n+    OB-->>GW: Analysis\n+    GW-->>C: Response + usage\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.14 Async Jobs\n+\n+Consumer can request async execution for long-running operations. Gateway returns job ID, consumer polls for result.\n+\n+Gateway abstracts provider behavior:\n+- Sync provider + async request → Gateway simulates job\n+- Async provider + sync request → Gateway polls internally\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: chat_completion(async=true)\n+    GW->>OB: Start request\n+    OB->>P: Request\n+    P-->>OB: job started\n+    OB-->>GW: job started\n+    GW-->>C: job_id\n+\n+    C->>GW: get_job(job_id)\n+    GW->>OB: Check status\n+    OB->>P: Poll\n+    P-->>OB: result\n+    OB-->>GW: result\n+    GW-->>C: result\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.15 Realtime Audio\n+\n+Bidirectional audio streaming via WebSocket for voice conversations.\n+\n+```mermaid\n+sequenceDiagram\n+    participant C as Consumer\n+    participant GW as LLM Gateway\n+    participant OB as Outbound API Gateway\n+    participant P as Provider\n+\n+    C->>GW: WebSocket connect\n+    GW->>OB: WebSocket connect\n+    OB->>P: WebSocket connect\n+\n+    loop Session\n+        C->>GW: audio chunk\n+        GW->>OB: audio chunk\n+        OB->>P: audio chunk\n+        P-->>OB: audio/text\n+        OB-->>GW: audio/text\n+        GW-->>C: audio/text\n+    end\n+\n+    C->>GW: close\n+    GW-->>C: usage summary\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+### [ ] S1.16 Usage Tracking\n+\n+Gateway reports usage after each request via Usage Plugin: tokens, cost estimate, latency, attribution (tenant, user, conversation, model).","path":"modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md","commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","original_commit_id":"10ead9a75b24501956b240af80221e57ccc0c971","user":{"login":"pr0tey","id":1847966,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDc5NjY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1847966?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey","html_url":"https://github.com/pr0tey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pr0tey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Need to discuss and agree on terminology. From my perspective, a module is a huge part of the fabric. A plugin is a changeable part of the module's logic.","created_at":"2026-01-27T08:29:11Z","updated_at":"2026-01-27T08:29:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730838721","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730838721"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#discussion_r2730838721"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2730838721/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":453,"original_line":453,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2729703860,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":453,"position":453,"subject_type":"line"}],"source_reviews":[{"id":3664407188,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7aamqU","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 1**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/README.md`:\n- Around line 55-63: Update the README code block that starts with\n\"modules/llm_gateway/\" to include a language identifier by replacing the opening\ntriple backticks with ```plaintext (and keep the closing triple backticks\nunchanged); this ensures the tree listing (llm_gateway-sdk, llm_gateway-gw,\nplugins/openai_plugin, plugins/anthropic_plugin, plugins/ollama_plugin) is\nrendered with proper syntax highlighting.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-88`: **Consider following spec-driven development guidelines for this new module.**\n\nThis PR introduces a new module with extensive capabilities and architectural components. Based on learnings, new modules and architectural proposals should follow the project's spec-driven development workflow.\n\n\n\n\nThe verification script checks for `openspec/AGENTS.md` and `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`. If these files exist:\n1. **OpenSpec workflow**: Consider creating an OpenSpec change proposal to formally document the LLM Gateway architecture, requirements, and implementation phases\n2. **Module guidelines**: Follow any module creation conventions specified in `guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`\n\nThis approach helps:\n- Maintain consistency with project standards\n- Provide clear requirements before implementation\n- Enable better tracking of this significant architectural addition\n- Facilitate review by documenting design decisions\n\nIf the repository uses OpenSpec or similar spec-driven processes, this planning documentation would benefit from being formalized within that workflow.\n\nBased on learnings about new capabilities and architectural changes.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 971e292d79dfb0adafee33704534fd0036f21d35 and c45c0513e9607ffe3e60bd626baacda72f1288d8.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (1)</summary>\n\n* `modules/llm_gateway/README.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📓 Common learnings</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:36.009Z\nLearning: When a request mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan), or introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work, open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n```\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:14.316Z\nLearning: Always open `@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md` to learn about how to create a new module\n```\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md</summary>\n\n55-55: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`67-71`: **Verify that referenced documentation files exist or are planned.**\n\nThe README references five documentation files in `modules/llm_gateway/docs/` that should either exist in this PR or be tracked for creation:\n- SCENARIOS.md\n- ARCHITECTURE.md\n- API.md\n- PROVIDERS.md\n- CONFIGURATION.md\n\nEnsure these files are either included in this PR or documented as TODOs/planned work.\n\n\n\nRun the verification script above to check which files exist. If any are missing, consider either:\n1. Adding them to this PR (since the title mentions \"add SCENARIOS\")\n2. Creating follow-up issues to track their creation\n3. Marking them as TODO in the README if they're placeholders\n\n---\n\n`7-52`: **Comprehensive capability matrix shows good planning.**\n\nThe structured breakdown of capabilities into priority levels (P1-P4) provides excellent clarity on the module's scope and implementation roadmap. The progression from core functionality through enterprise features is well-organized.\n\n---\n\n`73-88`: **Dependencies and consumers are clearly documented.**\n\nThe explicit listing of module dependencies and consumers provides valuable context for understanding the LLM Gateway's role in the broader system architecture. This will help with integration planning and dependency management.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3664407188","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3664407188"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T08:22:05Z","commit_id":"c45c0513e9607ffe3e60bd626baacda72f1288d8"},{"id":3666204708,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7ahdgk","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 2**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md`:\n- Around line 234-280: The S1.2 \"Client disconnect → persist partial response\"\nedge case contradicts the Gateway's stateless design; update the scenario to\nremove or reword it so persistence is explicitly delegated to the Chat Engine or\nanother downstream component. Specifically, in the S1.2 Streaming Chat\nCompletion section (and any other streaming edge case lists), replace or clarify\nthe client-disconnect bullet to state that the Gateway will stop streaming and\nemit an appropriate SSE error/close event, and that any persistence of partial\nresponses must be handled by the Chat Engine (or a named downstream service)\nrather than the Gateway.\n\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/README.md`:\n- Around line 67-71: The README currently links to ARCHITECTURE.md, API.md,\nPROVIDERS.md, and CONFIGURATION.md which are not present in this PR; update\nmodules/llm_gateway/README.md to either remove these broken links or replace\nthem with TODO placeholders (e.g., \"ARCHITECTURE.md — TODO: add architecture\ndoc\") for each missing file so the README does not contain dead references;\nensure the remaining valid link SCENARIOS.md stays unchanged.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`55-63`: **Add language identifier to code block.**\n\nThe module structure code block should specify `plaintext` as the language identifier for proper rendering.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`680-741`: **Async job storage exceeds \"mappings\" described in design principles.**\n\nThe async jobs implementation (especially lines 716-718, 726-727) stores complete results when simulating async behavior for sync providers, not just \"mappings\" as stated in the design principle (line 190). The gateway caches full responses, manages TTLs, and provides job status endpoints—this is substantial state management beyond temporary ID mappings.\n\nConsider updating line 190 to accurately reflect that \"async job state (including mappings and cached results)\" is stored, so the design principles align with the implementation details.\n\n---\n\n`130-130`: **Add blank lines around tables for better formatting.**\n\nThree tables lack surrounding blank lines (lines 130, 770, 987), which affects markdown rendering. Adding blank lines before and after these tables improves readability.\n\n\n\nBased on static analysis hints.\n\n\nAlso applies to: 770-770, 987-987\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 1684f3907b2143d2484158961d8b0c4bc948e40c and 9a18759ffdf8f5214c073effe09f4d428bc8753b.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `modules/llm_gateway/README.md`\n* `modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧠 Learnings (1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📚 Learning: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z</summary>\n\n```\nLearnt from: CR\nRepo: hypernetix/hyperspot PR: 0\nFile: modules/system/types-registry/openspec/AGENTS.md:0-0\nTimestamp: 2026-01-14T17:18:55.263Z\nLearning: Create design.md only when the change is cross-cutting, introduces new architecture patterns, adds external dependencies, makes significant data model changes, involves security/performance complexity, or has ambiguity\n```\n\n**Applied to files:**\n- `modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md`\n\n</details>\n\n</details><details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md</summary>\n\n55-55: Fenced code blocks should have a language specified\n\n(MD040, fenced-code-language)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md</summary>\n\n130-130: Tables should be surrounded by blank lines\n\n(MD058, blanks-around-tables)\n\n---\n\n770-770: Tables should be surrounded by blank lines\n\n(MD058, blanks-around-tables)\n\n---\n\n987-987: Tables should be surrounded by blank lines\n\n(MD058, blanks-around-tables)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (10)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/README.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-52`: **Well-structured capabilities overview.**\n\nThe P1-P4 prioritization framework clearly organizes features from core capabilities through enterprise concerns. The checklist format makes it easy to track implementation progress.\n\n---\n\n`73-89`: **Clear dependency and consumer relationships.**\n\nThe tables effectively document the module's integration points, making it easy to understand the system context and usage patterns.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md (8)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-44`: **Well-defined content format with good extensibility.**\n\nThe typed block approach for content provides a clean, extensible structure that handles diverse media types uniformly. Supporting both FileStorage URLs and data URLs (line 38) gives consumers flexibility in how they provide media.\n\n---\n\n`46-122`: **Solid normalization strategy with provider flexibility.**\n\nThe response format strikes a good balance between providing consistent normalized fields (content, usage, metadata) while allowing provider-specific features through extensions. The principle that \"extensions don't affect Gateway logic\" (line 120) maintains the pass-through design.\n\n---\n\n`168-172`: **Verify feasibility of streaming normalization guarantees.**\n\nThe claim that \"tool_calls always streamed after text (consistent ordering)\" and consistent usage placement may be challenging to achieve across providers. As noted in past discussions, different providers stream tools in varying formats, orders, and timing (some interleaved with text, some as separate chunks, some with usage deltas vs. final totals). Implementing this level of normalization might require significant buffering and reordering logic, which could conflict with the stated \"pass-through\" design principle (line 192) and add latency to streaming responses.\n\n\n\nConsider documenting the buffering/reordering strategy if this normalization is essential, or relax the guarantee to \"best-effort ordering\" to maintain true pass-through behavior.\n\n---\n\n`188-193`: **Design principles clearly articulated.**\n\nThe stateless and pass-through principles establish clear boundaries for the Gateway's responsibilities. Explicitly noting the async job exception (line 190) helps set expectations about where state is permitted.\n\n---\n\n`196-229`: **Solid error handling with industry standard format.**<!-- [scratchpad_start]\n[task review_file_2/2 section_5/10]\nReview lines 196-229: Error handling (continued)\n\n[observations]\n- RFC 9457 search results confirm it's a valid, recent standard (published July 2023)\n- RFC 9457 obsoletes RFC 7807\n- It's an IETF Standards Track document\n- Widely adopted in frameworks (Spring, .NET, etc.)\n\n[analysis]\n- Using RFC 9457 is appropriate and current\n- Error code table is comprehensive\n- Example response follows the standard correctly\n\n[actions]\n- Include search results in comment to validate the choice\n\n[scratchpad_end] -->\n\nAdopting RFC 9457 (published July 2023, obsoletes RFC 7807) provides a standardized, machine-readable error format. The comprehensive error code table covers key failure scenarios, and the GTS namespacing pattern enables versioned error types.\n\n---\n\n`550-789`: **Comprehensive P1 scenario coverage.**\n\nThe scenarios provide clear workflows for core capabilities including tool calling with GTS Schema integration (S1.10), structured output validation (S1.11), model discovery with capability advertising (S1.12), and WebSocket-based realtime audio (S1.15). The sequence diagrams and examples effectively illustrate each workflow.\n\n---\n\n`791-1001`: **Well-designed reliability and governance features.**\n\nThe P2 scenarios provide robust operational patterns. Provider fallback with transparent metadata (lines 813-817), multi-level rate limiting with standard headers (line 999), and hook-based interceptors (S2.4-S2.5) demonstrate good production-readiness design.\n\n---\n\n`1003-1041`: **Optimization and enterprise scenarios appropriately scoped.**\n\nCost-aware routing (S3.1) and embeddings batching (S3.2) provide intelligent optimizations, while audit events (S4.1) cover compliance needs. The constraint against cross-tenant batching (line 1023) is a good security practice.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3666204708","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3666204708"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-15T15:31:03Z","commit_id":"9a18759ffdf8f5214c073effe09f4d428bc8753b"},{"id":3670156185,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7awiOZ","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md`:\n- Around line 342-374: Update the S1.4 (and related S1.6, S1.8, S1.13) scenario\ndocs to explicitly document FileStorage fetch failure handling: define specific\nerror cases (service unavailable, invalid URL/404, missing file, oversized file)\nand map them to response behavior and status codes (e.g., use existing\nprovider_error for provider-side textual failures but introduce a new error code\nmedia_fetch_failed for client-facing fetch failures with subcodes like\nmedia_fetch_unavailable, media_fetch_not_found, media_fetch_too_large); specify\nexpected HTTP status (e.g., 503 for unavailable, 404 for missing, 400/413 for\nvalidation/size) and sample response shape including where usage and provider\nmetadata appear, and update the sequence diagrams/text in S1.4 to show GW -> C\nerror flow when FileStorage returns these errors so all scenarios referencing\nFileStorage URL fetches reference the same media_fetch_failed semantics.\n- Around line 1074-1081: Update the S3.2 Embeddings Batching scenario to\nexplicitly define the partial-failure response: state that the gateway returns\nHTTP 207 Multi-Status for any partial failures and a JSON array of per-request\nresults (preserve request order) where each element includes the request id and\neither an \"embedding\" field with the vector or an \"error\" object following RFC\n9457 (include \"type\", \"title\", \"status\", and optional \"detail\" and \"instance\");\nalso document that fully successful batches return 200 with the same array shape\n(all elements containing \"embedding\"), and add an optional top-level \"summary\"\nobject with counts (succeeded, failed) to help consumers handle results\nprogrammatically; update the text under \"S3.2 Embeddings Batching\" and replace\nthe ambiguous note \"Partial failure → return error per failed item\" with this\nexplicit schema description.\n- Line 503: Clarify the \"Streaming\" bullet by specifying the transport and\nresponse shape: state whether streaming uses SSE (like S1.2) or WebSocket (like\nS1.15) and add a short example of the stream messages—e.g., per-chunk event\ncontaining binary/base64 audio payload plus timestamp/seq id and a final event\ncontaining metadata (duration, sample-rate, format) and an optional storage URL\n(explicitly \"none\" if not stored). Update the \"Streaming\" line to reference the\nchosen protocol and show the final-message fields (metadata keys such as\nduration, sample_rate, format, stored_url:null) so consumers know how to\nassemble and detect completion.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`73-76`: **Consider documenting governance implications explicitly.**\n\nThe table distinguishes when to use `schema_id` (with \"governance required\") versus inline schemas, but the actual governance enforcement mechanism isn't specified. Consider adding a note about whether schema_id tools are subject to additional validation, logging, or policy enforcement compared to inline tools.\n\n---\n\n`86-88`: **Clarify response format for non-chat endpoints.**\n\nLine 88 states that only `chat_completion` responses are fully normalized, while other endpoints have \"endpoint-specific response structures.\" Consider adding a brief note or cross-reference indicating where these endpoint-specific formats are documented (e.g., API.md) to avoid ambiguity.\n\n---\n\n`787-789`: **Consider documenting TTL guidance for async job storage.**\n\nLine 789 mentions \"configurable TTL\" for job expiry, but provides no default value or guidance. Consider adding:\n- Recommended default TTL (e.g., 24 hours, 7 days)\n- Factors affecting TTL selection (e.g., storage cost, use case patterns)\n- Whether different job types (video generation vs embedding) might have different TTLs\n\nThis would help operators make informed configuration decisions.\n\n---\n\n`1055-1055`: **Consider documenting rate limit headers in Response Format section.**\n\nLine 1055 mentions standard rate limit headers (`X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset`, `Retry-After`), but these aren't documented in the Response Format section (lines 86-162). Consider adding a subsection about standard HTTP headers that are always included in responses, not just in rate limit scenarios.\n\n---\n\n`1098-1098`: **Define content policy levels in detail.**\n\nLine 1098 mentions three audit content policy levels (`full | redacted | metadata_only`) but doesn't define what each includes or excludes. Consider adding a specification:\n- **full**: Complete request/response payloads?\n- **redacted**: What is redacted (PII, user content, API keys in provider_hints)?\n- **metadata_only**: Which metadata fields (model, tokens, timestamp)?\n\nThis is important for compliance (GDPR, HIPAA) and helps tenants choose appropriate policies.\n\n---\n\n`36-38`: **Consider documenting data URL size limits.**\n\nLine 38 mentions data URLs are passed directly to providers. Consider documenting whether the Gateway enforces size limits on data URLs (e.g., max base64 payload size) to prevent:\n- Request body size exceeding reasonable limits\n- Memory issues from decoding large base64 strings\n- Provider-specific limits being exceeded\n\nThis is an optional operational safeguard.\n\n---\n\n`1-8`: **Consider adding a \"Scope & Non-Goals\" section.**\n\nThe document comprehensively covers LLM Gateway scenarios, but lacks an explicit scope definition. Consider adding a brief section before line 3 stating:\n- What is in scope (unified LLM API abstraction, normalization, routing)\n- What is explicitly out of scope (conversation state management, tool execution, prompt engineering, RAG, fine-tuning)\n\nThis helps readers quickly understand the Gateway's boundaries, especially given the \"Pass-through\" principle (line 233).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between aa038d978f23408610e53e037d80674d2c7a52ba and 329c72deb6f63ab6ae16dc8433fe4a8506cbc360.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `modules/llm_gateway/README.md`\n* `modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Files skipped from review due to trivial changes (1)</summary>\n\n* modules/llm_gateway/README.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/SCENARIOS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`209-212`: **Verify feasibility of tool_calls ordering guarantee.**\n\nLine 211 guarantees \"tool_calls always streamed after text (consistent ordering)\" across all providers. Past discussions (per learnings) noted that providers stream tools in different formats and orders. Enforcing this guarantee may require:\n- Buffering text and tool deltas until the Gateway can determine complete ordering\n- Reordering events from providers that stream tools before or interleaved with text\n- Additional latency and memory overhead\n\nConsider whether this strict ordering guarantee is necessary, or if consumers can handle flexible ordering with clear event indexing.\n\nBased on learnings and past review comments.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3670156185","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3670156185"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T10:36:58Z","commit_id":"329c72deb6f63ab6ae16dc8433fe4a8506cbc360"},{"id":3670893819,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7azWT7","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 4**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md`:\n- Line 503: Update the \"Streaming\" sentence to explicitly specify the transport\nand payload format: state whether streaming uses SSE (S1.2-style) or WebSocket\n(S1.15-style), define that each audio chunk event contains base64-encoded audio\nframes (or binary if using WebSocket), and describe the final \"done\"\nevent/message structure including metadata fields (duration, sample_rate,\nformat) and a stored_url field that is either a URL or null; reference the\nexisting \"Streaming\" line/section so the PRD entry replaces \"stream audio chunks\ndirectly (no storage)\" with this concrete protocol, chunk encoding, final\nmetadata, and stored_url behavior.\n- Around line 740-746: Update the PRD matrix and surrounding text for the\nGateway's handling of provider-side async jobs (the \"async=false\" + \"provider\nasync\" case) to specify a maximum internal polling timeout (e.g., 30s), the\nreturned error when exceeded (e.g., \"provider_timeout\" with guidance to retry\nusing async=true), and that the Gateway enforces a connection/polling timeout to\navoid resource exhaustion; also state whether the Gateway will automatically\nswitch to returning a job_id after the threshold (explicitly specify it will not\nauto-switch but will return the timeout error unless configured otherwise) so\nreaders know polling behavior, retry suggestion, and enforced connection timeout\npolicy.\n- Around line 1074-1081: Update S3.2 Embeddings Batching to explicitly specify\nthe partial-failure response format: define the HTTP status to return (recommend\n207 Multi-Status or 200 with documented mixed-results) and require a top-level\nobject containing a \"results\" array preserving request order where each element\nis either { \"index\": N, \"embedding\": [...] } or { \"index\": N, \"error\":\n<RFC-9457-style problem object> }, plus a \"summary\" object with counts (e.g.,\nsucceeded/failed); reference this format in the S3.2 section and note that\nordering must mirror the request indices so clients can correlate responses to\ninputs.\n- Around line 36-40: Update the PRD section describing Media input/output\n(around the FileStorage descriptions) to add explicit FileStorage error\nhandling: for service unavailable return 503 with a standard error JSON {error,\ncode:\"filestorage_unavailable\", message}, for not found return 404 with {error,\ncode:\"file_not_found\", message}, for file too large return 413 with {error,\ncode:\"file_too_large\", message, maxAllowedBytes}, and for network/fetch failures\nreturn 502 with {error, code:\"filestorage_bad_gateway\", message, upstreamError};\ndocument that Gateway will not retry client-supplied FileStorage URLs\nautomatically except for transient 503/502 with an exponential backoff capped at\n2 retries (log each attempt) and that scenarios S1.4, S1.6, S1.8, and S1.13\nshould reference this behavior and response schema so callers can handle errors\nuniformly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`231-231`: **Consider clarifying \"stateless\" with job state exception.**\n\nLine 231 states the Gateway is stateless but immediately includes an exception for async job state. While technically accurate (job state is temporary and bounded by TTL), this might confuse readers expecting pure statelessness.\n\nConsider rephrasing to emphasize that conversation state is externally managed while job orchestration state is ephemeral:\n\n> **Conversation-stateless**: Gateway does not store conversation history—consumers provide full message history with each request. Conversation state is managed by Chat Engine. **Job orchestration**: Async job mappings (gw_job_id → provider_job_id or cached results) are stored temporarily with configurable TTL for retrieval.\n\n---\n\n`646-666`: **Consider adding validation failure response example.**\n\nS1.11 describes structured output validation, and line 665 mentions returning `schema_validation_failed` with \"raw response in Problem extensions,\" but no example structure is provided.\n\nAdding a brief example would help consumers understand how to handle validation failures:\n\n```plaintext\n{\n  \"type\": \"https://errors.hyperspot.io/.../schema_validation_failed.v1\",\n  \"title\": \"Schema Validation Failed\",\n  \"status\": 422,\n  \"detail\": \"Response does not match provided JSON schema\",\n  \"extensions\": {\n    \"raw_response\": \"...\",\n    \"validation_errors\": [...]\n  }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n`823-831`: **Consider adding WebSocket message format examples.**\n\nThe WebSocket events table (lines 823-831) defines event types but lacks message format examples, unlike the SSE format section (lines 165-213) which provides detailed event structures.\n\nAdding message format examples for `audio_delta`, `text_delta`, `function_call`, and `session_end` would help consumers implement clients correctly, especially for binary audio chunk encoding.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 329c72deb6f63ab6ae16dc8433fe4a8506cbc360 and 77141627cc1b39e5c7e71bc096b2b1615deed89b.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `modules/llm_gateway/README.md`\n* `modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (1)</summary>\n\n* modules/llm_gateway/README.md\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/llm_gateway/docs/PRD.md (7)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`44-84`: **Well-structured tool format specification.**\n\nThe dual-format approach (schema_id reference vs inline schema) is clearly documented with appropriate use cases. The clarification that `tool_call.tool_id` preserves the original format (line 82) ensures proper round-tripping.\n\n---\n\n`86-162`: **Excellent normalization and extensions design.**\n\nThe response format specification demonstrates strong architectural thinking:\n- Clear normalization guarantees prevent consumer confusion\n- Extensions design (optional, provider-keyed, type-safe) balances flexibility with maintainability\n- The principle that \"Extensions don't affect Gateway logic\" (line 160) maintains clean separation of concerns\n\n---\n\n`165-213`: **Clear streaming format specification.**\n\nThe SSE event structure is well-designed:\n- Distinct event types prevent ambiguity\n- Usage always emitted before done (line 212) ensures consumers can reliably collect metrics\n- Normalization rules (lines 209-212) provide consistency across providers\n\n---\n\n`237-269`: **Robust error specification.**\n\nRFC 9457-compliant error format with comprehensive error codes covering validation, authorization, rate limiting, and provider failures. The example (lines 258-269) demonstrates proper structure including trace_id for observability.\n\n---\n\n`275-339`: **Core scenarios well-defined with clear diagrams.**\n\nS1.1-S1.3 provide comprehensive specifications:\n- S1.1 basic flow includes credential resolution\n- S1.2 properly delegates persistence to consumer (line 319), addressing previous design concerns\n- S1.3 supports both single and batch embeddings\n- Sequence diagrams enhance clarity\n\n---\n\n`846-1056`: **Comprehensive reliability and governance scenarios.**\n\nP2 scenarios demonstrate mature reliability patterns:\n- S2.1 fallback metadata (lines 868-872) enables transparent failover tracking\n- S2.2 retry logic properly distinguishes transient vs permanent failures (lines 900-901)\n- S2.4/S2.5 interceptor hooks (lines 911-962) provide extensibility for policy enforcement\n- S2.7 cancellation (lines 993-1016) covers all modalities (sync, streaming, async)\n- S2.8 rate limiting (lines 1041-1051) with tiered enforcement and standard headers\n\n---\n\n`1084-1097`: **Well-defined audit event specification.**\n\nS4.1 provides essential compliance features:\n- Event types (lines 1090-1096) cover key lifecycle points\n- Content policy options (line 1097) enable tenant-specific compliance requirements\n- Event naming convention (`llm.*`) follows observable pattern\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/245#pullrequestreview-3670893819","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/245","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberw