ough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a detailed `/health` JSON endpoint and a Kubernetes-style liveness `/healthz` endpoint to the API gateway; updates README to document the JSON health response and show a `curl` example for the liveness probe.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Health endpoints** <br> `modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs` | Registers both `/health` (detailed JSON) and `/healthz` (liveness) routes in router construction and REST capability setup; updates related debug logging. |\n| **Documentation** <br> `README.md` | Updates health check documentation to reflect the detailed JSON `/health` response and adds a Kubernetes-style liveness probe example using `/healthz`. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 1 (Trivial) | ⏱️ ~5 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I sniffed the routes, both small and spry,  \n> > /health speaks JSON, /healthz says hi,  \n> > Kubernetes nods with a cheerful ping,  \n> > Two little endpoints — how they make me sing!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                     |\n|     Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title accurately and specifically describes the main change: fixing README and adjusting health check endpoints to provide both detailed and simple liveness probes (/health and /healthz). |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                                                            |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n\n---\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Recent review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between a95d2e82661acea0b00d9b5af41f71694bac3315 and da6770a8da93b270c0b9159a321614109b086562.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (2)</summary>\n\n* `README.md`\n* `modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (2)</summary>\n\n* modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs\n* README.md\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3750466768/reactions","total_count