15:56:12Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T16:18:47Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nRenames the security context type from `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext` across crates and examples, swaps the binary serialization backend from `bincode` to `postcard`, and removes an advisory ignore entry (`RUSTSEC-2025-0141`) from `deny.toml`.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Root & workspace manifests** <br> `Cargo.toml`, `libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml` | Replaced `bincode` dependency entries with `postcard` (workspace-scoped where applicable). |\n| **Advisory policy** <br> `deny.toml` | Removed `RUSTSEC-2025-0141` from `[advisories.ignore]`. |\n| **Core security codec** <br> `libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs` | Renamed `SecurityCtx` → `SecurityContext`; replaced `bincode` APIs/errors with `postcard` (`PostcardError`); updated `encode_bin`/`decode_bin` signatures and error enums; removed legacy config helper. |\n| **Security public API & tests** <br> `libs/modkit-security/src/lib.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs` | Public API surface changed: removed `AccessScope`/`SecurityCtx`/`Subject`, added `Permission` and `SecurityContext`; tests migrated to `SecurityContext::builder()` and permission-based assertions. |\n| **Transport (gRPC) layer** <br> `libs/modkit-transport-grpc/src/lib.rs` | `attach_secctx()` and `extract_secctx()` signatures and docs updated to use `SecurityContext`; metadata encode/decode now uses `postcard`-based codec. |\n| **Examples — calculator SDKs** <br> `examples/oop-modules/calculator/.../src/api.rs`, `.../src/client.rs` | Replaced imports and parameter types `SecurityCtx` → `SecurityContext` in public traits and client implementations (e.g., `add()` signatures). |\n| **Examples — calculator_gateway** <br> `examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/.../src/api.rs`, `.../src/client.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/handlers.rs`, `.../src/domain/service.rs` | Updated imports and method/handler parameter types from `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext`; no behavioral changes beyond type rename and propagation. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n(omitted)\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I swapped the bins for swifter mail,  \n> Names hopped over every trail,  \n> Permissions bloom where scopes once stood,  \n> Small changes stitched across the wood—  \n> A rabbit cheers: build green without fail!\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning)</summary>\n\n|  Check name | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Resolution                                                                                                                                                                                                                     |\n| :---------: | :--------- | :-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Title check | ⚠️ Warning | The PR title 'Remove SecurityCtx from Calculator example' is misleading. The changeset encompasses far more than just the calculator example—it refactors the entire SecurityCtx/SecurityContext API across modkit-security, modkit-transport-grpc, and multiple calculator SDK/gateway implementations, plus replaces bincode with postcard. | Use a more accurate title reflecting the comprehensive nature of the changes, such as 'Migrate SecurityCtx to SecurityContext and replace bincode with postcard' or 'Refactor security context API and serialization backend'. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (2 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                          |\n| :----------------: | :------- | :----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                          |\n| Docstring Coverage | ✅ Passed | Docstring coverage is 100.00% which is sufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Recent nitpick comments</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`31-31`: **Consider adjusting initial capacity based on typical `SecurityContext` size.**\n\nThe initial capacity of 64 bytes may be undersized for `SecurityContext` instances with multiple permissions, potentially causing reallocation. However, since `to_allocvec` returns a new `Vec` that's then extended via `extend_from_slice`, the pre-allocation only saves space for the version byte.\n\n\nYou could simplify by removing the pre-allocation and constructing the final buffer more directly:\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Optional simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n pub fn encode_bin(ctx: &SecurityContext) -> Result<Vec<u8>, SecCtxEncodeError> {\n-    let mut buf = Vec::with_capacity(64);\n-    buf.push(SECCTX_BIN_VERSION);\n-\n     let payload = postcard::to_allocvec(ctx)?;\n-    buf.extend_from_slice(&payload);\n+    let mut buf = Vec::with_capacity(1 + payload.len());\n+    buf.push(SECCTX_BIN_VERSION);\n+    buf.extend_from_slice(&payload);\n \n     Ok(buf)\n }\n```\n</details>\n\nThis ensures exact allocation but trades off an extra capacity calculation. The current approach is fine if typical payloads are under 63 bytes.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Recent review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between e44a66edacdc43f5b4cfa56fab55fc2026e03dde and 849b48e957b228d17b8850c00ee8160472b994ed.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (12)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `deny.toml`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/client.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/api/rest/handlers.rs`\n* `examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml`\n* `libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs`\n* `libs/modkit-transport-grpc/src/lib.rs`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>💤 Files with no reviewable changes (1)</summary>\n\n* deny.toml\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚧 Files skipped from review as they are similar to previous changes (2)</summary>\n\n* examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs\n* examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Additional context used</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧬 Code graph analysis (4)</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (35-58)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (16-21)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (28-35)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (43-59)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs (2)</summary>\n\n* `decode_bin` (46-61)\n* `encode_bin` (30-38)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/access_scope.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `resource_ids` (23-25)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/security_ctx.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `subject_id` (71-73)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (15-15)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (35-58)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (16-21)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (43-59)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-transport-grpc/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs (2)</summary>\n\n* `decode_bin` (46-61)\n* `encode_bin` (30-38)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (8)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (16)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-14`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe dependency swap from `bincode` to `postcard` is consistent with the serialization backend migration in `bin_codec.rs`. Postcard is a well-suited choice for compact binary serialization, especially in embedded/no_std contexts.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/api/rest/handlers.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-8`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and parameter type updates from `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext` are consistent with the broader rename across the codebase. No logic changes, just a straightforward type migration.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 18-19\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-54`: **LGTM - Comprehensive round-trip test for new SecurityContext API.**\n\nThe test properly exercises the builder-based API for `SecurityContext` and `Permission`, validating that all core fields survive the encode/decode cycle. The permission iteration at lines 48-53 provides thorough field-level verification.\n\n---\n\n`56-76`: **LGTM - Version mismatch test.**\n\nGood coverage for the version byte validation in `decode_bin`. The test correctly mutates the version byte and verifies the appropriate error is returned.\n\n---\n\n`48-53`: **No issue found—test correctly verifies None is preserved.**\n\nThe `Permission::tenant_id()` calls in the test assertion (line 52) are valid. The two permissions created in the test do not explicitly set `tenant_id`, so both default to `None`. The assertion correctly verifies that `p.tenant_id() == orig_perms[i].tenant_id()` compares `None == None`, confirming the encode/decode cycle properly preserves permissions without explicit tenant IDs.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`46-61`: **LGTM - Decoding implementation is clean and well-guarded.**\n\nThe decode function properly validates:\n1. Non-empty input (line 47-49)\n2. Version compatibility (lines 51-54)\n3. Postcard deserialization (line 58)\n\nThe slice operation `&bytes[1..]` at line 56 is safe since the empty check ensures at least one byte exists.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`309-309`: **LGTM - Workspace dependency update to postcard.**\n\nThe `alloc` feature is correctly enabled to support `to_allocvec` usage in `bin_codec.rs` (line 34). Postcard provides efficient, compact binary serialization well-suited for security context transport.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-transport-grpc/src/lib.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **LGTM!**\n\nImport correctly updated to use `SecurityContext` from `modkit_security`.\n\n---\n\n`17-25`: **LGTM!**\n\nFunction signature and documentation consistently updated to reference `SecurityContext`. The implementation correctly passes the context to `encode_bin` which now accepts `SecurityContext`.\n\n---\n\n`28-42`: **LGTM!**\n\nFunction signature and documentation updated to return `SecurityContext`. The `decode_bin` call aligns with the updated return type shown in the relevant snippets.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-6`: **LGTM!**\n\nImport updated to use `SecurityContext`.\n\n---\n\n`11-15`: **LGTM!**\n\nTrait documentation and method signature consistently updated to use `SecurityContext`. This aligns with the implementations in `client.rs` and the gateway SDK shown in the relevant snippets.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/client.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-9`: **LGTM!**\n\nImport updated to use `SecurityContext`.\n\n---\n\n`35-57`: **LGTM!**\n\nMethod signature correctly updated to accept `&SecurityContext`, matching the trait definition in `api.rs`. The `attach_secctx` call correctly passes the `SecurityContext` to the transport layer for encoding into gRPC metadata. Comments are updated consistently.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-8`: **LGTM!**\n\nImport updated to use `SecurityContext`.\n\n---\n\n`28-35`: **LGTM!**\n\nMethod signature correctly updated to accept `&SecurityContext`, matching both the trait definition in `api.rs` and the underlying `Service::add` method shown in the relevant snippets. The delegation and error conversion remain unchanged.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3750249612/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","created_at":"2023-06-14T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-03-14T07:58:44Z","permissions":{"actions":"read","checks":"write","contents":"write","discussions":"read","issues":"write","members":"read","metadata":"read","pull_requests":"write","statuses":"write"},"events":["issues","issue_comment","label","organization","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","pull_request_review_thread","release","repository"]}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3750279088","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/241#issuecomment-3750279088","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/241","id":3750279088,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fiLew","user":{"login":"codecov-commenter","id":65553080,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1NTUzMDgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/65553080?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov-commenter","html_url":"https://github.com/codecov-commenter","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/codecov-comm