sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (28-35)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (43-59)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (15-15)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (35-58)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (16-21)\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary>\n\n* `add` (43-59)\n\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⏰ Context from checks skipped due to timeout of 90000ms. You can increase the timeout in your CodeRabbit configuration to a maximum of 15 minutes (900000ms). (8)</summary>\n\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (windows-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Dylint Lints Tests\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (ubuntu-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Run Dylint Lints\n* GitHub Check: users_info integration (Postgres)\n* GitHub Check: Test Suite (macos-latest, rust=stable)\n* GitHub Check: Code Coverage (cargo-llvm-cov)\n* GitHub Check: UI macro tests (trybuild)\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔇 Additional comments (15)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator/calculator-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-15`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import, documentation, and method signature are all consistently updated from `SecurityCtx` to `SecurityContext`. The changes align with the broader PR refactoring.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`309-309`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe postcard dependency is properly pinned to version `1.1.3` in the workspace dependencies. This is a good choice for compact binary serialization, especially for security contexts that need to be efficiently transmitted over gRPC metadata.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/api/rest/handlers.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-19`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and `Extension` type parameter are consistently updated to `SecurityContext`. The handler correctly extracts and passes the security context to the domain service.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`14-14`: **Verify postcard features are correctly configured.**\n\nThe switch from bincode to postcard is correct. However, note that `postcard` does NOT have serde support enabled by default—the default features are `[\"heapless-cas\"]`. Serde support requires explicit feature flags (`use-std` or `alloc`). The current codebase intentionally avoids these features, as evidenced by the comment in `bin_codec.rs` that states \"postcard may be compiled with heapless output,\" and the code uses `postcard::to_slice()` and `postcard::from_bytes()` which work without serde.\n\n\n\n> Likely an incorrect or invalid review comment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-10`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and method signature updates to `SecurityContext` are consistent with the broader refactor. The context is correctly propagated to the downstream `calculator.add()` call.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 42-43\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`4-4`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and trait method signature are correctly updated to use `SecurityContext`.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 16-21\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-54`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe round-trip test comprehensively validates the new `SecurityContext` structure with permissions. The builder pattern usage is clean and the assertions verify all relevant fields.\n\n---\n\n`56-76`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe version rejection test properly validates error handling for unsupported binary format versions.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>examples/oop-modules/calculator_gateway/calculator_gateway-sdk/src/client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-8`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and trait implementation are correctly updated to use `SecurityContext`. The delegation to `self.service.add()` properly propagates the security context.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 28-34\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-transport-grpc/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-13`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe import and function signatures for `attach_secctx` and `extract_secctx` are correctly updated to use `SecurityContext`. The encoding/decoding logic properly handles the renamed type.\n\n\n\nAlso applies to: 17-25, 32-42\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>libs/modkit-security/src/bin_codec.rs (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-5`: **LGTM!**\n\nImports and version constant are appropriate for the postcard-based serialization refactor.\n\n---\n\n`7-17`: **LGTM!**\n\nError type correctly wraps `PostcardError` with appropriate `From` implementation for ergonomic error propagation.\n\n---\n\n`19-35`: **LGTM!**\n\nDecode error enum provides good granularity for different failure modes (empty input, version mismatch, deserialization failure), enabling clear error handling upstream.\n\n---\n\n`57-78`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe decode function properly validates emptiness and version before deserializing. The slice operation `&bytes[1..]` is safe given the prior empty check.\n\n---\n\n`46-52`: > Likely an incorrect or invalid review comment.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/241#pullrequestreview-3661500370","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/241","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/241#pullrequestreview-3661500370"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/241"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-14T15:58:55Z","commit_id":"54755f2e6d8ec75c85bb8155c3135dcaa2817c6a"}]},{"source_pr_number":240,"source_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/240","source_state":"closed","source_author":"MikeFalcon77","target_issue_number":null,"title":"[PR #240] chore(module_orchestrator): module_orchestrator-contracts crate is renamed","status":"exported","mirrored_at":null,"comments_status":"none","comments_mirrored":0,"pr_head_ref":"233-unify-local-client-placement-across-modules-and-update-docs","pr_head_sha":"ff14011e1851a7fc42bbfa5351da949d7cd61d84","pr_base_ref":"main","pr_head_owner":"MikeFalcon77","pr_from_fork":1,"source_data":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/240","id":3173567810,"node_id":"PR_kwDOPaLyBs69KM1C","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/240","diff_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/240.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/240.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/240","number":240,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"chore(module_orchestrator): module_orchestrator-contracts crate is 