TGljZW5zZTI="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"has_pull_requests":true,"pull_request_creation_policy":"all","topics":["account-management","agentic-ai","ai","benchmarks","cloud","genai","llm","microservices","middleware","modkit","multi-tenancy","multi-tier","rust","saas","security","serverless","xaas"],"visibility":"private","forks":19,"open_issues":263,"watchers":32,"default_branch":"main"}},"_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230"},"issue":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/230"},"comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/230/comments"},"review_comments":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230/comments"},"review_comment":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments{/number}"},"commits":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230/commits"},"statuses":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/statuses/9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852"}},"author_association":"MEMBER","auto_merge":null,"assignee":null,"active_lock_reason":null},"source_issue_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3743814267","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#issuecomment-3743814267","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/230","id":3743814267,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fJhJ7","user":{"login":"nanoandrew4","id":14365320,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzY1MzIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14365320?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4","html_url":"https://github.com/nanoandrew4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-13T11:25:52Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T11:25:52Z","body":"The lints are failing because the `modkit-transport-grpc` lib has a config struct that is missing the now mandatory annotations for duration serialization/deserialization. We can either add them despite them not being necessary for the fields in that config struct, since it doesn't seem like it is populated from a file, or we can weaken the lint to only look at files called `config.rs` or something like that, so that not all config structs need to have their Durations marked with the serde macro. I'm leaning towards the first, but am interested in collecting some feedback before making any changes.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3743814267/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3745532862","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#issuecomment-3745532862","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/230","id":3745532862,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fQEu-","user":{"login":"nanoandrew4","id":14365320,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0MzY1MzIw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/14365320?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4","html_url":"https://github.com/nanoandrew4","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/nanoandrew4/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-13T17:25:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T17:25:13Z","body":"After speaking with @Bechma , we have decided to close this PR in favour of adding the recommendation to the guidelines. The issue is that no lint will reliably catch all durations that need to use the macro, and it would also force struct fields which don't need it to add it, which isn't helpful. ","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3745532862/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686609635","pull_request_review_id":3656022487,"id":2686609635,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gImjj","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_hir;\n+extern crate rustc_middle;\n+extern crate rustc_span;\n+\n+use clippy_utils::sym as clippy_sym;\n+use rustc_hir::{FieldDef, Item, ItemKind, VariantData};\n+use rustc_lint::{LateContext, LateLintPass, LintContext};\n+use rustc_middle::ty::{self, Ty};\n+use rustc_span::Symbol;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_late_lint! {\n+    /// DE0301: Duration fields in *Config must use humantime serde mapping\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that any `std::time::Duration` (or `Option<Duration>`) field in a struct whose\n+    /// name ends with `Config` has the appropriate `#[serde(with = \"...\")]` attribute.\n+    pub DE0301_CONFIG_DURATION_HUMANTIME_SERDE,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"Duration fields in *Config structs must use humantime serde mapping (DE0301)\"\n+}\n+\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde\";\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME_OPTION: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde::option\";","path":"dylint_lints/de12_config_layer/de12_enforce_humantime_serde/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","original_commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"what if used after a \r\n```rust\r\nuse modkit_utils::humantime_serde\r\n```","created_at":"2026-01-13T14:13:02Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T14:13:02Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#discussion_r2686609635","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686609635"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#discussion_r2686609635"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686609635/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":25,"original_line":25,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":25,"position":25,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686626990","pull_request_review_id":3656047237,"id":2686626990,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gIqyu","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_hir;\n+extern crate rustc_middle;\n+extern crate rustc_span;\n+\n+use clippy_utils::sym as clippy_sym;\n+use rustc_hir::{FieldDef, Item, ItemKind, VariantData};\n+use rustc_lint::{LateContext, LateLintPass, LintContext};\n+use rustc_middle::ty::{self, Ty};\n+use rustc_span::Symbol;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_late_lint! {\n+    /// DE0301: Duration fields in *Config must use humantime serde mapping\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that any `std::time::Duration` (or `Option<Duration>`) field in a struct whose\n+    /// name ends with `Config` has the appropriate `#[serde(with = \"...\")]` attribute.\n+    pub DE0301_CONFIG_DURATION_HUMANTIME_SERDE,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"Duration fields in *Config structs must use humantime serde mapping (DE0301)\"\n+}\n+\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde\";\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME_OPTION: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde::option\";\n+\n+fn normalize_serde_with_value(s: &str) -> &str {\n+    s.trim().strip_prefix(\"::\").unwrap_or(s.trim())\n+}\n+\n+fn is_duration_ty<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> bool {\n+    let ty::Adt(adt_def, _) = ty.kind() else {\n+        return false;\n+    };\n+\n+    let path = cx.tcx.def_path_str(adt_def.did());\n+    path == \"std::time::Duration\" || path == \"core::time::Duration\"\n+}\n+\n+fn option_inner_ty<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> Option<Ty<'tcx>> {\n+    let ty::Adt(adt_def, subst) = ty.kind() else {\n+        return None;\n+    };\n+\n+    let path = cx.tcx.def_path_str(adt_def.did());\n+    if path != \"core::option::Option\" && path != \"std::option::Option\" {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Option<T> has a single type argument.\n+    subst.types().next()\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+enum DurationFieldKind {\n+    Duration,\n+    OptionDuration,\n+}\n+\n+fn duration_field_kind<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> Option<DurationFieldKind> {\n+    if is_duration_ty(cx, ty) {\n+        return Some(DurationFieldKind::Duration);\n+    }\n+\n+    let inner = option_inner_ty(cx, ty)?;\n+    if is_duration_ty(cx, inner) {\n+        return Some(DurationFieldKind::OptionDuration);\n+    }\n+\n+    None\n+}\n+\n+fn field_has_expected_serde_with<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, field: &FieldDef<'tcx>, expected: &str) -> bool {\n+    let expected = expected;\n+    let with_sym = Symbol::intern(\"with\");\n+\n+    for attr in cx.tcx.hir_attrs(field.hir_id) {\n+        if !attr.has_name(clippy_sym::serde) {\n+            continue;\n+        }\n+\n+        let Some(items) = attr.meta_item_list() else {\n+            continue;\n+        };\n+\n+        for nested in items {\n+            let Some(mi) = nested.meta_item() else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+\n+            // We only care about `with = \"...\"`","path":"dylint_lints/de12_config_layer/de12_enforce_humantime_serde/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","original_commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"it's possible to have more than one attribute, so we need to locate the segment with ident name with_sym","created_at":"2026-01-13T14:17:20Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T14:17:21Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#discussion_r2686626990","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686626990"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/230#discussion_r2686626990"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/230"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686626990/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":91,"original_line":91,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":91,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2686648819","pull_request_review_id":3656077692,"id":2686648819,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gIwHz","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,184 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_hir;\n+extern crate rustc_middle;\n+extern crate rustc_span;\n+\n+use clippy_utils::sym as clippy_sym;\n+use rustc_hir::{FieldDef, Item, ItemKind, VariantData};\n+use rustc_lint::{LateContext, LateLintPass, LintContext};\n+use rustc_middle::ty::{self, Ty};\n+use rustc_span::Symbol;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_late_lint! {\n+    /// DE0301: Duration fields in *Config must use humantime serde mapping\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that any `std::time::Duration` (or `Option<Duration>`) field in a struct whose\n+    /// name ends with `Config` has the appropriate `#[serde(with = \"...\")]` attribute.\n+    pub DE0301_CONFIG_DURATION_HUMANTIME_SERDE,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"Duration fields in *Config structs must use humantime serde mapping (DE0301)\"\n+}\n+\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde\";\n+const SERDE_WITH_HUMANTIME_OPTION: &str = \"modkit_utils::humantime_serde::option\";\n+\n+fn normalize_serde_with_value(s: &str) -> &str {\n+    s.trim().strip_prefix(\"::\").unwrap_or(s.trim())\n+}\n+\n+fn is_duration_ty<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> bool {\n+    let ty::Adt(adt_def, _) = ty.kind() else {\n+        return false;\n+    };\n+\n+    let path = cx.tcx.def_path_str(adt_def.did());\n+    path == \"std::time::Duration\" || path == \"core::time::Duration\"\n+}\n+\n+fn option_inner_ty<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> Option<Ty<'tcx>> {\n+    let ty::Adt(adt_def, subst) = ty.kind() else {\n+        return None;\n+    };\n+\n+    let path = cx.tcx.def_path_str(adt_def.did());\n+    if path != \"core::option::Option\" && path != \"std::option::Option\" {\n+        return None;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Option<T> has a single type argument.\n+    subst.types().next()\n+}\n+\n+#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n+enum DurationFieldKind {\n+    Duration,\n+    OptionDuration,\n+}\n+\n+fn duration_field_kind<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, ty: Ty<'tcx>) -> Option<DurationFieldKind> {\n+    if is_duration_ty(cx, ty) {\n+        return Some(DurationFieldKind::Duration);\n+    }\n+\n+    let inner = option_inner_ty(cx, ty)?;\n+    if is_duration_ty(cx, inner) {\n+        return Some(DurationFieldKind::OptionDuration);\n+    }\n+\n+    None\n+}\n+\n+fn field_has_expected_serde_with<'tcx>(cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, field: &FieldDef<'tcx>, expected: &str) -> bool {\n+    let expected = expected;\n+    let with_sym = Symbol::intern(\"with\");\n+\n+    for attr in cx.tcx.hir_attrs(field.hir_id) {\n+        if !attr.has_name(clippy_sym::serde) {\n+            continue;\n+        }\n+\n+        let Some(items) = attr.meta_item_list() else {\n+            continue;\n+        };\n+\n+        for nested in items {\n+            let Some(mi) = nested.meta_item() else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+\n+            // We only care about `with = \"...\"`\n+            if mi.path.segments.len() != 1 || mi.path.segments[0].ident.name != with_sym {\n+                continue;\n+            }\n+\n+            let Some(val) = mi.value_str() else {\n+                continue;\n+            };\n+\n+            let val = normalize_serde_with_value(val.as_str());\n+            if val == expected {\n+                return true;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    false\n+}\n+\n+fn field_label<'tcx>(field: &FieldDef<'tcx>, idx: usize) -> String {\n+    // Tuple struct fields may have no meaningful identifier.\n+    let name = field.ident.name.as_str();\n+    if name.is_empty() {\n+        format!(\"#{}\", idx)\n+    } else {\n+        name.to_string()\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+impl<'tcx> LateLintPass<'tcx> for De0301ConfigDurationHumantimeSerde {\n+    fn check_item(&mut self, cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, item: &'tcx Item<'tcx>) {\n+        let ItemKind::Struct(ident, _generics, variant) = &item.kind else {\n+            return;\n+        };\n+\n+        let struct_name = ident.name.as_str();\n+        if !struct_name.ends_with(\"Config\") {","path":"dylint_lints/de12_config_layer/de12_enforce_humantime_serde/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","original_commit_id":"9a940f2f1adfb7070908eb1dd525910197cdc852","user":{"login":"Bechma","id":19294519,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5Mjk0NTE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19294519?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma","html_url":"https://github.com/Bechma","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Bechma/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"regarding your comment, checking the name of the struct ends with Config maybe it's not the best approach, but to call the struct FileConfig or something like that. We could have Config names everywhere without the need of having this rule","created_at":"2026-01-13T14:22:46Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T14:22:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/p