ps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T17:30:10Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:47Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nThis PR introduces nine new Dylint lints across domain, infrastructure, security, and documentation layers; removes a workspace member; updates core security and registry APIs from SecurityContext to SecurityCtx and TypesRegistryClient to TypesRegistryApi throughout example modules and libraries; and allows the bincode 2.0.1 advisory.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Advisory & Workspace Configuration** <br> `deny.toml`, `dylint_lints/Cargo.toml` | Added bincode 2.0.1 advisory allowlist entry; removed de0503_plugin_client_suffix workspace member; added 8 new lint workspace members (DE0301, DE0308, DE0407, DE0409, DE0703, DE0705, DE0706, DE1107) and workspace dev dependencies (sea-orm, sqlx, axum, uuid, anyhow, thiserror). |\n| **.gitignore Cleanup** <br> `dylint_lints/de0[1-2]*/de*/../.gitignore`, `dylint_lints/de0[89]*/de*/.gitignore`, `dylint_lints/de05_client_layer/de0503_plugin_client_suffix/.gitignore` | Removed /target entries from 9 .gitignore files across multiple lint crates, allowing target directories to be version-controlled. |\n| **Domain Layer Lints (DE0301, DE0308)** <br> `dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0301_no_infra_in_domain/*`, `dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/*` | Added two new lint crates: DE0301 (No Infrastructure in Domain) with detection of infra imports in domain modules; DE0308 (No HTTP in Domain) with HTTP type pattern matching. Each includes .cargo/config.toml, Cargo.toml, README, rust-toolchain, src/lib.rs, and UI test examples/stderr pairs. |\n| **Infrastructure Layer Lints (DE0407, DE0409)** <br> `dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/*`, `dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0409_no_secrets_in_migrations/*` | Added two new lint crates: DE0407 (No Hardcoded Connection Strings) detecting URL scheme patterns; DE0409 (No Secrets in Migrations) using pattern and entropy-based secret detection. Each includes configuration, documentation, implementation, and test fixtures. |\n| **Security Layer Lints (DE0703, DE0705, DE0706)** <br> `dylint_lints/de07_security/de0703_no_hardcoded_secrets/*`, `dylint_lints/de07_security/de0705_no_prebuild_sql_queries/*`, `dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/*` | Added three new security-focused lint crates: DE0703 (No Hardcoded Secrets) with entropy-based detection; DE0705 (No Prebuilt SQL Queries) detecting string concatenation and format! patterns; DE0706 (No Direct sqlx) preventing direct sqlx imports. Each fully configured with examples and tests. |\n| **Documentation Layer Lint (DE1107)** <br> `dylint_lints/de11_documentation/de1107_public_apis_doc_comments/*` | Added new lint crate DE1107 (Public APIs Doc Comments) requiring documentation on public contract module items. Includes configuration, README, implementation, and test examples. |\n| **Utility Library Enhancement** <br> `dylint_lints/lint_utils/src/lib.rs` | Added two new public path-checking functions: is_in_modkit_db_path() and is_in_hyperspot_server_path() for span-based path filtering in lint implementations. |\n| **Security & Registry API Migration (Examples)** <br> `examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/plugins/contoso_tr_plugin/src/module.rs`, `examples/.../fabrikam_tr_plugin/src/module.rs`, `examples/.../tenant_resolver-gw/src/...` | Replaced TypesRegistryClient with TypesRegistryApi and SecurityContext with SecurityCtx; updated registry.register() calls to include SecurityCtx::root_ctx() parameter; adjusted imports throughout. |\n| **Security & Registry API Migration (System Modules)** <br> `modules/system/api_gateway/src/module.rs`, `modules/system/types-registry/.../local_client.rs`, `modules/system/types-registry/.../module.rs` | Replaced trait implementations RestApiCapability→RestfulModule, ApiGatewayCapability→RestHostModule; swapped SecurityContext→SecurityCtx and TypesRegistryClient→TypesRegistryApi; added SecurityCtx parameters to API method signatures; updated root context injection and security context handling in middleware. |\n| **Test Updates (Security & Auth)** <br> `modules/system/api_gateway/tests/auth_disabled_root_context.rs`, `libs/modkit-db/src/secure/tests.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/tests/bin_codec.rs`, `libs/modkit-security/tests/root_constants.rs` | Updated test implementations to use SecurityCtx instead of SecurityContext; added root_ctx() construction patterns; added new test cases for root scope semantics and context behavior; adjusted assertions to verify scope.is_root(), subject identity, and deny states. |\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~60 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- **#249**: Modifies TypesRegistry client trait naming and usage across multiple modules (TypesRegistryClient ↔ TypesRegistryApi changes intersect with this PR's API migration).\n- **#241**: Updates security context API surface (SecurityCtx vs SecurityContext) across examples and libraries, directly overlapping with this PR's context refactoring.\n- **#248**: Modifies security context symbols and call sites where SecurityCtx is passed, sharing the same code-level changes as the security API migration portion of this PR.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Bechma\n- MikeFalcon77\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐰 *Hop, hop! New lints now guard the way,*  \n> *Domain and security say their say,*  \n> *With schemas safe and secrets hid,*  \n> *SecurityCtx keeps chaos forbid!*  \n> *Eight lints strong, the code's now bright,*  \n> *Hyperspot's patterns shine so right!* ✨\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 3 | ❌ 2</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (2 warnings)</summary>\n\n|         Check name         | Status     | Explanation                                                                                                                                                       | Resolution                                                                                                                                                              |\n| :------------------------: | :--------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Out of Scope Changes check | ⚠️ Warning | Changes to security contexts (SecurityCtx, SecurityContext) and API trait updates (TypesRegistryApi, RestfulModule) appear unrelated to the dylint lints feature. | Review and separate security/API refactoring changes into a distinct PR; focus this PR solely on dylint lints additions as described in the title and issue objectives. |\n|     Docstring Coverage     | ⚠️ Warning | Docstring coverage is 35.51% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%.                                                                             | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold.                                                                                      |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (3 passed)</summary>\n\n|      Check name     | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                                                                          |\n| :-----------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n|  Description Check  | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                                                                          |\n|     Title check     | ✅ Passed | The title 'feat(dylint): add top-10 new lints' accurately and specifically describes the main change: adding new dylint linters.                                                                     |\n| Linked Issues check | ✅ Passed | The PR successfully implements the linked issue `#68` requirements: generates DyLint rules, splits by categories (DE03, DE04, DE07, DE11), and delivers top-10 new lints with documentation and tests. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start 