fy MD001 and maintain proper markdown hierarchy.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385918","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385918"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385918"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385918/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":5,"original_line":5,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":5,"position":5,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385935","pull_request_review_id":3666862054,"id":2695385935,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqFNP","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@\n+[toolchain]\n+channel = \"nightly-2025-09-18\"\n+components = [\"llvm-tools-preview\", \"rustc-dev\"]","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/rust-toolchain","commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","original_commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Verify toolchain consistency across dylint lint crates\n\necho \"=== Checking for rust-toolchain files in dylint_lints ===\"\nfind dylint_lints -type f -name 'rust-toolchain' -o -name 'rust-toolchain.toml' | sort\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Content of each file ===\"\nfind dylint_lints -type f \\( -name 'rust-toolchain' -o -name 'rust-toolchain.toml' \\) | sort | while read f; do\n  echo \"--- $f ---\"\n  cat \"$f\"\n  echo\ndone\n\necho \"=== Checking workspace root toolchain configuration ===\"\nif [ -f rust-toolchain.toml ]; then\n  echo \"rust-toolchain.toml exists at workspace root:\"\n  cat rust-toolchain.toml\nelse\n  echo \"No rust-toolchain.toml at workspace root\"\nfi\n\nif [ -f rust-toolchain ]; then\n  echo \"rust-toolchain file exists at workspace root:\"\n  cat rust-toolchain\nelse\n  echo \"No rust-toolchain file at workspace root\"\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 5612\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**The reviewed file is correct, but toolchain inconsistencies exist across the workspace.**\n\nThe file at `de0308_no_http_in_domain/rust-toolchain` is properly formatted and uses the correct channel. However, verification found inconsistencies in other lint crates:\n\n- `de0706_no_direct_sqlx/rust-toolchain` uses `nightly-2025-05-01` instead of `nightly-2025-09-18`\n- `de0110_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/rust-toolchain` and `de0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/rust-toolchain` use plain text format instead of TOML with components\n\nStandardize all individual lint crate rust-toolchain files to match the workspace-level configuration (TOML format with `nightly-2025-09-18` channel and required components).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/rust-toolchain`\naround lines 1 - 3, Multiple crate-level rust-toolchain files are inconsistent\nwith the workspace standard; update each lint crate's rust-toolchain to the TOML\nformat and the same channel/components as the workspace: set channel =\n\"nightly-2025-09-18\" and include components =\n[\"llvm-tools-preview\",\"rustc-dev\"]. Specifically, change\nde0706_no_direct_sqlx/rust-toolchain from \"nightly-2025-05-01\" to\n\"nightly-2025-09-18\" and convert\nde0110_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/rust-toolchain and\nde0902_no_schema_for_on_gts_structs/rust-toolchain from plain text to the TOML\nform matching de03.../rust-toolchain (i.e., include the [toolchain] table,\nchannel key, and components array).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385935","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385935"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385935"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385935/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":3,"original_line":3,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":3,"position":3,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385941","pull_request_review_id":3666862054,"id":2695385941,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqFNV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,133 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+\n+use rustc_ast::{Item, ItemKind, UseTree, UseTreeKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{EarlyLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+use lint_utils::is_in_domain_path;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_early_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Checks that domain modules do not reference HTTP types or status codes.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Domain modules should be transport-agnostic. HTTP is just one possible\n+    /// transport layer. Referencing HTTP types in domain code couples the business\n+    /// logic to a specific transport mechanism.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - HTTP types in domain\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     use http::StatusCode;\n+    ///     \n+    ///     pub fn check_result() -> StatusCode {\n+    ///         StatusCode::OK  // ❌ HTTP-specific\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - domain errors converted in API layer\n+    /// mod domain {\n+    ///     pub enum DomainResult {\n+    ///         Success,\n+    ///         NotFound,\n+    ///         InvalidData,\n+    ///     }\n+    /// }\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0308_NO_HTTP_IN_DOMAIN,\n+    Deny,\n+    \"domain modules should not reference HTTP types or status codes (DE0308)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// HTTP-related patterns forbidden in domain code\n+const HTTP_PATTERNS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"http::\",\n+    \"http::StatusCode\",\n+    \"http::Method\",\n+    \"http::HeaderMap\",\n+    \"http::Request\",\n+    \"http::Response\",\n+    \"axum::http\",\n+    \"hyper::StatusCode\",\n+    \"hyper::Method\",\n+    \"actix_web::http\",\n+    \"reqwest::StatusCode\",\n+];\n+\n+fn use_tree_to_string(tree: &UseTree) -> String {\n+    match &tree.kind {\n+        UseTreeKind::Simple(..) | UseTreeKind::Glob => {\n+            tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n+                .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                .join(\"::\")\n+        }\n+        UseTreeKind::Nested { items, .. } => {\n+            let prefix = tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n+                .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n+                .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n+                .join(\"::\");\n+            \n+            for (nested_tree, _) in items {\n+                let nested_str = use_tree_to_string(nested_tree);\n+                if !nested_str.is_empty() {\n+                    return format!(\"{}::{}\", prefix, nested_str);\n+                }\n+            }\n+            prefix\n+        }\n+    }","path":"dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","original_commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Nested use tree handling only checks first item.**\n\nThe `use_tree_to_string` function returns after finding the first non-empty nested item (line 84), missing subsequent items in grouped imports like `use http::{StatusCode, Method}`.\n\nThis means if `StatusCode` doesn't match but `Method` would, the lint won't trigger. The function should check all nested items.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix to check all nested items</summary>\n\n```diff\n fn use_tree_to_string(tree: &UseTree) -> String {\n     match &tree.kind {\n         UseTreeKind::Simple(..) | UseTreeKind::Glob => {\n             tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n                 .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n                 .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n                 .join(\"::\")\n         }\n         UseTreeKind::Nested { items, .. } => {\n             let prefix = tree.prefix.segments.iter()\n                 .map(|seg| seg.ident.name.as_str())\n                 .collect::<Vec<_>>()\n                 .join(\"::\");\n-            \n-            for (nested_tree, _) in items {\n-                let nested_str = use_tree_to_string(nested_tree);\n-                if !nested_str.is_empty() {\n-                    return format!(\"{}::{}\", prefix, nested_str);\n-                }\n-            }\n-            prefix\n+            // Return all nested paths joined, or just prefix if empty\n+            let nested_paths: Vec<String> = items\n+                .iter()\n+                .map(|(nested_tree, _)| {\n+                    let nested_str = use_tree_to_string(nested_tree);\n+                    if nested_str.is_empty() {\n+                        prefix.clone()\n+                    } else {\n+                        format!(\"{}::{}\", prefix, nested_str)\n+                    }\n+                })\n+                .collect();\n+            nested_paths.join(\",\")\n         }\n     }\n }\n```\n</details>\n\nAlternatively, refactor to return `Vec<String>` of all paths and check each against patterns.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de03_domain_layer/de0308_no_http_in_domain/src/lib.rs` around\nlines 75 - 89, The nested branch in UseTreeKind::Nested inside\nuse_tree_to_string currently returns on the first non-empty nested item, missing\nlater items (e.g., use http::{StatusCode, Method}); update use_tree_to_string to\niterate all items instead of returning early: either (a) collect all nested_str\nresults for each (nested_tree, _) in items, filter out empty strings and join\nthem with \"::\" or \",\" to produce a combined string, or (b) change the function\nsignature to return Vec<String> and have the caller iterate over each returned\npath for pattern checks; ensure you update callers of use_tree_to_string to\nhandle the new aggregated output and keep references to UseTreeKind::Nested and\nuse_tree_to_string for locating the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385941","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385941"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385941"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385941/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":75,"original_start_line":75,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":89,"original_line":89,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":89,"position":89,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385944","pull_request_review_id":3666862054,"id":2695385944,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqFNY","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+extern crate rustc_hir;\n+\n+use rustc_ast::LitKind;\n+use rustc_hir::{Expr, ExprKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{LateContext, LateLintPass, LintContext};\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_late_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Detects hardcoded database and service connection strings in source code.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Hardcoded connection strings are a security and operational risk:\n+    /// - Connection strings often contain credentials (username/password)\n+    /// - Different environments need different connection strings\n+    /// - Secrets are exposed in version control history\n+    /// - Changes require code modifications and redeployment\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - hardcoded connection string\n+    /// let db_url = \"postgres://user:password@localhost:5432/mydb\";\n+    /// let cache = \"redis://localhost:6379\";\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - load from environment or config\n+    /// let db_url = std::env::var(\"DATABASE_URL\")?;\n+    /// let cache = config.redis_url.clone();\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0407_NO_HARDCODED_CONNECTION_STRINGS,\n+    Warn,\n+    \"avoid hardcoding database connection strings (DE0407)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// Connection string URL schemes that indicate hardcoded database/service URLs\n+const CONNECTION_SCHEMES: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"postgres://\",\n+    \"postgresql://\",\n+    \"mysql://\",\n+    \"mariadb://\",\n+    \"mongodb://\",\n+    \"mongodb+srv://\",\n+    \"redis://\",\n+    \"rediss://\",\n+    \"amqp://\",\n+    \"amqps://\",\n+    \"nats://\",\n+    \"kafka://\",\n+    \"mssql://\",\n+    \"sqlserver://\",\n+    \"oracle://\",\n+    \"sqlite://\",\n+];\n+\n+impl<'tcx> LateLintPass<'tcx> for De0407NoHardcodedConnectionStrings {\n+    fn check_expr(&mut self, cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, expr: &'tcx Expr<'tcx>) {\n+        // Check string literals for connection string patterns\n+        let ExprKind::Lit(lit) = &expr.kind else { return };\n+        let LitKind::Str(symbol, _) = lit.node else { return };\n+\n+        let string_value = symbol.as_str();\n+\n+        // Check if it matches any connection scheme\n+        for scheme in CONNECTION_SCHEMES {\n+            if string_value.starts_with(scheme) {\n+                // Only flag if there's actual connection info after the scheme\n+                // (not just the scheme prefix used for URL detection)\n+                let after_scheme = &string_value[scheme.len()..];\n+                if !after_scheme.is_empty() && !after_scheme.starts_with('/') {\n+                    // Has host/path info - this is a real connection string\n+                    cx.span_lint(DE0407_NO_HARDCODED_CONNECTION_STRINGS, expr.span, |diag| {\n+                        diag.primary_message(\"hardcoded connection string detected (DE0407)\");\n+                        diag.help(\"load connection strings from environment variables (std::env::var) or configuration files\");\n+                        diag.note(\"hardcoded connection strings expose credentials and make environment-specific configuration difficult\");\n+                    });\n+                    return;\n+                }","path":"dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","original_commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check test files for SQLite coverage\nfind dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings -type f -name \"*.rs\" -o -name \"*.txt\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 348\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for SQLite in test files\nrg -i \"sqlite\" dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 285\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Read the complete implementation\ncat -n dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/src/lib.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4452\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/ui/bad_connection_strings.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 896\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n dylint_lints/de04_infrastructure/de0407_no_hardcoded_connection_strings/ui/good_config_usage_0407.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1141\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**SQLite connection strings are not detected due to overly restrictive path filtering.**\n\nThe condition on line 78 (`!after_scheme.starts_with('/')`) prevents detection of SQLite connection strings that use file paths. Standard SQLite URLs follow the format `sqlite:///absolute/path` or `sqlite://./relative/path`—both of which would fail the filter since they begin with `/` or `.` immediately after the scheme.\n\nAdditionally, `sqlite://` is included in `CONNECTION_SCHEMES` but has no test coverage in the test files, leaving this gap undetected.\n\nThe proposed fix correctly identifies that SQLite requires special handling to allow path-based connection strings while maintaining the intent of filtering empty/scheme-only strings for other database types.\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385944","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385944"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385944"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385944/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":74,"original_start_line":74,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":86,"original_line":86,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":86,"position":86,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385946","pull_request_review_id":3666862054,"id":2695385946,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqFNa","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,167 @@\n+#![feature(rustc_private)]\n+#![warn(unused_extern_crates)]\n+\n+extern crate rustc_ast;\n+extern crate rustc_hir;\n+extern crate rustc_span;\n+\n+use clippy_utils::macros::root_macro_call_first_node;\n+use rustc_ast::LitKind;\n+use rustc_hir::{Expr, ExprKind};\n+use rustc_lint::{LateContext, LateLintPass, LintContext};\n+use rustc_span::sym;\n+\n+dylint_linting::declare_late_lint! {\n+    /// ### What it does\n+    ///\n+    /// Detects prebuilt SQL queries where strings are concatenated or formatted\n+    /// instead of using parameterized queries.\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Why is this bad?\n+    ///\n+    /// Prebuilt SQL queries create security vulnerabilities:\n+    /// - Attackers can inject malicious SQL through user input\n+    /// - Can lead to data breaches and authentication bypass\n+    /// - Parameterized queries are the industry standard for SQL safety\n+    ///\n+    /// ### Example\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Bad - prebuilt query with string formatting\n+    /// let query = format!(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = {}\", user_input);\n+    /// let query = \"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '\".to_string() + name + \"'\";\n+    /// ```\n+    ///\n+    /// Use instead:\n+    ///\n+    /// ```rust,ignore\n+    /// // Good - use parameterized queries\n+    /// sqlx::query(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = $1\").bind(user_input);\n+    /// conn.execute(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = ?\", &[name])?;\n+    /// ```\n+    pub DE0705_NO_PREBUILD_SQL_QUERIES,\n+    Warn,\n+    \"avoid prebuilt SQL queries; use parameterized queries instead (DE0705)\"\n+}\n+\n+/// SQL keywords that indicate a query string\n+const SQL_KEYWORDS: &[&str] = &[\n+    \"SELECT \",\n+    \"INSERT \",\n+    \"UPDATE \",\n+    \"DELETE \",\n+    \"DROP \",\n+    \"CREATE \",\n+    \"ALTER \",\n+    \"TRUNCATE \",\n+    \"EXEC \",\n+    \"EXECUTE \",\n+];\n+\n+fn is_sql_query(s: &str) -> bool {\n+    let upper = s.to_uppercase();\n+    SQL_KEYWORDS.iter().any(|kw| upper.contains(kw))\n+}\n+\n+impl<'tcx> LateLintPass<'tcx> for De0705NoPrebuildSqlQueries {\n+    fn check_expr(&mut self, cx: &LateContext<'tcx>, expr: &'tcx Expr<'tcx>) {\n+        // Check for format! macro with SQL content\n+        if let Some(macro_call) = root_macro_call_first_node(cx, expr) {\n+            if cx.tcx.is_diagnostic_item(sym::format_macro, macro_call.def_id) {\n+                // Check if the format string contains SQL keywords\n+                if let ExprKind::Call(_, args) = &expr.kind {\n+                    if let Some(first_arg) = args.first() {\n+                        if let Some(sql_string) = extract_format_string(cx, first_arg) {\n+                            if is_sql_query(&sql_string) && sql_string.contains(\"{}\") {\n+                                cx.span_lint(DE0705_NO_PREBUILD_SQL_QUERIES, macro_call.span, |diag| {\n+                                    diag.primary_message(\"prebuilt SQL query detected: format! with SQL query (DE0705)\");\n+                                    diag.help(\"use parameterized queries with .bind() instead of string formatting\");\n+                                    diag.note(\"prebuilt queries are vulnerable to SQL injection attacks\");\n+                                });\n+                            }","path":"dylint_lints/de07_security/de0705_no_prebuild_sql_queries/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","original_commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Placeholder detection misses named and positional format specifiers.**\n\nThe check `sql_string.contains(\"{}\")` only catches the basic `{}` placeholder. Rust's `format!` also supports `{0}`, `{name}`, `{:?}`, etc., which would bypass this lint:\n\n```rust\n// These would NOT trigger DE0705:\nformat!(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = {user_id}\", user_id = input);\nformat!(\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = {0}\", input);\n```\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix: check for any format placeholder</summary>\n\n```diff\n-                            if is_sql_query(&sql_string) && sql_string.contains(\"{}\") {\n+                            // Check for any format placeholder: {}, {0}, {name}, {:?}, etc.\n+                            let has_placeholder = sql_string.contains('{') && sql_string.contains('}');\n+                            if is_sql_query(&sql_string) && has_placeholder {\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de07_security/de0705_no_prebuild_sql_queries/src/lib.rs` around\nlines 74 - 81, The placeholder check using sql_string.contains(\"{}\") in the\nblock that calls extract_format_string(...) and is_sql_query(...) is too narrow\nand misses named/positional/format-spec placeholders; replace that check with a\nrobust placeholder detection (e.g. a regex matching any `{...}` sequence such as\nr\"\\{[^}]*\\}\" or use a format-argument parser) and use that to decide whether to\nemit DE0705_NO_PREBUILD_SQL_QUERIES at macro_call.span, keeping the same\ndiagnostic text and helper messages.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:49Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:52Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385946","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385946"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385946"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385946/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":74,"orig