r_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix heading hierarchy.**\n\nThe heading jumps from h1 to h3, skipping h2. This applies to all section headings in this file.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n # DE0706: No Direct sqlx Usage\n \n-### What it does\n+## What it does\n \n Prohibits direct usage of the `sqlx` crate in the codebase.\n \n-### Why is this bad?\n+## Why is this bad?\n```\n\nApply the same pattern to the remaining headings: `### Example` → `## Example`, `### Configuration` → `## Configuration`, `### See Also` → `## See Also`.\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n# DE0706: No Direct sqlx Usage\n\n## What it does\n\nProhibits direct usage of the `sqlx` crate in the codebase.\n\n## Why is this bad?\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n3-3: Heading levels should only increment by one level at a time\nExpected: h2; Actual: h3\n\n(MD001, heading-increment)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/README.md` at line 3, The\nREADME uses h1 then jumps to h3 headers; update the heading hierarchy by\nchanging the h3 headings \"### What it does\", \"### Example\", \"### Configuration\",\nand \"### See Also\" to h2 (\"## ...\") so they follow the h1 correctly and maintain\nconsistent section levels throughout the file.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T17:49:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385966","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385966"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/224#discussion_r2695385966"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/224"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":3,"original_line":3,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":3,"position":3,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2695385978","pull_request_review_id":3666862054,"id":2695385978,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gqFN6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1 @@\n+nightly-2025-05-01","path":"dylint_lints/de07_security/de0706_no_direct_sqlx/rust-toolchain","commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","original_commit_id":"072f9b8ead8d2f587f07e787b943da0164a19e24","user"