url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3740310619","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#issuecomment-3740310619","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/223","id":3740310619,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7e8Jxb","user":{"login":"Artifizer","id":192502778,"node_id":"U_kgDOC3lb-g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/192502778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer","html_url":"https://github.com/Artifizer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-12T20:12:06Z","updated_at":"2026-01-12T20:12:06Z","body":"@alizid10 , can you please rename `settings` module name to `simple-user-settings` as it's temporary name and we will replace it soon anyway. Otherwise we'll not be able to create proper settings module under `settings`","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3740310619/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3754297080","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#issuecomment-3754297080","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/223","id":3754297080,"node_id":"IC_kwDOPaLyBs7fxgb4","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-15T11:35:03Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T15:13:39Z","body":"<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: summarize by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_start -->\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> ## Other AI code review bot(s) detected\n> \n> CodeRabbit has detected other AI code review bot(s) in this pull request and will avoid duplicating their findings in the review comments. This may lead to a less comprehensive review.\n\n<!-- other_code_reviewer_warning_end -->\n\n<!-- walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Walkthrough</summary>\n\n## Walkthrough\n\nAdds a new simple-user-settings Rust SDK and implementation crates, registers them in the workspace and server, implements REST endpoints (GET/POST/PATCH), SeaORM storage and migrations with composite (tenant_id,user_id) PK, domain/service/repo layers, unit and E2E tests, and OpenSpec documentation.\n\n## Changes\n\n| Cohort / File(s) | Summary |\n|---|---|\n| **Workspace & App Registration**<br>`Cargo.toml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/src/registered_modules.rs`, `apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs`, `config/e2e-local.yaml`, `config/quickstart.yaml` | Added two workspace members for simple-user-settings SDK and impl; added local dependency in hyperspot-server; imported crate alias in registered_modules; updated configs and smoke test YAML to include simple-user-settings. |\n| **SDK Crate**<br>`modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/Cargo.toml`, `.../src/lib.rs`, `.../src/api.rs`, `.../src/errors.rs`, `.../src/models.rs` | New SDK crate exposing SimpleUserSettingsClient trait (async get/update/patch), SettingsError, and transport-agnostic models (SimpleUserSettings, Patch, Update). |\n| **Implementation Manifest & Config**<br>`modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/Cargo.toml`, `.../src/config.rs`, `.../gts/errors.json` | New crate manifest and workspace bindings; SettingsConfig with max_field_length default (100); static error catalog JSON added. |\n| **Module Surface & Wiring**<br>`.../src/lib.rs`, `.../src/module.rs`, `.../src/local_client.rs` | Crate root re-exports SDK types; new SettingsModule implementing Database/Module/RestApi capabilities; LocalClient implements SDK trait and registers into client hub. |\n| **Domain Layer**<br>`.../src/domain/mod.rs`, `.../src/domain/error.rs`, `.../src/domain/fields.rs`, `.../src/domain/repo.rs`, `.../src/domain/service.rs`, `.../src/domain/service_test.rs` | Added DomainError, SettingsFields constants, SettingsRepository trait, Service with validation/default/upsert/patch logic and ServiceConfig; extensive unit tests. |\n| **Storage & Migrations**<br>`.../src/infra/mod.rs`, `.../src/infra/storage/entity.rs`, `.../src/infra/storage/mapper.rs`, `.../src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs`, `.../src/infra/storage/migrations/*`, `.../src/infra/storage/mapper_test.rs` | SeaORM entity with composite PK and Scopable secure attrs, mapper conversions, SeaOrmSettingsRepository implementing repo trait (scoped queries, ON CONFLICT upserts), initial migration and migrator. |\n| **REST API Layer**<br>`.../src/api/mod.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/dto.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/error.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/handlers.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/routes.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/dto_test.rs`, `.../src/api/rest/error_test.rs` | DTOs and conversions, DomainError→RFC9457 Problem mapping, Axum handlers (GET/POST/PATCH) with auth/license gating and OpenAPI metadata, routes registration, and unit tests. |\n| **E2E Tests & Docs**<br>`testing/e2e/modules/settings/*`, `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/**`, `modules/simple-user-settings/AGENTS.md` | New pytest E2E test suite (GET/POST/PATCH/integration), README, and extensive OpenSpec design/proposal/tasks/spec docs and agent guidance. |\n| **Misc & Infra**<br>`guidelines/DNA`, `libs/modkit/src/contracts.rs`, `testing/docker/hyperspot.Dockerfile` | Submodule pointer update, small trait-object type change in modkit contracts, and COPY proto added to Dockerfile builder stage. |\n\n## Sequence Diagram(s)\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant Handler as \"REST Handler\"\n    participant Service\n    participant Repo as \"SeaORM Repo\"\n    participant DB as \"Settings Table\"\n\n    Client->>Handler: GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings (with SecurityContext)\n    Handler->>Service: get_settings(ctx)\n    Service->>Repo: find_by_user(ctx)\n    Repo->>DB: SELECT WHERE tenant_id,user_id\n    DB-->>Repo: Model / none\n    alt Model found\n        Repo-->>Service: Some(settings)\n    else Not found\n        Service-->>Service: construct defaults from SecurityContext\n    end\n    Service-->>Handler: SimpleUserSettings\n    Handler-->>Client: 200 + JSON\n```\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    participant Client\n    participant Handler as \"REST Handler\"\n    participant Service\n    participant Repo as \"SeaORM Repo\"\n    participant DB as \"Settings Table\"\n\n    Client->>Handler: POST/PATCH {theme?, language?}\n    Handler->>Service: update_settings(ctx, update) / patch_settings(ctx, patch)\n    Service->>Service: validate_field(length)\n    alt Validation fails\n        Service-->>Handler: DomainError::Validation\n        Handler-->>Client: 422 Problem\n    else Validation passes\n        Service->>Repo: upsert_full/upsert_patch(ctx,...)\n        Repo->>DB: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT DO UPDATE / upsert logic\n        DB-->>Repo: Updated Model\n        Repo-->>Service: SimpleUserSettings\n        Service-->>Handler: SimpleUserSettings\n        Handler-->>Client: 200 + JSON\n    end\n```\n\n## Estimated code review effort\n\n🎯 4 (Complex) | ⏱️ ~45 minutes\n\n## Possibly related PRs\n\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#273 — touches module-local client/SDK surface and exports similar areas (LocalClient / SDK trait).\n- hypernetix/hyperspot#248 — related to SecurityContext changes relied upon by the new module.\n\n## Suggested reviewers\n\n- Artifizer  \n- Bechma\n\n## Poem\n\n> 🐇 I hopped through crates to plant a seed,  \n> tenant and user found with speed,  \n> GET, POST, PATCH — a tiny tune,  \n> migrations, tests, docs by noon,  \n> settings snug beneath the moon.\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- walkthrough_end -->\n\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🚥 Pre-merge checks | ✅ 2 | ❌ 1</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>❌ Failed checks (1 warning)</summary>\n\n|     Check name     | Status     | Explanation                                                                           | Resolution                                                                         |\n| :----------------: | :--------- | :------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Docstring Coverage | ⚠️ Warning | Docstring coverage is 48.55% which is insufficient. The required threshold is 80.00%. | Write docstrings for the functions missing them to satisfy the coverage threshold. |\n\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Passed checks (2 passed)</summary>\n\n|     Check name    | Status   | Explanation                                                                                                                                    |\n| :---------------: | :------- | :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Description Check | ✅ Passed | Check skipped - CodeRabbit’s high-level summary is enabled.                                                                                    |\n|    Title check    | ✅ Passed | The title 'Implementation of temp settings module' accurately describes the main objective of the PR—implementing a temporary settings module. |\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can configure your own custom pre-merge checks in the settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- pre_merge_checks_walkthrough_end -->\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>✨ Finishing touches</summary>\n\n- [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\": \"7962f53c-55bc-4827-bfbf-6a18da830691\"} --> 📝 Generate docstrings\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- finishing_touch_checkbox_end -->\n\n<!-- tips_start -->\n\n---\n\n\n\n<sub>Comment `@coderabbitai help` to get the list of available commands and usage tips.</sub>\n\n<!-- tips_end -->\n\n<!-- internal state start -->\n\n\n<!--  -->\n\n<!-- internal state end -->","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3754297080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":{"id":347564,"client_id":"Iv1.6aaafe4fe882736b","slug":"coderabbitai","node_id":"A_kwHOB96YWc4ABU2s","owner":{"login":"coderabbitai","id":132028505,"node_id":"O_kgDOB96YWQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132028505?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai","html_url":"https://github.com/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai/received_events","type":"Organization","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"name":"coderabbitai","description":"# Transforming Code Reviews with AI\r\n\r\n## Features\r\n\r\n**Automated Reviews**: Continuous reviews of the pull requests including incremental commits. \r\n\r\n**Summarization**: Generates high-level summary and a technical walkthrough of the PR changes. \r\n\r\n**Line-by-line review**: Provides line-by-line suggestions committable with one click.\r\n\r\n**Codebase verification**:  Verifies the impact on the overall codebase and identifies missing changes.\r\n\r\n**Insights into your code**:  Ask any questions on your codebase within the pull request \r\n\r\n**Chat about your code** : Chat with the bot around your code. The more you chat, the smarter it gets.\r\n\r\n**Issue Validation**:  Validates the PR against the linked issues and identifies other related issues \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n","external_url":"https://coderabbit.ai?utm_source=cr_app&utm_medium=github","html_url":"https://github