 for the settings module.\n+//! This trait defines the public API for the simple user settings module.\n //! All methods require a `SecurityContext` for authorization and access control.\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n//! `SimpleUserSettingsApi` trait definition.\n//!\n//! This trait defines the public API for the simple user settings module.\n//! All methods require a `SecurityContext` for authorization and access control.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/api.rs` around lines 1 - 4, The\nmodule doc comment incorrectly references \"SettingsApi\" while the actual trait\nis named SimpleUserSettingsApi; update the top-of-file doc comment to reference\nSimpleUserSettingsApi (or adjust wording to be trait-agnostic) so the\ndocumentation matches the declared trait name SimpleUserSettingsApi and reflects\nthat all methods require a SecurityContext for authorization.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T11:51:51Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T11:51:53Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694086279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694086279"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694086279"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyber