:"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406843","pull_request_review_id":3665656478,"id":2694406843,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gmWK7","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,172 @@\n+# user-settings Specification\n+\n+## Purpose\n+TBD - created by archiving change add-settings-module-rust. Update Purpose after archive.","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md","commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","original_commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update the Purpose section.**\n\nThe placeholder text \"TBD - created by archiving change add-settings-module-rust. Update Purpose after archive.\" should be replaced with an actual description of the module's purpose before merging.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md` around\nlines 3 - 4, Replace the placeholder under the \"## Purpose\" header (the line\ncontaining \"TBD - created by archiving change add-settings-module-rust. Update\nPurpose after archive.\") with a concise description of the module's purpose:\nsummarize the simple-user-settings module's responsibilities, its core\nfeatures/behavior, intended users or services, and any scope or constraints so\nthe Purpose section clearly states why the module exists and what it provides.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 617e89a","created_at":"2026-01-15T13:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:17:36Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406843","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406843"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406843"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":3,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":4,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":4,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406847","pull_request_review_id":3665656478,"id":2694406847,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gmWK_","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,172 @@\n+# user-settings Specification\n+\n+## Purpose\n+TBD - created by archiving change add-settings-module-rust. Update Purpose after archive.\n+## Requirements\n+### Requirement: User Settings Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL store user-specific settings (theme and language preferences) with automatic tenant and user isolation via `SecurityContext`.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Settings are tenant and user scoped\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves their settings via `SecurityContext`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only settings for that specific user and tenant combination\n+- **AND** settings from other users or tenants are not accessible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Default settings for new users\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves settings for the first time (no record exists)\n+- **THEN** the system returns empty/default values for theme and language\n+- **AND** no database record is created until the user performs an update\n+\n+### Requirement: Retrieve User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to retrieve the current user's settings using `SecurityContext` for authentication and authorization.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Successful settings retrieval\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `GET /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 200 with the user's settings (theme, language)\n+- **AND** the response uses camelCase JSON field naming\n+\n+#### Scenario: First-time user retrieval\n+- **WHEN** a new user (no existing settings record) sends `GET /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 200 with empty default values\n+- **AND** no database insert occurs\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized access\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `GET /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Full Update User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to perform a full update of user settings, replacing all fields.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Successful full update\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `POST /settings/v1/settings` with theme and language\n+- **THEN** the system updates or creates the settings record\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the updated settings\n+- **AND** both theme and language are set to the provided values\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create settings on first update\n+- **WHEN** a user without existing settings sends `POST /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system creates a new settings record\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the created settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update existing settings\n+- **WHEN** a user with existing settings sends `POST /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system updates the existing record (not create duplicate)\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized update\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `POST /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Partial Update User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to partially update user settings, modifying only the fields provided in the request.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update only theme\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /settings/v1/settings` with only theme field\n+- **THEN** the system updates only the theme value\n+- **AND** the language value remains unchanged\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update only language\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /settings/v1/settings` with only language field\n+- **THEN** the system updates only the language value\n+- **AND** the theme value remains unchanged\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update both fields via PATCH\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /settings/v1/settings` with both theme and language\n+- **THEN** the system updates both values\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Patch creates settings if not exists\n+- **WHEN** a user without existing settings sends `PATCH /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system creates a new settings record with provided fields\n+- **AND** unspecified fields remain empty/default\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the created settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized partial update\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `PATCH /settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Security Context Integration\n+\n+The system SHALL use `SecurityContext` to automatically extract tenant_id and user_id without requiring these values in the request payload or URL.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Tenant isolation enforcement\n+- **WHEN** a user from tenant A attempts to access settings\n+- **THEN** the system only returns/modifies settings for tenant A\n+- **AND** settings from other tenants are never accessible regardless of user_id\n+\n+#### Scenario: User isolation enforcement\n+- **WHEN** user X from a tenant attempts to access settings\n+- **THEN** the system only returns/modifies settings for user X\n+- **AND** settings from other users in the same tenant are not accessible\n+\n+### Requirement: Data Model\n+\n+The system SHALL store user settings with the following fields:\n+- `user_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+- `tenant_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+- `theme` (String, optional)\n+- `language` (String, optional)","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind modules/simple-user-settings -type f -name \"*.md\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 684\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind modules/simple-user-settings -type f -name \"*initial*\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 157\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md | sed -n '100,120p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1067\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/migrations/initial_001.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1619\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind modules/simple-user-settings -type f -name \"*.rs\" | grep -E \"(entity|model|settings)\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1451\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/migrations -type f -name \"*.rs\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 243\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nrg -l \"created_at|updated_at\" modules/simple-user-settings --type rust | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind modules/simple-user-settings -type f -name \"*.rs\" | xargs grep -l \"entity\\|Entity\" | grep -E \"(entity|entities)\" | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 141\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/fields.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 253\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/mod.rs | head -50\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 217\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/entity.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 815\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3158\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Spec-implementation mismatch on field optionality and missing timestamp columns.**\n\nThe spec declares `theme` and `language` as optional, but the migration creates them with `.not_null()` constraints (lines 16-17 of `initial_001.rs`). The entity defines these as non-optional `String` types, requiring values always present.\n\nAdditionally, the spec requires `created_at` and `updated_at` fields (lines 114-115), but the migration and entity omit them entirely.\n\nOptions to resolve:\n1. Update the spec to reflect that `theme` and `language` are required, and remove `created_at`/`updated_at` requirements, OR\n2. Modify the migration to use `.nullable()` for `theme`/`language` and add timestamp columns with appropriate defaults.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md` around\nlines 112 - 113, The migration in initial_001.rs and the corresponding entity\ncurrently make theme and language non-nullable but the spec marks them optional,\nand created_at/updated_at are missing from both spec and implementation; decide\nand apply one of the two fixes: either (A) update the spec to mark theme and\nlanguage as required and remove created_at/updated_at requirements, or (B)\nchange the migration in initial_001.rs to make the theme and language columns\nnullable (use .nullable() instead of .not_null()) and add created_at and\nupdated_at timestamp columns with appropriate defaults (e.g.,\nCURRENT_TIMESTAMP/now()) and update the entity struct to make theme and language\nOption<String> and add created_at/updated_at fields (e.g., chrono::DateTime) to\nmatch the migration.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 617e89a","created_at":"2026-01-15T13:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:17:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406847","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406847"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406847"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":118,"original_start_line":112,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":119,"original_line":113,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":113,"position":119,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406854","pull_request_review_id":3665656478,"id":2694406854,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gmWLG","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,271 @@\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::super::*;\n+    use async_trait::async_trait;\n+    use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+    use simple_user_settings_sdk::models::{SimpleUserSettings, SimpleUserSettingsPatch};\n+    use std::sync::Arc;\n+    use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+    // Mock repository for testing\n+    struct MockRepository {\n+        find_result: Option<SimpleUserSettings>,\n+        upsert_result: SimpleUserSettings,\n+    }\n+\n+    #[async_trait]\n+    impl repo::SettingsRepository for MockRepository {\n+        async fn find_by_user(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<Option<SimpleUserSettings>> {\n+            Ok(self.find_result.clone())\n+        }\n+\n+        async fn upsert_full(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+            theme: String,\n+            language: String,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n+            Ok(SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id: self.upsert_result.user_id,\n+                tenant_id: self.upsert_result.tenant_id,\n+                theme,\n+                language,\n+            })\n+        }\n+\n+        async fn upsert_patch(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+            patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n+            let mut result = self.upsert_result.clone();\n+            if let Some(theme) = patch.theme {\n+                result.theme = theme;\n+            }\n+            if let Some(language) = patch.language {\n+                result.language = language;\n+            }\n+            Ok(result)\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    fn create_test_context() -> SecurityContext {\n+        SecurityContext::anonymous()\n+    }\n+\n+    #[tokio::test]\n+    async fn test_get_settings_returns_existing() {\n+        let user_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+        let tenant_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+        let existing = SimpleUserSettings {\n+            user_id,\n+            tenant_id,\n+            theme: \"dark\".to_owned(),\n+            language: \"en\".to_owned(),\n+        };\n+\n+        let repo = Arc::new(MockRepository {\n+            find_result: Some(existing.clone()),\n+            upsert_result: existing.clone(),\n+        });\n+\n+        let service = service::Service::new(repo, service::ServiceConfig::default());\n+        let ctx = create_test_context();\n+\n+        let result = service.get_settings(&ctx).await.unwrap();\n+\n+        assert_eq!(result.theme, \"dark\");\n+        assert_eq!(result.language, \"en\");\n+    }\n+\n+    #[tokio::test]\n+    async fn test_get_settings_returns_defaults_when_not_found() {\n+        let user_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+        let tenant_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+\n+        let repo = Arc::new(MockRepository {\n+            find_result: None,\n+            upsert_result: SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id,\n+                tenant_id,\n+                theme: String::new(),\n+                language: String::new(),\n+            },\n+        });\n+\n+        let service = service::Service::new(repo, service::ServiceConfig::default());\n+        let ctx = create_test_context();\n+\n+        let result = service.get_settings(&ctx).await.unwrap();\n+\n+        assert_eq!(result.theme, \"\");\n+        assert_eq!(result.language, \"\");\n+    }","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"h