created UUIDs on lines 86-87 should either be removed if unused, or verified against the returned result.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs`\naround lines 84 - 106, The test\ntest_get_settings_returns_defaults_when_not_found creates local user_id and\ntenant_id but doesn't assert returned IDs; update the test to either remove the\nunused local UUIDs or add assertions that the returned result.user_id equals\nctx.subject_id() and result.tenant_id equals ctx.tenant_id() so the defaults\nfrom service::Service::get_settings are verified; reference the test function\nname and the SecurityContext accessors ctx.subject_id() and ctx.tenant_id() when\nmaking the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 617e89a","created_at":"2026-01-15T13:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:17:39Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406854","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406854"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406854"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406854/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":86,"original_start_line":84,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":107,"original_line":106,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":106,"position":107,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406860","pull_request_review_id":3665656478,"id":2694406860,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gmWLM","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@\n+use sea_orm_migration::prelude::*;\n+\n+#[derive(DeriveMigrationName)]\n+pub struct Migration;\n+\n+#[async_trait::async_trait]\n+impl MigrationTrait for Migration {\n+    async fn up(&self, manager: &SchemaManager) -> Result<(), DbErr> {\n+        manager\n+            .create_table(\n+                Table::create()\n+                    .table(Settings::Table)\n+                    .if_not_exists()\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::TenantId).uuid().not_null())\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::UserId).uuid().not_null())\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::Theme).string().not_null())\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::Language).string().not_null())","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/migrations/initial_001.rs","commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","original_commit_id":"5e234d6ef6dfa938ff81aac93a8943ee6647e684","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Missing `created_at` and `updated_at` columns required by specification.**\n\nThe spec defines that the system SHALL store user settings with `created_at` (Timestamp) and `updated_at` (Timestamp) fields. The migration creates only `theme` and `language` but omits the timestamp columns needed for \"Automatic timestamp management\" scenarios.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🐛 Proposed fix to add timestamp columns</summary>\n\n```diff\n                     .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::TenantId).uuid().not_null())\n                     .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::UserId).uuid().not_null())\n                     .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::Theme).string().not_null())\n                     .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::Language).string().not_null())\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::CreatedAt).timestamp_with_time_zone().not_null())\n+                    .col(ColumnDef::new(Settings::UpdatedAt).timestamp_with_time_zone().not_null())\n                     .primary_key(\n```\n\nAlso update the `Settings` enum:\n\n```diff\n #[derive(DeriveIden)]\n enum Settings {\n     Table,\n     TenantId,\n     UserId,\n     Theme,\n     Language,\n+    CreatedAt,\n+    UpdatedAt,\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/migrations/initial_001.rs`\naround lines 14 - 17, Add the missing timestamp columns to the migration and the\nSettings enum: in the table builder (where ColumnDef::new(Settings::TenantId),\nColumnDef::new(Settings::UserId), ColumnDef::new(Settings::Theme),\nColumnDef::new(Settings::Language) are defined) add ColumnDef entries for\nSettings::CreatedAt and Settings::UpdatedAt using the timestamp type (e.g.,\n.timestamp()), mark created_at as not_null (and updated_at as not_null or\nnullable per spec), and optionally add defaults (CURRENT_TIMESTAMP) if required;\nalso update the Settings enum to include CreatedAt and UpdatedAt variants so the\ncolumn identifiers compile and align with the spec.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:medusa:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-15T13:32:38Z","updated_at":"2026-01-15T13:32:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406860","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406860"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2694406860"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2694406860/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":14,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":17,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":17,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906015","pull_request_review_id":3670091410,"id":2697906015,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzsdf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@\n+# Change: Add User Settings Module in Rust","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"99963e5edb47a5770c7b071a20a3fd01001d7f95","user":{"login":"alizid10","id":247960800,"node_id":"U_kgDODseU4A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/247960800?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10","html_url":"https://github.com/alizid10","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alizid10/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"done","created_at":"2026-01-16T10:23:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:23:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906015","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906015"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906015"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906015/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":1,"original_line":1,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2694066114,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":1,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906300","pull_request_review_id":3670091713,"id":2697906300,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzsh8","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@\n+# User Settings Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: User Settings Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL store user-specific settings (theme and language preferences) with automatic tenant and user isolation via `SecurityContext`.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Settings are tenant and user scoped\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves their settings via `SecurityContext`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only settings for that specific user and tenant combination\n+- **AND** settings from other users or tenants are not accessible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Default settings for new users\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves settings for the first time (no record exists)\n+- **THEN** the system returns empty/default values for theme and language\n+- **AND** no database record is created until the user performs an update\n+\n+### Requirement: Retrieve User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to retrieve the current user's settings using `SecurityContext` for authentication and authorization.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Successful settings retrieval\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 200 with the user's settings (theme, language)\n+- **AND** the response uses camelCase JSON field naming","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md","commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16","original_commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Spec says camelCase but REST DTOs serialize snake_case.**  \nLine 26 conflicts with the actual JSON field naming (the REST DTOs use `#[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]`). This is an API contract mismatch.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- - **AND** the response uses camelCase JSON field naming\n+ - **AND** the response uses snake_case JSON field naming\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md`\naround lines 23 - 26, The spec's \"camelCase JSON field naming\" is incorrect and\nmust be aligned with the REST DTOs which use #[serde(rename_all =\n\"snake_case\")]; update the Scenario in specs/user-settings/spec.md (the GET\n/simple-user-settings/v1/settings scenario) to state that the response uses\nsnake_case JSON field naming (or alternatively change the REST DTO attribute on\nthe UserSettings/response struct from #[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")] to\ncamelCase if you intend the API to be camelCase), and ensure the example\nresponse and any references to field names match the chosen casing.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 2cbe52a","created_at":"2026-01-16T10:23:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T10:39:55Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906300","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906300"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906300"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":23,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":26,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":26,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906307","pull_request_review_id":3670091713,"id":2697906307,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzsiD","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@\n+# User Settings Specification\n+\n+## ADDED Requirements\n+\n+### Requirement: User Settings Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL store user-specific settings (theme and language preferences) with automatic tenant and user isolation via `SecurityContext`.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Settings are tenant and user scoped\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves their settings via `SecurityContext`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only settings for that specific user and tenant combination\n+- **AND** settings from other users or tenants are not accessible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Default settings for new users\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves settings for the first time (no record exists)\n+- **THEN** the system returns empty/default values for theme and language\n+- **AND** no database record is created until the user performs an update\n+\n+### Requirement: Retrieve User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to retrieve the current user's settings using `SecurityContext` for authentication and authorization.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Successful settings retrieval\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 200 with the user's settings (theme, language)\n+- **AND** the response uses camelCase JSON field naming\n+\n+#### Scenario: First-time user retrieval\n+- **WHEN** a new user (no existing settings record) sends `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 200 with empty default values\n+- **AND** no database insert occurs\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized access\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Full Update User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to perform a full update of user settings, replacing all fields.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Successful full update\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `POST /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` with theme and language\n+- **THEN** the system updates or creates the settings record\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the updated settings\n+- **AND** both theme and language are set to the provided values\n+\n+#### Scenario: Create settings on first update\n+- **WHEN** a user without existing settings sends `POST /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system creates a new settings record\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the created settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update existing settings\n+- **WHEN** a user with existing settings sends `POST /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system updates the existing record (not create duplicate)\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized update\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `POST /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Partial Update User Settings\n+\n+The system SHALL provide a REST endpoint to partially update user settings, modifying only the fields provided in the request.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update only theme\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` with only theme field\n+- **THEN** the system updates only the theme value\n+- **AND** the language value remains unchanged\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update only language\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` with only language field\n+- **THEN** the system updates only the language value\n+- **AND** the theme value remains unchanged\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Update both fields via PATCH\n+- **WHEN** an authenticated user sends `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` with both theme and language\n+- **THEN** the system updates both values\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the complete updated settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Patch creates settings if not exists\n+- **WHEN** a user without existing settings sends `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system creates a new settings record with provided fields\n+- **AND** unspecified fields remain empty/default\n+- **AND** returns HTTP 200 with the created settings\n+\n+#### Scenario: Unauthorized partial update\n+- **WHEN** an unauthenticated request is sent to `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`\n+- **THEN** the system returns HTTP 401 Unauthorized\n+\n+### Requirement: Security Context Integration\n+\n+The system SHALL use `SecurityContext` to automatically extract tenant_id and user_id without requiring these values in the request payload or URL.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Tenant isolation enforcement\n+- **WHEN** a user from tenant A attempts to access settings\n+- **THEN** the system only returns/modifies settings for tenant A\n+- **AND** settings from other tenants are never accessible regardless of user_id\n+\n+#### Scenario: User isolation enforcement\n+- **WHEN** user X from a tenant attempts to access settings\n+- **THEN** the system only returns/modifies settings for user X\n+- **AND** settings from other users in the same tenant are not accessible\n+\n+### Requirement: Data Model\n+\n+ The system SHALL store user settings with the following fields:\n+ - `user_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+ - `tenant_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+ - `theme` (String, optional)\n+ - `language` (String, optional)\n+ \n+ #### Scenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\n+ - **WHEN** the system stores settings\n+ - **THEN** the combination of (tenant_id, user_id) is unique\n+ - **AND** no duplicate settings records exist for the same user-tenant pair","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md","commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16","original_commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Fix heading/list indentation to satisfy markdownlint.**  \nMarkdownlint flags the indented heading/list in this section.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n- The system SHALL store user settings with the following fields:\n- - `user_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n- - `tenant_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n- - `theme` (String, optional)\n- - `language` (String, optional)\n- \n- #### Scenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\n- - **WHEN** the system stores settings\n- - **THEN** the combination of (tenant_id, user_id) is unique\n- - **AND** no duplicate settings records exist for the same user-tenant pair\n+The system SHALL store user settings with the following fields:\n+- `user_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+- `tenant_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n+- `theme` (String, optional)\n+- `language` (String, optional)\n+\n+#### Scenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\n+- **WHEN** the system stores settings\n+- **THEN** the combination of (tenant_id, user_id) is unique\n+- **AND** no duplicate settings records exist for the same user-tenant pair\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\nThe system SHALL store user settings with the following fields:\n- `user_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n- `tenant_id` (UUID, part of composite primary key)\n- `theme` (String, optional)\n- `language` (String, optional)\n\n#### Scenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\n- **WHEN** the system stores settings\n- **THEN** the combination of (tenant_id, user_id) is unique\n- **AND** no duplicate settings records exist for the same user-tenant pair\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧰 Tools</summary>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🪛 markdownlint-cli2 (0.18.1)</summary>\n\n109-109: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n110-110: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n111-111: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n112-112: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n114-114: Headings must start at the beginning of the line\n\n(MD023, heading-start-left)\n\n---\n\n115-115: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n116-116: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n---\n\n117-117: Unordered list indentation\nExpected: 0; Actual: 1\n\n(MD007, ul-indent)\n\n</details>\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md`\naround lines 108 - 117, The \"Scenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\" heading\nand its following list are over-indented causing markdownlint errors; open the\nspecs/user-settings/spec.md and fix the indentation by unindenting the \"####\nScenario: Composite primary key uniqueness\" heading and the subsequent list\nitems so they align with the top-level list (remove the extra leading spaces),\nensure there is a blank line before the heading, and make the bullet lines for\nWHEN/THEN/AND use consistent top-level indentation so markdownlint no longer\nflags them.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit fba0482","created_at":"2026-01-16T10:23:59Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T12:56:24Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906307","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906307"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2697906307"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906307/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":108,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":117,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":117,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2697906312","pull_request_review_id":3670091713,"id":2697906312,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6gzsiI","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,178 @@\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use axum::{extract::Extension, Json};\n+use modkit::api::prelude::*;\n+use modkit_auth::axum_ext::AuthzContext;\n+\n+use crate::domain::service::Service;\n+\n+use super::dto::{\n+    PatchSimpleUserSettingsRequest, SimpleUserSettingsDto, UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest,\n+};\n+\n+pub async fn get_settings(\n+    AuthzContext(ctx): AuthzContext,\n+    Extension(svc): Extension<Arc<Service>>,\n+) -> ApiResult<JsonBody<SimpleUserSettingsDto>> {\n+    let settings = svc.get_settings(&ctx).await?;\n+    Ok(Json(settings.into()))\n+}\n+\n+pub async fn update_settings(\n+    AuthzContext(ctx): AuthzContext,\n+    Extension(svc): Extension<Arc<Service>>,\n+    Json(req): Json<UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest>,\n+) -> ApiResult<impl IntoResponse> {\n+    let settings = svc\n+        .update_settings(&ctx, Some(req.theme), Some(req.language))\n+        .await?;\n+    let dto: SimpleUserSettingsDto = settings.into();\n+    Ok((StatusCode::OK, Json(dto)))\n+}\n+\n+pub async fn patch_settings(\n+    AuthzContext(ctx): AuthzContext,\n+    Extension(svc): Extension<Arc<Service>>,\n+    Json(req): Json<PatchSimpleUserSettingsRequest>,\n+) -> ApiResult<JsonBody<SimpleUserSettingsDto>> {\n+    let settings = svc.patch_settings(&ctx, req.into()).await?;\n+    Ok(Json(settings.into()))\n+}\n+\n+#[cfg(test)]\n+mod tests {\n+    use super::*;\n+    use crate::domain::repo::SettingsRepository;\n+    use crate::domain::service::ServiceConfig;\n+    use async_trait::async_trait;\n+    use axum::body::Body;\n+    use axum::http::{Request, StatusCode};\n+    use axum::routing::{get, patch, post};\n+    use axum::Router;\n+    use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+    use simple_user_settings_sdk::models::{SimpleUserSettings, SimpleUserSettingsPatch};\n+    use tower::ServiceExt as _;\n+    use uuid::Uuid;\n+\n+    struct MockRepository {\n+        find_result: Option<SimpleUserSettings>,\n+        upsert_result: SimpleUserSettings,\n+    }\n+\n+    #[async_trait]\n+    impl SettingsRepository for MockRepository {\n+        async fn find_by_user(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<Option<SimpleUserSettings>> {\n+            Ok(self.find_result.clone())\n+        }\n+\n+        async fn upsert_full(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+            theme: Option<String>,\n+            language: Option<String>,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n+            Ok(SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id: self.upsert_result.user_id,\n+                tenant_id: self.upsert_result.tenant_id,\n+                theme,\n+                language,\n+            })\n+        }\n+\n+        async fn upsert_patch(\n+            &self,\n+            _ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+            patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n+        ) -> anyhow::Result<SimpleUserSettings> {\n+            let mut result = self.upsert_result.clone();\n+            if let Some(theme) = patch.theme {\n+                result.theme = Some(theme);\n+            }\n+            if let Some(language) = patch.language {\n+                result.language = Some(language);\n+            }\n+            Ok(result)\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    fn create_test_service() -> Arc<Service> {\n+        let user_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+        let tenant_id = Uuid::new_v4();\n+        let repo = Arc::new(MockRepository {\n+            find_result: Some(SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id,\n+                tenant_id,\n+                theme: Some(\"dark\".to_owned()),\n+                language: Some(\"en\".to_owned()),\n+            }),\n+            upsert_result: SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id,\n+                tenant_id,\n+                theme: Some(\"dark\".to_owned()),\n+                language: Some(\"en\".to_owned()),\n+            },\n+        });\n+        Arc::new(Service::new(repo, ServiceConfig::default()))\n+    }\n+\n+    fn create_test_router(service: Arc<Service>) -> Router {\n+        Router::new()\n+            .route(\"/get\", get(get_settings))\n+            .route(\"/update\", post(update_settings))\n+            .route(\"/patch\", patch(patch_settings))\n+            .layer(Extension(service))\n+            .layer(Extension(SecurityContext::anonymous()))\n+    }","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/handlers.rs","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# First, find the handlers.rs file and understand the imports\nfind . -name \"handlers.rs\" -path \"*/rest/*\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 488\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Search for AuthzContext extractor implementation\nrg \"impl FromRequestParts\" -A 20 --type rust | grep -A 20 \"AuthzContext\"\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Also search for the AuthzContext type definition\nrg \"struct AuthzContext|enum AuthzContext\" -B 2 -A 10 --type rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 882\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Get the full FromRequestParts implementation for AuthzContext\ncat -n libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs | sed -n '1,50p'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1771\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Rea