- Full update of settings\n+  - `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` - Partial update of settings\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n- Implement REST API with three endpoints:\n  - `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` - Retrieve user settings\n  - `POST /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` - Full update of settings\n  - `PATCH /simple-user-settings/v1/settings` - Partial update of settings\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn\n`@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md`\naround lines 11 - 14, Update the REST endpoint paths listed in the proposal to\nmatch the implementation by replacing `/settings/v1/settings` with the canonical\npath `/simple-user-settings/v1/settings` for all three endpoints (`GET`, `POST`,\n`PATCH`) so the bullets read `GET /simple-user-settings/v1/settings`, `POST\n/simple-user-settings/v1/settings`, and `PATCH\n/simple-user-settings/v1/settings`.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit bff26a2","created_at":"2026-01-16T12:08:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T17:05:12Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2698280132","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698280132"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2698280132"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698280132/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":11,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":null,"original_line":14,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":14,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698280141","pull_request_review_id":3670586975,"id":2698280141,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6g1HzN","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,161 @@\n+# user-settings Specification\n+\n+## Purpose\n+The `simple-user-settings` module provides per-user, per-tenant storage and retrieval of basic UI preferences (currently theme and language) scoped automatically via `SecurityContext`. It exposes REST endpoints for get/full update/partial update and ships a transport-agnostic SDK (`simple-user-settings-sdk`) for inter-module access. Scope is intentionally limited to simple user preferences (not admin/global settings), enforcing tenant/user isolation and secure, deny-by-default data access.\n+## Requirements\n+### Requirement: User Settings Storage\n+\n+The system SHALL store user-specific settings (theme and language preferences) with automatic tenant and user isolation via `SecurityContext`.\n+\n+#### Scenario: Settings are tenant and user scoped\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves their settings via `SecurityContext`\n+- **THEN** the system returns only settings for that specific user and tenant combination\n+- **AND** settings from other users or tenants are not accessible\n+\n+#### Scenario: Default settings for new users\n+- **WHEN** a user retrieves settings for the first time (no record exists)\n+- **THEN** the system returns empty/default values for theme and language\n+- **AND** no database record is created until the 