le-user-settings\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 186\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check REST error construction paths to understand how errors are mapped\nrg -n \"ProblemDetails|problem|error\" -g '*.rs' modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest --context 3\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 15629\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for SettingsError usage throughout the codebase\nrg -n \"SettingsError\" -g '*.rs' modules/simple-user-settings\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1840\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check domain/error.rs to understand DomainError structure\ncat -n modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/error.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1244\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Look at service.rs to see how validation errors are created\nsed -n '80,95p' modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 504\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Preserve validation field info in SDK errors.**\n\n`SettingsError::Validation` loses field-level structure when converting from `DomainError::Validation` (see domain/error.rs:28–29, where field and message are concatenated into a single string). Add `field: String` to keep the data structured end‑to‑end, and update the conversion and constructor accordingly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✅ Proposed adjustment</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    #[error(\"Validation error: {message}\")]\n-    Validation { message: String },\n+    #[error(\"Validation error on {field}: {message}\")]\n+    Validation { field: String, message: String },\n...\n-    pub fn validation(message: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n+    pub fn validation(field: impl Into<String>, message: impl Into<String>) -> Self {\n         Self::Validation {\n+            field: field.into(),\n             message: message.into(),\n         }\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\nUpdate the conversion in domain/error.rs to preserve structure:\n```diff\n-            DomainError::Validation { field, message } => {\n-                Self::validation(format!(\"{field}: {message}\"))\n-            }\n+            DomainError::Validation { field, message } => {\n+                Self::validation(field, message)\n+            }\n```\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/errors.rs` around\nlines 10 - 12, SettingsError::Validation currently flattens domain validation\ninfo into a single message causing loss of the field name; change the enum\nvariant to include field: String (i.e., Validation { field: String, message:\nString }) and update the conversion from DomainError::Validation (and any\nrelated constructor functions) to map domain.field -> field and domain.message\n-> message so the field-level structure is preserved end-to-end (update the\nSettingsError::from / impl From<DomainError> and any\nSettingsError::new_validation helper to accept and set the field).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit bff26a2","created_at":"2026-01-16T12:08:32Z","updated_at":"2026-01-16T17:05:17Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2698280144","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698280144"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2698280144"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2698280144/reactions","total_co