pi.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_🛠️ Refactor suggestion_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check what database backends other modules in the codebase use for sea-orm\necho \"=== Checking sea-orm features in Cargo.toml files ===\"\nfind . -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f -exec grep -l \"sea-orm\" {} \\; | head -20\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Detailed sea-orm dependency configuration ===\"\nfind . -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f -exec grep -A 2 \"sea-orm\" {} + | head -100\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Checking for database configuration patterns ===\"\nfind . -name \"*.rs\" -o -name \"*.toml\" | xargs grep -l \"DATABASE_URL\\|db_url\\|postgres\\|sqlite\" 2>/dev/null | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3783\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check what dependencies simple-user-settings module has\necho \"=== simple-user-settings module dependencies ===\"\ncat ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/Cargo.toml | grep -A 2 \"\\[dependencies\\]\"\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Check if simple-user-settings uses modkit-db ===\"\ngrep -r \"modkit.db\\|modkit_db\" ./modules/simple-user-settings/ 2>/dev/null || echo \"No modkit-db usage found\"\n\necho -e \"\\n=== Check if simple-user-settings has its own sea-orm queries ===\"\nfind ./modules/simple-user-settings -name \"*.rs\" | xargs grep -l \"sea_orm\\|sea-orm\" | head -10\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1425\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\necho \"=== modkit-db Cargo.toml features section ===\"\nsed -n '/\\[features\\]/,/\\[dependencies\\]/p' ./libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml | head -20\n\necho -e \"\\n=== How modkit-db declares sea-orm ===\"\ngrep -A 2 'sea-orm = ' ./libs/modkit-db/Cargo.toml\n\necho -e \"\\n=== simple-user-settings full dependencies ===\"\nsed -n '/\\[dependencies\\]/,/\\[dev-dependencies\\]/p' ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 2017\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Remove hard-coded SQLite dependency and use modkit-db's configurable database abstraction.**\n\nThe `simple-user-settings` module depends on `modkit-db`, which provides configurable database backends via Cargo features (`pg`, `mysql`, `sqlite`). However, the module also declares a direct `sea-orm` dependency with hard-coded `sqlx-sqlite` feature, bypassing the abstraction. This locks the module to SQLite regardless of how `modkit-db` is configured, creating potential deployment mismatches (e.g., if `modkit-db` is built with PostgreSQL features for production, this module still uses SQLite).\n\nRemove the direct `sea-orm` and `sea-orm-migration` dependencies, or if they are necessary, configure them as optional and expose database selection via Cargo features (following `modkit-db`'s pattern).\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/Cargo.toml` at line 26, The\nCargo.toml currently hard-codes sea-orm with the sqlx-sqlite feature which\noverrides modkit-db's configurable backend; remove the direct sea-orm and\nsea-orm-migration entries (or make them optional) and instead mirror modkit-db's\nfeature-driven pattern: add optional dependencies for sea-orm/sea-orm-migration\nwith default-features = false and create cargo features (e.g., pg, mysql,\nsqlite) that enable the appropriate sqlx backend feature on sea-orm and/or\nsimply rely on modkit-db transitively; update the features section to expose the\nsame database selection flags and ensure any code references to sea-orm types\nremain behind these features or use modkit-db abstractions (reference symbols:\nthe sea-orm dependency line, sea-orm-migration line, and modkit-db feature\nnames).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:15:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T13:15:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2704735884","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735884"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2704735884"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735884/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":26,"original_line":26,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":26,"position":26,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735889","pull_request_review_id":3678053160,"id":2704735889,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hNv6R","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@\n+use std::sync::Arc;\n+\n+use modkit_security::SecurityContext;\n+use simple_user_settings_sdk::models::{\n+    SimpleUserSettings, SimpleUserSettingsPatch, SimpleUserSettingsUpdate,\n+};\n+\n+use super::error::DomainError;\n+use super::fields::SettingsFields;\n+use super::repo::SettingsRepository;\n+\n+pub struct ServiceConfig {\n+    pub max_field_length: usize,\n+}\n+\n+impl Default for ServiceConfig {\n+    fn default() -> Self {\n+        Self {\n+            max_field_length: 100,\n+        }\n+    }\n+}\n+\n+pub struct Service {\n+    repo: Arc<dyn SettingsRepository>,\n+    config: ServiceConfig,\n+}\n+\n+impl Service {\n+    pub fn new(repo: Arc<dyn SettingsRepository>, config: ServiceConfig) -> Self {\n+        Self { repo, config }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub async fn get_settings(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+    ) -> Result<SimpleUserSettings, DomainError> {\n+        if let Some(settings) = self.repo.find_by_user(ctx).await? {\n+            Ok(settings)\n+        } else {\n+            let user_id = ctx.subject_id();\n+            let tenant_id = ctx.tenant_id();\n+\n+            Ok(SimpleUserSettings {\n+                user_id,\n+                tenant_id,\n+                theme: None,\n+                language: None,\n+            })\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    pub async fn update_settings(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+        update: SimpleUserSettingsUpdate,\n+    ) -> Result<SimpleUserSettings, DomainError> {\n+        self.validate_field(SettingsFields::THEME, &update.theme)?;\n+        self.validate_field(SettingsFields::LANGUAGE, &update.language)?;\n+\n+        let settings = self\n+            .repo\n+            .upsert_full(ctx, Some(update.theme), Some(update.language))\n+            .await?;\n+        Ok(settings)\n+    }\n+\n+    pub async fn patch_settings(\n+        &self,\n+        ctx: &SecurityContext,\n+        patch: SimpleUserSettingsPatch,\n+    ) -> Result<SimpleUserSettings, DomainError> {\n+        if let Some(ref theme) = patch.theme {\n+            self.validate_field(SettingsFields::THEME, theme)?;\n+        }\n+        if let Some(ref language) = patch.language {\n+            self.validate_field(SettingsFields::LANGUAGE, language)?;\n+        }\n+\n+        let settings = self.repo.upsert_patch(ctx, patch).await?;\n+        Ok(settings)\n+    }\n+\n+    fn validate_field(&self, field: &str, value: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n+        if value.len() > self.config.max_field_length {\n+            return Err(DomainError::validation(\n+                field,\n+                format!(\"exceeds maximum length of {}\", self.config.max_field_length),\n+            ));\n+        }\n+        Ok(())","path":"modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"0eb00141e0dbb376fab73e812618ecde0b320974","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfind . -type f -name \"service.rs\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 974\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nfd \"simple-user-settings\" --type d\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 199\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ngit ls-files | grep -E \"(simple-user-settings|service\\.rs)\" | head -20\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 1522\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs | head -120\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 3273\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\nwc -l ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 140\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ngrep -n \"max_field_length\" ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 286\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Search for config definition and types\nrg \"struct.*Config|max_field_length\" ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src --type rust -A 5 -B 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 6645\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\ncat -n ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 10632\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if there are any tests with multi-byte characters\nrg \"测|日|こ|é|ñ|Ω\" ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src --type rust\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 46\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check for any documentation or comments about field length\nrg \"max_field_length|field.*length|character|byte\" ./modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src --type rust -B 2 -A 2\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 6501\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Clarify length semantics (bytes vs. characters).**\n\n`value.len()` counts bytes, so non-ASCII input may be rejected earlier than intended. If the limit is meant to be user-visible characters, consider using `chars().count()` instead. Currently, all test cases and default field values are ASCII, so this doesn't affect the present implementation, but should be clarified for future use with internationalized content.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Possible fix (character count)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-        if value.len() > self.config.max_field_length {\n+        let length = value.chars().count();\n+        if length > self.config.max_field_length {\n             return Err(DomainError::validation(\n                 field,\n                 format!(\"exceeds maximum length of {}\", self.config.max_field_length),\n             ));\n         }\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n    fn validate_field(&self, field: &str, value: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n        let length = value.chars().count();\n        if length > self.config.max_field_length {\n            return Err(DomainError::validation(\n                field,\n                format!(\"exceeds maximum length of {}\", self.config.max_field_length),\n            ));\n        }\n        Ok(())\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs`\naround lines 84 - 91, The validation in validate_field currently uses\nvalue.len() (byte length) which incorrectly counts bytes for non-ASCII text;\nchange the check to count user-visible characters by using value.chars().count()\ncompared against self.config.max_field_length (or document that max_field_length\nis bytes if that is intended), and update the error message/logic in\nvalidate_field and any related tests to reflect character-based limits\n(references: validate_field, self.config.max_field_length,\nDomainError::validation).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-19T13:15:26Z","updated_at":"2026-01-19T13:15:27Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2704735889","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735889"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#discussion_r2704735889"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735889/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":84,"original_start_line":84,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":91,"original_line":91,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":91,"position":91,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2704735897","pull_request_review_id":3678053160,"id":2704735897,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6hNv6Z","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,70 @@\n+# Settings Module E2E Tests\n+\n+This directory contains end-to-end tests for the settings module REST API.\n+\n+## Test Files\n+\n+- **test_settings_get.py** - Tests for GET /settings/v1/settings endpoint\n+  - Returns defaults when settings don't exist (lazy creation)\n+  - Idempotency\n+  - Authentication handling\n+\n+- **test_settings_update.py** - Tests for POST /settings/v1/settings endpoint (full update)\n+  - Creates settings on first call (upsert)\n+  - Replaces existing settings\n+  - Validation (max length)\n+  - Error handling (missing fields)\n+\n+- **test_settings_patch.py** - Tests for PATCH /settings/v1/settings endpoint (partial update)\n+  - Updates only provided fields\n+  - Creates settings if not exist (upsert)\n+  - Sequential partial updates\n+  - Empty patch handling\n+\n+- **test_settings_integration.py** - Integration tests covering full workflows","path":"testing/e2e/modules/settings/README.md","commit_id":"f154644beca8697855955fa21f5b6fc95b5eb0bd","original_commit_id":"0eb00141e0dbb376fab73e812618ecde0b320974","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n**Update endpoint paths to `/simple-user-settings/v1/settings`.**  \nLine 7–24 list `/settings/v1/settin