ng with the actual module location and Artifizer's rename request.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/project.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-136`: **LGTM!**\n\nThis project context documentation is comprehensive and well-structured. It clearly outlines the tech stack, conventions, and references to relevant guideline documents for the simple-user-settings module.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/gts/errors.json (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-17`: **LGTM!**\n\nThe error catalog is well-structured with appropriate HTTP status codes and descriptive error codes following the project's naming convention.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-456`: **LGTM!**\n\nComprehensive OpenSpec instructions document covering the complete workflow for spec-driven development. The three-stage workflow, CLI commands, and best practices are well documented.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/models.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-22`: **LGTM!**\n\nClean, transport-agnostic SDK models following the project's SDK pattern. The separation of full entity (`SimpleUserSettings`) and partial update (`SimpleUserSettingsPatch`) is appropriate for the GET/POST/PATCH semantics documented in the design.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/design.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`110-113`: **Race condition mitigation is well addressed.**\n\nThe UPSERT approach using `INSERT ... ON CONFLICT UPDATE` or SeaORM's `save()` method is the correct solution for handling concurrent PATCH requests for new users.\n\n---\n\n`1-157`: **LGTM!**\n\nThorough design document with clear decisions, rationale, and risk mitigations. The SDK pattern, composite key design, and lazy creation approach are well-justified and align with ModKit conventions.\n\n---\n\n`147-148`: The string length validation for theme/language fields has been properly implemented in the domain layer. The `validate_field` method enforces the 100-character limit specified in the design, applied to both `update_settings` and `patch_settings` operations. Comprehensive tests verify this behavior, including boundary conditions.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/config.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-18`: **LGTM: config defaults are clear and consistent.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/repo.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-24`: **LGTM: repository interface is clean and complete.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/dto.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-51`: **LGTM: DTOs and conversions are straightforward.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/dto_test.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-100`: **LGTM: DTO tests cover key conversions and serde behavior.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/handlers.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`13-40`: **LGTM! Clean handler implementations following Axum patterns.**\n\nThe three handlers are well-structured with appropriate use of `AuthzContext` for authentication, `Extension<Arc<Service>>` for dependency injection, and `ApiResult` for error propagation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-7`: **LGTM! Standard module organization for the storage layer.**\n\nThe module declarations are clean with proper test-only gating for `mapper_test`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`44-44`: **LGTM! Dependency correctly added under the user modules section.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/mapper.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-14`: **LGTM! Clean and idiomatic `From` implementation.**\n\nThe field mapping is straightforward and correctly converts the entity model to the SDK domain type.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-53`: **LGTM! Well-structured mock repository and test setup.**\n\nThe `MockRepository` implementation covers all three repository methods with appropriate behavior for unit testing the service layer.\n\n---\n\n`84-105`: **Past review issue has been addressed.**\n\nThe test now correctly asserts that `result.user_id` and `result.tenant_id` match the values from `ctx.subject_id()` and `ctx.tenant_id()` when no existing settings are found (lines 101-102).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/migrations/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-11`: **LGTM — migrator wiring is clear and minimal.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/error_test.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-70`: **Solid coverage for error-to-problem mapping.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/routes.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`9-47`: **Enums and auth/license trait wiring look good.**\n\n---\n\n`49-116`: **Route registration + OpenAPI metadata are consistent.**\n\n---\n\n`119-169`: **Tests for string mapping and trait bounds are clean.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/settings/test_settings_integration.py (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-82`: **Full workflow test is thorough and well-structured.**\n\n---\n\n`84-125`: **Idempotency test is clear and consistent.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>config/quickstart.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`123-129`: **Module config addition looks good.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-9`: **Module wiring looks good.**\n\nPublic REST submodules and scoped test modules are cleanly exposed.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>testing/e2e/modules/settings/test_settings_update.py (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`6-41`: **Solid full-update coverage.**\n\nThis test validates a full POST update and response shape well.\n\n---\n\n`44-92`: **Upsert-on-first-call test looks good.**\n\nThe GET + POST + verify GET sequence is clear and effective.\n\n---\n\n`94-137`: **Good replacement semantics check.**\n\nThe second POST overwrites values as intended and is verified.\n\n---\n\n`139-166`: **Empty-string acceptance covered well.**\n\n---\n\n`197-222`: **Missing-field handling test is clear and robust.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/errors.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-34`: **Error type and constructors are clean and consistent.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/error.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-34`: **LGTM! Well-structured domain error handling.**\n\nThe error enum design is clean:\n- `thiserror` derive provides proper `Error` trait implementation\n- The `validation()` helper constructor offers ergonomic field-level error creation\n- The `From<DomainError> for SettingsError` conversion correctly maps domain errors to SDK-facing errors, appropriately hiding internal database details by mapping to `internal()`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-22`: **LGTM! Clean SDK public API surface.**\n\nThe crate structure is well-organized:\n- `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` enforces memory safety\n- Clear re-exports provide an ergonomic API for consumers\n- Documentation with example usage is helpful\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/local_client.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-52`: **LGTM! Clean adapter implementation.**\n\nThe `LocalClient` correctly implements the adapter pattern:\n- Delegates all operations to the underlying `Service`\n- Uses `map_err(Into::into)` to convert `DomainError` to `SettingsError` via the `From` implementation in `domain/error.rs`\n- `#[must_use]` on the constructor prevents accidental discarding\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/entity.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-15`: **LGTM! Well-defined SeaORM entity.**\n\nThe entity correctly defines:\n- Composite primary key with `(tenant_id, user_id)` and `auto_increment = false`\n- Multi-tenant security via `#[secure]` macro\n- Optional `theme` and `language` fields\n\nOne consideration: the table name is `\"settings\"` while the module is `simple-user-settings`. Per the PR comments, there was a request to keep \"settings\" reserved for a future proper settings module. You may want to consider renaming the table to `\"simple_user_settings\"` to avoid potential conflicts.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/sea_orm_repo.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`24-38`: **LGTM! Correct scoped query implementation.**\n\nThe `find_by_user` method properly uses `AccessScope::both` to scope the query by both tenant and user, ensuring proper multi-tenant isolation.\n\n---\n\n`40-74`: **LGTM! Atomic upsert addresses the previously flagged race condition.**\n\nThe `upsert_full` method now correctly uses `OnConflict` for an atomic insert-or-update operation, eliminating the TOCTOU vulnerability from the previous implementation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-23`: **Well-structured public API surface.**\n\nThe re-exports from the SDK provide a clean public interface, and using `#[doc(hidden)]` for internal modules appropriately hides implementation details while still allowing access for integration purposes. The module organization follows good Rust crate design patterns.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/module.rs (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-52`: **Module structure and initialization look correct.**\n\nThe use of `ArcSwapOption` for late initialization of the service is appropriate for this two-phase initialization pattern (init then register_rest). The `Default` and `Clone` implementations are correctly handling the optional service state, and the migration implementation properly uses the SeaORM migrator.\n\n---\n\n`54-79`: **Clean initialization flow.**\n\nThe `init` method properly sequences configuration loading, database connection setup, repository creation, service instantiation, and client registration. Using `db_required()` appropriately enforces the database capability requirement.\n\n---\n\n`81-101`: **REST registration correctly guards against uninitialized state.**\n\nThe implementation properly checks for service initialization before attempting to register routes, preventing runtime errors if the module lifecycle is violated.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-20`: **ServiceConfig with sensible defaults.**\n\nThe default `max_field_length` of 100 aligns with the configuration defaults shown in `config.rs`. Clean separation of configuration from service logic.\n\n---\n\n`32-49`: **Get-or-default pattern is appropriate.**\n\nReturning a default `SimpleUserSettings` when none exists (without persisting it) is a clean approach that avoids unnecessary database writes for users who never customize their settings.\n\n---\n\n`51-82`: **Validate-then-persist pattern is correctly implemented.**\n\nBoth `update_settings` and `patch_settings` properly validate fields before persisting, preventing invalid data from reaching the database.\n\n---\n\n`84-92`: **Clarify if byte-based length limit is intentional.**\n\n`value.len()` returns the byte count in UTF-8, not the character count. For multi-byte characters (e.g., `\"café\"` is 5 bytes, `\"🎉\"` is 4 bytes), this may behave unexpectedly from a user perspective. If this is intentional (e.g., to match database column byte limits), this is fine. If character count is intended, use `value.chars().count()` instead.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#pullrequestreview-3670091713","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#pullrequestreview-3670091713"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223"}},"submitted_at":"2026-01-16T10:24:01Z","commit_id":"617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16"},{"id":3670233443,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOPaLyBs7aw1Fj","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Actionable comments posted: 3**\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Fix all issues with AI agents</summary>\n\n````\nIn\n`@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md`:\n- Around line 24-29: Update the \"Affected code\" paths in the Impact section to\nuse the actual module paths used in this PR: replace\n`modules/settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/` with\n`modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/` and\n`modules/settings/simple-user-settings/` with\n`modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/`; ensure the modified\nentries for Root `Cargo.toml`, `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml`, and the new\nE2E test path remain accurate relative to those corrected module paths.\n\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/project.md`:\n- Around line 36-50: Update the fenced code block containing the module tree\n(the block starting with \"modules/<module>/\" and ending with \"infra/storage/   \n# SeaORM entities, migrations\") to include a language tag after the opening ```\n(for example, use ```text) so the block is ```text ... ``` and satisfies\nmarkdownlint MD040; no other content changes needed.\n\nIn `@modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/api.rs`:\n- Around line 25-32: The update_settings trait method currently accepts\nOption<String> for theme and language which contradicts the POST \"full update\"\nsemantics; change the signature of update_settings to take non-optional String\nfor both theme and language (fn update_settings(&self, ctx: &SecurityContext,\ntheme: String, language: String) -> Result<SimpleUserSettings, SettingsError>),\nthen update all trait implementations, callers, tests and related documentation\nto pass concrete values and handle validation/ defaults before calling this\nmethod (or, if you prefer the alternate design, update the spec/docs to state\nPOST allows optional fields and keep Options consistently everywhere); ensure\nreferences to SecurityContext, SimpleUserSettings and SettingsError remain\nintact while you update implementations.\n````\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`15-15`: **Verify SecurityContext vs SecurityCtx naming.**\n\nA past review flagged that `SecurityContext` was renamed to `SecurityCtx` per commit message, but this line still references `SecurityContext`. Please verify which name is correct in the current implementation and update for consistency.\n\n\n\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check which naming is used in the implementation\nrg -n \"SecurityContext|SecurityCtx\" modules/simple-user-settings --type rust | head -20\n```\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/infra/storage/entity.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`5-7`: **Consider namespacing the table name to avoid future collisions.**\n\nGiven this is a temporary module and there’s intent to add a proper settings module later, a generic `\"settings\"` table name could conflict with future schema. Consider renaming to a scoped table name and update the migration/repo accordingly.\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested change</summary>\n\n```diff\n-#[sea_orm(table_name = \"settings\")]\n+#[sea_orm(table_name = \"simple_user_settings\")]\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`123-141`: **Consider adding language specifiers to fenced code blocks.**\n\nThe directory structure diagrams could use `text` or `plaintext` as language specifiers to satisfy markdown linters, though this is purely cosmetic.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Optional fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-```\n+```text\n openspec/\n ├── project.md              # Project conventions\n```\n\nApply similarly to the decision tree at line 147 and multi-capability example at line 351.\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`84-93`: **Consider using character count instead of byte length for Unicode-safe validation.**\n\n`value.len()` returns the byte length, not the character count. For fields like `theme` and `language` that may contain Unicode characters (e.g., `日本語`), a 3-character string would consume 9 bytes and fail a limit of 5 despite being only 3 characters. If the intent is to limit user-visible string length, use `value.chars().count()` instead.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested change for Unicode-safe length check</summary>\n\n```diff\n fn validate_field(&self, field: &str, value: &str) -> Result<(), DomainError> {\n-    if value.len() > self.config.max_field_length {\n+    if value.chars().count() > self.config.max_field_length {\n         return Err(DomainError::validation(\n             field,\n             format!(\"exceeds maximum length of {}\", self.config.max_field_length),\n         ));\n     }\n     Ok(())\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between 617e89ab7df6e18df15aa9ce03c79a7872619d16 and 61201e763921f5e1ce3837dd429946cd122f2d03.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (50)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml`\n* `apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs`\n* `config/e2e-local.yaml`\n* `config/quickstart.yaml`\n* `libs/modkit-auth/src/axum_ext.rs`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/design.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/tasks.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/project.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/Cargo.toml`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/api.rs`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/errors.rs`\n* `modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/lib.rs`\n* `modu