.**\n\nThe empty `Relation` enum and default `ActiveModelBehavior` are standard and fit this entity setup.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/tests/cli_smoke_tests.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`213-221`: **Config enables the new module in the CLI smoke test.**  \nThis addition fits the module enablement pattern and keeps the test config aligned.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-1`: **REST submodule export looks good.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/errors.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-10`: **Generated error catalog setup looks good.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/specs/user-settings/spec.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-159`: **Requirements spec is clear and consistent.**\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/design.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-157`: **Design document is comprehensive and well-structured.**\n\nThe document thoroughly covers the architectural decisions for the settings module migration, including:\n- Clear SDK pattern rationale with SecurityContext\n- Justified composite primary key choice\n- Well-documented lazy creation and REST semantics\n- Proper risk assessment with mitigations\n\nThe migration plan and rollback strategy are practical and aligned with the implementation changes in this PR.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/specs/user-settings/spec.md (3)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-4`: **Purpose section has been properly populated.**\n\nThe Purpose section now contains a clear description of the module's responsibilities, replacing the previous placeholder text.\n\n---\n\n`120-133`: **Error handling requirements are well-defined.**\n\nThe RFC-9457 Problem Details requirement with appropriate scenarios for validation and internal errors provides clear guidance for implementation.\n\n---\n\n`107-118`: **No action needed—implementation correctly matches spec.**\n\nThe migration in `initial_001.rs` properly implements `theme` and `language` as optional fields. Both use `.string()` without `.not_null()`, which makes them nullable and aligns with the spec's declaration of these fields as optional.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-456`: **Comprehensive OpenSpec documentation.**\n\nThis AGENTS.md provides thorough guidance for spec-driven development workflows, including:\n- Clear three-stage workflow (Creating → Implementing → Archiving)\n- Practical CLI command reference\n- Well-documented delta operations and troubleshooting\n\nThe content aligns well with the retrieved learnings about OpenSpec conventions.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/api.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`16-41`: **Trait design follows SDK pattern correctly.**\n\nThe trait properly:\n- Uses `async_trait` for async method support\n- Requires `Send + Sync` bounds for thread-safe usage via `ClientHub`\n- Takes `&SecurityContext` as first parameter for all methods per the design\n- Returns domain-specific `SettingsError` type\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/proposal.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-30`: **Proposal correctly archived.**\n\nThe proposal has been properly moved to the archive directory with the date prefix (2026-01-15), following the OpenSpec workflow for completed changes.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/error.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-34`: **Clean error surface and mapping.**\n\nThe variants, helper constructor, and SettingsError conversion align cleanly with expected API error shaping.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/error_test.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-70`: **Solid coverage of error-to-problem mappings.**\n\nThe tests validate status, instance, and detail content across all DomainError variants.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-22`: **Nice, clean SDK façade.**\n\nPublic exports and `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]` provide a clear, safe crate surface.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>apps/hyperspot-server/Cargo.toml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`41-45`: **Dependency addition looks consistent.**\n\nLocal path dependency for the new module matches the intended integration.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>config/quickstart.yaml (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`123-129`: **Config block is clear and well-scoped.**\n\nModule-specific DB and config keys are easy to follow and consistent with existing structure.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs (4)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-57`: **LGTM! Well-structured test setup with mock repository.**\n\nThe `MockRepository` implementation correctly simulates the `SettingsRepository` trait behavior for testing. The `create_test_context()` helper using `SecurityContext::anonymous()` provides a consistent test context.\n\n---\n\n`59-82`: **LGTM!**\n\nTest correctly verifies that existing settings are returned with the expected `theme` and `language` values.\n\n---\n\n`84-105`: **LGTM! Assertions now correctly verify default ID behavior.**\n\nThe test properly validates that when no settings exist, the returned `user_id` and `tenant_id` come from the `SecurityContext`, addressing the previous review feedback.\n\n---\n\n`107-269`: **LGTM! Comprehensive test coverage for update/patch operations.**\n\nTests thoroughly cover:\n- Successful updates with valid data\n- Validation failures when exceeding `max_field_length`\n- Partial patch behavior preserving unchanged fields\n- Empty patch no-op behavior\n\nThe use of `matches!(err, error::DomainError::Validation { .. })` correctly verifies error variants.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/mod.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`1-7`: **LGTM! Clean domain module organization.**\n\nThe module structure follows standard Rust conventions with properly separated concerns (error, fields, repo, service) and test module correctly gated behind `#[cfg(test)]`.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/module.rs (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`17-23`: **LGTM! Module naming updated as requested.**\n\nThe module is now correctly named `\"simple-user-settings\"` per reviewer feedback, avoiding conflict with a future proper settings module.\n\n---\n\n`33-39`: **Clone implementation is correct.**\n\nThe implementation properly clones the inner `Arc<Service>` from the `ArcSwapOption`. The previous review concern about using move instead of clone has been addressed in the test.\n\n---\n\n`54-79`: **LGTM! Well-structured module initialization.**\n\nThe init flow correctly:\n1. Reads configuration from context\n2. Obtains secure database connection for runtime operations\n3. Constructs repository and service with proper Arc wrapping\n4. Registers the local client for SDK consumers\n\n---\n\n`81-101`: **LGTM! Defensive service access in REST registration.**\n\nThe `register_rest` method correctly fails with a clear error message if called before `init()` completes, preventing null-pointer-like issues at runtime.\n\n---\n\n`103-120`: **LGTM! Tests correctly verify Default and Clone behavior.**\n\nThe clone test now properly calls `.clone()` (addressing previous feedback) and verifies both the cloned and original module retain the expected state.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service.rs (5)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`10-20`: **LGTM! ServiceConfig with sensible defaults.**\n\nThe default `max_field_length` of 100 aligns with the module-level `SettingsConfig` default, ensuring consistency across configuration layers.\n\n---\n\n`22-30`: **LGTM! Clean Service constructor.**\n\nThe constructor properly accepts dependencies via `Arc<dyn SettingsRepository>` for testability and configuration via `ServiceConfig`.\n\n---\n\n`32-49`: **LGTM! get_settings correctly handles missing settings.**\n\nWhen no settings exist in the repository, the method returns a default `SimpleUserSettings` populated with `user_id` and `tenant_id` from the `SecurityContext`, which is the expected behavior for a user-settings service.\n\n---\n\n`51-66`: **LGTM! update_settings validates before persisting.**\n\nValidation is correctly performed before the repository call, ensuring invalid data never reaches storage.\n\n---\n\n`68-82`: **LGTM! patch_settings validates only provided fields.**\n\nThe partial update correctly validates only the fields present in the patch, allowing unchanged fields to bypass validation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<sub>✏️ Tip: You can disable this entire section by setting `review_details` to `false` in your review settings.</sub>\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit for review status -->","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/223#pullrequestreview-3670233443","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/223","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"http