pdate_data[\"theme\"] = \"a\"\n* (max_field_length + 1) (or fallback to a very large sentinel like 10000 if the\nconfig endpoint is unavailable), and keep the existing assertion that the POST\nto f\"{base_url}/simple-user-settings/v1/settings\" returns 422; update references\nto update_data, test_update_settings_validation_max_length, base_url and\nauth_headers accordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Duplicate comments (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/error.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`8-10`: **Extract the actual trace ID from OpenTelemetry context instead of the span ID.**\n\nThis extracts `Span::current().id()` (span ID) but names it `trace_id`. Per W3C Trace Context, trace ID (128-bit) and span ID (64-bit) are distinct identifiers. Use `tracing_opentelemetry::OpenTelemetrySpanExt` to extract the real trace ID for proper distributed tracing correlation.\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/AGENTS.md (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`43-47`: **Use proper heading syntax instead of bold text.**\n\nMarkdownlint flags `**Workflow**` as emphasis used instead of a heading (MD036). Convert to proper heading syntax for consistency.\n\n```diff\n-**Workflow**\n+#### Workflow\n```\n\nAlso applies to lines 293, 297, 301 (`**\"Change must have at least one delta\"**`, `**\"Requirement must have at least one scenario\"**`, `**Silent scenario parsing failures**`).\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧹 Nitpick comments (8)</summary><blockquote>\n\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/openspec/changes/archive/2026-01-15-add-settings-module-rust/design.md (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`118-118`: **Complete the sentence for clarity.**\n\nThe sentence fragment \"Can be added later...\" lacks a subject. Based on static analysis hints.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-**Reasoning:** Simplifies implementation, matches Go behavior. Can be added later if needed via event sourcing or audit log.\n+**Reasoning:** This simplifies implementation and matches Go behavior. It can be added later if needed via event sourcing or audit log.\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`151-151`: **Complete the sentence for clarity.**\n\nSame sentence fragment issue as line 118. Based on static analysis hints.\n\n<details>\n<summary>✏️ Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-   - **Decision:** No, keep it simple with two string fields. Can be extended later if needed.\n+   - **Decision:** No, keep it simple with two string fields. This can be extended later if needed.\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/domain/service_test.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`109-140`: **Consider verifying user_id and tenant_id in update test.**\n\nThe `user_id` and `tenant_id` variables (lines 111-112) are set on `upsert_result` but never verified in assertions. While not critical, adding assertions for these would improve test completeness.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Optional enhancement</summary>\n\n```diff\n         assert_eq!(result.theme, Some(\"light\".to_owned()));\n         assert_eq!(result.language, Some(\"es\".to_owned()));\n+        assert_eq!(result.user_id, user_id);\n+        assert_eq!(result.tenant_id, tenant_id);\n     }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/dto_test.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`27-36`: **Consider renaming test to reflect its purpose.**\n\nThe test name `test_update_request_to_dto` is slightly misleading since it only verifies field values on the request struct itself, not a conversion to another DTO type.\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>💡 Suggested rename</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    fn test_update_request_to_dto() {\n+    fn test_update_request_fields() {\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings-sdk/src/lib.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`4-6`: **Minor doc inconsistency: `SimpleUserSettingsUpdate` missing from model list.**\n\nThe doc comment lists `SimpleUserSettings` and `SimpleUserSettingsPatch` but omits `SimpleUserSettingsUpdate`, which is re-exported on line 22.\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n //! - `SimpleUserSettingsApi` trait for inter-module communication\n-//! - Model types (`SimpleUserSettings`, `SimpleUserSettingsPatch`)\n+//! - Model types (`SimpleUserSettings`, `SimpleUserSettingsPatch`, `SimpleUserSettingsUpdate`)\n //! - Error type (`SettingsError`)\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/handlers.rs (1)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`22-34`: **Inconsistent return type pattern.**\n\n`update_settings` uses `ApiResult<impl IntoResponse>` with an explicit `(StatusCode::OK, Json(dto))` tuple, while `get_settings` and `patch_settings` return `ApiResult<JsonBody<SimpleUserSettingsDto>>`. The explicit `StatusCode::OK` is redundant since JSON responses default to 200.\n\nConsider aligning with the other handlers for consistency:\n\n\n\n<details>\n<summary>♻️ Suggested refactor</summary>\n\n```diff\n pub async fn update_settings(\n     Authz(ctx): Authz,\n     Extension(svc): Extension<Arc<Service>>,\n     Json(req): Json<UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest>,\n-) -> ApiResult<impl IntoResponse> {\n+) -> ApiResult<JsonBody<SimpleUserSettingsDto>> {\n     let update = SimpleUserSettingsUpdate {\n         theme: req.theme,\n         language: req.language,\n     };\n     let settings = svc.update_settings(&ctx, update).await?;\n-    let dto: SimpleUserSettingsDto = settings.into();\n-    Ok((StatusCode::OK, Json(dto)))\n+    Ok(Json(settings.into()))\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n<details>\n<summary>modules/simple-user-settings/simple-user-settings/src/api/rest/dto.rs (2)</summary><blockquote>\n\n`28-33`: **Consider adding a `From` impl for `SimpleUserSettingsUpdate`.**\n\nFor consistency with `PatchSimpleUserSettingsRequest` (which has a `From` impl), consider adding a `From<UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest>` for `SimpleUserSettingsUpdate`. This would centralize the DTO-to-domain conversion logic.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested implementation</summary>\n\n```rust\nimpl From<UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest> for SimpleUserSettingsUpdate {\n    fn from(req: UpdateSimpleUserSettingsRequest) -> Self {\n        Self {\n            theme: req.theme,\n            language: req.language,\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n</details>\n\n---\n\n`35-42`: **The `#[serde(default)]` annotations are redundant on `Option` fields.**\n\nWhen deserializing with serde, `Option<T>` fields already default to `None` if the field is missing from the input. The `#[serde(default)]` annotations here have no practical effect and could be removed for cleaner code.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested simplification</summary>\n\n```diff\n #[derive(Debug, Deserialize, ToSchema)]\n #[serde(rename_all = \"snake_case\")]\n pub struct PatchSimpleUserSettingsRequest {\n-    #[serde(default)]\n     pub theme: Option<String>,\n-    #[serde(default)]\n     pub language: Option<String>,\n }\n```\n</details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n</blockquote></details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📜 Review details</summary>\n\n**Configuration used**: defaults\n\n**Review profile**: CHILL\n\n**Plan**: Pro\n\n<details>\n<summary>📥 Commits</summary>\n\nReviewing files that changed from the base of the PR and between e3a24cda8143cb53d8b74e085246f4a4da416c0c and 738ad1cfd2eee942b46586157312771596154df5.\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>⛔ Files ignored due to path filters (1)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.lock` is excluded by `!**/*.lock`\n\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>📒 Files selected for processing (57)</summary>\n\n* `Cargo.toml`\n* `apps/hyperspot-server/Ca