c","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check if guidelines exist and read them\nif [ -f guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md ]; then\n  echo \"=== DEPENDENCIES.md ===\" && wc -l guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md\n  head -250 guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md\nfi\n\nif [ -f guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md ]; then\n  echo \"=== NEW_MODULE.md ===\" && wc -l guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\n  head -250 guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\nfi\n\nif [ -f docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md ]; then\n  echo \"=== MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM/README.md ===\" && wc -l docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md\n  head -250 docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md\nfi\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 11395\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Examine the module structure for types module\necho \"=== Module structure ===\" && \\\nfind modules/system/types -type f | head -20 && \\\necho \"\" && \\\necho \"=== types module Cargo.toml ===\" && \\\ncat modules/system/types/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 875\n\n---\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n# Check for similar modules to understand patterns\necho \"=== Other modules in system ===\" && \\\nls -la modules/system/ && \\\necho \"\" && \\\necho \"=== Example module structure ===\" && \\\nfind modules/system -name \"Cargo.toml\" -type f | head -3 | xargs -I {} sh -c 'echo \"--- {} ---\" && cat {}'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 4033\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Refactor to follow SDK pattern: separate `types-sdk` and `types` crates.**\n\nThe `types` module violates the mandatory SDK pattern outlined in `@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`. All modules must have a separate `<module>-sdk` crate (public API, models, errors) and a `<module>` implementation crate. \n\nCurrent state has only a single `types` crate with no SDK separation, no models/errors/API trait definitions, and missing required internal structure (domain, infra, api subdirectories per canonical layout).\n\nCreate:\n- `modules/system/types-sdk/` with public API trait, error types, and domain models\n- Refactor `modules/system/types/` to depend on `types-sdk` and implement domain/infra/api layers\n- Align with the `types-registry-sdk` pattern already established in the codebase\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/types/Cargo.toml` around lines 1 - 28, The package currently\nexposes a single \"types\" crate; split it into a public SDK crate and an\nimplementation crate by creating modules/system/types-sdk with public API\ntraits, domain models and error types (mirroring the types-registry-sdk pattern)\nand refactoring modules/system/types to depend on types-sdk and implement\ndomain/, infra/, and api/ layers; update the Cargo.toml entries so the workspace\ncontains both a types-sdk crate (exports models/errors/api traits) and a types\ncrate (path \"src/lib.rs\" -> implementation that depends on types-sdk and on\ntypes-registry-sdk, modkit and modkit-security), and move any public type\ndefinitions and errors out of the existing types crate into types-sdk while\nkeeping only implementation code in types.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commits 84540b5 to 70fe3ff","created_at":"2026-01-29T08:44:56Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T16:58:08Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2740554475","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2740554475"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2740554475"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218"}},"reactions":{"url":"