"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_\n\n**Avoid hard-coding plugin deps that contradict the module docs.**  \nLine 37 adds hard deps on `contoso_tr_plugin` and `fabrikam_tr_plugin`, but the module docs explicitly state the gateway does **not** declare hard dependencies on plugins. This change forces those plugins to be present and undermines dynamic discovery. Either remove the hard deps or update the docs/behavior to match the new coupling.  \n\n\n<details>\n<summary>🔧 Suggested fix (preserve dynamic discovery)</summary>\n\n```diff\n-    deps = [\"types_registry\", \"types\", \"contoso_tr_plugin\", \"fabrikam_tr_plugin\"],\n+    deps = [\"types_registry\", \"types\"],\n```\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_start -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>\n\n> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**\n> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.\n\n```suggestion\n#[modkit::module(\n    name = \"tenant_resolver_gw\",\n    deps = [\"types_registry\", \"types\"],\n    capabilities = [rest]\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- suggestion_end -->\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@examples/plugin-modules/tenant_resolver/tenant_resolver-gw/src/module.rs`\naround lines 35 - 38, The module attribute for tenant_resolver_gw currently\nhard-codes plugin dependencies in the deps list (specifically\n\"contoso_tr_plugin\" and \"fabrikam_tr_plugin\"), which contradicts the gateway\ndocs that require dynamic plugin discovery; remove those two plugin entries from\nthe deps array in the #[modkit::module(...)] attribute (leave \"types_registry\"\nand \"types\" as needed) so the gateway does not force presence of those plugins,\nor alternatively update module docs/behavior if you intentionally want hard\ncoupling—refer to the #[modkit::module(name = \"tenant_resolver_gw\", deps =\n[...])] declaration to make the change.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-29T17:16:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T17:16:26Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742702167","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742702167"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742702167"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742702167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":35,"original_start_line":35,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":38,"original_line":38,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":8,"position":8,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742702178","pull_request_review_id":3724044315,"id":2742702178,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jelBi","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@\n+[package]\n+name = \"types\"\n+version.workspace = true\n+edition.workspace = true\n+license.workspace = true\n+authors.workspace = true\n+description = \"Core types registration system module - implementation crate\"\n+\n+[lints]\n+workspace = true\n+\n+[lib]\n+name = \"types\"\n+path = \"src/lib.rs\"\n+\n+[dependencies]\n+# Core dependencies\n+anyhow = { workspace = true }\n+async-trait = { workspace = true }\n+tracing = { workspace = true }\n+inventory = { workspace = true }\n+arc-swap = { workspace = true }\n+\n+# ModKit dependencies\n+modkit = { workspace = true }\n+modkit-security = { workspace = true }\n+\n+# Types SDK (public API, errors, models)\n+types-sdk = { path = \"../types-sdk\" }\n+\n+# Types registry for registering core types\n+types-registry-sdk = { workspace = true }","path":"modules/system/types/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"f2aca5f74683e7fd0fa5e0a0f1dd80b46bbfb3d5","original_commit_id":"dab863e0a96e3be53ab8ab92387f6d2aba8328df","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n\n# Retrieve the three guideline documents mentioned in the review\necho \"=== DEPENDENCIES.md (first 300 lines) ===\"\nhead -300 guidelines/DEPENDENCIES.md\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== NEW_MODULE.md (first 300 lines) ===\"\nhead -300 guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== modkit_unified_system/README.md (first 300 lines) ===\"\nhead -300 docs/modkit_unified_system/README.md\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Module structure: types ===\"\nfind modules/system/types -type f -name \"*.rs\" -o -name \"*.toml\" | head -20\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Module structure: types-sdk ===\"\nfind modules/system/types-sdk -type f -name \"*.rs\" -o -name \"*.toml\" | head -20\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== Cargo.toml dependencies context ===\"\ncat modules/system/types/Cargo.toml\n\necho \"\"\necho \"=== types-sdk Cargo.toml ===\"\ncat modules/system/types-sdk/Cargo.toml\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 20649\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Add `publish = false` to the implementation crate manifest.**\n\nThe `types/Cargo.toml` is missing `publish = false` in the `[package]` section. Per NEW_MODULE.md guidelines, implementation crates should prevent accidental publishing by setting `publish = false`. The SDK crate (`types-sdk`) may be published, but the implementation crate should not be.\n\nAdd this line to `[package]` in `modules/system/types/Cargo.toml`:\n```toml\npublish = false\n```\n\nThe module follows the SDK pattern correctly (separate SDK + implementation crates), uses workspace dependencies consistently, and has appropriate minimal dependencies. No YAML serialization issues detected.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/types/Cargo.toml` around lines 1 - 32, The Cargo manifest for\nthe implementation crate named \"types\" is missing the publish safeguard; open\nthe [package] section of the Cargo.toml for the types crate and add publish =\nfalse so the implementation crate cannot be published (leave the SDK crate\ntypes-sdk unchanged); update the [package] block containing name = \"types\"\naccordingly.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit 7e669b7","created_at":"2026-01-29T17:16:23Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T17:24:46Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742702178","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742702178"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742702178"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742702178/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":33,"original_line":32,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":32,"position":33,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742754657","pull_request_review_id":3723942634,"id":2742754657,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jex1h","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,67 @@\n+use std::env;\n+use std::fs::File;\n+use std::io::prelude::*;\n+use std::path::Path;\n+\n+fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {\n+    let out_dir = env::var(\"OUT_DIR\")?;\n+    let dest_path = Path::new(&out_dir).join(\"core_gts_schemas.zip\");\n+\n+    // Create ZIP archive containing all schema files\n+    let file = File::create(&dest_path)?;\n+    let mut zip = zip::ZipWriter::new(file);\n+\n+    let schemas_dir = \"schemas\";\n+\n+    // Add manifest.json\n+    let manifest_path = Path::new(schemas_dir).join(\"manifest.json\");\n+    if manifest_path.exists() {\n+        let buffer = std::fs::read(&manifest_path)?;\n+\n+        let options = zip::write::FileOptions::<()>::default()\n+            .compression_method(zip::CompressionMethod::Deflated)\n+            .unix_permissions(0o755);\n+        zip.start_file(\"manifest.json\", options)?;\n+        zip.write_all(&buffer)?;\n+    }\n+\n+    // Add all .schema.json files\n+    if Path::new(schemas_dir).exists() {\n+        let mut entries: Vec<_> = std::fs::read_dir(schemas_dir)?.collect::<Result<_, _>>()?;\n+        entries.sort_by_key(std::fs::DirEntry::path);\n+        for entry in entries {\n+            let path = entry.path();\n+            if path.extension().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) == Some(\"json\")\n+                && path\n+                    .file_name()\n+                    .and_then(|s| s.to_str())\n+                    .is_some_and(|s| s.contains(\".schema.\"))\n+            {\n+                let buffer = std::fs::read(&path)?;\n+\n+                let Some(file_name) = path.file_name().and_then(|s| s.to_str()) else {\n+                    continue;\n+                };\n+                let options = zip::write::FileOptions::<()>::default()\n+                    .compression_method(zip::CompressionMethod::Deflated)\n+                    .unix_permissions(0o755);\n+                zip.start_file(file_name, options)?;\n+                zip.write_all(&buffer)?;\n+            }\n+        }\n+    }\n+\n+    zip.finish()?;\n+\n+    // Register individual files for rerun-if-changed to detect content changes\n+    // (cargo only detects directory mtime changes, not file content changes)\n+    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed=Cargo.toml\");\n+    if Path::new(schemas_dir).exists() {\n+        for entry in std::fs::read_dir(schemas_dir)? {\n+            let entry = entry?;\n+            let path = entry.path();\n+            println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", path.display());\n+        }\n+    }","path":"libs/modkit/build.rs","commit_id":"f2aca5f74683e7fd0fa5e0a0f1dd80b46bbfb3d5","original_commit_id":"7e669b794bbd371e1ad022365f4ec53e5122d1d2","user":{"login":"graphite-app[bot]","id":96075541,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOBbn_FQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/158384?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/graphite-app","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/graphite-app%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The build script will rerun if `schemas/` files change, but it does not explicitly declare a dependency on the `schemas/` directory itself. If the `schemas/` directory doesn't exist at build time, the script will create an empty ZIP archive without failing the build. This will cause a runtime failure when `get_core_gts_schemas()` returns an empty schemas vector and triggers the error on line 44-47 of `schemas.rs`.\n\nFix: Add an explicit check and fail the build if the schemas directory or required files don't exist:\n\n```rust\nlet schemas_dir = \"schemas\";\nlet manifest_path = Path::new(schemas_dir).join(\"manifest.json\");\n\nif !Path::new(schemas_dir).exists() {\n    return Err(\"schemas directory not found\".into());\n}\nif !manifest_path.exists() {\n    return Err(\"manifest.json not found in schemas directory\".into());\n}\n```\n```suggestion\n    // Register individual files for rerun-if-changed to detect content changes\n    // (cargo only detects directory mtime changes, not file content changes)\n    println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed=Cargo.toml\");\n    \n    let manifest_path = Path::new(schemas_dir).join(\"manifest.json\");\n\n    if !Path::new(schemas_dir).exists() {\n        return Err(\"schemas directory not found\".into());\n    }\n    if !manifest_path.exists() {\n        return Err(\"manifest.json not found in schemas directory\".into());\n    }\n    \n    for entry in std::fs::read_dir(schemas_dir)? {\n        let entry = entry?;\n        let path = entry.path();\n        println!(\"cargo:rerun-if-changed={}\", path.display());\n    }\n```\n  \n\n*Spotted by [Graphite Agent](https://app.graphite.com/diamond/?org=hypernetix&ref=ai-review-comment)*<i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br /><a href=\"https://app.graphite.com/github/pr/hypernetix/hyperspot/218?chatWithGeneratedComment=110fad6f-3b6b-44c5-9598-bc412eb2b349\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Fix in Graphite\" src=\"https://static.graphite.dev/github-diamond-fix-in-graphite-dark.svg\"></picture></a></i><i class='graphite__hidden'><br /><br />Is this helpful? React 👍 or 👎 to let us know.</i>","created_at":"2026-01-29T17:30:05Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T17:30:07Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742754657","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742754657"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2742754657"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2742754657/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":62,"original_start_line":56,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":70,"original_line":65,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":65,"position":70,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2746629467","pull_request_review_id":3728749780,"id":2746629467,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jtj1b","diff_hunk":"@@ -84,6 +84,7 @@ schemars = { workspace = true, features = [\"derive\"] }\n # GTS support\n gts = { workspace = true }\n gts-macros = { workspace = true }\n+zip = { version = \"2.2\", default-features = false, features = [\"deflate\"] }","path":"libs/modkit/Cargo.toml","commit_id":"2eeeb5fe977ec4aa1a88bc9e425583fd2d7ab91c","original_commit_id":"2eeeb5fe977ec4aa1a88bc9e425583fd2d7ab91c","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_\n\n<details>\n<summary>🧩 Analysis chain</summary>\n\n🏁 Script executed:\n\n```shell\n#!/bin/bash\n# Check crates.io API for zip crate latest version and versions info\ncurl -s https://crates.io/api/v1/crates/zip | jq '.crate | {name, max_stable_version, max_version, newest_version}'\n```\n\nRepository: hypernetix/hyperspot\n\nLength of output: 181\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`zip crate rust latest version 2024 2025`\n\n💡 Result:\n\n- **Latest overall (as of Jan 30, 2026):** `zip` **7.2.0** (released **2026-01-20**). [1]  \n- **Latest release in 2025:** `zip` **7.0.0** (released **2025-12-19**). [1][2]  \n- **Latest release in 2024:** `zip` **2.2.2** (released **2024-12-16**). [1]  \n\n**Sources:** [1] docs.rs version history for `zip` (shows dates/versions), [2] Cargo Run crate summary (confirms 7.0.0 release date).\n\n---\n\n🌐 Web query:\n\n`zip crate rust security advisories vulnerabilities`\n\n💡 Result:\n\nAs of **January 30, 2026**, the main publicly tracked security issue for the Rust **`zip` crate** (zip-rs / “zip2”) is:\n\n- **CVE-2025-29787 / GHSA-94vh-gphv-8pm8** — **incorrect path canonicalization during archive extraction**. A malicious ZIP can use **symlinks earlier in the archive** so that later extracted entries can **write outside the intended extraction directory**, leading to **arbitrary file overwrite** (and potentially code execution depending on what gets overwritten). **Affected:** `zip` **>= 1.3.0 and < 2.3.0**. **Fixed:** **2.3.0**. [1][2][3]\n\n## What to do\n- **Upgrade**: ensure `zip` is **>= 2.3.0**. [1][2]\n- If you must handle **untrusted ZIPs**, be extra cautious with any “extract all” style API usage (the CVE specifically concerns extraction behavior). [1][2]\n- **Audit your dependency tree** with RustSec-backed tooling:\n  - `cargo audit` (RustSec advisory DB) [4]\n  - `cargo deny` (RustSec advisory DB) [4]\n\n## Sources\n[1] NVD CVE record (CVE-2025-29787): https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-29787  \n[2] OSV entry (CVE-2025-29787): https://osv.dev/vulnerability/CVE-2025-29787  \n[3] Ubuntu CVE page referencing GHSA: https://ubuntu.com/security/CVE-2025-29787  \n[4] RustSec Advisory Database / tooling notes: https://rustsec.org/\n\n---\n\n\n\n</details>\n\n**Upgrade `zip` crate to 2.3.0 or later—version 2.2 is vulnerable to CVE-2025-29787.**\n\nThe `zip` 2.2 dependency at lines 87 and 116-118 is affected by CVE-2025-29787 (path canonicalization vulnerability), which allows malicious ZIP archives to write outside the intended extraction directory using symlinks. This is fixed in `zip` 2.3.0 and all later versions. The current stable release is 7.2.0 (as of January 2026). Update to at least 2.3.0 immediately, or consider upgrading to a newer stable version.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@libs/modkit/Cargo.toml` at line 87, The zip crate is pinned to vulnerable\nversion 2.2; update the dependency specification(s) for \"zip\" in\nlibs/modkit/Cargo.toml to at least \"2.3.0\" (or a newer stable like 7.x) to\nremediate CVE-2025-29787, ensuring you preserve existing feature flags (e.g.,\ndefault-features = false, features = [\"deflate\"]) when changing the version and\nupdate every occurrence of the \"zip\" entry in the file so both entries are\nconsistent.\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:ocelot -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->\n\n✅ Addressed in commit f2aca5f","created_at":"2026-01-30T14:42:42Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:07:37Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2746629467","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2746629467"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2746629467"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust