ling inappropriate for public SDK types. Add `uuid` and `time` for domain model support (IDs, timestamps). Optionally add `modkit-odata` if the module supports OData filtering.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Template (from NEW_MODULE.md Step 1a)</summary>\n\n```toml\n[package]\nname = \"types-sdk\"\nversion.workspace = true\nedition.workspace = true\nlicense.workspace = true\nauthors.workspace = true\ndescription = \"SDK for types: API trait, domain models and error definitions\"\n\n[lints]\nworkspace = true\n\n[dependencies]\n# Core dependencies for API trait\nasync-trait = { workspace = true }\nthiserror = { workspace = true }\nuuid = { workspace = true }\ntime = { workspace = true }\n\n# Security context for API methods\nmodkit-security = { workspace = true }\n\n# OData support for pagination (if needed)\nmodkit-odata = { workspace = true }\n```\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>\n\n```\nIn `@modules/system/types-sdk/Cargo.toml` around lines 1 - 20, Update the\ntypes-sdk Cargo.toml to remove transport-specific serde and serde_json from\n[dependencies] and instead add uuid and time as workspace dependencies for\ndomain model IDs and timestamps; keep async-trait, thiserror and\nmodkit-security, and optionally add modkit-odata if OData filtering/pagination\nis required; ensure the [package] name/description remains \"types-sdk\" and\ndependencies entries use { workspace = true } for uuid and time (and\nmodkit-odata if added).\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<!-- fingerprinting:phantom:poseidon:eagle -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment by CodeRabbit -->","created_at":"2026-01-30T15:00:00Z","updated_at":"2026-01-30T15:00:01Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2746694413","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2746694413"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/218#discussion_r2746694413"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/218"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2746694413/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":1,"original_start_line":1,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":22,"original_line":20,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":20,"position":22,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2746694421","pull_request_review_id":3728826226,"id":2746694421,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6jtzsV","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@\n+//! Core Types Registration Module\n+//!\n+//! This system module is responsible for registering core GTS types that are used\n+//! throughout the framework, particularly for plugin systems.\n+//!\n+//! ## Purpose\n+//!\n+//! Previously, core types like `BaseModkitPluginV1` were registered directly\n+//! by the `types_registry` module, creating a circular dependency issue.\n+//! This module resolves that by:\n+//!\n+//! - Acting as the owner of core framework types\n+//! - Registering these types during its initialization\n+//! - Depending on `types_registry` (not the other way around)\n+//!\n+//! ## Dependency Chain\n+//!\n+//! ```text\n+//! `types_registry` → `types` → `plugin_modules`\n+//! ```","path":"modules/system/types/src/lib.rs","commit_id":"f2aca5f74683e7fd0fa5e0a0f1dd80b46bbfb3d5","original_commit_id":"fa45c68b3e475222feb3bbbbb7bbc28e0f0af562","user":{"login":"coderabbitai[bot]","id":136622811,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOCCSy2w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/347564?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/coderabbitai","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/coderabbitai%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_u