rl":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Artifizer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-03T08:29:11Z","updated_at":"2026-02-03T08:29:11Z","body":"We have a new design documents about PRD, ADR, and other documents, as well as for the tooling (Spider)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/issues/comments/3839845218/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null}],"source_review_comments":[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658110559","pull_request_review_id":3623580992,"id":2658110559,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eb4xf","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow FAQ\n+\n+This document answers common questions about the module development workflow, providing rationale and decision-making guidance.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [General Questions](#general-questions)\n+  - [Why both Design Docs AND OpenSpec?](#why-both-design-docs-and-openspec)\n+  - [Is OpenSpec a strict requirement?](#is-openspec-a-strict-requirement-for-this-workflow)\n+- [Design Phase](#design-phase)\n+  - [Why are DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md created together?](#why-are-designmd-and-requirementsmd-created-together)\n+  - [Why keep them as separate files?](#why-keep-them-as-separate-files)\n+  - [Why use implementation phases?](#why-use-implementation-phases-in-designmd)\n+  - [Reference vs. duplicate global requirements?](#should-i-reference-global-requirements-req1-req2-or-duplicate-them-in-module-requirementsmd)\n+  - [When to create new vs. reference existing requirements?](#when-should-i-create-a-new-requirement-vs-referencing-an-existing-one)\n+- [Workflow Questions](#workflow-questions)\n+  - [What if my design is wrong during implementation?](#what-if-i-discover-during-implementation-that-my-design-is-wrong)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## General Questions\n+\n+### Why both Design Docs AND OpenSpec?\n+\n+**Design docs are not suitable for OpenSpec format:**\n+- **Design is exploratory** — You need to iterate on architecture, components, and data flow before committing to implementation\n+- **High-level thinking** — Design docs capture the \"why\" and \"how\" at a conceptual level, not detailed scenarios\n+- **Free-form flexibility** — Markdown allows diagrams, prose explanations, and open questions that don't fit spec format\n+- **AI collaboration** — Free-form documents work better for AI-assisted design discussions and brainstorming\n+\n+**OpenSpec is for implementation tracking:**\n+- **Concrete behavior** — Specs document exact inputs, outputs, and edge cases that are verified by code\n+- **Feature-by-feature** — Each change focuses on a single, implementable unit of work\n+- **Living documentation** — Specs evolve with the code and are kept in sync through archiving\n+- **Validation** — Structured format enables automated validation and consistency checks\n+\n+**Clear workflow phases:**\n+1. **Design Phase** → Use DESIGN.md, REQUIREMENTS.md (free-form, exploratory)\n+2. **Implementation Phase** → Use OpenSpec changes (structured, verified)\n+3. **Archive** → Specs become the verified documentation of what actually works\n+\n+**TL;DR:** Design docs answer \"what should we build and why?\"; OpenSpec specs answer \"what did we build and how does it behave?\"\n+\n+### Is OpenSpec a strict requirement for this workflow?\n+\n+**No, OpenSpec is a tool choice, not a requirement.**","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/FAQ.md","commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Again, my concern: OpenSpec works good if the whole team uses it consistently. In this case specs are always in-sync with code. Once openspec workflow becomes optional, it might create more friction than value.\r\n\r\nAlso OpenSpec relies on instructions in AGENTS.md to define proper workflow. Once openspec flow becomes optional, these instructions will pollute context.\r\n\r\nSo IMO we either need to commit to openspec as a team until we discover a better flow/tool or not to use openspec at all or at least avoid bringing openspec-specific AGENTS.md and prompts into repository.\r\n\r\nIf your suggestion is to agree on a single tool (for example OpenSpec) for a while but replace it when time comes, then I believe it's a good approach.","created_at":"2026-01-02T17:26:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T17:34:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658110559","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658110559"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658110559"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658110559/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":47,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658127664","pull_request_review_id":3623598336,"id":2658127664,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eb88w","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Should openspec folder exist on monorepo level  in this workflow? \r\n\r\nIf it's on monorepo level, then we already have openspecs inside modules. Do we remove them?","created_at":"2026-01-02T17:38:55Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T17:39:31Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658127664","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658127664"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658127664"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658127664/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":245,"original_line":209,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":209,"position":245,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658129338","pull_request_review_id":3623599999,"id":2658129338,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eb9W6","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)\n+\n+**Input:** Feature name and scope from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, reference to the module's design documents.\n+\n+**Output:** `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/proposal.md`","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"04a95b0bb3eb442b331858558cf92153fd770ba6","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"OpenSpec prompts recommend different naming convention starting with verb. We will need to modify these prompts to avoid confusing instructions","created_at":"2026-01-02T17:40:07Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T17:42:25Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658129338","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658129338"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658129338"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658129338/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":213,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658132080","pull_request_review_id":3623602786,"id":2658132080,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6eb-Bw","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)\n+\n+**Input:** Feature name and scope from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, reference to the module's design documents.\n+\n+**Output:** `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/proposal.md`","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"04a95b0bb3eb442b331858558cf92153fd770ba6","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"There's also another output `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/specs/{capability}/spec.md`.\r\n\r\nAnd also for complicated implementations it's recommended to introduce `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/design.md` which should contain design and implementation details required for given feature.","created_at":"2026-01-02T17:42:13Z","updated_at":"2026-01-02T17:42:14Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658132080","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658132080"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2658132080"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2658132080/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":213,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659149179","pull_request_review_id":3624560866,"id":2659149179,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6ef2V7","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,164 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow FAQ\n+\n+This document answers common questions about the module development workflow, providing rationale and decision-making guidance.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [General Questions](#general-questions)\n+  - [Why both Design Docs AND OpenSpec?](#why-both-design-docs-and-openspec)\n+  - [Is OpenSpec a strict requirement?](#is-openspec-a-strict-requirement-for-this-workflow)\n+- [Design Phase](#design-phase)\n+  - [Why are DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md created together?](#why-are-designmd-and-requirementsmd-created-together)\n+  - [Why keep them as separate files?](#why-keep-them-as-separate-files)\n+  - [Why use implementation phases?](#why-use-implementation-phases-in-designmd)\n+  - [Reference vs. duplicate global requirements?](#should-i-reference-global-requirements-req1-req2-or-duplicate-them-in-module-requirementsmd)\n+  - [When to create new vs. reference existing requirements?](#when-should-i-create-a-new-requirement-vs-referencing-an-existing-one)\n+- [Workflow Questions](#workflow-questions)\n+  - [What if my design is wrong during implementation?](#what-if-i-discover-during-implementation-that-my-design-is-wrong)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+---\n+\n+## General Questions\n+\n+### Why both Design Docs AND OpenSpec?\n+\n+**Design docs are not suitable for OpenSpec format:**\n+- **Design is exploratory** — You need to iterate on architecture, components, and data flow before committing to implementation\n+- **High-level thinking** — Design docs capture the \"why\" and \"how\" at a conceptual level, not detailed scenarios\n+- **Free-form flexibility** — Markdown allows diagrams, prose explanations, and open questions that don't fit spec format\n+- **AI collaboration** — Free-form documents work better for AI-assisted design discussions and brainstorming\n+\n+**OpenSpec is for implementation tracking:**\n+- **Concrete behavior** — Specs document exact inputs, outputs, and edge cases that are verified by code\n+- **Feature-by-feature** — Each change focuses on a single, implementable unit of work\n+- **Living documentation** — Specs evolve with the code and are kept in sync through archiving\n+- **Validation** — Structured format enables automated validation and consistency checks\n+\n+**Clear workflow phases:**\n+1. **Design Phase** → Use DESIGN.md, REQUIREMENTS.md (free-form, exploratory)\n+2. **Implementation Phase** → Use OpenSpec changes (structured, verified)\n+3. **Archive** → Specs become the verified documentation of what actually works\n+\n+**TL;DR:** Design docs answer \"what should we build and why?\"; OpenSpec specs answer \"what did we build and how does it behave?\"\n+\n+### Is OpenSpec a strict requirement for this workflow?\n+\n+**No, OpenSpec is a tool choice, not a requirement.**","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/FAQ.md","commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"> Again, my concern: OpenSpec works good if the whole team uses it consistently. In this case specs are always in-sync with code. Once openspec workflow becomes optional, it might create more friction than value.\r\n\r\nGood point. Since HyperSpot is a monorepo, I think we need to keep consistency per module. I've updated the FAQ to be clearer on this:\r\n1. OpenSpec is the recommended default.\r\n2. Module-level consistency is required - once a module uses OpenSpec, everyone on that module should use it consistently. No mixing approaches within the same module.\r\n3. Monorepo flexibility - since different modules may have different maintainers, a new module could experiment with alternatives if those maintainers agree. This is about future flexibility, not about mixing tools in existing modules.\r\n\r\n> Also OpenSpec relies on instructions in `AGENTS.md` to define proper workflow. Once openspec flow becomes optional, these instructions will pollute context.\r\n\r\nWe may have a list of OpenSpec-enabled modules in `AGENTS.md` with instruction that OpenSpec workflow should be applied only for them.","created_at":"2026-01-03T21:02:50Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T21:02:50Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659149179","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659149179"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659149179"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659149179/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":47,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2658110559,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":47,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659200618","pull_request_review_id":3624590776,"id":2659200618,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6egC5q","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I've updated the workflow to use per-module openspec directories (`modules/{module}/openspec/`) for better isolation.\r\n\r\nThe challenge was that slash commands must be defined at root level for AI tool discovery (for Claude Code: `.claude/commands/`). My solution: add a \"Monorepo Context\" section to each slash command that instructs the AI to detect the target scope (module vs. root) and run `openspec` commands in the appropriate directory. See the three `openspec` commands in this PR for examples.","created_at":"2026-01-03T23:04:27Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T23:04:34Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659200618","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659200618"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659200618"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659200618/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":245,"original_line":209,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2658127664,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":209,"position":245,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201193","pull_request_review_id":3624591082,"id":2659201193,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6egDCp","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)\n+\n+**Input:** Feature name and scope from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, reference to the module's design documents.\n+\n+**Output:** `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/proposal.md`","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"04a95b0bb3eb442b331858558cf92153fd770ba6","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I've updated the workflow to use per-module openspec directories (modules/{module}/openspec/) for better isolation, so we can use native openspec naming convention.","created_at":"2026-01-03T23:05:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T23:05:48Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659201193","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201193"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659201193"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201193/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2658129338,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":213,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201578","pull_request_review_id":3624591351,"id":2659201578,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6egDIq","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,317 @@\n+# Module Development Workflow\n+\n+This document describes the module development workflow:\n+- **New modules** — design and implement from scratch\n+- **Existing modules** — add new features post-1.0 release\n+\n+It combines AI-assisted design with [OpenSpec-driven](https://openspec.dev/) implementation tracking.\n+\n+> **Intended Audience:** Human developers. AI assistance generates documentation and code; developers perform workflow steps, decision-making, and validation.\n+\n+## Index\n+\n+- [Workflow Overview](#workflow-overview)\n+- [Quick Reference](#quick-reference)\n+- [Using Prompt Templates](#using-prompt-templates)\n+- [Step 1: Design & Planning](#step-1-design--planning)\n+  - [1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md](#step-11-create-designmd-and-requirementsmd-iterative)\n+  - [1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md](#step-12-create-implementation_planmd)\n+  - [1.3: Validate Design Documents](#step-13-validate-design-documents)\n+  - [1.4: Create PR for Design Review](#step-14-create-pr-for-design-review)\n+- [Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)](#step-2-implementation-openspec)\n+  - [2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal](#step-21-create-openspec-change-proposal)\n+  - [2.2: Review and Refine Proposal](#step-22-review-and-refine-proposal)\n+  - [2.3: Implement the Feature](#step-23-implement-the-feature)\n+  - [2.4: Generate E2E Tests](#step-24-write-e2e-tests-if-applicable)\n+  - [2.5: Archive the OpenSpec Change](#step-25-archive-the-openspec-change)\n+- [Adding Features to Existing Modules](#adding-features-to-existing-modules)\n+- [Best Practices](#best-practices)\n+- [References](#references)\n+\n+## Quick Links\n+\n+- [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md) — ID formats, document templates, directory structure\n+- [FAQ](./FAQ.md) — Common questions and rationale\n+- [Prompt Templates](./prompts/) — AI prompts for each step\n+- [ROADMAP](./ROADMAP.md) — Future improvements of the workflow\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Workflow Overview\n+\n+### New Module Development\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Design & Planning                                       │\n+│  └─ 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (iterative)       │\n+│  └─ 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md                          │\n+│  └─ 1.3: Validate design documents                              │\n+│  └─ 1.4: Create PR for design review                            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)                               │\n+│  └─ For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN:                    │\n+│      1. Create OpenSpec change proposal                         │\n+│      2. Review and refine proposal, specs and tasks             │\n+│      3. Implement code + unit tests                             │\n+│      4. Generate E2E tests (if applicable)                         │\n+│      5. Archive change → specs updated                          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+### Adding Features to Existing Module\n+\n+```\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 1: Update Design Documents                                 │\n+│  └─ Review existing docs, update as needed, validate            │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec) — same as new module          │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+                              ↓\n+┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│ Step 3: Update CHANGELOG.md                                     │\n+└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Quick Reference\n+\n+| Term | Format | Example |\n+|------|--------|---------|\n+| Implementation Phase | `{MODULE}-P{N}` | `OAGW-P1` |\n+| Module Requirement | `{MODULE}-REQ{N}` | `OAGW-REQ01` |\n+| Global Requirement | `REQ{N}` | `REQ1` |\n+\n+For detailed formats and templates, see [Module Development Reference](./REFERENCE.md).\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Using Prompt Templates\n+\n+All design steps use prompt templates from [`prompts/`](./prompts/):\n+\n+1. Open the prompt template file\n+2. Replace `{module_name}` (snake_case) and `{MODULE}` (UPPERCASE prefix)\n+3. Submit to AI assistant with module context\n+4. Review and refine the generated output\n+\n+| Step | Prompt File | Output |\n+|------|-------------|--------|\n+| 1.1 | [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md) | `DESIGN.md` + `REQUIREMENTS.md` |\n+| 1.2 | [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md) | `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` |\n+| 1.3 | [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md) | Validation report |\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 1: Design & Planning\n+\n+### Step 1.1: Create DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md (Iterative)\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_design_and_requirements.md`](./prompts/create_design_and_requirements.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- Review [`guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) for module development standards\n+- Review [`MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) for ModKit framework patterns\n+- Review global requirements in [`REQUIREMENTS.md`](../REQUIREMENTS.md)\n+- Clarify module purpose, scope, and key use cases\n+\n+**Output:** Both `DESIGN.md` and `REQUIREMENTS.md` with cross-references\n+\n+**Iterative Process:**\n+\n+Design and requirements evolve together through iteration:\n+\n+```\n+┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n+│  Draft Design → Extract Requirements → Refine Design → ...  │\n+│       ↑                                        │             │\n+│       └────────────────────────────────────────┘             │\n+│                    Iterate until consistent                  │\n+└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n+```\n+\n+1. **Draft Initial Design** — Architecture, components, data flow, phases\n+2. **Extract Requirements** — What the system SHALL/SHOULD/MAY do\n+3. **Refine Design** — Requirements often reveal missing components or unclear flows\n+4. **Cross-Reference** — Add requirement IDs to design, verify alignment\n+5. **Iterate** — Repeat until both documents are internally consistent\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Focus on **what** and **why**, not implementation details\n+- Requirements must be atomic and testable\n+- Reference global requirements (REQ1, REQ2...) — don't duplicate\n+- Use RFC 2119 language: SHALL (mandatory), SHOULD (recommended), MAY (optional)\n+- Mark open questions for design review\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.2: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`create_implementation_plan.md`](./prompts/create_implementation_plan.md)\n+\n+**Prerequisites:**\n+- DESIGN.md and REQUIREMENTS.md exist with cross-references (from Step 1.1)\n+\n+**Tips:**\n+- Each checkbox = 1 feature (maps to 1 OpenSpec change)\n+- Include requirement references: `({MODULE}-REQ{X}, REQ{Y})`\n+- Add scope hints: `Scope: contract, domain service, REST endpoint`\n+- Organize by phases if defined in DESIGN.md\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.3: Validate Design Documents\n+\n+**Prompt:** [`validate_design_docs.md`](./prompts/validate_design_docs.md)\n+\n+**What Gets Validated:**\n+\n+| Category | Checks |\n+|----------|--------|\n+| **Format** | Required sections, ID formats, checkbox syntax, RFC 2119 language |\n+| **Consistency** | Phases match across docs, requirement phases reference valid phases |\n+| **Cross-References** | All referenced requirements exist, all features reference requirements |\n+| **Completeness** | All phases have features, scope hints present, rationale present |\n+\n+**Pass Criteria:** Zero errors required to proceed. Address warnings where appropriate.\n+\n+---\n+\n+### Step 1.4: Create PR for Design Review\n+\n+1. **Verify** Step 1.3 completed with zero errors\n+2. **Commit docs and create PR** with title: `docs({module}): add design documents`\n+3. **PR description** should include: module purpose, key requirements summary, phases overview, open questions\n+\n+**Review Checklist:**\n+- [ ] Architecture aligns with ModKit patterns\n+- [ ] Requirements are clear, testable, use RFC 2119 language\n+- [ ] Implementation plan covers all requirements\n+- [ ] Phases are independently implementable\n+- [ ] No conflicts with existing modules\n+\n+---\n+\n+## Step 2: Implementation (OpenSpec)\n+\n+For each feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, use OpenSpec to implement incrementally.\n+\n+### Step 2.1: Create OpenSpec Change Proposal\n+\n+Create a change proposal for the next unchecked feature in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n+\n+**Command:** `/openspec:proposal` (or equivalent AI command)\n+\n+**Input:** Feature name and scope from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md, reference to the module's design documents.\n+\n+**Output:** `openspec/changes/module-{name}-{feature}/proposal.md`","path":"docs/module_dev_workflow/README.md","commit_id":"04a95b0bb3eb442b331858558cf92153fd770ba6","original_commit_id":"e103c35fbd0d670e6b23b1621b63cf84bb6e3d38","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"fixed, all files (proposal.md, specs/{capability}/spec.md, design.md, tasks.md) are mentioned","created_at":"2026-01-03T23:06:48Z","updated_at":"2026-01-03T23:06:49Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659201578","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201578"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2659201578"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2659201578/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":null,"original_line":213,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2658132080,"author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":213,"position":1,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664698341","pull_request_review_id":3630648590,"id":2664698341,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6e1BHl","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,9 +1,32 @@\n+<!-- OPENSPEC:START -->\n+# OpenSpec Instructions\n+\n+These instructions are for AI assistants working in this project.\n+\n+Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request:\n+- Mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan)\n+- Introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n+- Sounds ambiguous and you need the authoritative spec before coding\n+\n+Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn:\n+- How to create and apply change proposals\n+- Spec format and conventions\n+- Project structure and guidelines\n+\n+Keep this managed block so 'openspec update' can refresh the instructions.\n+\n+<!-- OPENSPEC:END -->\n+\n+# HyperSpot Instructions\n+\n These instructions are for AI assistants working in this project.\n \n If the instruction sounds unclear, vague or requires more context. Ask for clarification.\n \n Always open `@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md` to have context about how is the project.\n \n+Always open `@/docs/module_dev_workflow/REFERENCE.md` when defining requirements, designing new modules or adding new features for the existing modules.","path":"AGENTS.md","commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","original_commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thought (maybe out of scope of this PR):\r\nI am a bit concerned about multiple \"Always open\" instructions. I notice that in practice they pollute context even if they are not needed for the task, and some of these docs (like Architecture Manifest) are not optimized for agents. I'd rather prefer some well-defined condition when appropriate docs should be opened or maybe use claude skills for conditional context activation (downside: afaik not supported by windsurf out-of-box)","created_at":"2026-01-06T12:00:43Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T12:17:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2664698341","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664698341"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2664698341"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664698341/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":28,"original_line":28,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":28,"position":28,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664730114","pull_request_review_id":3630648590,"id":2664730114,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6e1I4C","diff_hunk":"@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@\n+# Project Context\n+\n+## Purpose\n+\n+HyperSpot Server is a modular, high-performance platform for building AI services in Rust. Built on the **ModKit** framework, it provides:\n+\n+- **Modular architecture** — Everything is a Module with composable, independent units\n+- **Type safety** — Compile-time guarantees via typestate builders and trait-based APIs\n+- **Multi-tenancy** — Built-in tenant isolation with secure ORM layer\n+- **Database agnostic** — PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite via unified API\n+- **GTS extensibility** — Global Type System for versioned, pluggable extensions\n+\n+## Tech Stack\n+\n+- **Language**: Rust (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md))\n+- **Framework**: ModKit (see [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md))\n+- **HTTP**: Axum with `tower-http` middleware\n+- **gRPC**: Tonic (out-of-process modules)\n+- **Database**: SeaORM / SQLx with secure ORM layer (see [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../docs/SECURE-ORM.md))\n+- **Observability**: `tracing` + OpenTelemetry (see [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md))\n+- **OpenAPI**: `utoipa` for automatic documentation generation\n+- **Testing**: cargo test, pytest (E2E), testcontainers\n+- **Linting**: Clippy (pedantic), custom dylint linters\n+\n+## Project Conventions\n+\n+### Architecture\n+\n+Follow the architecture manifest: [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md)\n+\n+**Key principles:**\n+- **Everything is a Module** — composable, independent units\n+- **DDD-light structure** — API / Contract / Domain / Infra layers\n+- **SDK pattern** — separate `-sdk` crate for public API surface\n+- **Type-safe REST** — OperationBuilder prevents half-wired routes at compile time\n+\n+### Module Structure\n+\n+Follow the new module guideline: [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md)\n+\n+```\n+modules/<module>/\n+├─ <module>-sdk/           # Public API: trait, models, errors (NO serde)\n+│  └─ src/\n+│     ├─ api.rs            # API trait (all methods take &SecurityCtx)\n+│     ├─ models.rs         # Transport-agnostic models\n+│     └─ errors.rs         # Transport-agnostic errors\n+└─ <module>/               # Implementation\n+   └─ src/\n+      ├─ module.rs         # #[modkit::module] declaration\n+      ├─ local_client.rs   # Local client implementing SDK trait\n+      ├─ api/rest/         # DTOs, handlers, routes, error mapping\n+      ├─ domain/           # Business logic, events, repository traits\n+      └─ infra/storage/    # SeaORM entities, migrations\n+```\n+\n+### Code Style\n+\n+See [`@/guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md`](../guidelines/DNA/languages/RUST.md)\n+\n+- **Formatting**: `cargo fmt` with max line length 100, 4-space indentation\n+- **Linting**: `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings`\n+- **Architecture lints**: Custom dylint linters enforce layer separation\n+- **No unsafe code**: `#![forbid(unsafe_code)]`\n+- **No panics**: Deny `unwrap()` and `expect()` in production code\n+- **JSON naming**: `camelCase` via `#[serde(rename_all = \"camelCase\")]`\n+\n+### REST API Design\n+\n+Follow the REST API guidelines: [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md)\n+\n+**Key conventions:**\n+- **Endpoint format**: `/{service-name}/v{N}/{resource}` (versioning required)\n+- **Status codes**: See [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md)\n+- **Errors**: RFC-9457 Problem Details (`application/problem+json`)\n+- **Pagination**: Cursor-based with OData filtering (see [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md))\n+\n+### Error Handling\n+\n+- **Domain errors** → `src/domain/error.rs` (pure business errors)\n+- **SDK errors** → `<module>-sdk/src/errors.rs` (transport-agnostic)\n+- **REST mapping** → `impl From<DomainError> for Problem` in `src/api/rest/error.rs`\n+- **Handler return** → `ApiResult<T, DomainError>` with `ApiError::from_domain(e)`\n+\n+### Security\n+\n+Follow security guidelines: [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../guidelines/SECURITY.md)\n+\n+**Key requirements:**\n+- **All API methods MUST accept `&SecurityCtx`** as first parameter\n+- **Use SecureConn** for database access with automatic tenant isolation\n+- **Input validation** via `validator` crate\n+- **No secrets in code** — use environment variables\n+\n+### Database Access\n+\n+Follow secure ORM patterns: [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../docs/SECURE-ORM.md)\n+\n+- **Typestate enforcement**: Unscoped queries cannot execute\n+- **Deny-by-default**: Empty scopes return `WHERE 1=0`\n+- **Request-scoped**: `SecurityCtx` passed per-operation\n+\n+### Testing Strategy\n+\n+Target: **90%+ code coverage**\n+\n+- **Unit tests**: `cargo test --workspace`\n+- **Integration tests**: `make test-pg` / `make test-sqlite`\n+- **E2E tests**: `make e2e-docker` (Python/pytest)\n+- **All checks**: `make check` or `make ci`\n+\n+### Git Workflow\n+\n+**Commit format:** `<type>(<scope>): <description>`\n+\n+Types: `feat`, `fix`, `tech`, `cleanup`, `refactor`, `test`, `docs`, `style`, `chore`, `perf`, `ci`, `build`, `revert`, `security`, `breaking`\n+\n+**DCO required:** All commits must be signed off (`git commit -s`)\n+\n+## Important Constraints\n+\n+### Linter-Enforced Rules (dylint)\n+- **DE01xx**: Contract layer must be pure — NO serde, NO utoipa, NO HTTP types\n+- **DE02xx**: DTOs must be in `api/rest/` with serde + utoipa derives\n+- **DE08xx**: REST endpoints MUST be versioned (`/service/v1/resource`)\n+\n+### Breaking Changes\n+- No breaking changes without version bump and deprecation period\n+- All dependencies specified in root `Cargo.toml` (workspace inheritance)\n+- Backward compatibility: Clients must ignore unknown fields\n+\n+## Module-Specific OpenSpec\n+\n+Each module in `modules/` can have its own `openspec/` directory for module-specific specs and changes. This enables domain teams to own their module's specifications.\n+\n+**Example**: See [`modules/types-registry/openspec/`](../modules/types-registry/openspec/) for a complete example:\n+\n+```\n+modules/types-registry/openspec/\n+├── project.md              # Module-specific context (references parent guidelines)\n+├── AGENTS.md               # AI assistant instructions\n+├── specs/                  # Current module specifications\n+│   ├── types-registry/\n+│   │   └── spec.md\n+│   └── types-registry-sdk/\n+│       └── spec.md\n+└── changes/                # Module change proposals\n+    └── archive/            # Completed changes\n+```\n+\n+**Root vs Module OpenSpec:**\n+- **Root (`openspec/`)**: Cross-cutting concerns, shared infrastructure, project-wide changes\n+- **Module (`modules/<name>/openspec/`)**: Module-specific features, APIs, and implementations\n+\n+## Reference Documents\n+\n+| Document | Purpose |\n+|----------|---------|\n+| [`@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md`](../docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md) | System architecture and design principles |\n+| [`@/docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md`](../docs/MODKIT_UNIFIED_SYSTEM.md) | ModKit framework guide |\n+| [`@/docs/SECURE-ORM.md`](../docs/SECURE-ORM.md) | Secure database access patterns |\n+| [`@/docs/TRACING_SETUP.md`](../docs/TRACING_SETUP.md) | Observability configuration |\n+| [`@/guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md`](../guidelines/NEW_MODULE.md) | Step-by-step module creation |\n+| [`@/guidelines/SECURITY.md`](../guidelines/SECURITY.md) | Security best practices |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/API.md) | REST API design |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/STATUS_CODES.md) | HTTP status code usage |\n+| [`@/guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md`](../guidelines/DNA/REST/PAGINATION.md) | Cursor pagination spec |","path":"openspec/project.md","commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","original_commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","user":{"login":"hyphen-2025","id":248559081,"node_id":"U_kgDODtC16Q","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/248559081?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025","html_url":"https://github.com/hyphen-2025","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hyphen-2025/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"It seems that this document is missing in DNA master, there is QUERYING.md though","created_at":"2026-01-06T12:13:19Z","updated_at":"2026-01-06T12:17:19Z","html_url":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2664730114","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664730114"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pull/188#discussion_r2664730114"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/188"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664730114/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":167,"original_line":167,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":167,"position":167,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/cyberfabric/cyberware-rust/pulls/comments/2664789989","pull_request_review_id":3630745989,"id":2664789989,"node_id":"PRRC_kwDOPaLyBs6e1Xfl","diff_hunk":"@@ -1,9 +1,32 @@\n+<!-- OPENSPEC:START -->\n+# OpenSpec Instructions\n+\n+These instructions are for AI assistants working in this project.\n+\n+Always open `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` when the request:\n+- Mentions planning or proposals (words like proposal, spec, change, plan)\n+- Introduces new capabilities, breaking changes, architecture shifts, or big performance/security work\n+- Sounds ambiguous and you need the authoritative spec before coding\n+\n+Use `@/openspec/AGENTS.md` to learn:\n+- How to create and apply change proposals\n+- Spec format and conventions\n+- Project structure and guidelines\n+\n+Keep this managed block so 'openspec update' can refresh the instructions.\n+\n+<!-- OPENSPEC:END -->\n+\n+# HyperSpot Instructions\n+\n These instructions are for AI assistants working in this project.\n \n If the instruction sounds unclear, vague or requires more context. Ask for clarification.\n \n Always open `@/docs/ARCHITECTURE_MANIFEST.md` to have context about how is the project.\n \n+Always open `@/docs/module_dev_workflow/REFERENCE.md` when defining requirements, designing new modules or adding new features for the existing modules.","path":"AGENTS.md","commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","original_commit_id":"4517a36116cfd36feb8556bd983d6307d4968f8d","user":{"login":"aviator5","id":245955115,"node_id":"U_kgDODqj6Kw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/245955115?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5","html_url":"https://github.com/aviator5","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/aviator5/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Your concern is valid. I have \"Migration to Agent Skills\" item in the [docs/module_dev_workflow/ROADMAP.md](https://github.com/hypernetix/hyperspot/pull/188/files#diff-21e72